(function(){if(!window.__hermes_register_book)return;window.__hermes_register_book("khordeh-avesta",[{"sp":"HDR","t":"Khordeh Avesta"},{"ref":"1.1","t":"<em>Translated by James Darmesteter, 1898<\/em>"},{"sp":"IMG","src":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","t":"A third century Mithraic depiction of Zoroaster found in Dura Europos, Syria"},{"sp":"HDR","t":"Ashem Vohu (invocation of Asha)"},{"ref":"4.1","t":"Holiness (Asha) is the best of all good: it is also happiness."},{"ref":"4.2","t":"Happy the man who is holy with perfect holiness!"},{"sp":"HDR","t":"Ahunwar (most sacred manthra of Zoroastrianism)"},{"ref":"5.1","t":"The will of the Lord is the law of righteousness."},{"ref":"5.2","t":"The gifts of Vohu-mano to the deeds done in this world for Mazda."},{"ref":"5.3","t":"He who relieves the poor makes Ahura king."},{"sp":"HDR","t":"Kem Na Mazda (exorcism)"},{"ref":"6.1","t":"What protector hast thou given unto me, O Mazda! while the"},{"ref":"6.2","t":"hate of the wicked encompasses me? Whom but thy Atar and Vohu-mano,"},{"ref":"6.3","t":"through whose work I keep on the world of righteousness? Reveal"},{"ref":"6.4","t":"therefore to me thy Religion as thy rule!"},{"ref":"6.5","t":"(Ke verethrem-ja:)"},{"ref":"6.6","t":"Who is the victorious who will protect thy teaching? Make"},{"ref":"6.7","t":"it clear that I am the guide for both worlds. May Sraosha come"},{"ref":"6.8","t":"with Vohu-mano and help whomsoever thou pleasest, O Mazda!"},{"ref":"6.9","t":"(Pata-no:)"},{"ref":"6.10","t":"Keep us from our hater, O Mazda and Armaiti Spenta! Perish,"},{"ref":"6.11","t":"O fiendish Druj! Perish, O brood of the fiend! Perish, O creation"},{"ref":"6.12","t":"of the fiend! Perish, O world of the fiend! Perish away, O Druj!"},{"ref":"6.13","t":"Rush away, O Druj! Perish away, O Druj! Perish away to the regions"},{"ref":"6.14","t":"of the north, never more to give unto death the living world of"},{"ref":"6.15","t":"Righteousness!"},{"ref":"6.16","t":"Homage, with which (are combined) devotion and milk offerings."},{"sp":"HDR","t":"Padyab-Kusti (ablution and formula for tying the kusti)"},{"ref":"7.0","t":"With satisfaction for Ahura Mazda. Ashem Vohu...."},{"ref":"7.0a","t":"Kem Na Mazda: What protector hast thou given..."},{"ref":"7.0b","t":"Ohrmazd is Lord! Ahriman he keeps at bay, he holds him back."},{"ref":"7.0c","t":"May Ahriman be struck and defeated, with devs and drujs, sorcerers"},{"ref":"7.0d","t":"and sinners, kayags and karbs, tyrants, wrongdoers and heretics,"},{"ref":"7.0e","t":"sinners, enemies and witches! May they (all) be struck and defeated!"},{"ref":"7.0f","t":"May evil rulers not exist, (or) be far away! May enemies be defeated!"},{"ref":"7.0g","t":"May enemies all not exist, (or) be far away!"},{"ref":"7.0h","t":"O Ohrmazd, Lord! I am contrite for all sins and I desist from"},{"ref":"7.0i","t":"them, from all bad thoughts, bad words and bad acts which I have"},{"ref":"7.0j","t":"thought, spoken or done in the world, or which have happened through"},{"ref":"7.0k","t":"me, or have originated with me. For those sins of thinking, speaking"},{"ref":"7.0l","t":"and acting, of body and soul, worldly or spiritual, O Ohrmazd!"},{"ref":"7.0m","t":"I am contrite, I renounce them. With three words I distance myself"},{"ref":"7.0n","t":"(from them)."},{"ref":"7.1","t":"With satisfaction for Ahura Mazda, scorn for Angra Mainyu!"},{"ref":"7.1a","t":"The true achievement of what is most wonderful, according to wish!"},{"ref":"7.1b","t":"I praise Asha! Ashem Vohu...."},{"ref":"7.1c","t":"Yatha Ahu Vairyo...."},{"ref":"7.1d","t":"Ashem Vohu...."},{"ref":"7.2","t":"Come to my aid, O Mazda."},{"ref":"7.2a","t":"I profess myself a Mazda-worshipper, a Zoroastrian, having"},{"ref":"7.2b","t":"vowed it and professed it. I pledge myself to the well-thought"},{"ref":"7.2c","t":"thought, I pledge myself to the well-spoken word, I pledge myself"},{"ref":"7.2d","t":"to the well-done action."},{"ref":"7.2e","t":"I pledge myself to the Mazdayasnian religion, which causes"},{"ref":"7.2f","t":"the attack to be put off and weapons put down; which upholds khvaetvadatha"},{"ref":"7.2g","t":"(kin-marriage), which possesses Asha; which of all religions that"},{"ref":"7.2h","t":"exist or shall be, is the greatest, the best, and the most beautiful:"},{"ref":"7.2i","t":"Ahuric, Zoroastrian. I ascribe all good to Ahura Mazda. This is"},{"ref":"7.2j","t":"the creed of the Mazdayasnian religion."},{"ref":"7.2k","t":"Ashem Vohu...!!"},{"sp":"HDR","t":"Baj before meals"},{"ref":"8.1","t":"Thus therefore do we worship Ahura Mazda,"},{"ref":"8.2","t":"who made the Kine (the living creation), and the"},{"ref":"8.3","t":"(embodied) Righteousness (which is incarnate in the"},{"ref":"8.4","t":"clean), and the waters, and the wholesome plants,"},{"ref":"8.5","t":"the stars, and the earth, and all (existing) objects"},{"ref":"8.6","t":"that are good."},{"ref":"8.7","t":"(after meal:)"},{"ref":"8.8","t":"Ashem vohu...."},{"ref":"8.9","t":"Yatha Ahu Vairyo...."},{"ref":"8.10","t":"To him splendor..."},{"sp":"HDR","t":"Baj when answering the call of nature"},{"ref":"9.1","t":"(Modi 374. This prayer is also known as “Pishab ni Baj”.)"},{"ref":"9.2","t":"May wrong actions be done away with a hundred-thousand times."},{"ref":"9.3","t":"Yatha Ahu Vairyo..."},{"ref":"9.4","t":"(here perform the natural function)"},{"ref":"9.5","t":"Ashem vohu...."},{"ref":"9.6","t":"We are praisers of good thoughts, of good"},{"ref":"9.7","t":"words, and of good actions, of those now and those"},{"ref":"9.8","t":"hereafter [(Pazand) of those being done; and of those"},{"ref":"9.9","t":"completed]. We implant (?) them (with our homage,"},{"ref":"9.10","t":"and we do this) the more, and yet the more since we"},{"ref":"9.11","t":"are (praisers) of the good (from whom they spring)."},{"ref":"9.12","t":"(y35.2)."},{"ref":"9.13","t":"To the best of good rulers (is) verily the Kingdom,"},{"ref":"9.14","t":"because we render and ascribe it to Him, and"},{"ref":"9.15","t":"make it thoroughly His own (?), to Mazda Ahura"},{"ref":"9.16","t":"do we ascribe it, and to Righteousness the Best."},{"ref":"9.17","t":"(y35.5)."},{"ref":"9.18","t":"Yatha ahu Vairyo...."},{"ref":"9.19","t":"Ashem vohu...."},{"ref":"9.20","t":"We worship the Ahunwar."},{"ref":"9.21","t":"We worship Best Asha, the most beautiful Amesha Spenta."},{"ref":"9.22","t":"Yenghe... (Y18.9)."},{"sp":"HDR","t":"Nirang-i Abezar"},{"ref":"10.1","t":"Broken, broken be Satan Ahriman..... not reach me."},{"ref":"10.2","t":"May the thirty-three Ameshaspands and the creator Ormazd be victorious."},{"ref":"10.3","t":"I praise Asha. Ashem vohu...."},{"ref":"10.4","t":"<strong>The Gah Dedications<\/strong>"},{"ref":"10.5","t":"(Hawan Gah)"},{"ref":"10.6","t":"To Hawan, Ashavan, the master of Asha, for worship, adoration,"},{"ref":"10.7","t":"propitiation and praise. To Savanghi and Visya, Ashavan, the"},{"ref":"10.8","t":"master(s) of Asha, for worship, adoration, propitiation and praise."},{"ref":"10.9","t":"(Rapithwin Gah)"},{"ref":"10.10","t":"To Rapithwin, Ashavan, the master of Asha, for worship,"},{"ref":"10.11","t":"adoration, propitiation and praise. To Fradat-Fshu and"},{"ref":"10.12","t":"Zangtuma, Ashavan, the master(s) of Asha, for worship,"},{"ref":"10.13","t":"adoration, propitiation and praise."},{"ref":"10.14","t":"(Uzerin Gah)"},{"ref":"10.15","t":"To Uzerin, Ashavan, the master of Asha, for worship,"},{"ref":"10.16","t":"adoration, propitiation and praise. To Fradat-Vira"},{"ref":"10.17","t":"and Dakhyuma, Ashavan, the master(s) of Asha, for worship,"},{"ref":"10.18","t":"adoration, propitiation and praise."},{"ref":"10.19","t":"(Aiwisruthrem Gah)"},{"ref":"10.20","t":"To Aiwisruthrem that furthers life, Ashavan, the master"},{"ref":"10.21","t":"of Asha, for worship, adoration, propitiation and praise."},{"ref":"10.22","t":"To Fradat-vispam-hujyaiti and Zarathushtrotema, Ashavan,"},{"ref":"10.23","t":"the master(s) of Asha, for worship, adoration, propitiation"},{"ref":"10.24","t":"and praise."},{"ref":"10.25","t":"(Ushahin Gah)"},{"ref":"10.26","t":"To Ushahin that furthers life, Ashavan, the master of"},{"ref":"10.27","t":"Asha, for worship, adoration, propitiation and praise."},{"ref":"10.28","t":"To Berejya and Nmanya, Ashavan, the master(s) of Asha,"},{"ref":"10.29","t":"for worship, adoration, propitiation and praise."},{"sp":"HDR","t":"Srosh Baj"},{"ref":"11.0","t":"In the name of God, May the bounteous miraculous power and"},{"ref":"11.0a","t":"glory of Ohrmazd the lord increase. May it (i.e. the prayer) reach"},{"ref":"11.0b","t":"Srosh, the righteous, the vigorous, whose body is the command,"},{"ref":"11.0c","t":"having a hard weapon, powerful of weapon, the lord of the creations"},{"ref":"11.0d","t":"of Ohrmazd. I am contrite for all sins and I desist from them,"},{"ref":"11.0e","t":"from all bad thoughts, bad words and bad acts which I have thought,"},{"ref":"11.0f","t":"spoken or done in the world, or which have happened through me,"},{"ref":"11.0g","t":"or have originated with me. For those sins of thinking, speaking"},{"ref":"11.0h","t":"and acting, of body and soul, worldly or spiritual, o Ohrmazd!"},{"ref":"11.0i","t":"I am contrite, I renounce them. With three words I distance myself"},{"ref":"11.0j","t":"(from them)."},{"ref":"11.1","t":"Yatha Ahu Vairyo...."},{"ref":"11.1a","t":"Ashem Vohu...."},{"ref":"11.1b","t":"I profess myself a Mazda-worshipper, a follower of Zarathushtra,"},{"ref":"11.1c","t":"opposing the Daevas, accepting the Ahuric doctrine."},{"ref":"11.1d","t":"(Here recite the appropriate Gah dedication.)"},{"ref":"11.1e","t":"With propitiation of Sraosha, companion of Ashi, the brave, who"},{"ref":"11.1f","t":"has the Manthra for body, with bold club, the ahurian, for worship,"},{"ref":"11.1g","t":"adoration, propitiation, and praise."},{"ref":"11.1h","t":"‘Yatha Ahu Vairyo’, the zaotar should say to me"},{"ref":"11.1i","t":"‘Atha ratush ashatchit hacha’, the Asha-sanctified knowing one"},{"ref":"11.1j","t":"should say."},{"ref":"11.2","t":"We worship Sraosha, companion of Ashi, fair of form, victorious,"},{"ref":"11.2a","t":"world-promoting, the Ashavan, master of Asha. The Ahuna Vairya"},{"ref":"11.2b","t":"prayer protects the body."},{"ref":"11.2c","t":"Yatha Ahu Vairyo...."},{"ref":"11.2d","t":"(Here recite the Kem Na Mazda prayer.)"},{"ref":"11.2e","t":"Yatha Ahu Vairyo...."},{"ref":"11.4","t":"I desire worship and adoration and strength and force for"},{"ref":"11.4a","t":"Sraosha, companion of Ashi, the brave, who has the Manthra for"},{"ref":"11.4b","t":"body, with bold club, the ahurian."},{"ref":"11.4c","t":"Ashem Vohu...."},{"ref":"11.5","t":"Bestow on him riches and good things; bestow health of body,"},{"ref":"11.5a","t":"toughness of body, and resistance of body; bestow on him possessions"},{"ref":"11.5b","t":"giving abundant ease, future noble offspring, and a lengthy long"},{"ref":"11.5c","t":"life; bestow on him the best existence of the Asha-sanctified,"},{"ref":"11.5d","t":"the luminous, offering all happy. [This paragraph follows Bailey]"},{"ref":"11.5e","t":"Thus may it come as I wish."},{"ref":"11.5f","t":"Ashem Vohu...."},{"ref":"11.5g","t":"A thousand remedies, ten thousand remedies. Ashem Vohu...."},{"ref":"11.5h","t":"Come to my help, O Mazda."},{"ref":"11.5i","t":"To Ama, well-built, fair of form, Verethraghna, Ahura-created;"},{"ref":"11.5j","t":"and to Triumphing Uparatat; and to Raman of good pastures, and"},{"ref":"11.5k","t":"to Vayu of superior activity, superior to other creatures. That"},{"ref":"11.5l","t":"part of you, Vayu, which belongs to Spenta Mainyu; to self-governed"},{"ref":"11.5m","t":"Thwasha, to boundless Zurwan, to Zurwan of the long dominion."},{"ref":"11.5n","t":"Ashem Vohu...."},{"ref":"11.5o","t":"For the reward of virtue and the forgiveness of sins, I do (deeds"},{"ref":"11.5p","t":"of) righteousness for the love of my soul. May all virtuousness"},{"ref":"11.5q","t":"of all good ones of the earth of seven climes reach the width"},{"ref":"11.5r","t":"of the earth, the length of the rivers, the height of the sun"},{"ref":"11.5s","t":"in their original form. May it be righteous, live long. Thus may"},{"ref":"11.5t","t":"it come as I wish."},{"ref":"11.5u","t":"Ashem Vohu...!!"},{"sp":"HDR","t":"Hoshbam (Prayer at Dawn)"},{"ref":"12.1","t":"Then thou shalt say those victorious, most healing words;"},{"ref":"12.1a","t":"thou shalt chant the Ahunwar five times:"},{"ref":"12.1b","t":"Yatha ahu vairyo..."},{"ref":"12.1c","t":"The Ahunwar protects the body...."},{"ref":"12.1d","t":"(Here recite the Kem Na Mazda prayer.)"},{"ref":"12.1e","t":"Ashem vohu...."},{"ref":"12.1f","t":"Yatha Ahu Vairyo...."},{"ref":"12.1g","t":"Ashem vohu..."},{"ref":"12.2","t":"Homage to you, O Dawn."},{"ref":"12.2a","t":"(Y27.1-2:)"},{"ref":"12.2b","t":"This is to render Him who is of all the greatest, our lord"},{"ref":"12.2c","t":"and master (even) Ahura Mazda. And this to smite the wicked Angra"},{"ref":"12.2d","t":"Mainyu, and to smite Aeshma of the bloody spear, and the Mazainya"},{"ref":"12.2e","t":"Daevas, and to smite all the wicked Varenya Daevas."},{"ref":"12.3","t":"And this is to further Ahura Mazda, the resplendent, the glorious,"},{"ref":"12.3a","t":"to further the Bountiful Immortals, and the influences of the"},{"ref":"12.3b","t":"star Tishtrya, the resplendent, the glorious, (and) to the furtherance"},{"ref":"12.3c","t":"of the holy man, and of all the (bountiful and) holy creatures"},{"ref":"12.3d","t":"of the Bounteous Spirit."},{"ref":"12.3e","t":"(Y52.1-4:)"},{"ref":"12.4","t":"I pray with benedictions for a benefit, and for the good,"},{"ref":"12.4a","t":"even for the entire creation of the holy (and the clean); I beseech"},{"ref":"12.4b","t":"for them for the (generation which is) now alive, for that which"},{"ref":"12.4c","t":"is just coming into life, and for that which shall be hereafter."},{"ref":"12.4d","t":"And (I pray for that) sanctity which leads to prosperity, and"},{"ref":"12.4e","t":"which has long afforded shelter, which goes on hand in hand with"},{"ref":"12.4f","t":"it, which joins it in its walk, and of itself becoming its close"},{"ref":"12.4g","t":"companion as it delivers forth its precepts, bearing every form"},{"ref":"12.4h","t":"of healing virtue which comes to us in waters, appertains to cattle,"},{"ref":"12.4i","t":"or is found in plants, and overwhelming, all the harmful malice"},{"ref":"12.4j","t":"of the Daevas, (and their servants) who might harm this dwelling"},{"ref":"12.4k","t":"and its lord, bringing good gifts, and better blessings, given"},{"ref":"12.4l","t":"very early, and later (gifts), leading to successes, and for a"},{"ref":"12.4m","t":"long time giving shelter. And so the greatest, and the best, and"},{"ref":"12.4n","t":"most beautiful benefits of sanctity fall likewise to our lot."},{"ref":"12.4o","t":"For the sacrifice, homage, propitiation, and the praise of the"},{"ref":"12.4p","t":"Bountiful Immortals, for the bringing prosperity to this abode,"},{"ref":"12.4q","t":"and for the prosperity of the entire creation of the holy, and"},{"ref":"12.4r","t":"the clean, (and as for this, so) for the opposition of the entire"},{"ref":"12.4s","t":"evil creation. (And I pray for this) as I praise through Righteousness,"},{"ref":"12.4t","t":"I who am beneficent, those who are (likewise of a better mind)."},{"ref":"12.4u","t":"(Y8.5-7:)"},{"ref":"12.4v","t":"May’st Thou, O Ahura Mazda! reign at Thy will, and with a"},{"ref":"12.4w","t":"saving rule over Thine own creatures, and render Ye the holy (man)"},{"ref":"12.4x","t":"also a sovereign at his will over waters, and over plants, and"},{"ref":"12.4y","t":"over all the clean and sacred (creatures) which contain the seed"},{"ref":"12.4z","t":"of Righteousness. Strip ye the wicked of all power!"},{"ref":"12.4aa","t":"Absolute in power may the holy be, bereft of all free choice the"},{"ref":"12.4ba","t":"wicked! Gone (may he be), met as foe, carried out from the creatures"},{"ref":"12.4ca","t":"of Spenta Mainyu, hemmed in without power over any wish!"},{"ref":"12.4da","t":"I will incite, even I who am Zarathushtra, the heads of the houses,"},{"ref":"12.4ea","t":"villages, Zantus, and provinces, to the careful following of this"},{"ref":"12.4fa","t":"Religion which is that of Ahura, and according to Zarathushtra,"},{"ref":"12.4ga","t":"in their thoughts, their words, and their deeds."},{"ref":"12.4ha","t":"(Y60.11 seq.:)"},{"ref":"12.5","t":"In order that our minds may be delighted, and our souls the"},{"ref":"12.5a","t":"best, let our bodies be glorified as well, and let them; O Mazda!"},{"ref":"12.5b","t":"go likewise openly (unto Heaven) as the best world of the saints"},{"ref":"12.5c","t":"as devoted to Ahura, and accompanied by Asha Vahishta (who is"},{"ref":"12.5d","t":"Righteousness the Best), and the most beautiful! And may we see"},{"ref":"12.5e","t":"Thee, and may we, approaching, come around about Thee, and attain"},{"ref":"12.5f","t":"to entire companionship with Thee!"},{"ref":"12.5g","t":"Ashem Vohu...."},{"ref":"12.5h","t":"Bestow on him riches... (Recite SrB5.)"},{"ref":"12.5i","t":"Ashem Vohu...!!"},{"sp":"HDR","t":"Hawan Gah (sunrise to midday)"},{"ref":"14.1","t":"Propitiation to Ahura Mazda."},{"ref":"14.1a","t":"Ashem Vohu...."},{"ref":"14.1b","t":"I profess myself a Mazda-worshipper, a follower of Zarathushtra,"},{"ref":"14.1c","t":"opposing the Daevas, accepting the Ahuric doctrine."},{"ref":"14.1d","t":"To Hawan, Ashavan, the master of Asha, for worship, adoration,"},{"ref":"14.1e","t":"propitiation and praise. To Savanghi and Visya, Ashavan, the master(s)"},{"ref":"14.1f","t":"of Asha, for worship, adoration, propitiation and praise."},{"ref":"14.2","t":"With propitiation of Mithra of wide pastures, with a thousand"},{"ref":"14.2a","t":"ears, ten thousand eyes, a Yazata who is invoked by name, (and)"},{"ref":"14.2b","t":"Raman Khwastra, for worship, adoration, propitiation and praise."},{"ref":"14.2c","t":"Yatha Ahu Vairyo, the zaotar should say to me Atha ratush ashatchit"},{"ref":"14.2d","t":"hacha, the knowing Asha-one should say."},{"ref":"14.3","t":"We worship Ahura Mazda, Ashavan, the master of Asha. We worship"},{"ref":"14.3a","t":"Zarathushtra, Ashavan, the master of Asha. We worship the Fravashi"},{"ref":"14.3b","t":"of Ashavan Zarathushtra. We worship the Ashavan Amesha Spentas."},{"ref":"14.4","t":"We worship the Ashavan, good, powerful, holy Fravashis, the"},{"ref":"14.4a","t":"material and the spiritual. We worship the most effective of masters,"},{"ref":"14.4b","t":"the most active of Yazatas, and the most worthy of the masters"},{"ref":"14.4c","t":"of Asha, who is best able to reach his goal of satisfaction, the"},{"ref":"14.4d","t":"Ashavan master of Asha!"},{"ref":"14.5","t":"We worship Hawan, Ashavan, the master of Asha, We worship"},{"ref":"14.5a","t":"Haurvatat, Ashavan, the master of Asha, We worship Ameretat, Ashavan,"},{"ref":"14.5b","t":"the master of Asha, We worship the Ahuric question, Ashavan, the"},{"ref":"14.5c","t":"master of Asha, We worship the Ahuric doctrine, Ashavan, the master"},{"ref":"14.5d","t":"of Asha, We worship the mighty Yasna Haptanghaiti, Ashavan, the"},{"ref":"14.5e","t":"master of Asha."},{"ref":"14.6","t":"We worship Savanghe and Visya, Ashavan, the master(s) of Asha,"},{"ref":"14.6a","t":"We worship the Airyema-ishyo (prayer), Ashavan, the master of"},{"ref":"14.6b","t":"Asha, mighty, victorious against the hostility [of Daevas], overcoming"},{"ref":"14.6c","t":"all hostility, destroying all hostility, which is the last, middle,"},{"ref":"14.6d","t":"and the foremost of the Manthras to be invoked, the five Gathas."},{"ref":"14.7","t":"We worship Mithra of wide pastures, And we worship Raman Khwastra,"},{"ref":"14.7a","t":"and the master Visya, for worship and praise; and we worship Visya,"},{"ref":"14.7b","t":"Asha-sanctified, the master of Asha."},{"ref":"14.8","t":"We worship Mithra of wide pastures, with a thousand ears,"},{"ref":"14.8a","t":"ten thousand eyes, a Yazata who is invoked by name. We worship"},{"ref":"14.8b","t":"Raman Khwastra!"},{"ref":"14.9","t":"We worship you, O Atar, son of Ahura Mazda, Ashavan, the master"},{"ref":"14.9a","t":"of Asha. We worship this Baresman spread with Asha and provided"},{"ref":"14.9b","t":"with Zaothra and girdle, Ashavan, the master of Asha. We worship"},{"ref":"14.9c","t":"Apam Napat, Nairyosangha, and the brave Yazata Damoish Upamana."},{"ref":"14.9d","t":"We worship the souls of the deceased, they, the Fravashis of the"},{"ref":"14.9e","t":"Ashavan."},{"ref":"14.9f","t":"We worship the exalted master who is Ahura Mazda, who is highest"},{"ref":"14.9g","t":"in Asha, who is furthest going in Asha. We worship all the teachings"},{"ref":"14.9h","t":"of Zarathushtra. We worship all well done deeds (those already)"},{"ref":"14.9i","t":"done, and those that will be done."},{"ref":"14.9j","t":"We worship all those Beings whom Ahura Mazda knows to be best"},{"ref":"14.9k","t":"for worship according to Asha, male and female."},{"ref":"14.10","t":"Yatha Ahu Vairyo...."},{"ref":"14.10a","t":"I desire worship and adoration and strength and force for Mithra"},{"ref":"14.10b","t":"of wide pastures, with a thousand ears, ten thousand eyes, a Yazata"},{"ref":"14.10c","t":"who is invoked by name, (and) Raman Khwastra."},{"ref":"14.10d","t":"Ashem Vohu...."},{"ref":"14.10e","t":"Bestow on him riches... (Recite SrB5.)"},{"sp":"HDR","t":"Rapithwin Gah (midday to mid-afternoon)"},{"ref":"15.1","t":"Propitiation to Ahura Mazda."},{"ref":"15.1a","t":"Ashem Vohu...."},{"ref":"15.1b","t":"I profess myself a Mazda-worshipper, a follower of Zarathushtra,"},{"ref":"15.1c","t":"opposing the Daevas, accepting the Ahuric doctrine."},{"ref":"15.1d","t":"To Rapithwin, Ashavan, the master of Asha, for worship, adoration,"},{"ref":"15.1e","t":"propitiation and praise. To Fradat-Fshu and Zangtuma, Ashavan,"},{"ref":"15.1f","t":"the master(s) of Asha, for worship, adoration, propitiation and"},{"ref":"15.1g","t":"praise."},{"ref":"15.2","t":"With propitiation of Asha Vahishta and Atar, (son) of Ahura"},{"ref":"15.2a","t":"Mazda, for worship, adoration, propitiation and praise."},{"ref":"15.2b","t":"Yatha Ahu Vairyo, the zaotar should say to me"},{"ref":"15.2c","t":"Atha ratush ashatchit hacha, the knowing Asha-one should say."},{"ref":"15.3","t":"We worship Ahura Mazda, Ashavan, the master of Asha. We worship"},{"ref":"15.3a","t":"Zarathushtra, Ashavan, the master of Asha. We worship the Fravashi"},{"ref":"15.3b","t":"of Ashavan Zarathushtra, We worship the Ashavan Amesha Spentas."},{"ref":"15.4","t":"We worship the good, powerful, holy Fravashis, Ashavan, the"},{"ref":"15.4a","t":"material and the spiritual. We worship the most effective of masters,"},{"ref":"15.4b","t":"the most active of Yazatas, and the most worthy of the masters"},{"ref":"15.4c","t":"of Asha, who is best able to reach his goal of satisfaction, the"},{"ref":"15.4d","t":"Ashavan master of Asha!"},{"ref":"15.5","t":"We worship Rapithwin, Ashavan, the master of Asha, We worship"},{"ref":"15.5a","t":"the Ahunawad Gatha, Ashavan, the master of Asha. We worship the"},{"ref":"15.5b","t":"Ushtawad Gatha, Ashavan, the master of Asha. We worship the Spentomad"},{"ref":"15.5c","t":"Gatha, Ashavan, the master of Asha. We worship the Wohukhshathra"},{"ref":"15.5d","t":"Gatha, Ashavan, the master of Asha. We worship the Wahishtoisht"},{"ref":"15.5e","t":"Gatha, Ashavan, the master of Asha."},{"ref":"15.6","t":"We worship Fradat-Fshu and the Ashavan Zantuma, the master"},{"ref":"15.6a","t":"of Asha, and we worship the Fshusho Manthra, and we worship the"},{"ref":"15.6b","t":"truthfully spoken word; we worship the truthfully spoken sayings,"},{"ref":"15.6c","t":"victorious, Daeva smiting. We worship the waters and the Earth;"},{"ref":"15.6d","t":"we worship the plants and the spiritual Ashavan Yazatas, conferring"},{"ref":"15.6e","t":"good; and we worship the Ashavan Amesha Spentas."},{"ref":"15.7","t":"We worship the Ashavan, good, powerful, holy Fravashis; and"},{"ref":"15.7a","t":"we worship the peak of Asha Vahishta: of great Manthra, of great"},{"ref":"15.7b","t":"operation, of great fidelity, of great performance, of great"},{"ref":"15.7c","t":"effect in spreading the Mazdayasnian religion."},{"ref":"15.8","t":"We worship that assembly and meeting of the Amesha Spentas"},{"ref":"15.8a","t":"when they visit the heights of Heaven, to worship and praise the"},{"ref":"15.8b","t":"master Zantuma, and the Ashavan Zantuma, the master of Asha."},{"ref":"15.9","t":"We worship Asha Vahishta, and Atar, the son of Ahura Mazda!"},{"ref":"15.10","t":"We worship you, O Atar, son of Ahura Mazda, Ashavan, the master"},{"ref":"15.10a","t":"of Asha. We worship this Baresman spread with Asha and provided"},{"ref":"15.10b","t":"with Zaothra and girdle, Ashavan, the master of Asha. We worship"},{"ref":"15.10c","t":"Apam Napat. We worship Nairyosangha. We worship the brave Yazata"},{"ref":"15.10d","t":"Damoish Upamana. We worship the souls of the deceased, they, the"},{"ref":"15.10e","t":"Fravashis of the Asha-sanctified."},{"ref":"15.11","t":"We worship the exalted master who is Ahura Mazda, who is highest"},{"ref":"15.11a","t":"in Asha, who is furthest going in Asha. We worship all the teachings"},{"ref":"15.11b","t":"of Zarathushtra. We worship all well done deeds (those already)"},{"ref":"15.11c","t":"done, and those that will be done."},{"ref":"15.11d","t":"We worship all those Beings whom Ahura Mazda knows to be best"},{"ref":"15.11e","t":"for worship according to Asha, male and female."},{"ref":"15.12","t":"Yatha Ahu Vairyo...."},{"ref":"15.12a","t":"I desire worship and adoration and strength and force for Asha"},{"ref":"15.12b","t":"Vahishta and Atar (son) of Ahura Mazda."},{"ref":"15.12c","t":"Ashem Vohu...."},{"ref":"15.12d","t":"Bestow on him riches... (Recite SrB5.)"},{"sp":"HDR","t":"Uzerin Gah (mid-afternoon to sunset)"},{"ref":"16.1","t":"Propitiation to Ahura Mazda."},{"ref":"16.1a","t":"Ashem Vohu...."},{"ref":"16.1b","t":"I profess myself a Mazda-worshipper, a follower of Zarathushtra,"},{"ref":"16.1c","t":"opposing the Daevas, accepting the Ahuric doctrine."},{"ref":"16.1d","t":"To Uzerin, Ashavan, the master of Asha, for worship, adoration,"},{"ref":"16.1e","t":"propitiation and praise. To Fradat-Vira and Dakhyuma, Ashavan,"},{"ref":"16.1f","t":"the master(s) of Asha, for worship, adoration, propitiation and"},{"ref":"16.1g","t":"praise."},{"ref":"16.2","t":"With propitiation of the lofty Ahura Apam Napat, and the waters"},{"ref":"16.2a","t":"made by Mazda, for worship, adoration, propitiation and praise."},{"ref":"16.2b","t":"Yatha Ahu Vairyo, the zaotar should say to me"},{"ref":"16.2c","t":"Atha ratush ashatchit hacha, the knowing Asha-one should say."},{"ref":"16.3","t":"We worship Ahura Mazda, Ashavan, the master of Asha. We worship"},{"ref":"16.3a","t":"Zarathushtra, Ashavan, the master of Asha. We worship the Fravashi"},{"ref":"16.3b","t":"of Ashavan Zarathushtra, We worship the Ashavan Amesha Spentas."},{"ref":"16.4","t":"We worship the good, powerful, holy Fravashis, Ashavan, the"},{"ref":"16.4a","t":"material and the spiritual. We worship the most effective of masters,"},{"ref":"16.4b","t":"the most active of Yazatas, and the most worthy of the masters"},{"ref":"16.4c","t":"of Asha, who is best able to reach his goal of satisfaction, the"},{"ref":"16.4d","t":"Ashavan master of Asha!"},{"ref":"16.5","t":"We worship Uzerin, Ashavan, the master of Asha; we worship"},{"ref":"16.5a","t":"the Zaotar, Ashavan, the master of Asha; we worship the Havanan,"},{"ref":"16.5b","t":"Ashavan, the master of Asha; we worship the Aterevaxsh, Ashavan,"},{"ref":"16.5c","t":"the master of Asha; we worship the Fraberetar, Ashavan, the master"},{"ref":"16.5d","t":"of Asha; we worship the Aberet, Ashavan, the master of Asha; we"},{"ref":"16.5e","t":"worship the Asnatar, Ashavan, the master of Asha; we worship the"},{"ref":"16.5f","t":"Rathwishkara, Ashavan, the master of Asha; we worship the Sraoshavarez,"},{"ref":"16.5g","t":"Ashavan, the master of Asha;"},{"ref":"16.6","t":"We worship the Fradat-Vira and Dakhyuma, Ashavan, the master(s)"},{"ref":"16.6a","t":"of Asha; we worship the stars and the Moon and the Sun, the [celestial]"},{"ref":"16.6b","t":"luminosity. We worship Anagra Raochah; and we worship the comfortable"},{"ref":"16.6c","t":"abode of the blissful, which is the torment of the druj-followers."},{"ref":"16.7","t":"We worship those Asha-ones who perform their duty, the master(s)"},{"ref":"16.7a","t":"of Asha; and we worship the later doctrine. We worship the Asha-believing"},{"ref":"16.7b","t":"creation of Asha, performing its duty by day and night with worthy"},{"ref":"16.7c","t":"offering of Zaothra, for worship and adoration of the master Dahvyuma;"},{"ref":"16.7d","t":"and we worship the Ashavan Dahvyuma, the master of Asha."},{"ref":"16.8","t":"We worship the lofty Ahura, the radiant Khshathra, Apam Napat,"},{"ref":"16.8a","t":"possessing swift horses; and we worship the Ashavan waters, made"},{"ref":"16.8b","t":"by Mazda."},{"ref":"16.9","t":"We worship you, O Atar, son of Ahura Mazda, Ashavan, the master"},{"ref":"16.9a","t":"of Asha. We worship this Baresman spread with Asha and provided"},{"ref":"16.9b","t":"with Zaothra and girdle, Ashavan, the master of Asha. We worship"},{"ref":"16.9c","t":"Apam Napat. We worship Nairyosangha. We worship the brave Yazata"},{"ref":"16.9d","t":"Damoish Upamana. We worship the souls of the deceased, they, the"},{"ref":"16.9e","t":"Fravashis of the Ashavan."},{"ref":"16.10","t":"We worship the exalted master who is Ahura Mazda, who is highest"},{"ref":"16.10a","t":"in Asha, who is furthest going in Asha. We worship all the teachings"},{"ref":"16.10b","t":"of Zarathushtra. We worship all well done deeds (those already)"},{"ref":"16.10c","t":"done, and those that will be done."},{"ref":"16.10d","t":"We worship all those Beings whom Ahura Mazda knows to be best"},{"ref":"16.10e","t":"for worship according to Asha, male and female."},{"ref":"16.11","t":"Yatha Ahu Vairyo...."},{"ref":"16.11a","t":"I desire worship and adoration and strength and force for Asha"},{"ref":"16.11b","t":"Vahishta and the fire of Ahura Mazda."},{"ref":"16.11c","t":"Ashem Vohu...."},{"ref":"16.11d","t":"Bestow on him riches... (Recite SrB5.)"},{"sp":"HDR","t":"Aiwisruthrem Gah (sunset to midnight)"},{"ref":"17.1","t":"Propitiation to Ahura Mazda."},{"ref":"17.1a","t":"Ashem Vohu...."},{"ref":"17.1b","t":"I profess myself a Mazda-worshipper, a follower of Zarathushtra,"},{"ref":"17.1c","t":"opposing the Daevas, accepting the Ahuric doctrine."},{"ref":"17.1d","t":"To Aiwisruthrem that furthers life, Ashavan, the master of Asha,"},{"ref":"17.1e","t":"for worship, adoration, propitiation and praise. To Fradat-vispam-hujyaiti"},{"ref":"17.1f","t":"and Zarathushtrotema, Ashavan, the master(s) of Asha, for worship,"},{"ref":"17.1g","t":"adoration, propitiation and praise."},{"ref":"17.2","t":"With propitiation of the Ashavan Fravashis, and to the women"},{"ref":"17.2a","t":"with their troops of heroes, and the Yairya Hushitay and to Ama,"},{"ref":"17.2b","t":"well-built, fair of form, Verethraghna, Ahura-created; and to"},{"ref":"17.2c","t":"Triumphing Uparatat, for worship, adoration, propitiation and"},{"ref":"17.2d","t":"praise."},{"ref":"17.2e","t":"Yatha Ahu Vairyo, the zaotar should say to me"},{"ref":"17.2f","t":"Atha ratush ashatchit hacha, the knowing Asha-one should say."},{"ref":"17.3","t":"We worship Ahura Mazda, Ashavan, the master of Asha. We worship"},{"ref":"17.3a","t":"Zarathushtra, Ashavan, the master of Asha. We worship the Fravashi"},{"ref":"17.3b","t":"of Ashavan Zarathushtra. We worship the Ashavan Amesha Spentas."},{"ref":"17.4","t":"We worship the good, powerful, holy Fravashis, Ashavan, the"},{"ref":"17.4a","t":"material and the spiritual. We worship the most effective of masters,"},{"ref":"17.4b","t":"the most active of Yazatas, and the most worthy of the masters"},{"ref":"17.4c","t":"of Asha, who is best able to reach his goal of satisfaction, the"},{"ref":"17.4d","t":"Ashavan master of Asha!"},{"ref":"17.5","t":"We worship Aiwisruthrima, Ashavan, the master of Asha. We"},{"ref":"17.5a","t":"worship Aibigaya, Ashavan, the master of Asha. We worship you,"},{"ref":"17.5b","t":"Atar, the son of Ahura Mazda, Ashavan, the master of Asha. We"},{"ref":"17.5c","t":"worship the stone mortar, the master of Asha. We worship the iron"},{"ref":"17.5d","t":"mortar, the master of Asha. We worship this Baresman spread with"},{"ref":"17.5e","t":"Asha and provided with Zaothra and girdle, Ashavan, the master"},{"ref":"17.5f","t":"of Asha. We worship the waters (and) plants; we worship the Aourvatam"},{"ref":"17.5g","t":"Urunay, Ashavan, the master of Asha."},{"ref":"17.6","t":"We worship the Fradat-vispam-hujyatay, Ashavan, the master"},{"ref":"17.6a","t":"of Asha. We worship Zarathushtra, Ashavan, the master of Asha."},{"ref":"17.6b","t":"We worship the sacred Manthra, Ashavan, the master of Asha. We"},{"ref":"17.6c","t":"worship the Geush Urvan, Ashavan, the master of Asha. We worship"},{"ref":"17.6d","t":"the Zarathushrotema, Ashavan, the master of Asha. We worship Zarathushtra,"},{"ref":"17.6e","t":"Ashavan, the master of Asha."},{"ref":"17.7","t":"We worship the Athravan, Ashavan, the master of Asha. We worship"},{"ref":"17.7a","t":"the warrior, Ashavan, the master of Asha. We worship the cattle"},{"ref":"17.7b","t":"farmer, Ashavan, the master of Asha. We worship the cattle farmer,"},{"ref":"17.7c","t":"Ashavan, the master of Asha. We worship the homes with a house-lord,"},{"ref":"17.7d","t":"Ashavan, the master of Asha. We worship the villages with a village-lord,"},{"ref":"17.7e","t":"Ashavan, the master of Asha. We worship the provinces with a province-lord,"},{"ref":"17.7f","t":"Ashavan, the master of Asha. We worship the countries with a country-lord,"},{"ref":"17.7g","t":"Ashavan, the master of Asha."},{"ref":"17.8","t":"We worship the youth of good thought, good words, good deeds,"},{"ref":"17.8a","t":"good Daena, Ashavan, the master of Asha. We worship the youth"},{"ref":"17.8b","t":"(who) makes intercession, Ashavan, the master of Asha. We worship"},{"ref":"17.8c","t":"the Khvaetvadatha, Ashavan, the master of Asha. We worship the"},{"ref":"17.8d","t":"(priest) within the country, Ashavan, the master of Asha. We worship"},{"ref":"17.8e","t":"the blessed (priest who) goes about abroad, Ashavan, the master"},{"ref":"17.8f","t":"of Asha. We worship the homes with a house-lady, Ashavan, the"},{"ref":"17.8g","t":"master of Asha."},{"ref":"17.9","t":"We also worship the Ashavan woman, predominating in good thoughts,"},{"ref":"17.9a","t":"predominating in good words, predominating in good deeds, well"},{"ref":"17.9b","t":"instructed, having power over the masters, Ashavan, (as are)"},{"ref":"17.9c","t":"Spenta Armaiti and your females, O Ahura Mazda."},{"ref":"17.9d","t":"We also worship the Ashavan man, predominating in good thoughts,"},{"ref":"17.9e","t":"predominating in good words, predominating in good deeds, knowing"},{"ref":"17.9f","t":"the creed, not knowing the Kayadha, through whose activity Creation"},{"ref":"17.9g","t":"is advanced in Asha, for worship and adoration of the master Zarathushtrotema,"},{"ref":"17.9h","t":"and we worship the Ashavan Zarathushtrotema, the master of Asha."},{"ref":"17.10","t":"We worship the good, powerful, holy Fravashis, Ashavan, the"},{"ref":"17.10a","t":"material and the spiritual. We also worship the women with their"},{"ref":"17.10b","t":"troops of heroes, and we worship the Yairya Hushitay. And we worship"},{"ref":"17.10c","t":"Ama, well-built, fair of form; and we worship Verethraghna, Ahura-created;"},{"ref":"17.10d","t":"and we worship Triumphing Uparatat."},{"ref":"17.11","t":"We worship you, O Atar, son of Ahura Mazda, Ashavan, the master"},{"ref":"17.11a","t":"of Asha. We worship this Baresman spread with Asha and provided"},{"ref":"17.11b","t":"with Zaothra and girdle, Ashavan, the master of Asha. We worship"},{"ref":"17.11c","t":"Apam Napat. We worship Nairyosangha. We worship the brave Yazata"},{"ref":"17.11d","t":"Damoish Upamana. We worship the souls of the deceased, they, the"},{"ref":"17.11e","t":"Fravashis of the Ashavan."},{"ref":"17.12","t":"We worship the exalted master who is Ahura Mazda, who is highest"},{"ref":"17.12a","t":"in Asha, who is furthest going in Asha. We worship all the teachings"},{"ref":"17.12b","t":"of Zarathushtra. We worship all well done deeds (those already)"},{"ref":"17.12c","t":"done, and those that will be done."},{"ref":"17.12d","t":"We worship all those Beings whom Ahura Mazda knows to be best"},{"ref":"17.12e","t":"for worship according to Asha, male and female."},{"ref":"17.13","t":"Yatha Ahu Vairyo...."},{"ref":"17.13a","t":"I desire worship and adoration and strength and force for the"},{"ref":"17.13b","t":"Ashavan Fravashis, and to the women with their troops of heroes,"},{"ref":"17.13c","t":"and the Yairya Hushitay and to Ama, well-built, fair of form,"},{"ref":"17.13d","t":"Verethraghna, Ahura-created; and to Triumphing Uparatat."},{"ref":"17.13e","t":"Ashem Vohu...."},{"ref":"17.13f","t":"Bestow on him riches... (Recite SrB5.)"},{"sp":"HDR","t":"Ushahin Gah (midnight to dawn)"},{"ref":"18.1","t":"Propitiation to Ahura Mazda."},{"ref":"18.1a","t":"Ashem Vohu...."},{"ref":"18.1b","t":"I profess myself a Mazda-worshipper, a follower of Zarathushtra,"},{"ref":"18.1c","t":"opposing the Daevas, accepting the Ahuric doctrine."},{"ref":"18.1d","t":"To Ushahin that furthers life, Ashavan, the master of Asha, for"},{"ref":"18.1e","t":"worship, adoration, propitiation and praise. To Berejya and Nmanya,"},{"ref":"18.1f","t":"Ashavan, the master(s) of Asha, for worship, adoration, propitiation"},{"ref":"18.1g","t":"and praise."},{"ref":"18.2","t":"With propitiation of Sraosha, companion of Ashi, procuring"},{"ref":"18.2a","t":"rewards, victorious, who furthers the world, (and) the very straight"},{"ref":"18.2b","t":"Razishta and Arshtad, who further the world, who augment the world,"},{"ref":"18.2c","t":"for worship, adoration, propitiation and praise."},{"ref":"18.2d","t":"Yatha Ahu Vairyo, the zaotar should say to me"},{"ref":"18.2e","t":"Atha ratush ashatchit hacha, the knowing Asha-one should say."},{"ref":"18.3","t":"We worship Ahura Mazda, Ashavan, the master of Asha. We worship"},{"ref":"18.3a","t":"Zarathushtra, Ashavan, the master of Asha. We worship the Fravashi"},{"ref":"18.3b","t":"of Ashavan Zarathushtra, We worship the Ashavan Amesha Spentas."},{"ref":"18.4","t":"We worship the good, powerful, holy Fravashis, Ashavan, the"},{"ref":"18.4a","t":"material and the spiritual. We worship the most effective of masters,"},{"ref":"18.4b","t":"the most active of Yazatas, and the most worthy of the masters"},{"ref":"18.4c","t":"of Asha, who is best able to reach his goal of satisfaction, the"},{"ref":"18.4d","t":"Ashavan master of Asha!"},{"ref":"18.5","t":"We worship Ushahin, Ashavan, the master of Asha. We worship"},{"ref":"18.5a","t":"the beautiful Ushah; we worship the radiant Ushah, with swift"},{"ref":"18.5b","t":"horses, the men... the insight of men... the deceased, together"},{"ref":"18.5c","t":"with (?) Nmanya; the swift Ushah, with swift horses, which appear"},{"ref":"18.5d","t":"throughout the seven regions of the earth; we worship that Ushah."},{"ref":"18.5e","t":"We worship Ahura Mazda, Ashavan, the master of Asha. We worship"},{"ref":"18.5f","t":"Vohu Mano; we worship Asha Vahishta; we worship Khshathra Vairya;"},{"ref":"18.5g","t":"we worship the good Spenta Armaiti."},{"ref":"18.6","t":"We worship Berejya, Ashavan, the master of Asha; for the practice"},{"ref":"18.6a","t":"of Asha Vahishta, for the practice of the good Mazdayasnian"},{"ref":"18.6b","t":"religion, for worship and adoration of the master Nmanya; and"},{"ref":"18.6c","t":"we worship Nmanya, Ashavan, the master of Asha."},{"ref":"18.7","t":"We worship Sraosha, companion of Ashi, fair of form, victorious,"},{"ref":"18.7a","t":"world-promoting, the Ashavan, the master of Asha. We worship the"},{"ref":"18.7b","t":"very straight Rashnu; and we worship Arshtad, who further the"},{"ref":"18.7c","t":"world, who augment the world!"},{"ref":"18.8","t":"We worship you, O Atar, son of Ahura Mazda, Ashavan, the master"},{"ref":"18.8a","t":"of Asha. We worship this Baresman spread with Asha and provided"},{"ref":"18.8b","t":"with Zaothra and girdle, Ashavan, the master of Asha. We worship"},{"ref":"18.8c","t":"Apam Napat. We worship Nairyosangha. We worship the brave Yazata"},{"ref":"18.8d","t":"Damoish Upamana. We worship the souls of the deceased, they, the"},{"ref":"18.8e","t":"Fravashis of the Ashavan."},{"ref":"18.9","t":"We worship the exalted master who is Ahura Mazda, who is highest"},{"ref":"18.9a","t":"in Asha, who is furthest going in Asha. We worship all the teachings"},{"ref":"18.9b","t":"of Zarathushtra. We worship all well done deeds (those already)"},{"ref":"18.9c","t":"done, and those that will be done."},{"ref":"18.9d","t":"We worship all those Beings whom Ahura Mazda knows to be best"},{"ref":"18.9e","t":"for worship according to Asha, male and female."},{"ref":"18.10","t":"Yatha Ahu Vairyo...."},{"ref":"18.10a","t":"I desire worship and adoration and strength and force for Sraosha,"},{"ref":"18.10b","t":"companion of Ashi, procuring rewards, victorious, who furthers"},{"ref":"18.10c","t":"the world, (and) the very straight Razishta and Arshtad, who further"},{"ref":"18.10d","t":"the world, who augment the world."},{"ref":"18.10e","t":"Ashem Vohu...."},{"ref":"18.10f","t":"Bestow on him riches... (Recite SrB5.)"},{"sp":"HDR","t":"Khwarshed Niyayesh (Sun Litany)"},{"ref":"20.1","t":"<em>Translation by Dhalla, 1908.<\/em>"},{"ref":"20.0","t":"In the name of God. I praise and invoke the creator Ormazd,"},{"ref":"20.0a","t":"the radiant, glorious, omniscient, maker, lord of lords, king"},{"ref":"20.0b","t":"over all kings, watchful, creator of the universe, giver of daily"},{"ref":"20.0c","t":"bread, powerful, strong, eternal, forgiver, merciful, loving,"},{"ref":"20.0d","t":"mighty, wise, holy, and nourisher. May (his) just kingdom be imperishable."},{"ref":"20.0e","t":"May the majesty and glory of Ormazd, the beneficent lord, increase."},{"ref":"20.0f","t":"(Hither) may come the immortal, radiant, swift-horsed Sun. Of"},{"ref":"20.0g","t":"all sins... I repent."},{"ref":"20.1a","t":"Homage to you, O Ahura Mazda, trice prior to other creatures."},{"ref":"20.1aa","t":"Homage to you, O Amesha Spentas, all of one accord with the Sun."},{"ref":"20.1b","t":"May this (homage) seek its way so as to reach to Ahura Mazda,"},{"ref":"20.1c","t":"this (homage) to the Amesha Spentas, this (homage) to the Fravashis"},{"ref":"20.1d","t":"of the righteous, this to Vayu, that follows its own law for the"},{"ref":"20.1e","t":"Long Period."},{"ref":"20.2","t":"Propitiation to Ahura Mazda.... I praise Asha."},{"ref":"20.3","t":"I praise good thoughts, good words, and good deeds and those"},{"ref":"20.3a","t":"that are to be thought, spoken, and done. I do accept all good"},{"ref":"20.3b","t":"thoughts, good words, and good deeds. I do renounce all evil thoughts,"},{"ref":"20.3c","t":"evil words, and evil deeds."},{"ref":"20.4","t":"I proffer to you, O Amesha Spentas, sacrifice and prayer,"},{"ref":"20.4a","t":"with thought, with word, with deed, with (my) being, with the"},{"ref":"20.4b","t":"very life of my body. I praise Asha."},{"ref":"20.5","t":"Homage to Ahura Mazda. Homage to the Amesha Spentas. Homage"},{"ref":"20.5a","t":"to Mithra of wide cattle pastures. Homage to the Sun, the swift-horsed."},{"ref":"20.5b","t":"Homage to these two eyes that are of Ahura Mazda. Homage to the"},{"ref":"20.5c","t":"Bull. Homage to Gaya (Maretan). Homage to the Fravashi of the"},{"ref":"20.5d","t":"righteous Spitama Zarathushtra. Homage to the whole creation of"},{"ref":"20.5e","t":"the Righteous One, that is, that is coming into being and that"},{"ref":"20.5f","t":"will be."},{"ref":"20.5g","t":"(At the Hawan Gah:)"},{"ref":"20.5h","t":"Further the body through Vohuman, Khshathra, and Asha in accordance"},{"ref":"20.5i","t":"with (my) desire."},{"ref":"20.5j","t":"(At the Rapithwin Gah:)"},{"ref":"20.5k","t":"(To) these lights, the highest (light) of the high."},{"ref":"20.5l","t":"(At the Uzerin Gah:)"},{"ref":"20.5m","t":"At which end you (i.e. Ahura Mazda) will come with your Beneficent"},{"ref":"20.5n","t":"Spirit."},{"ref":"20.6","t":"We sacrifice to the immortal, radiant, swift-horsed Sun. We"},{"ref":"20.6a","t":"sacrifice to Mithra of wide cattle pastures,"},{"ref":"20.6b","t":"Whose word is true, who is of the assembly,"},{"ref":"20.6c","t":"Who has a thousand ears, the well-shaped one,"},{"ref":"20.6d","t":"Who has ten thousand eyes, the exalted one,"},{"ref":"20.6e","t":"Who has wide knowledge, the helpful one,"},{"ref":"20.6f","t":"Who sleeps not, the ever wakeful."},{"ref":"20.7","t":"We sacrifice to Mithra"},{"ref":"20.7a","t":"The lord of all countries,"},{"ref":"20.7b","t":"Whom Ahura Mazda created the most glorious"},{"ref":"20.7c","t":"Of the supernatural yazads."},{"ref":"20.7d","t":"So may there come to us for aid"},{"ref":"20.7e","t":"Both Mithra and Ahura, the two exalted ones."},{"ref":"20.7f","t":"We sacrifice to the immortal,"},{"ref":"20.7g","t":"Radiant, swift-horsed Sun."},{"ref":"20.8","t":"We sacrifice to Tishtrya of sound eyes. We sacrifice to Tishtrya."},{"ref":"20.8a","t":"We sacrifice to those attendants on Tishtrya. We sacrifice to"},{"ref":"20.8b","t":"Tishtrya, the radiant (and) glorious. We sacrifice to the star"},{"ref":"20.8c","t":"Vanant, made by Mazda. We sacrifice to the star Tishtrya, the"},{"ref":"20.8d","t":"radiant (and) glorious. We sacrifice to the Sky that follows its"},{"ref":"20.8e","t":"own law. We sacrifice to the boundless Time. We sacrifice to Time,"},{"ref":"20.8f","t":"that follows its own law for the long period. We sacrifice to"},{"ref":"20.8g","t":"the wind, the holy (and) beneficent. We sacrifice to Wisdom, the"},{"ref":"20.8h","t":"most upright, righteous, made by Mazda. We sacrifice to the good"},{"ref":"20.8i","t":"Mazdayasnian Religion. We sacrifice to the Path leading to the"},{"ref":"20.8j","t":"good state. We sacrifice to the golden shaft. We sacrifice to"},{"ref":"20.8k","t":"Mount Saokanta, made by Mazda."},{"ref":"20.9","t":"We sacrifice to every righteous Yazad of the spiritual world."},{"ref":"20.9a","t":"We sacrifice to every righteous Yazad of the material world. We"},{"ref":"20.9b","t":"sacrifice to our own soul. We sacrifice to our own Fravashi. Come"},{"ref":"20.9c","t":"to my help, O Mazda. We sacrifice to the good, helpful, holy Fravashis"},{"ref":"20.9d","t":"of the righteous. We sacrifice to the immortal, radiant, swift-horsed"},{"ref":"20.9e","t":"Sun."},{"ref":"20.10","t":"I proclaim... of the Ahurian Faith."},{"ref":"20.10a","t":"(Here recite the appropriate Gah dedication)"},{"ref":"20.10b","t":"Propitiation... glorification to the immortal, radiant, swift-horsed"},{"ref":"20.10c","t":"Sun. As (he is) the Lord that is to be chosen... let one who"},{"ref":"20.10d","t":"knows it pronounce it to me."},{"ref":"20.11","t":"We sacrifice to the immortal, radiant, swift-horsed Sun. When"},{"ref":"20.11a","t":"the Sun warms with its light, when the sunlight gives warmth,"},{"ref":"20.11b","t":"there stand the spiritual Yazads, a hundred and a thousand. They"},{"ref":"20.11c","t":"gather together this glory. They distribute this glory. They bestow"},{"ref":"20.11d","t":"this glory upon the earth made by Ahura, with the furtherance"},{"ref":"20.11e","t":"of the world of Asha, with the furtherance of the material existence"},{"ref":"20.11f","t":"of Asha, with the furtherance of the Sun that (is) immortal, radiant,"},{"ref":"20.11g","t":"swift-horsed."},{"ref":"20.12","t":"When the Sun rises up, purification comes to the earth made"},{"ref":"20.12a","t":"by Ahura, purification to the flowing waters, purification to"},{"ref":"20.12b","t":"the waters of the wells, purification to the water of the seas,"},{"ref":"20.12c","t":"purification to the water that is standing. Purification comes"},{"ref":"20.12d","t":"to the righteous creation, which is of the Beneficent Spirit."},{"ref":"20.13","t":"If indeed the Sun were not to rise, then the daevas would"},{"ref":"20.13a","t":"kill all things that are in the seven regions. Not at all would"},{"ref":"20.13b","t":"the spiritual Yazads find support and stability in the material"},{"ref":"20.13c","t":"world."},{"ref":"20.14","t":"Whoever sacrifices to the Sun that is immortal, radiant, (and)"},{"ref":"20.14a","t":"swift-horsed, in order to withstand darkness, to withstand the"},{"ref":"20.14b","t":"daevas, the progeny of darkness, to withstand the thieves and","hvShift6":[[0,0],[52,53],[54,54]]},{"ref":"20.14c","t":"robbers, to withstand the sorcerers and the enchantresses, to"},{"ref":"20.14d","t":"withstand death that creeps on,"},{"ref":"20.14e","t":"He sacrifices to Ahura Mazda, he sacrifices to the Amesha Spentas,"},{"ref":"20.14f","t":"he sacrifices to his own soul."},{"ref":"20.14g","t":"He propitiates all heavenly and earthly Yazads, who sacrifices"},{"ref":"20.14h","t":"to the Sun that is immortal, radiant, swift-horsed."},{"ref":"20.15","t":"I shall sacrifice to Mithra of wide cattle pastures, who has"},{"ref":"20.15a","t":"a thousand ears, ten thousand eyes. I shall sacrifice to his mace,"},{"ref":"20.15b","t":"well aimed against the skulls of the Daevas, Mithra of wide cattle"},{"ref":"20.15c","t":"pastures. And I shall sacrifice to that friendship which is the"},{"ref":"20.15d","t":"best of friendships, that between the Moon and the Sun."},{"ref":"20.16","t":"For his splendor and fortune I shall sacrifice to him with"},{"ref":"20.16a","t":"audible worship, the immortal, radiant, swift-horsed Sun, with"},{"ref":"20.16b","t":"libations. We sacrifice to the immortal, radiant, swift-horsed"},{"ref":"20.16c","t":"Sun, with milk provided with Haoma, with the Barsom, with skill"},{"ref":"20.16d","t":"of tongue, and with the spell, and with word, and with deeds,"},{"ref":"20.16e","t":"and with libations, and with rightly spoken words."},{"ref":"20.16f","t":"Of whomsoever among beings Ahura Mazda has known the excellence"},{"ref":"20.16g","t":"(lit. something better) in Yasna-sacrifice in accordance with"},{"ref":"20.16h","t":"Asha, to both these males and females we sacrifice."},{"ref":"20.16i","t":"(Recite quietly:)...."},{"ref":"20.16j","t":"Y.A.V."},{"ref":"20.16k","t":"I desire worship and adoration and strength and force for the"},{"ref":"20.16l","t":"immortal, radiant, swift-horsed Sun."},{"ref":"20.17","t":"I bless the sacrifice... of the immortal, radiant, swift-horsed"},{"ref":"20.17a","t":"Sun."},{"ref":"20.18","t":"(Whoso sacrifices to) the Ahuranis (Ladies) of Ahura with"},{"ref":"20.18a","t":"most excellent libation, with fairest libations, with libations"},{"ref":"20.18b","t":"filtered by the pious man, (give) to that man radiance... as"},{"ref":"20.18c","t":"I bless."},{"ref":"20.18d","t":"A thousand... ten thousand of the healing remedies."},{"ref":"20.18e","t":"Come to me for help, O Mazda!... of the Time of Long Duration."},{"ref":"20.18f","t":"(Paz.) The reward of merit... as I bless."},{"ref":"20.19","t":"Homage to the creator of the creatures of the world, on the"},{"ref":"20.19a","t":"day (N.) of good name, of holy name, of auspicious name, of the"},{"ref":"20.19b","t":"month (N.) of auspicious name, of the gah (N.)."},{"ref":"20.19c","t":"Propitiation... I praise Asha."},{"ref":"20.19d","t":"May there be an increase in the luster and glory of the immortal,"},{"ref":"20.19e","t":"radiant, swift-horsed Sun, the courageous, victorious in courage"},{"ref":"20.19f","t":"and victory. May the knowledge, promulgation, and glory of the"},{"ref":"20.19g","t":"good Mazdayasnian Law and Religion be in the seven regions of"},{"ref":"20.19h","t":"the earth. So be it. I must go thither (i.e. the next world)."},{"ref":"20.19i","t":"(Homage) to the Creator of the world, to the Mazdayasnian Religion,"},{"ref":"20.19j","t":"the Law of Zartusht. Homage to you, O righteous Ardvisura Anahita,"},{"ref":"20.19k","t":"most profitable, righteous one."},{"ref":"20.19l","t":"Homage to you, good Tree, righteous one, created by Ormazd!"},{"ref":"20.19m","t":"We sacrifice to the immortal, radiant, swift-horsed Sun."},{"ref":"20.19n","t":"(Hither) may reach the immortal, radiant, swift-horsed Sun."},{"sp":"HDR","t":"Mihr Niyayesh (Litany to Mithra)"},{"ref":"21.0","t":"In the name of God. May the majesty and glory of Ormazd, the"},{"ref":"21.0a","t":"beneficent lord, increase. (Hither) may come Mithra of wide cattle pastures,"},{"ref":"21.0b","t":"the true judge. Of all sins... I repent."},{"ref":"21.0c","t":"1-9. Homage to you, O Ahura Mazda... come to my help, O Mazda. We"},{"ref":"21.0d","t":"sacrifice to the good, helpful, holy Fravashis of the righteous."},{"ref":"21.0e","t":"We sacrifice to Mithra of wide cattle pastures."},{"ref":"21.10","t":"I proclaim... of the Ahurian Faith."},{"ref":"21.10a","t":"(Here recite the appropriate Gah dedication)"},{"ref":"21.10b","t":"Propitiation... glorification to Mithra of wide cattle pastures, who has a"},{"ref":"21.10c","t":"thousand ears, who has ten thousand eyes, the Yazad who is invoked by name,"},{"ref":"21.10d","t":"(and) to Rama Khvastra. As (he is) the Lord that is to be chosen... let one"},{"ref":"21.10e","t":"who knows it pronounce it to me."},{"ref":"21.11","t":"We sacrifice to Mithra of wide cattle pastures, whose word is true"},{"ref":"21.11a","t":"... the ever wakeful. We sacrifice to Mithra, who is around the country. We"},{"ref":"21.11b","t":"sacrifice to Mithra, who is within the country. We sacrifice to Mithra, who"},{"ref":"21.11c","t":"is in the country. We sacrifice to Mithra, who is above the country. We"},{"ref":"21.11d","t":"sacrifice to Mithra, who is under the country. We sacrifice to Mithra, who is"},{"ref":"21.11e","t":"before the country. We sacrifice to Mithra, who is behind the country."},{"ref":"21.12","t":"We sacrifice to Mithra and Ahura, the exalted, imperishable,"},{"ref":"21.12a","t":"righteous ones, and the Stars, the Moon, and the Sun, by means of trees"},{"ref":"21.12b","t":"yielding Barsom. We sacrifice to Mitha, the Lord of all countries."},{"ref":"21.13","t":"For his splendor and fortune I shall sacrifice to him with audible"},{"ref":"21.13a","t":"worship, Mithra of wide cattle pastures with libations. We sacrifice to"},{"ref":"21.13b","t":"Mithra of wide cattle pastures, who gives an abode of joy, and a good abode to"},{"ref":"21.13c","t":"the Aryan countries."},{"ref":"21.14","t":"May he come hither to us in order to help"},{"ref":"21.14a","t":"(us). May he come hither to us for spaciousness. May he come hither to"},{"ref":"21.14b","t":"us to support (us). May he come hither to us to (grant us) mercy. May"},{"ref":"21.14c","t":"he come hither to us to cure (us of disease). May he come hither to us"},{"ref":"21.14d","t":"so that we are able to defeat our enemies. May he come hither to us to"},{"ref":"21.14e","t":"(grant us) a good life. May he come hither to us to grant us possession"},{"ref":"21.14f","t":"of Truth. (May) strong, unshakable, undeceivable Mithra of wide pastures,"},{"ref":"21.14g","t":"who is worthy of worship and praise, (come hither) for the sake of the"},{"ref":"21.14h","t":"whole material world."},{"ref":"21.15","t":"This powerful strong god Mithra, strongest in the (world of)"},{"ref":"21.15a","t":"creatures, I will worship with libations. I will cultivate him with praise"},{"ref":"21.15b","t":"and reverence, worship him with audible prayer, with libations, Mithra of wide"},{"ref":"21.15c","t":"cattle pastures."},{"ref":"21.15d","t":"We worship Mithra of wide cattle pastures with Haoma-containing milk and"},{"ref":"21.15e","t":"baresman twigs, with skill of tongue and magic word, with speech and action"},{"ref":"21.15f","t":"and libations, and with correctly uttered words."},{"ref":"21.15g","t":"We worship the male and female Entities in the worship of whom Ahura Mazda"},{"ref":"21.15h","t":"knows (there is (or: consists) what is) best (lit. better) according to Asha."},{"sp":"HDR","t":"Vispa Humata"},{"ref":"22.1","t":"All good thoughts, all good words, all good deeds I do willingly."},{"ref":"22.2","t":"All evil thoughts, all evil words, all evil deeds I do unwillingly."},{"ref":"22.3","t":"All good thoughts, all good words, all good deeds will reach Paradise."},{"ref":"22.4","t":"All evil thoughts, all evil words, all evil deeds will reach Hell."},{"ref":"22.5","t":"And all good thoughts, all good words, all good deeds are the"},{"ref":"22.6","t":"badge of the Ashavans for Paradise. Ashem Vohu...."},{"sp":"HDR","t":"Nam Stayishn"},{"ref":"23.1","t":"(Translation by B. N. Dhabhar, Translation of Zand-i Khurtak"},{"ref":"23.2","t":"Avistak, Bombay, 1963, p ff.)"},{"ref":"23.1a","t":"With propitiation of Ahura Mazda. Ashem Vohu...."},{"ref":"23.1aa","t":"Praise be to the name of Him Who always was, always is and"},{"ref":"23.1b","t":"always will be. (He is), by name, the Yazad Spena Menoi. Even"},{"ref":"23.1c","t":"among the spiritual (yazads). He is Menoi (i.e. an invisible spirit)."},{"ref":"23.1d","t":"One of His own names is also Ohrmazd. (He is) the greatest Lord,"},{"ref":"23.1e","t":"powerful and wise, creator, nourisher, protector, compassionate,"},{"ref":"23.1f","t":"virtuous, forgiver, pure, a good dispenser of justice and all"},{"ref":"23.1g","t":"powerful."},{"ref":"23.2a","t":"Thanks be to that Great Architect who, with His own unrivaled"},{"ref":"23.2aa","t":"strength and wisdom, created the sublime world, the six Amahraspands"},{"ref":"23.2b","t":"of higher rank, many wonderful Yazads, the bright paradise Garothman,"},{"ref":"23.2c","t":"the revolution of the sky, the shining sun, the brilliant moon,"},{"ref":"23.2d","t":"stars of different germs, the wind, atmosphere, water, fire, the"},{"ref":"23.2e","t":"earth, trees, beneficent cattle, the metals and mankind."},{"ref":"23.3","t":"Adoration and praise be to the righteous Lord Who made man"},{"ref":"23.3a","t":"the greatest of all earthly creatures and through (the gift of)"},{"ref":"23.3b","t":"speech and the power of reasoning, created them for the sovereignty"},{"ref":"23.3c","t":"of the times and for the management of the creatures through the"},{"ref":"23.3d","t":"contest in battles against the daevas."},{"ref":"23.4","t":"Homage to the Omniscient One, to him who is compassionate,"},{"ref":"23.4a","t":"who, through Zartosht Spitaman of holy farohar, sent for the creatures"},{"ref":"23.4b","t":"the apostleship (of religion), the knowledge of and the trustworthiness"},{"ref":"23.4c","t":"with regard to, the Religion, innate wisdom and wisdom acquired"},{"ref":"23.4d","t":"through the ears, and the instruction of, and guidance for all"},{"ref":"23.4e","t":"who are, were, and will be, and the science of sciences, viz."},{"ref":"23.4f","t":"the bountiful Manthra, so that the soul at the Chinwad bridge"},{"ref":"23.4g","t":"may be released from hell, and may cause them to pass over the"},{"ref":"23.4h","t":"Best Existence of the holy, the bright sweet-smelling, and all-beneficent."},{"ref":"23.5","t":"In obedience to your command, o compassionate one, I accept"},{"ref":"23.5a","t":"your pure religion, and think, speak, and practice (in accordance"},{"ref":"23.5b","t":"with it). I am steadfast on every meritorious deed and desist"},{"ref":"23.5c","t":"from all sins. I keep pure my own personal conduct and completely"},{"ref":"23.5d","t":"preserve the six powers of life, viz. first, thought, second,"},{"ref":"23.5e","t":"word, third, deed, and again fourth, reasoning, fifth, memory,"},{"ref":"23.5f","t":"and sixth, intellect."},{"ref":"23.6","t":"O righteous one, according to your will, I shall accomplish"},{"ref":"23.6a","t":"to the extent of (my) power, your worship with good thoughts,"},{"ref":"23.6b","t":"good words, and good deeds. I shall open (for myself) the brilliant"},{"ref":"23.6c","t":"way (of paradise) so that the grievous punishment of hell may"},{"ref":"23.6d","t":"not be inflicted on me. I shall pass over the Chinwad bridge and"},{"ref":"23.6e","t":"attain to the abode of paradise (which is) very fragrant, all-embroidered,"},{"ref":"23.6f","t":"and of all happiness."},{"ref":"23.7","t":"Praise be to the merciful Lord who bestows rewards for meritorious"},{"ref":"23.7a","t":"deeds on those who obey his commands according to his will, and"},{"ref":"23.7b","t":"at last will liberate even the wicked from (the torture of) hell"},{"ref":"23.7c","t":"and will embellish with purity the whole creation."},{"ref":"23.8","t":"All praise to the creator Ohrmazd the omniscient, omnipotent,"},{"ref":"23.8a","t":"and powerful, and to the seven Amahraspands, to the victorious"},{"ref":"23.8b","t":"Yazad Warharan, the vanquisher of foes, and to the well-shapen"},{"ref":"23.8c","t":"(Yazad) Ama (strength). (May all these) come (to my help)."},{"ref":"23.8d","t":"[May the glory of the pure and good religion of the Mazdayasnians be triumphant]."},{"ref":"23.9","t":"Homage to these places and cities [these regions and districts],"},{"ref":"23.9a","t":"[know that they are not specially mentioned], pasture lands [i.e."},{"ref":"23.9b","t":"stalls of cattle are so called], houses [i.e. dwellings], drinking"},{"ref":"23.9c","t":"places [i.e. fountains of water], to the waters, lands, and trees,"},{"ref":"23.9d","t":"to this earth and the yonder sky, and even to the holy wind, to"},{"ref":"23.9e","t":"the stars, the moon and the sun, and also to the self-sustained"},{"ref":"23.9f","t":"eternal lights, [know that the self-sustainedness is this that"},{"ref":"23.9g","t":"every one of them acts for itself] and to all creations of Spena"},{"ref":"23.9h","t":"Menoi, males and females, [especially] the lords of holiness."},{"ref":"23.9i","t":"Ashem Vohu...."},{"sp":"HDR","t":"Namaz-i Chahar nemag"},{"ref":"24.1","t":"Of all sins I repent. Ashem Vohu...."},{"ref":"24.2","t":"(Recite once facing East, West, South, and North respectively:)"},{"ref":"24.3","t":"Homage to these places and these lands, and for these"},{"ref":"24.4","t":"pastures, and these abodes vith their hay-racks, and for the waters,"},{"ref":"24.5","t":"land, and plants, and for this earth and for yon heaven, and for"},{"ref":"24.6","t":"the Asha-owning wind, and for the stars, moon, and sun, and for"},{"ref":"24.7","t":"the eternal stars without beginning, and self-disposing, and for"},{"ref":"24.8","t":"all the Asha-owning creatures of Spenta Mainyu, male and female,"},{"ref":"24.9","t":"the regulators of Asha. Ashem Vohu...."},{"ref":"24.10","t":"Bestow on him riches... (Recite SrB5.)"},{"ref":"24.11","t":"Ashem Vohu...."},{"sp":"HDR","t":"Mah Niyayesh (Moon Litany)"},{"ref":"25.0","t":"In the name of God. May the majesty and glory of Ormazd, the"},{"ref":"25.0a","t":"beneficent lord, increase. (Hither) may come the purifier Moon, the Yazad"},{"ref":"25.0b","t":"Moon. Of all sins... I repent."},{"ref":"25.1","t":"Homage to Ahura Mazda. Homage to the Amesha Spentas. Homage to the"},{"ref":"25.1a","t":"Moon that has the seed of the Bull. Homage (to the Moon) when looked at."},{"ref":"25.1b","t":"Homage with the look."},{"ref":"25.2","t":"Propitiation to Ahura Mazda.... I praise Asha. I proclaim... of"},{"ref":"25.2a","t":"Ahurian Faith."},{"ref":"25.2b","t":"(Here recite the appropriate Gah dedication.)"},{"ref":"25.2c","t":"Propitiation... glorification to the Moon that has the seed of"},{"ref":"25.2d","t":"the Bull. To the sole-created Bull. To the Bull of many species."},{"ref":"25.2e","t":"As (he is) the Lord that is to be chosen... let one who knows it"},{"ref":"25.2f","t":"pronounce it to me."},{"ref":"25.3","t":"Homage to Ahura Mazda.... Homage with the look."},{"ref":"25.4","t":"How does the Moon wax? How does the Moon wane? Fifteen (days) does"},{"ref":"25.4a","t":"the Moon wax. Fifteen days does the moon wane. As long as (is) her waxing,"},{"ref":"25.4b","t":"so long the waning. So long (is) the waning, even as the waxing. Who (is it)"},{"ref":"25.4c","t":"through whom the Moon waxes (and) wanes, (other) than you?"},{"ref":"25.5","t":"We sacrifice to the Moon that has the seed of the Bull, the"},{"ref":"25.5a","t":"righteous and master of Asha. Now I look at the Moon. Now I present myself"},{"ref":"25.5b","t":"to the Moon. Now I behold the brilliant Moon. I present myself to the"},{"ref":"25.5c","t":"brilliant Moon. There stand up the Amesha Spentas, they hold the glory."},{"ref":"25.5d","t":"There stand the Amesha Spentas, they bestow the glory on the earth created by"},{"ref":"25.5e","t":"Ahura."},{"ref":"25.6","t":"When the Moon warms with its light, then the golden-colored plants"},{"ref":"25.6a","t":"always grow up together from the earth in the spring. (We sacrifice to) the"},{"ref":"25.6b","t":"new-moon days, the full-moon days, and the intervening seventh day. We"},{"ref":"25.6c","t":"sacrifice to the new-moon, the righteous, master of Asha. We sacrifice to the"},{"ref":"25.6d","t":"full-moon, the righteous, master of Asha. We sacrifice to the intervening"},{"ref":"25.6e","t":"day, the righteous, master of Asha."},{"ref":"25.7","t":"I will sacrifice to the Moon that has the seed of the Bull, the"},{"ref":"25.7a","t":"bestower, radiant, glorious, possessed of water, possessed of warmth,"},{"ref":"25.7b","t":"possessed of knowledge, possessed of wealth, possessed of riches, possessed of"},{"ref":"25.7c","t":"discernment, possessed of weal, possessed of verdure, possessed of good, the"},{"ref":"25.7d","t":"bestower, the healing."},{"ref":"25.8","t":"For his splendor and fortune I shall sacrifice to him with audible"},{"ref":"25.8a","t":"worship, the Moon that has the seed of the Bull, with libations."},{"ref":"25.8b","t":"We sacrifice to the Moon that has the seed of the Bull, the righteous,"},{"ref":"25.8c","t":"master of Asha,"},{"ref":"25.8d","t":"With Haoma-containing milk... and with correctly uttered words."},{"ref":"25.8e","t":"We worship the male and female Entities in the worship of whom Ahura"},{"ref":"25.8f","t":"Mazda knows (there is (or: consists) what is) best (lit. better) according to"},{"ref":"25.8g","t":"Asha."},{"ref":"25.9","t":"Y.A.V.."},{"ref":"25.9a","t":"I desire worship... of the Moon that has the seed of the Bull, of the sole-"},{"ref":"25.9b","t":"created Bull, of cattle of all species. Ashem.... 10.Give strength"},{"ref":"25.9c","t":"and victory. Give a satisfactory supply of cattle. Give a multitude of men,"},{"ref":"25.9d","t":"steadfast, belonging to the assembly, vanquishing, not vanquished, vanquishing"},{"ref":"25.9e","t":"adversaries at one stroke, vanquishing enemies at one stroke, of manifest help"},{"ref":"25.9f","t":"to the blessed."},{"ref":"25.11","t":"O Yazads full of fortune! O Yazads full of healing! Manifest by"},{"ref":"25.11a","t":"your greatness, manifest be those of you who help when invoked. O waters give"},{"ref":"25.11b","t":"indeed just your own manifest fortune to the worshiper."},{"sp":"HDR","t":"Aban Niyayesh (Litany to Water)"},{"ref":"26.0","t":"In the name of God. May the majesty and glory of Ormazd, the"},{"ref":"26.0a","t":"beneficent lord, increase. (Hither) may come Banu Aban Ardvisur."},{"ref":"26.0b","t":"Of all sins... I repent."},{"ref":"26.1","t":"To the good waters, created by Mazda. To the waters of Aredvi"},{"ref":"26.1a","t":"Anahita, the righteous. To all waters created by Mazda. To all"},{"ref":"26.1b","t":"plants created by Mazda. Propitiation... glorification. As (he"},{"ref":"26.1c","t":"is) the Lord that is to be chosen... let one who knows it pronounce"},{"ref":"26.1d","t":"it to me."},{"ref":"26.2","t":"Ahura Mazda spoke to Spitama Zarathushtra: ‘May you sacrifice"},{"ref":"26.2a","t":"for me, O Spitama Zarathushtra, to her who is Aredvi Sura Anahita,"},{"ref":"26.2b","t":"The wide-expanding, the healing,"},{"ref":"26.2c","t":"Foe to the daevas, of Ahura’s Faith,"},{"ref":"26.2d","t":"Worthy of sacrifice in the material world,"},{"ref":"26.2e","t":"Worthy of prayer in the material world,"},{"ref":"26.2f","t":"Life-increasing, the righteous,"},{"ref":"26.2g","t":"Herd-increasing, the righteous,"},{"ref":"26.2h","t":"Fold-increasing, the righteous,"},{"ref":"26.2i","t":"Wealth-increasing, the righteous,"},{"ref":"26.2j","t":"Country-increasing, the righteous.’"},{"ref":"26.3","t":"Who purifies the seed of all males."},{"ref":"26.3a","t":"Who purifies the wombs of"},{"ref":"26.3b","t":"All females for bearing. Who makes all females have easy childbirth."},{"ref":"26.3c","t":"Who bestows on all females"},{"ref":"26.3d","t":"Right (and) timely milk."},{"ref":"26.4","t":"The great, far-famed,"},{"ref":"26.4a","t":"Who is as much in greatness"},{"ref":"26.4b","t":"As all these waters"},{"ref":"26.4c","t":"That run along on this earth."},{"ref":"26.4d","t":"Who, the strong one, flows forth"},{"ref":"26.4e","t":"From the height Hukairya"},{"ref":"26.4f","t":"To the Sea Vourukasha."},{"ref":"26.5","t":"All the shores around the Sea Vourukasha"},{"ref":"26.5a","t":"Are in commotion,"},{"ref":"26.5b","t":"The whole middle is bubbling up"},{"ref":"26.5c","t":"When she flows forth to them,"},{"ref":"26.5d","t":"When she streams forth to them,"},{"ref":"26.5e","t":"Aredvi Sura Anahita."},{"ref":"26.5f","t":"To whom belong a thousand lakes,"},{"ref":"26.5g","t":"To whom a thousand outlets;"},{"ref":"26.5h","t":"Anyone of these lakes"},{"ref":"26.5i","t":"And any of these outlets"},{"ref":"26.5j","t":"(Is) a forty days’ ride"},{"ref":"26.5k","t":"For a man mounted on a good horse."},{"ref":"26.6","t":"And the outflow of this"},{"ref":"26.6a","t":"One water of mine penetrates to all the seven zones. And (the"},{"ref":"26.6b","t":"outflow) of this one water of mine"},{"ref":"26.6c","t":"Flows continuously"},{"ref":"26.6d","t":"Both summer and winter."},{"ref":"26.6e","t":"She purifies my waters, she (purifies) the seed of males, the"},{"ref":"26.6f","t":"wombs of females, the milk of females."},{"ref":"26.7","t":"Whom I, Ahura Mazda by movement of tongue (?) brought forth"},{"ref":"26.7a","t":"for the furtherance of the house, village, town, and country."},{"ref":"26.8","t":"Inasmuch as I shall henceforth recite the Staota Yasna, and"},{"ref":"26.8a","t":"shall recite the Ahuna Vairya, and shall pour forth (?) the Asha"},{"ref":"26.8b","t":"Vahishta, and shall purify the good waters with (lit. together"},{"ref":"26.8c","t":"with) that Gathic word ‘Ahura Mazda attained first in the Abode"},{"ref":"26.8d","t":"of Praise’ - she will therefore give me reward."},{"ref":"26.9","t":"For her splendor and fortune I shall sacrifice to her with"},{"ref":"26.9a","t":"audible worship, I shall sacrifice to her with the well-sacrificed"},{"ref":"26.9b","t":"worship. Through this may you be commanded when invoked! Through"},{"ref":"26.9c","t":"this may you be more than well-sacrificed! (We sacrifice) to Aredvi"},{"ref":"26.9d","t":"Sura Anahita, the righteous, with libations. We sacrifice to Aredvi"},{"ref":"26.9e","t":"Sura Anahita, the righteous, master of Asha,"},{"ref":"26.9f","t":"With Haoma-containing milk... and with correctly uttered words."},{"ref":"26.9g","t":"We worship the male and female Entities in the worship of whom"},{"ref":"26.9h","t":"Ahura Mazda knows (there is (or: consists) what is) best (lit."},{"ref":"26.9i","t":"better) according to Asha."},{"sp":"HDR","t":"Atash Niyayesh (Litany to Fire)"},{"ref":"27.0","t":"With propitiation of Ahura Mazda. Homage to you, O Fire of"},{"ref":"27.0a","t":"Ahura Mazda, O good created, great Yazata."},{"ref":"27.0b","t":"Ashem Vohu.... In the name of God. May the majesty and glory of"},{"ref":"27.0c","t":"Ormazd, the beneficent Lord, increase."},{"ref":"27.0d","t":"(Note: If praying at an Atash Bahram, recite:)"},{"ref":"27.0e","t":"To the Fire Behram, the great Fire."},{"ref":"27.0f","t":"(Note: If praying at an Atash Adaran, recite:)"},{"ref":"27.0g","t":"To the Fire Adaran, the great Fire."},{"ref":"27.0h","t":"(Note: If praying at an Atash Dadgah, recite:)"},{"ref":"27.0i","t":"To the Fire Dadgah, the great Fire."},{"ref":"27.0j","t":"Of all sins... I repent."},{"ref":"27.1","t":"Arise unto me, O Ahura! give vigor through Armaiti, Strength"},{"ref":"27.1a","t":"by the good reward through Thy Holy Spirit, O Mazda! Mighty power"},{"ref":"27.1b","t":"through Asha, supremacy through Vohu Manah."},{"ref":"27.2","t":"For my support, O Far-seeing One, may Ye manifest unto me"},{"ref":"27.2a","t":"those incomparable things"},{"ref":"27.2b","t":"Of your Khshathra, O Ahura, which are the reward of Vohu Manah;"},{"ref":"27.2c","t":"Instruct our consciences, O Holy Armaiti, through Asha."},{"ref":"27.3","t":"So Zarathushtra gives as an offering even the life of his body,"},{"ref":"27.3a","t":"And the excellence of Vohu Manah unto Mazda,"},{"ref":"27.3b","t":"As also obedience and power of deed and word unto Asha."},{"ref":"27.4","t":"Propitiation unto Ahura Mazda. Homage unto thee, O Fire of"},{"ref":"27.4a","t":"Ahura Mazda, thou good-created, great Yazata."},{"ref":"27.4b","t":"Ashem Vohu...."},{"ref":"27.4c","t":"I profess myself a Mazda-worshipper, a follower of Zarathushtra,"},{"ref":"27.4d","t":"opposing the Daevas, accepting the Ahuric doctrine."},{"ref":"27.4e","t":"(Here recite the appropriate Gah dedication.)"},{"ref":"27.4f","t":"Unto Fire, the son of Ahura Mazda. Unto thee, O Fire, son of Ahura"},{"ref":"27.4g","t":"Mazda."},{"ref":"27.5","t":"To Fire, the son of Ahura Mazda; to the good fortune and Prosperity,"},{"ref":"27.5a","t":"created by Mazda; to the Aryan good fortune, created by Mazda;"},{"ref":"27.5b","t":"to the kingly good fortune, created by Mazda; to Fire, the son"},{"ref":"27.5c","t":"of Ahura Mazda; to Kavi Husravah, to the Lake of Husravah; to"},{"ref":"27.5d","t":"Mount Asnavant, created by Mazda; to Lake Chaechista, created"},{"ref":"27.5e","t":"by Mazda; to the kingly good fortune, created by Mazda."},{"ref":"27.6","t":"To Fire, the son of Ahura Mazda; to Mount Raevant, created"},{"ref":"27.6a","t":"by Mazda, to the kingly good fortune, created by Mazda; to Fire,"},{"ref":"27.6b","t":"the son of Ahura Mazda; O Fire! holy warrior, O Yazata full of"},{"ref":"27.6c","t":"fortune, O Yazata full of healing; to Fire, the son of Ahura Mazda,"},{"ref":"27.6d","t":"with all fires; to the Yazata Nairyosangha, offspring of sovereignty"},{"ref":"27.6e","t":"(Khshathra). Propitiation for worship, adoration, propitiation,"},{"ref":"27.6f","t":"and praise."},{"ref":"27.6g","t":"‘Yatha Ahu Vairyo’, the zaotar should say to me"},{"ref":"27.6h","t":"‘Atha ratush ashatchit hacha’, the Asha-owning, knowing one should"},{"ref":"27.6i","t":"say."},{"ref":"27.7","t":"I bless in reverence and adoration the abiding offering, the"},{"ref":"27.7a","t":"joyous offering, and the devotional offering (offered) to you,"},{"ref":"27.7b","t":"O Fire! son of Ahura Mazda."},{"ref":"27.7c","t":"Worthy of sacrifice you are, worthy of prayer,"},{"ref":"27.7d","t":"worthy of sacrifice may you always be, worthy of prayer,"},{"ref":"27.7e","t":"in the dwellings of men."},{"ref":"27.7f","t":"May there be hope to that man who verily shall sacrifice to you"},{"ref":"27.7g","t":"with fuel in his hand, with the Baresma in his hand,"},{"ref":"27.7h","t":"with milk in his hand, with the mortar in his hand."},{"ref":"27.8","t":"May you be provided with proper fuel! May you be provided"},{"ref":"27.8a","t":"with proper incense! May you be provided with proper nourishment!"},{"ref":"27.8b","t":"May you be provided with proper upkeep! May you be maintained"},{"ref":"27.8c","t":"by one of full age! May you be maintained by one wise (in religion),"},{"ref":"27.8d","t":"O Fire, son of Ahura Mazda."},{"ref":"27.9","t":"In order to be burning in this house, in order to be ever"},{"ref":"27.9a","t":"burning in this house, in order to be blazing in this house, in"},{"ref":"27.9b","t":"order to be increasing in this house,"},{"ref":"27.9c","t":"Even throughout the Long Time,"},{"ref":"27.9d","t":"until the mighty Renovation, including the mighty, good Renovation."},{"ref":"27.10","t":"Give me, O Fire, son of Ahura Mazda! well-being immediately,"},{"ref":"27.10a","t":"sustenance immediately; life immediately, well-being in abundance;"},{"ref":"27.10b","t":"sustenance in abundance, life in abundance; knowledge, holiness,"},{"ref":"27.10c","t":"a ready tongue, understanding for (my) soul; and afterwards wisdom"},{"ref":"27.10d","t":"(which is) comprehensive, great, imperishable."},{"ref":"27.11","t":"(Give me) then the manly valor, which is ever afoot, sleepless,"},{"ref":"27.11a","t":"(for one third of the days and nights), watchful while lying in"},{"ref":"27.11b","t":"bed. (Give me) native offspring that give support, ruling over"},{"ref":"27.11c","t":"the region, belonging to the assembly, thoroughly developed, possessed"},{"ref":"27.11d","t":"of good works, delivering from distress, of good intellect, that"},{"ref":"27.11e","t":"may further my house, village, town, country, (and) the renown"},{"ref":"27.11f","t":"of the country."},{"ref":"27.12","t":"Give me, O Fire, son of Ahura Mazda, the Best"},{"ref":"27.12a","t":"World of the righteous, the shining, the all-happy, so that it"},{"ref":"27.12b","t":"may fulfill my wish, now and for ever, so as to attain to good"},{"ref":"27.12c","t":"reward, and to good renown, and to long happiness of my soul!"},{"ref":"27.13","t":"The Fire of Ahura Mazda"},{"ref":"27.13a","t":"Gives command to all"},{"ref":"27.13b","t":"For whom he cooks"},{"ref":"27.13c","t":"The night and the morning meals."},{"ref":"27.13d","t":"From all he solicits"},{"ref":"27.13e","t":"A good offering, and a wished-for offering,"},{"ref":"27.13f","t":"And a devotional offering, O Spitama!"},{"ref":"27.14","t":"The Fire looks at the hands of all passers-by - ‘what does"},{"ref":"27.14a","t":"the friend bring to the friend, the one that goes forth to the"},{"ref":"27.14b","t":"one that sits still?’ We sacrifice unto the holy Fire, the bold,"},{"ref":"27.14c","t":"good warrior."},{"ref":"27.15","t":"Then if that one brings unto him either fuel righly brought,"},{"ref":"27.15a","t":"or Baresma rightly spread, or the plant Hadhanaepata, to him thereupon,"},{"ref":"27.15b","t":"in fulfillment of his wish, the Fire of Ahura Mazda, propitiated,"},{"ref":"27.15c","t":"unoffended, gives a blessing:"},{"ref":"27.16","t":"‘May a herd of cattle attend you,"},{"ref":"27.16a","t":"A multitude of men to you,"},{"ref":"27.16b","t":"And may an active mind"},{"ref":"27.16c","t":"And an active spirit attend you."},{"ref":"27.16d","t":"May you live with a joyous life"},{"ref":"27.16e","t":"The nights which you live!’"},{"ref":"27.16f","t":"This is the Fire’s blessing (on him)"},{"ref":"27.16g","t":"Who brings him fuel,"},{"ref":"27.16h","t":"Dry, exposed to the light,"},{"ref":"27.16i","t":"Purified in accordance with the ritual of Asha."},{"ref":"27.17","t":"(Recite silently:)"},{"ref":"27.17a","t":"Ormazd the Lord! the increaser of mankind, of the species"},{"ref":"27.17b","t":"of mankind, of all species, and of all good ones! May he cause"},{"ref":"27.17c","t":"intelligence, steadfastness, and goodness, unto me (who am) one"},{"ref":"27.17d","t":"of the good Mazdayasnians. So be it!"},{"ref":"27.17e","t":"(Recite aloud:)"},{"ref":"27.17f","t":"Yatha Ahu Vairyo...."},{"ref":"27.17g","t":"I desire worship and adoration and strength and force for Fire,"},{"ref":"27.17h","t":"son of Ahura Mazda. For Fire, son of Ahura Mazda, to the good"},{"ref":"27.17i","t":"fortune and prosperity, created by Mazda, to the Aryan good fortune,"},{"ref":"27.17j","t":"created by Mazda; to the kingly good fortune, created by Mazda;"},{"ref":"27.17k","t":"to Fire, the son of Ahura Mazda; to Kavi Husravah; to the Lake"},{"ref":"27.17l","t":"of Husravah, to Mount Asnavant, created by Mazda; to Lake Chaechista,"},{"ref":"27.17m","t":"created by Mazda; to the kingly good fortune, created by Mazda."},{"ref":"27.17n","t":"To Fire, the son of Ahura Mazda; to Mount Raevant, created by"},{"ref":"27.17o","t":"Mazda; to the kingly good fortune, created by Mazda; to Fire,"},{"ref":"27.17p","t":"the son of Ahura Mazda; O Fire! holy warrior, O Yazata full of"},{"ref":"27.17q","t":"fortune, O Yazata full of healing; to Fire, the son of Ahura Mazda,"},{"ref":"27.17r","t":"with all fires; to the Yazata Nairyosangha, offspring of sovereignty"},{"ref":"27.17s","t":"(Khshathra)."},{"ref":"27.17t","t":"Ashem Vohu...."},{"ref":"27.18","t":"Then through Asha, O Ahura! we wish your mighty and powerful"},{"ref":"27.18a","t":"Fire, which is taught through Asha, to be a manifest help to the"},{"ref":"27.18b","t":"ally, but a visible harm at your beck, O Mazda! to the foe."},{"ref":"27.18c","t":"Ashem Vohu...."},{"ref":"27.19","t":"Bestow on him riches... (SrB5)"},{"ref":"27.20","t":"Homage to the creator of the creatures of the world, on the"},{"ref":"27.20a","t":"day (name the day) of good name, of holy name, of auspicious name,"},{"ref":"27.20b","t":"on the month (name the month) of auspicious name, of the Gah (name"},{"ref":"27.20c","t":"the Gah). With propitiation of Ahura Mazda. Homage to you, O Fire"},{"ref":"27.20d","t":"of Ahura Mazda, O good created, great Yazata."},{"ref":"27.20e","t":"Ashem Vohu...."},{"ref":"27.20f","t":"May there be an increase in the luster and fortune."},{"ref":"27.20g","t":"(Note: If praying at an Atash Bahram, recite:)"},{"ref":"27.20h","t":"To the Fire Behram, the great Fire."},{"ref":"27.20i","t":"(Note: If praying at an Atash Adaran, recite:)"},{"ref":"27.20j","t":"To the Fire Adaran, the great Fire."},{"ref":"27.20k","t":"(Note: If praying at an Atash Dadgah, recite:)"},{"ref":"27.20l","t":"To the Fire Dadgah, the great Fire."},{"ref":"27.20m","t":"May the powerful and victorious fires - Adar Gushasp, Adar Khordad"},{"ref":"27.20n","t":"and Adar Burzin Meher and other Adaran and Atashan which are established"},{"ref":"27.20o","t":"in their proper places (dad-gah) be on the increase. May the greatness"},{"ref":"27.20p","t":"and brightness of Menoi Karko which is powerful and victorious"},{"ref":"27.20q","t":"be on the increase. May these be on the increase - these fires"},{"ref":"27.20r","t":"which possess power and victory. May the knowledge, promulgation,"},{"ref":"27.20s","t":"and glory of the Mazdayasnian law and religion be in the seven"},{"ref":"27.20t","t":"regions of the earth! So be it!"},{"ref":"27.20u","t":"I must go thither."},{"ref":"27.20v","t":"Ashem Vohu...."},{"ref":"27.20w","t":"(Recite facing south:)"},{"ref":"27.20x","t":"To the creator of the world, to the Mazdayasnian religion,"},{"ref":"27.20y","t":"the Law of Zarthusht. Homage to you! O righteous Ardvisura Anahita,"},{"ref":"27.20z","t":"most profitable, O righteous one."},{"ref":"27.20aa","t":"Ashem Vohu...."},{"ref":"27.20ba","t":"Homage to you, O good tree, righteous, created by Mazda."},{"ref":"27.20ca","t":"Ashem Vohu...."},{"ref":"27.20da","t":"With propitiation of Ahura Mazda. Homage to you, O Fire of Ahura"},{"ref":"27.20ea","t":"Mazda, O good created, great Yazata."},{"ref":"27.20fa","t":"Ashem Vohu...."},{"sp":"HDR","t":"1. Ohrmazd Yasht (Hymn to Ahura Mazda)"},{"ref":"29.0","t":"May Ahura Mazda be rejoiced! May Angra Mainyu be destroyed"},{"ref":"29.0a","t":"by those who do truly what is the foremost wish (of God)."},{"ref":"29.0b","t":"I praise well-thought, well-spoken, and well-done thoughts, words,"},{"ref":"29.0c","t":"and deeds. I embrace all good thoughts, good words, and good deeds;"},{"ref":"29.0d","t":"I reject all evil thoughts, evil words, and evil deeds."},{"ref":"29.0e","t":"I give sacrifice and prayer unto you, O Amesha-Spentas! even with"},{"ref":"29.0f","t":"the fullness of my thoughts, of my words, of my deeds, and of"},{"ref":"29.0g","t":"my heart: I give unto you even my own life."},{"ref":"29.0h","t":"I recite the ‘Praise of Holiness:’"},{"ref":"29.0i","t":"‘Ashem Vohu: Holiness is the best of all good. Well is it for"},{"ref":"29.0j","t":"it, well is it for that holiness which is perfection of holiness!’"},{"ref":"29.0k","t":"I confess myself a worshipper of Mazda, a follower of Zarathushtra,"},{"ref":"29.0l","t":"one who hates the Daevas and obeys the laws of Ahura;"},{"ref":"29.0m","t":"For sacrifice, prayer, propitiation, and glorification unto [Havani],"},{"ref":"29.0n","t":"the holy and master of holiness;"},{"ref":"29.0o","t":"For sacrifice, prayer, propitiation, and glorification unto [Savanghi"},{"ref":"29.0p","t":"and Visya], the holy and masters of holiness;"},{"ref":"29.0q","t":"For sacrifice, prayer, propitiation, and glorification unto the"},{"ref":"29.0r","t":"Masters of the days, of the periods of the day, of the months,"},{"ref":"29.0s","t":"of the seasons, and of the years;"},{"ref":"29.0t","t":"Unto AHURA MAZDA, bright and glorious, be propitiation, with sacrifice,"},{"ref":"29.0u","t":"prayer, propitiation, and glorification."},{"ref":"29.0v","t":"Yatha ahu vairyo: The will of the Lord is the law of holiness:"},{"ref":"29.0w","t":"the riches of Vohu-Mano shall he given to him who works in this"},{"ref":"29.0x","t":"world for Mazda, and wields according to the will of Ahura the"},{"ref":"29.0y","t":"power he gave him to relieve the poor."},{"ref":"29.1","t":"Zarathushtra asked Ahura Mazda: ‘O Ahura Mazda, most beneficent"},{"ref":"29.1a","t":"Spirit, Maker of the material world, thou Holy One!"},{"ref":"29.1b","t":"‘What of the Holy Word is the strongest? What is the most victorious?"},{"ref":"29.1c","t":"What is the most glorious? What is the most effective?"},{"ref":"29.2","t":"‘What is the most fiend-smiting? What is the best-healing?"},{"ref":"29.2a","t":"What destroyeth best the malice of Daevas and Men? What maketh"},{"ref":"29.2b","t":"the material world best come to the fulfillment of its wishes?"},{"ref":"29.2c","t":"What freeth the material world best from the anxieties of the"},{"ref":"29.2d","t":"heart?’"},{"ref":"29.3","t":"Ahura Mazda answered: ‘Our Name, O Spitama Zarathushtra! who"},{"ref":"29.3a","t":"are the Amesha-Spentas, that is the strongest part of the Holy"},{"ref":"29.3b","t":"Word; that is the most victorious; that is the most glorious;"},{"ref":"29.3c","t":"that is the most effective;"},{"ref":"29.4","t":"‘That is the most fiend-smiting; that is the best-healing;"},{"ref":"29.4a","t":"that destroyeth best the malice of Daevas and Men: that maketh"},{"ref":"29.4b","t":"the material world best come to the fulfillment of its wishes;"},{"ref":"29.4c","t":"that freeth the material World best from the anxieties of the"},{"ref":"29.4d","t":"heart.’"},{"ref":"29.5","t":"Then Zarathushtra said: ‘Reveal unto me that name of thine,"},{"ref":"29.5a","t":"O Ahura Mazda! that is the greatest, the best, the fairest, the"},{"ref":"29.5b","t":"most effective, the most fiend-smiting, the best-healing, that"},{"ref":"29.5c","t":"destroyeth best the malice of Daevas and Men;"},{"ref":"29.6","t":"‘That I may afflict all Daevas and Men; that I may afflict"},{"ref":"29.6a","t":"all Yatus and Pairikas; that neither Daevas nor Men may be able"},{"ref":"29.6b","t":"to afflict me; neither Yatus nor Pairikas.’"},{"ref":"29.7","t":"Ahura Mazda replied unto him: ‘My name is the One of whom"},{"ref":"29.7a","t":"questions are asked, O holy Zarathushtra!"},{"ref":"29.7b","t":"‘My second name is the Herd-giver"},{"ref":"29.7c","t":"‘My third name is the Strong One"},{"ref":"29.7d","t":"‘My fourth name is Perfect Holiness."},{"ref":"29.7e","t":"‘My fifth name is All good things created by Mazda, the offspring"},{"ref":"29.7f","t":"of the holy principle."},{"ref":"29.7g","t":"‘My sixth name is Understanding;"},{"ref":"29.7h","t":"‘My seventh name is the One with understanding."},{"ref":"29.7i","t":"‘My eighth name is Knowledge;"},{"ref":"29.7j","t":"‘My ninth name is the One with Knowledge."},{"ref":"29.8","t":"‘My tenth name is Weal;"},{"ref":"29.8a","t":"‘My eleventh name is He who produces weal."},{"ref":"29.8b","t":"‘My twelfth name is AHURA (the Lord)."},{"ref":"29.8c","t":"‘My thirteenth name is the most Beneficent."},{"ref":"29.8d","t":"‘My fourteenth name is He in whom there is no harm."},{"ref":"29.8e","t":"‘My fifteenth name is the unconquerable One."},{"ref":"29.8f","t":"‘My sixteenth name is He who makes the true account."},{"ref":"29.8g","t":"‘My seventeenth name is the All-seeing One."},{"ref":"29.8h","t":"‘My eighteenth name is the healing One."},{"ref":"29.8i","t":"‘My nineteenth name is the Creator."},{"ref":"29.8j","t":"‘My twentieth name is MAZDA (the All-knowing One)."},{"ref":"29.9","t":"Worship me, O Zarathushtra, by day and by night, with offerings"},{"ref":"29.9a","t":"of libations well accepted I will come unto thee for help and"},{"ref":"29.9b","t":"joy, I, Ahura Mazda; the good, holy Sraosha will come unto thee"},{"ref":"29.9c","t":"for help and joy; the waters, the plants, and the Fravashis of"},{"ref":"29.9d","t":"the holy ones will come unto thee for help and joy."},{"ref":"29.10","t":"‘If thou wantest, O Zarathushtra, to destroy the malice of"},{"ref":"29.10a","t":"Daevas and Men, of the Yatus and Pairikas, of the oppressors,"},{"ref":"29.10b","t":"of the blind and of the deaf, of the two-legged ruffians, of the"},{"ref":"29.10c","t":"two-legged Ashemaoghas, of the four-legged wolves;"},{"ref":"29.11","t":"‘And of the hordes with the wide front, with the many spears,"},{"ref":"29.11a","t":"with the straight spears, with the spears uplifted, bearing the"},{"ref":"29.11b","t":"spear of havock; then, recite thou these my names every day and"},{"ref":"29.11c","t":"every night."},{"ref":"29.12","t":"‘I am the Keeper; I am the Creator and the Maintainer; I am"},{"ref":"29.12a","t":"the Discerner; I am the most beneficent Spirit."},{"ref":"29.12b","t":"‘My name is the bestower of health; my name is the best bestower"},{"ref":"29.12c","t":"of health."},{"ref":"29.12d","t":"‘My name is the Athravan; my name is the most Athravan-like of"},{"ref":"29.12e","t":"all Athravans."},{"ref":"29.12f","t":"‘My name is Ahura (the Lord)"},{"ref":"29.12g","t":"‘My name is Mazdau (the all-knowing)."},{"ref":"29.12h","t":"‘My name is the Holy; my name is the most Holy."},{"ref":"29.12i","t":"‘My name is the Glorious; my name is the most Glorious."},{"ref":"29.12j","t":"‘My name is the Full-seeing; my name is the Fullest-seeing."},{"ref":"29.12k","t":"‘My name is the Far-seeing; my name is the Farthest-seeing."},{"ref":"29.13","t":"‘My name is the Protector; my name is the Well-wisher; my"},{"ref":"29.13a","t":"name is the Creator; my name is the Keeper; my name is the Maintainer."},{"ref":"29.13b","t":"‘My name is the Discerner; my name is the Best Discerner."},{"ref":"29.13c","t":"‘My name is the Prosperity-producer; my name is the Word of Prosperity."},{"ref":"29.13d","t":"‘My name is the King who rules at his will; my name is the King"},{"ref":"29.13e","t":"who rules most at his will."},{"ref":"29.13f","t":"‘My name is the liberal King; my name is the most liberal King."},{"ref":"29.14","t":"‘My name is He who does not deceive; my name is He who is"},{"ref":"29.14a","t":"not deceived."},{"ref":"29.14b","t":"‘My name is the good Keeper; my name is He who destroys malice;"},{"ref":"29.14c","t":"my name is He Who conquers at once; my name is He who conquers"},{"ref":"29.14d","t":"everything; my name is He who has shaped everything."},{"ref":"29.14e","t":"‘My name is All weal; my name is full weal; my name is the Master"},{"ref":"29.14f","t":"of weal."},{"ref":"29.15","t":"‘My name is He who can benefit at his wish; my name is He"},{"ref":"29.15a","t":"who can best benefit at his wish."},{"ref":"29.15b","t":"‘My name is the Beneficent One; my name is the Energetic One;"},{"ref":"29.15c","t":"my name is the most Beneficent."},{"ref":"29.15d","t":"‘My name is Holiness; my name is the Great One; my name is the"},{"ref":"29.15e","t":"good Sovereign; my name is the Best of Sovereigns."},{"ref":"29.15f","t":"‘My name is the Wise One; my name is the Wisest of the Wise; my"},{"ref":"29.15g","t":"name is He who does good for a long time."},{"ref":"29.16","t":"‘These are my names."},{"ref":"29.16a","t":"‘And he who in this material world, O Spitama Zarathushtra! shall"},{"ref":"29.16b","t":"recite and pronounce those names of mine either by day or by night;"},{"ref":"29.17","t":"‘He who shall pronounce them, when he rises up or when he"},{"ref":"29.17a","t":"lays him down; when he lays him down or when he rises up; when"},{"ref":"29.17b","t":"he binds on the sacred girdle or when he unbinds the sacred girdle;"},{"ref":"29.17c","t":"when he goes out of his dwelling-place, or when he goes out of"},{"ref":"29.17d","t":"his town, or when he goes out of his country and comes into another"},{"ref":"29.17e","t":"country:"},{"ref":"29.18","t":"‘That man, neither in that day nor in that night, shall be"},{"ref":"29.18a","t":"wounded by the weapons of the foe who rushes Aeshma-like and is"},{"ref":"29.18b","t":"Druj-minded; not the knife, not the cross-bow, not the arrow,"},{"ref":"29.18c","t":"not the sword, not the club, not the sling-stone shall reach and"},{"ref":"29.18d","t":"wound him."},{"ref":"29.19","t":"‘But those names shall come in to keep him from behind and"},{"ref":"29.19a","t":"to keep him in front, from the Druj unseen, from the female Varenya"},{"ref":"29.19b","t":"fiend, from the evil-doer bent on mischief, and from that fiend"},{"ref":"29.19c","t":"who is all death, Angra Mainyu. It will be as if there were a"},{"ref":"29.19d","t":"thousand men watching over one man."},{"ref":"29.20","t":"‘“Who is he who will smite the fiend in order to maintain"},{"ref":"29.20a","t":"thy ordinances? Teach me clearly thy rules for this world and"},{"ref":"29.20b","t":"for the next, that Sraosha may come with Vohu-Mano and help whomsoever"},{"ref":"29.20c","t":"thou pleasest.”"},{"ref":"29.21","t":"‘Hail to the Glory of the Kavis! Hail to the Airyanem Vaejah!"},{"ref":"29.21a","t":"Hail to the Saoka, made by Mazda! Hail to the waters of the Daitya!"},{"ref":"29.21b","t":"Hail to Ardvi, the undefiled well! Hail to the whole world of"},{"ref":"29.21c","t":"the holy Spirit!"},{"ref":"29.21d","t":"‘Yatha ahu vairyo: The will of the Lord..."},{"ref":"29.21e","t":"‘Ashem Vohu: Holiness is the best of all good...."},{"ref":"29.22","t":"‘We worship the Ahuna Vairya. We worship Asha-Vahishta, most"},{"ref":"29.22a","t":"fair, undying, and beneficent. We worship Strength and Prosperity"},{"ref":"29.22b","t":"and Might and Victory and Glory and Vigour. We worship Ahura Mazda,"},{"ref":"29.22c","t":"bright and glorious."},{"ref":"29.22d","t":"‘Yenghe hatam: All those beings of whom Ahura Mazda knows the"},{"ref":"29.22e","t":"goodness for a sacrifice [performed] in holiness, all those beings,"},{"ref":"29.22f","t":"males and females, do we worship."},{"ref":"29.23","t":"‘Yatha ahu vairyo: The will of the Lord is the law of holiness...."},{"ref":"29.23a","t":"I bless the sacrifice and the prayer unto Ahura Mazda, bright"},{"ref":"29.23b","t":"and glorious, and his strength and vigour.’"},{"ref":"29.23c","t":"(Bahman Yasht.)"},{"ref":"29.24","t":"‘O Zarathushtra! keep thou for ever that man who is friendly"},{"ref":"29.24a","t":"[to me] from the foe unfriendly [to me]! Do not give up that friend"},{"ref":"29.24b","t":"unto the stroke (of the foe), unto vexations to be borne; wish"},{"ref":"29.24c","t":"no harm unto that man who would offer me a sacrifice, be it ever"},{"ref":"29.24d","t":"so great or ever so small, if it has reached unto us, the Amesha-Spentas."},{"ref":"29.25","t":"‘Here is Vohu-Mano, my creature, O Zarathushtra! here is Asha-Vahishta,"},{"ref":"29.25a","t":"my creature, O Zarathushtra! here is Khshathra-Vairya, my creature,"},{"ref":"29.25b","t":"O Zarathushtra! here is Spenta-Armaiti, my creature, O Zarathushtra!"},{"ref":"29.25c","t":"here are Haurvatat and Ameretat, who are the reward of the holy"},{"ref":"29.25d","t":"ones, when freed from their bodies, my creatures, O Zarathushtra!"},{"ref":"29.26","t":"‘Thou knowest this, and how it is, O holy Zarathushtra! from"},{"ref":"29.26a","t":"my understanding and from my knowledge; namely, how the world"},{"ref":"29.26b","t":"first began, and how it will end."},{"ref":"29.26c","t":"‘A thousand remedies, ten thousand remedies!"},{"ref":"29.26d","t":"‘A thousand remedies, ten thousand remedies!"},{"ref":"29.26e","t":"‘A thousand remedies, ten thousand remedies!"},{"ref":"29.27","t":"‘[We worship] the well-shapen, tall-formed Strength; Verethraghna,"},{"ref":"29.27a","t":"made by Ahura; the crushing Ascendant, and Spenta-Armaiti."},{"ref":"29.28","t":"‘And with the help of Spenta-Armaiti, break ye asunder their"},{"ref":"29.28a","t":"malice, turn their minds astray, bind their hands, make their"},{"ref":"29.28b","t":"knees quake against one another, bind their tongues."},{"ref":"29.28c","t":"‘When, O Mazda! shall the faithful smite the wicked? When shall"},{"ref":"29.28d","t":"the faithful smite the Druj? When shall the faithful smite the"},{"ref":"29.28e","t":"wicked?’"},{"ref":"29.29","t":"Then Zarathushtra said: ‘I threw you back into the earth,"},{"ref":"29.29a","t":"and by the eyes of Spenta-Armaiti the ruffian was made powerless."},{"ref":"29.30","t":"‘We worship the powerful Gaokerena, made by Mazda; the powerful"},{"ref":"29.30a","t":"Gaokerena, made by Mazda."},{"ref":"29.31","t":"‘We worship the memory of Ahura Mazda to keep the Holy Word."},{"ref":"29.31a","t":"We worship the understanding of Ahura Mazda, to study the Holy"},{"ref":"29.31b","t":"Word."},{"ref":"29.31c","t":"‘We worship the tongue of Ahura Mazda, to speak forth the Holy"},{"ref":"29.31d","t":"Word."},{"ref":"29.31e","t":"‘We worship the mountain that gives understanding, that preserves"},{"ref":"29.31f","t":"understanding; [we worship it] by day and by night, with offerings"},{"ref":"29.31g","t":"of libations well-accepted."},{"ref":"29.32","t":"‘We worship that creation [of Ahura’s], Spenta-Armaiti; and"},{"ref":"29.32a","t":"the holy creations of that creature and of Asha [Vahishta], that"},{"ref":"29.32b","t":"are foremost in holiness."},{"ref":"29.32c","t":"‘Here I take as lord and master the greatest of all, Ahura Mazda;"},{"ref":"29.32d","t":"to smite the fiend Angra Mainyu; to smite Aeshma of the wounding"},{"ref":"29.32e","t":"spear; to smite the Mazainya fiends; to smite all the Daevas and"},{"ref":"29.32f","t":"the Varenya fiends; to increase Ahura Mazda, bright and glorious;"},{"ref":"29.32g","t":"to increase the Amesha-Spentas; to increase the star Tishtrya,"},{"ref":"29.32h","t":"the bright and glorious; to increase the faithful men; to increase"},{"ref":"29.32i","t":"all the holy creatures of the beneficent Spirit."},{"ref":"29.32j","t":"‘Ashem Vohu: Holiness is the best of all good...."},{"ref":"29.33","t":"Bestow on him riches... (Recite SrB5.)"},{"ref":"29.33a","t":"‘Ashem Vohu: Holiness is the best of all good....’"},{"sp":"HDR","t":"2. Haft Amahraspand Yasht"},{"ref":"30.0","t":"May Ahura Mazda be rejoiced!..."},{"ref":"30.0a","t":"Ashem Vohu: Holiness is the best of all good...."},{"ref":"30.0b","t":"I confess myself a worshipper of Mazda, a follower of"},{"ref":"30.0c","t":"Zarathushtra, one who hates the Daevas and obeys the laws of"},{"ref":"30.0d","t":"Ahura;"},{"ref":"30.0e","t":"For sacrifice, prayer, propitiation, and glorification unto"},{"ref":"30.0f","t":"[Havani], the holy and master of holiness...."},{"ref":"30.1","t":"<span class=\"hv-secn\">I.<\/span> To Ahura Mazda, bright and glorious, and to the"},{"ref":"30.1a","t":"Amesha-Spentas;"},{"ref":"30.1b","t":"To Vohu-Mano; to Peace, whose breath is friendly, and who is"},{"ref":"30.1c","t":"more powerful to destroy than all other creatures; to the"},{"ref":"30.1d","t":"heavenly Wisdom, made by Mazda, and to the Wisdom acquired"},{"ref":"30.1e","t":"through the ear, made by Mazda;"},{"ref":"30.2","t":"To Asha-Vahishta, the fairest; to the much-desired Airyaman;"},{"ref":"30.2a","t":"to the instrument made by Mazda: and to the good Saoka, with eyes"},{"ref":"30.2b","t":"of love, made by Mazda and holy;"},{"ref":"30.2c","t":"To Khshathra-Vairya; to the metals; to Mercy and Charity."},{"ref":"30.3","t":"To the good Spenta-Armaiti, and to the good Rata, with eyes"},{"ref":"30.3a","t":"of love, made by Mazda and holy;"},{"ref":"30.3b","t":"To Haurvatat, the master; to the prosperity of the seasons"},{"ref":"30.3c","t":"and to the years, the masters of holiness;"},{"ref":"30.3d","t":"And to Ameretat, the master; to fatness and flocks; to the"},{"ref":"30.3e","t":"plenty of corn; and to the powerful Gaokerena, made by Mazda."},{"ref":"30.4","t":"(At the Gah Hawan): To Mithra, the lord of wide pastures and"},{"ref":"30.4a","t":"to Rama Hvastra."},{"ref":"30.4b","t":"(At the Gah Rapithwin): To Asha-Vahishta and to Atar, the"},{"ref":"30.4c","t":"son of Ahura Mazda."},{"ref":"30.4d","t":"(At the Gah, Uzerin): To Apam Napat, the tall lord, and to"},{"ref":"30.4e","t":"water, made by Mazda."},{"ref":"30.5","t":"(At the Gah Aiwisruthrem): To the Fravashis of the faithful"},{"ref":"30.5a","t":"and to the females that bring forth flocks of males; to the"},{"ref":"30.5b","t":"prosperity of the seasons; to the well-shapen and tall-formed"},{"ref":"30.5c","t":"Strength; to Verethraghna, made by Ahura, and to the crushing"},{"ref":"30.5d","t":"Ascendant."},{"ref":"30.5e","t":"(At the Gah Usahin): To the holy, devout, fiend-smiting"},{"ref":"30.5f","t":"Sraosha, who makes the world grow; to Rashnu-Razishta and to"},{"ref":"30.5g","t":"Arshtat, who makes the world grow, who makes the world increase;"},{"ref":"30.5h","t":"Be propitiation, with sacrifice, prayer, propitiation and"},{"ref":"30.5i","t":"glorification!"},{"ref":"30.5j","t":"Yatha ahu vairyo: The will of the Lord is the law of"},{"ref":"30.5k","t":"holiness...."},{"ref":"30.6","t":"<span class=\"hv-secn\">II.<\/span> We sacrifice unto Ahura Mazda, bright and glorious; we"},{"ref":"30.6a","t":"sacrifice unto the Amesha-Spentas, the all-ruling, the"},{"ref":"30.6b","t":"all-beneficent."},{"ref":"30.6c","t":"We sacrifice unto Vohu-Mano, the Amesha-Spenta; we sacrifice"},{"ref":"30.6d","t":"unto Peace, whose breath is friendly, and who is more powerful to"},{"ref":"30.6e","t":"destroy than all other creatures; we sacrifice unto the heavenly"},{"ref":"30.6f","t":"Wisdom, made by Mazda; we sacrifice unto the Wisdom acquired"},{"ref":"30.6g","t":"through the ear, made by Mazda."},{"ref":"30.7","t":"We sacrifice unto Asha-Vahishta, the fairest, the"},{"ref":"30.7a","t":"Amesha-Spenta; we sacrifice unto the much-desired Airyaman; we"},{"ref":"30.7b","t":"sacrifice unto the instrument made by Mazda; we sacrifice unto"},{"ref":"30.7c","t":"the good Saoka, with eyes of love, made by Mazda and holy."},{"ref":"30.7d","t":"We sacrifice unto Khshathra-Vairya; we sacrifice unto the"},{"ref":"30.7e","t":"metals; we sacrifice unto Mercy and Charity."},{"ref":"30.8","t":"We sacrifice unto the good Spenta-Armaiti; we sacrifice unto"},{"ref":"30.8a","t":"the good Rata, with eyes of love, made by Mazda and holy."},{"ref":"30.8b","t":"We sacrifice unto Haurvatat, the Amesha-Spenta; we sacrifice"},{"ref":"30.8c","t":"unto the prosperity of the seasons; we sacrifice unto the years,"},{"ref":"30.8d","t":"the holy and masters of holiness."},{"ref":"30.8e","t":"We sacrifice unto Ameretat, the Amesha-Spenta; we sacrifice"},{"ref":"30.8f","t":"unto fatness and flocks; we sacrifice unto the plenty of corn; we"},{"ref":"30.8g","t":"sacrifice unto the powerful Gaokerena, made by Mazda."},{"ref":"30.9","t":"(At the Gah Hawan): We sacrifice unto Mithra, the lord of"},{"ref":"30.9a","t":"wide pastures; we sacrifice unto Rama Hvastra."},{"ref":"30.9b","t":"(At the Gah Rapithwin): We sacrifice unto Asha-Vahishta and"},{"ref":"30.9c","t":"Atar, the son of Ahura Mazda."},{"ref":"30.9d","t":"(At the Gah Uzerin): We sacrifice unto Apam Napat, the"},{"ref":"30.9e","t":"swift-horsed, the tall and shining lord, the lord of the females;"},{"ref":"30.9f","t":"we sacrifice unto the holy waters, made by Mazda."},{"ref":"30.10","t":"(At the Gah Aiwisruthrem): We sacrifice unto the good,"},{"ref":"30.10a","t":"powerful, beneficent Fravashis of the faithful; we sacrifice unto"},{"ref":"30.10b","t":"the females who bring forth flocks of males; we sacrifice unto"},{"ref":"30.10c","t":"the prosperity of the seasons; we sacrifice unto the well-shapen,"},{"ref":"30.10d","t":"tall-formed Strength; we sacrifice unto Verethraghna, made by"},{"ref":"30.10e","t":"Mazda; we sacrifice unto the crushing Ascendant."},{"ref":"30.10f","t":"(At the Gah Ushahin): We sacrifice unto the holy,"},{"ref":"30.10g","t":"tall-formed, fiend-smiting Sraosha; who makes the world grow, the"},{"ref":"30.10h","t":"holy an master of holiness; we sacrifice unto Rashnu-Razishta; we"},{"ref":"30.10i","t":"sacrifice unto Arshtat, who makes the world grow, who makes the"},{"ref":"30.10j","t":"world increase"},{"ref":"30.11","t":"<span class=\"hv-secn\">III.<\/span> Let the Yatus be crushed, O Zarathushtra! both Daevas and"},{"ref":"30.11a","t":"men."},{"ref":"30.11b","t":"Who is he in whose house, O Spitama Zarathushtra! every Druj"},{"ref":"30.11c","t":"is destroyed, every Druj perishes, when he pronounces these"},{"ref":"30.11d","t":"words:"},{"ref":"30.12","t":"........?"},{"ref":"30.13","t":"It is he who takes the seven Amesha-Spentas, the all-ruling,"},{"ref":"30.13a","t":"the all-beneficent, as a shield against his enemies."},{"ref":"30.13b","t":"We worship the Law of the worshippers of Mazda; we worship"},{"ref":"30.13c","t":"the waters coming in the shape of a horse, made by Mazda."},{"ref":"30.13d","t":"14-15."},{"ref":"30.13e","t":"He has renounced trespasses and faults, O Zarathustra! he"},{"ref":"30.13f","t":"has renounced all trespasses and faults, O Zarathustra! when he"},{"ref":"30.13g","t":"throws down the destroyer of Vohu-Mano and his words, with a"},{"ref":"30.13h","t":"hundred times hundredfold, with a many times manifold preaching"},{"ref":"30.13i","t":"and smiting, and he takes away the Law of Mazda, that was carried"},{"ref":"30.13j","t":"away as a prisoner, from the hands of the [ungodly], who are"},{"ref":"30.13k","t":"destroyed by his strength."},{"ref":"30.13l","t":"Ashem Vohu: Holiness is the best of all good...."},{"ref":"30.16","t":"Yatha ahu vairyo: The will of the Lord is the law of"},{"ref":"30.16a","t":"holiness...."},{"ref":"30.16b","t":"I bless the sacrifice and the prayer, the strength and"},{"ref":"30.16c","t":"vigour"},{"ref":"30.16d","t":"Of Ahura Mazda, bright and glorious, and of the"},{"ref":"30.16e","t":"Amesha-Spentas;"},{"ref":"30.16f","t":"Of Vohu-Mano; of Peace, whose breath is friendly...."},{"ref":"30.16g","t":"Of Asha-Vahishta, the fairest; of the much-desired"},{"ref":"30.16h","t":"Airyaman...."},{"ref":"30.16i","t":"Of Khshathra-Vairya, of the metals...."},{"ref":"30.16j","t":"Of the good Spenta-Armaiti and of the good Rata...."},{"ref":"30.16k","t":"Of Haurvatat, the master...."},{"ref":"30.16l","t":"Of Ameretat, the master...."},{"ref":"30.16m","t":"(At the Gah Hawan): Of Mithra...."},{"ref":"30.16n","t":"(At the Gah Rapithwin): Of Asha-Vahishta...."},{"ref":"30.16o","t":"(At the Gah Uzerin): Of the high lord Apam Napat...."},{"ref":"30.16p","t":"(At the Gah Aiwisruthrem): Of the Fravashis of the"},{"ref":"30.16q","t":"faithful...."},{"ref":"30.16r","t":"(At the Gah Ushahin): Of the holy, devout, fiend-smiting"},{"ref":"30.16s","t":"Sraosha, who makes the world grow; of Rashnu-Razishta and of"},{"ref":"30.16t","t":"Arshtat, who makes the world grow, who makes the world increase."},{"ref":"30.16u","t":"Ashem Vohu: Holiness is the best of all good...."},{"ref":"30.16v","t":"Give unto that man brightness and glory, give him health of"},{"ref":"30.16w","t":"body, give him sturdiness of body, give him victorious strength"},{"ref":"30.16x","t":"of body, give him full welfare of wealth, give him a virtuous"},{"ref":"30.16y","t":"offspring,"},{"ref":"30.16z","t":"give him long, long life, give him the bright, all-happy,"},{"ref":"30.16aa","t":"blissful abode of the holy Ones."},{"sp":"HDR","t":"3. Ardwahisht Yasht"},{"ref":"31.0","t":"May Ahura Mazda be rejoiced!...."},{"ref":"31.0a","t":"Ashem Vohu: Holiness is the best of all good...."},{"ref":"31.0b","t":"I confess myself a worshipper of Mazda, a follower of"},{"ref":"31.0c","t":"Zarathushtra, one who hates the Daevas and obeys the laws of"},{"ref":"31.0d","t":"Ahura;"},{"ref":"31.0e","t":"For sacrifice, prayer, propitiation, and glorification unto"},{"ref":"31.0f","t":"[Havani], the holy and master of holiness...."},{"ref":"31.0g","t":"Unto Asha-Vahishta, the fairest; unto the much-desired"},{"ref":"31.0h","t":"Airyaman, made by Mazda, and unto the good Saoka, with eyes of"},{"ref":"31.0i","t":"love, made by Mazda and holy;"},{"ref":"31.0j","t":"Be propitiation, with sacrifice, prayer, propitiation, and"},{"ref":"31.0k","t":"glorification."},{"ref":"31.0l","t":"Yatha ahu vairyo: The will of the Lord is the law of"},{"ref":"31.0m","t":"holiness...."},{"ref":"31.1","t":"<span class=\"hv-secn\">I.<\/span> Ahura Mazda spake unto Spitama Zarathushtra, saying: ‘That"},{"ref":"31.1a","t":"thou mayest increase Asha-Vahishta, O Spitama Zarathushtra! with"},{"ref":"31.1b","t":"hymns of praise, with performance of the office, with"},{"ref":"31.1c","t":"invocations, holy words, sacrifice, blessings, and adoration -"},{"ref":"31.1d","t":"once to abide in the shining luminous space, in the beautiful"},{"ref":"31.1e","t":"abodes - for the sacrifice and invocation of us, the"},{"ref":"31.1f","t":"Amesha-Spentas’...."},{"ref":"31.2","t":"Zarathushtra said: ‘Say unto me the right words, such as"},{"ref":"31.2a","t":"they are, O Ahura Mazda! that I may increase Asha-Vahishta, with"},{"ref":"31.2b","t":"hymns of praise, with performance of the office, with"},{"ref":"31.2c","t":"invocations, holy words, sacrifice, blessings, and adoration, -"},{"ref":"31.2d","t":"once to abide in the shining luminous space, in the beautiful"},{"ref":"31.2e","t":"abodes, - for the sacrifice and invocation of you, the"},{"ref":"31.2f","t":"Amesha-Spentas."},{"ref":"31.3","t":"‘.... I proclaim Asha-Vahishta: if I proclaim Asha-Vahishta,"},{"ref":"31.3a","t":"then easy is the way to the abode of the other Amesha-Spentas,"},{"ref":"31.3b","t":"which Ahura Mazda keeps with Good Thoughts, which Ahura Mazda"},{"ref":"31.3c","t":"keep with Good Words, which Ahura Mazda keeps with Good Deeds;"},{"ref":"31.4","t":"‘(Easy is the way to the Garo-nmana of Ahura Mazda): the"},{"ref":"31.4a","t":"Garo-nmana is for the holy souls, and no one of the wicked can"},{"ref":"31.4b","t":"enter the Garo-nmana and its bright, wide, holy ways; (no one of"},{"ref":"31.4c","t":"them can go) to Ahura Mazda."},{"ref":"31.5","t":"<span class=\"hv-secn\">II.<\/span> ‘The Airyaman prayer smites down the strength of all the"},{"ref":"31.5a","t":"creatures of Angra Mainyu, of the Yatus and Pairikas. It is the"},{"ref":"31.5b","t":"greatest of spells, the best of spells, the very best of all"},{"ref":"31.5c","t":"spells; the fairest of spells, the very fairest of all spells;"},{"ref":"31.5d","t":"the fearful one amongst spells, the most fearful of all spells;"},{"ref":"31.5e","t":"the firm one amongst spells, the firmest of all spells; the"},{"ref":"31.5f","t":"victorious one amongst spells, the most victorious of all spells;"},{"ref":"31.5g","t":"the healing one amongst spells, the best-healing of all spells."},{"ref":"31.6","t":"‘One may heal with Holiness, one may heal with the Law, one"},{"ref":"31.6a","t":"may heal with the knife, one may heal with herbs, one may heal"},{"ref":"31.6b","t":"with the Holy Word: amongst all remedies this one is the healing"},{"ref":"31.6c","t":"one that heals with the Holy Word; this one it is at will best"},{"ref":"31.6d","t":"drive away sickness from the body of the faithful: for this one"},{"ref":"31.6e","t":"is the best-healing of all remedies."},{"ref":"31.7","t":"‘Sickness fled away [before it], Death fled away; the Daeva"},{"ref":"31.7a","t":"fled away, the Daeva’s counter-work fled away; the unholy"},{"ref":"31.7b","t":"Ashemaogha fled away, the oppressor of men fled away."},{"ref":"31.8","t":"‘The brood of the Snake fled away; the brood of the Wolf"},{"ref":"31.8a","t":"fled away; the brood of the Two-legged fled away. Pride fled"},{"ref":"31.8b","t":"away; Scorn fled away; Hot Fever fled away; Slander fled away;"},{"ref":"31.8c","t":"Discord fled away; the Evil Eye fled away."},{"ref":"31.9","t":"‘The most lying words of falsehood fled away; the Jahi,"},{"ref":"31.9a","t":"addicted to the Yatu, fled away; the Jahi, who makes one pine,"},{"ref":"31.9b","t":"fled away; the wind that blows from the North fled away; the"},{"ref":"31.9c","t":"wind that blows from the North vanished away."},{"ref":"31.10","t":"‘He it is who smites me that brood of the Snake, and who"},{"ref":"31.10a","t":"might smite those Daevas by thousands of thousands, by ten"},{"ref":"31.10b","t":"thousands of ten thousands; he smites sickness, he smites death,"},{"ref":"31.10c","t":"he smites the Daevas, he smites the Daeva’s counter-work, he"},{"ref":"31.10d","t":"smites the unholy Ashemaogha, he smites the oppressor of men."},{"ref":"31.11","t":"‘He smites the brood of the Snake; he smites the brood of"},{"ref":"31.11a","t":"the Wolf; he smites the brood of the Two-legged. He smites"},{"ref":"31.11b","t":"Pride; he smites Scorn; he smites Hot Fever; he smites Slander;"},{"ref":"31.11c","t":"he smites Discord; he smites the Evil Eye."},{"ref":"31.12","t":"‘He smites the most lying words of falsehood; he smites the"},{"ref":"31.12a","t":"Jahi, addicted to the Yatu; he smites the Jahi, who makes one"},{"ref":"31.12b","t":"pine. He smites the wind that blows from the North; the wind"},{"ref":"31.12c","t":"that blows from the North vanished away."},{"ref":"31.13","t":"‘He it is who smites me that brood of the Two-legged, and"},{"ref":"31.13a","t":"who might smite those Daevas, by thousands of thousands, by ten"},{"ref":"31.13b","t":"thousands of ten thousands. Angra Mainyu, who is all death, the"},{"ref":"31.13c","t":"worst-lying of all Daevas, rushed from before him:"},{"ref":"31.14","t":"‘He exclaimed, did Angra Mainyu: “Woe is me! Here is the"},{"ref":"31.14a","t":"god Asha-Vahishta, who will smite the sickliest of all"},{"ref":"31.14b","t":"sicknesses, who will afflict the sickliest of all sicknesses;"},{"ref":"31.14c","t":"‘“He will smite the deadliest of all deaths, he will afflict"},{"ref":"31.14d","t":"the deadliest of all deaths;"},{"ref":"31.14e","t":"‘“He will smite the most fiendish of all fiends, he will"},{"ref":"31.14f","t":"afflict the most fiendish of all fiends;"},{"ref":"31.14g","t":"‘“He will smite the most counter-working of all"},{"ref":"31.14h","t":"counter-works, he will afflict the most counter-working of all"},{"ref":"31.14i","t":"counter-works;"},{"ref":"31.14j","t":"‘“He will smite the unholy Ashemaogha, he will afflict the"},{"ref":"31.14k","t":"unholy Ashemaogha;"},{"ref":"31.14l","t":"‘“He will smite the most oppressive of the oppressors of"},{"ref":"31.14m","t":"men, he will afflict most oppressive of the oppressors of men."},{"ref":"31.15","t":"‘“He will smite the snakiest of the Snake’s brood, he will"},{"ref":"31.15a","t":"afflict the snakiest of the Snake’s brood;"},{"ref":"31.15b","t":"‘“He will smite the most wolfish of the Wolf’s brood, he"},{"ref":"31.15c","t":"will afflict the most wolfish of the Wolf’s brood;"},{"ref":"31.15d","t":"‘“He will smite the worst of the two-legged brood, he will"},{"ref":"31.15e","t":"afflict the worst of the two-legged brood;"},{"ref":"31.15f","t":"‘“He will smite Pride, he will afflict Pride;"},{"ref":"31.15g","t":"‘“He will smite Scorn, he will afflict Scorn;"},{"ref":"31.15h","t":"‘“He will smite the hottest of hot fevers, he will afflict"},{"ref":"31.15i","t":"the hottest of hot fevers;"},{"ref":"31.15j","t":"‘“He will smite the most slanderous of slanders, he will"},{"ref":"31.15k","t":"afflict the most slanderous of slanders;"},{"ref":"31.15l","t":"‘“He will smite the most discordant of discords, he will"},{"ref":"31.15m","t":"afflict the most discordant of discords;"},{"ref":"31.15n","t":"‘“He will smite the worst of the Evil Eye, he will afflict"},{"ref":"31.15o","t":"the worst of the Evil Eye."},{"ref":"31.16","t":"‘“He will smite the most lying words of falsehood, he will"},{"ref":"31.16a","t":"afflict the most lying words of falsehood;"},{"ref":"31.16b","t":"‘“He will smite the Jahi, addicted to the Yatu, he will"},{"ref":"31.16c","t":"afflict the Jahi, addicted to the Yatu;"},{"ref":"31.16d","t":"‘“He will smite the Jahi, who makes one pine, he will"},{"ref":"31.16e","t":"afflict the Jahi, who makes one pine;"},{"ref":"31.16f","t":"‘“He will smite the wind that blows from the North, he will"},{"ref":"31.16g","t":"afflict the wind that blows from the North.”"},{"ref":"31.17","t":"‘The Druj will perish away, the Druj will perish; the Druj"},{"ref":"31.17a","t":"will rush, the Druj will vanish. Thou perishest away to the"},{"ref":"31.17b","t":"regions of the North, never more to give unto death the living"},{"ref":"31.17c","t":"world of the holy spirit."},{"ref":"31.18","t":"‘For his brightness and glory I will offer unto him a"},{"ref":"31.18a","t":"sacrifice worth being heard, namely, unto Asha-Vahishta, the"},{"ref":"31.18b","t":"fairest - the Amesha-Spenta. Unto Asha-Vahishta, the fairest, the"},{"ref":"31.18c","t":"Amesha-Spenta, we offer up the libations, the Haoma and meat,"},{"ref":"31.18d","t":"the baresma, the wisdom of the tongue, the holy spells, the"},{"ref":"31.18e","t":"speech, the deeds, the libations, and the rightly-spoken words."},{"ref":"31.18f","t":"‘Yenhe hatam: All those beings of whom Ahura Mazda knows the"},{"ref":"31.18g","t":"goodness...."},{"ref":"31.19","t":"‘Yatha ahu vairyo: The will of the Lord is the law of"},{"ref":"31.19a","t":"holiness...."},{"ref":"31.19b","t":"‘I bless the sacrifice and prayer and the strength and"},{"ref":"31.19c","t":"vigour of Asha-Vahishta, the fairest; of the much-desired"},{"ref":"31.19d","t":"Airyaman, made by Mazda; and of the good Saoka, with eyes of"},{"ref":"31.19e","t":"love, made by Mazda and holy."},{"ref":"31.19f","t":"‘Ashem Vohu: Holiness is the best of all good...."},{"ref":"31.19g","t":"‘[Give] unto that man brightness and glory, give him health"},{"ref":"31.19h","t":"of body;.... give him the bright, all-happy, blissful abode of"},{"ref":"31.19i","t":"the holy Ones.’"},{"sp":"HDR","t":"4. Awerdad Yasht"},{"ref":"32.0","t":"May Ahura Mazda be rejoiced!...."},{"ref":"32.0a","t":"Ashem Vohu: Holiness is the best of all good...."},{"ref":"32.0b","t":"I confess myself a worshipper of Mazda, a follower of"},{"ref":"32.0c","t":"Zarathushtra, one who hates the Daevas and obeys the laws of"},{"ref":"32.0d","t":"Ahura;"},{"ref":"32.0e","t":"For sacrifice, prayer, propitiation, and glorification unto"},{"ref":"32.0f","t":"[Havani], the holy and master of holiness...."},{"ref":"32.0g","t":"Unto Haurvatat, the master; unto the prosperity of the"},{"ref":"32.0h","t":"seasons and unto the years, the masters of holiness,"},{"ref":"32.0i","t":"Be propitiation, with sacrifice, prayer, propitiation, and"},{"ref":"32.0j","t":"glorification."},{"ref":"32.0k","t":"Yatha ahu vairyo: The will of the Lord is the law of"},{"ref":"32.0l","t":"holiness...."},{"ref":"32.0m","t":"We sacrifice unto Haurvatat, the Amesha-Spenta; we sacrifice"},{"ref":"32.0n","t":"unto the prosperity of the seasons; we sacrifice unto the years,"},{"ref":"32.0o","t":"the holy and masters of holiness."},{"ref":"32.1","t":"Ahura Mazda spake unto Spitama Zarathushtra, saying: ‘I"},{"ref":"32.1a","t":"created for the faithful the help, the enjoyments, the comforts,"},{"ref":"32.1b","t":"and the pleasures of Haurvatat. We unite them with him who would"},{"ref":"32.1c","t":"come up to thee as one of the Amesha-Spentas, as he would come to"},{"ref":"32.1d","t":"any of the Amesha-Spentas, Vohu-Mano, Asha-Vahishta,"},{"ref":"32.1e","t":"Khshathra-Vairya, Spenta-Armaiti, Haurvatat, and Ameretat."},{"ref":"32.2","t":"‘He who against the thousands of thousands of those Daevas,"},{"ref":"32.2a","t":"against their ten thousands of ten thousands, against their"},{"ref":"32.2b","t":"numberless myriads would invoke the name of Haurvatat, as one of"},{"ref":"32.2c","t":"the Amesha-Spentas, he would smite the Nasu, he would smite"},{"ref":"32.2d","t":"Hashi, he would smite Bashi, he would smite Saeni, he would"},{"ref":"32.2e","t":"smite Buji."},{"ref":"32.3","t":"‘I proclaim the faithful man as the first [of men]; if I"},{"ref":"32.3a","t":"proclaim the faithful man as the first [of men], then Rashnu"},{"ref":"32.3b","t":"Razishta, then every heavenly Yazata of male nature in company"},{"ref":"32.3c","t":"with the Amesha-Spentas will free the faithful man"},{"ref":"32.4","t":"‘From the Nasu, from Hashi, from Gashi, from Saeni, from"},{"ref":"32.4a","t":"Buji; from the hordes with the wide front, from the hordes with"},{"ref":"32.4b","t":"the many spears uplifted, from the evil man who oppresses, from"},{"ref":"32.4c","t":"the willful sinner, from the oppressor of men, from the Yatu,"},{"ref":"32.4d","t":"from the Pairika, from the straying way."},{"ref":"32.5","t":"‘How does the way of the faithful turn and part from the way"},{"ref":"32.5a","t":"of the wicked?’"},{"ref":"32.5b","t":"Ahura Mazda answered: ‘It is when a man pronouncing my"},{"ref":"32.5c","t":"spell, either reading or reciting it by heart, draws the furrows"},{"ref":"32.5d","t":"and hides there himself, [saying]:"},{"ref":"32.6","t":"‘“I will smite thee, O Druj! whomsoever thou art, whomsoever"},{"ref":"32.6a","t":"thou art amongst the Drujes that come in an open way, whomsoever"},{"ref":"32.6b","t":"thou art amongst the Drujes that come by hidden way, whomsoever"},{"ref":"32.6c","t":"thou art amongst the Drujes that defile by contact; whatsoever"},{"ref":"32.6d","t":"Druj thou art, I smite thee away from the Aryan countries;"},{"ref":"32.6e","t":"whatsoever Druj thou art, I bind thee; I smite thee down, O Druj!"},{"ref":"32.6f","t":"I throw thee down below, O Druj!”"},{"ref":"32.7","t":"‘He draws [then] three furrows: I proclaim him one of the"},{"ref":"32.7a","t":"faithful; he draws six furrow: I proclaim him one of the"},{"ref":"32.7b","t":"faithful; he draws nine furrows: I proclaim him one of the"},{"ref":"32.7c","t":"faithful."},{"ref":"32.8","t":"‘The names of those (Amesha-Spentas) smite the men turned to"},{"ref":"32.8a","t":"Nasus by the Drujes: the seed and kin of the deaf are smitten,"},{"ref":"32.8b","t":"the scornful are dead, as the Zaotar Zarathushtra blows them"},{"ref":"32.8c","t":"away to woe, however fierce, at his will and wish, as many as he"},{"ref":"32.8d","t":"wishes."},{"ref":"32.9","t":"‘From the time when the sun is down he smites them with"},{"ref":"32.9a","t":"bruising blows; from the time when the sun is no longer up, he"},{"ref":"32.9b","t":"deals deadly blows on the Nasu with his club struck down, for the"},{"ref":"32.9c","t":"propitiation and glorification of the heavenly gods."},{"ref":"32.10","t":"‘O Zarathushtra! let not that spell be shown to any one,"},{"ref":"32.10a","t":"except by the father to his son, or by the brother to his brother"},{"ref":"32.10b","t":"from the same womb, or by the Athravan to his pupil in black"},{"ref":"32.10c","t":"hair, devoted to the good law, who, devoted to the good law,"},{"ref":"32.10d","t":"holy and brave, stills all the Drujes."},{"ref":"32.11","t":"‘For his brightness and glory, I will offer unto him a"},{"ref":"32.11a","t":"sacrifice worth being heard, namely, unto Haurvatat, the"},{"ref":"32.11b","t":"Amesha-Spenta. Unto Haurvatat, the Amesha-Spenta, we offer up the"},{"ref":"32.11c","t":"libations, the Haoma and meat, the baresma, the wisdom of the"},{"ref":"32.11d","t":"tongue, the holy spells, the speech, the deeds, the libations,"},{"ref":"32.11e","t":"and the rightly-spoken words."},{"ref":"32.12","t":"‘Yatha ahu vairyo: The will of the Lord is the law of"},{"ref":"32.12a","t":"holiness...."},{"ref":"32.12b","t":"‘I bless the sacrifice and prayer, and the strength and"},{"ref":"32.12c","t":"vigour of Haurvatat, the master; of the prosperity of the seasons"},{"ref":"32.12d","t":"and of the years, the masters of holiness."},{"ref":"32.12e","t":"‘Ashem Vohu: Holiness is the best of all good...."},{"ref":"32.12f","t":"‘[Give] unto that man brightness and glory,... give him"},{"ref":"32.12g","t":"the bright, all happy, blissful abode of the holy Ones.’"},{"sp":"HDR","t":"5. Ardui Sur Bano Yasht (Hymn to the Waters)"},{"ref":"33.0","t":"May Ahura Mazda be rejoiced!...."},{"ref":"33.0a","t":"Ashem Vohu: Holiness is the best of all good...."},{"ref":"33.0b","t":"I confess myself a worshipper of Mazda, a follower of Zarathushtra,"},{"ref":"33.0c","t":"one who hates the Daevas and obeys the laws of Ahura;"},{"ref":"33.0d","t":"For sacrifice, prayer, propitiation, and glorification unto [Havani],"},{"ref":"33.0e","t":"the holy and master of holiness...."},{"ref":"33.0f","t":"Unto the good Waters, made by Mazda; unto the holy water-spring"},{"ref":"33.0g","t":"Ardvi Anahita; unto all waters, made by Mazda; unto all plants,"},{"ref":"33.0h","t":"made by Mazda,"},{"ref":"33.0i","t":"Be propitiation, with sacrifice, prayer, propitiation, and glorification."},{"ref":"33.0j","t":"Yatha ahu vairyo: The will of the Lord is the law of holiness...."},{"ref":"33.1","t":"<span class=\"hv-secn\">I.<\/span> Ahura Mazda spake unto Spitama Zarathushtra, saying: ‘Offer"},{"ref":"33.1a","t":"up a sacrifice, O Spitama Zarathushtra! unto this spring of mine,"},{"ref":"33.1b","t":"Ardvi Sura Anahita, the wide-expanding and health-giving, who"},{"ref":"33.1c","t":"hates the Daevas and obeys the laws of Ahura, who is worthy of"},{"ref":"33.1d","t":"sacrifice in the material world, worthy of prayer in the material"},{"ref":"33.1e","t":"world; the life-increasing and holy, the herd-increasing and holy,"},{"ref":"33.1f","t":"the fold-increasing and holy, the wealth-increasing and holy,"},{"ref":"33.1g","t":"the country-increasing and holy;"},{"ref":"33.2","t":"‘Who makes the seed of all males pure, who makes the womb"},{"ref":"33.2a","t":"of all females pure for bringing forth, who makes all females"},{"ref":"33.2b","t":"bring forth in safety, who puts milk into the breasts of all females"},{"ref":"33.2c","t":"in the right measure and the right quality;"},{"ref":"33.3","t":"‘The large river, known afar, that is as large as the whole"},{"ref":"33.3a","t":"of the waters that run along the earth; that runs powerfully from"},{"ref":"33.3b","t":"the height Hukairya down to the sea Vouru-Kasha."},{"ref":"33.4","t":"‘All the shores of the sea Vouru-Kasha are boiling over, all"},{"ref":"33.4a","t":"the middle of it is boiling over, when she runs down there, when"},{"ref":"33.4b","t":"she streams down there, she, Ardvi Sura Anahita, who has a thousand"},{"ref":"33.4c","t":"cells and a thousand channels: the extent of each of those cells,"},{"ref":"33.4d","t":"of each of those channels is as much as a man can ride in forty"},{"ref":"33.4e","t":"days, riding on a good horse."},{"ref":"33.5","t":"‘From this river of mine alone flow all the waters that spread"},{"ref":"33.5a","t":"all over the seven Karshvares; this river of mine alone goes on"},{"ref":"33.5b","t":"bringing waters, both in summer and in winter. This river of mine"},{"ref":"33.5c","t":"purifies the seed in males, the womb in females the milk in females’"},{"ref":"33.5d","t":"breasts."},{"ref":"33.6","t":"‘I, Ahura Mazda, brought it down with mighty vigor, for the"},{"ref":"33.6a","t":"increase of the house, of the borough of the town, of the country,"},{"ref":"33.6b","t":"to keep them, to maintain them, to look over them, to keep and"},{"ref":"33.6c","t":"maintain them close."},{"ref":"33.7","t":"‘Then Ardvi Sura Anahita, O Spitama Zarathushtra! proceeded"},{"ref":"33.7a","t":"forth from the Maker Mazda. Beautiful were her white arms, thick"},{"ref":"33.7b","t":"as a horse’s shoulder or still thicker; beautiful was her...."},{"ref":"33.7c","t":"and thus came she, strong, with thick arms, thinking thus in her"},{"ref":"33.7d","t":"heart:"},{"ref":"33.8","t":"‘“Who will praise me? Who will offer me a sacrifice,"},{"ref":"33.8a","t":"with libations cleanly prepared and well-strained, together with"},{"ref":"33.8b","t":"the Haoma and meat? To whom shall I cleave, who cleaves unto me,"},{"ref":"33.8c","t":"and thinks with me, and bestows gifts upon me, and is of good"},{"ref":"33.8d","t":"will unto me?”"},{"ref":"33.9","t":"‘For her brightness and glory, I will offer her a sacrifice"},{"ref":"33.9a","t":"worth being heard; I will offer up unto the holy Ardvi Sura Anahita"},{"ref":"33.9b","t":"a good sacrifice with an offering of libations;- thus mayest thou"},{"ref":"33.9c","t":"advise us when thou art appealed to! Mayest thou be most fully"},{"ref":"33.9d","t":"worshipped, O Ardvi Sura Anahita! with the Haoma and meat, with"},{"ref":"33.9e","t":"the baresma, with the wisdom of the tongue, with the holy spells,"},{"ref":"33.9f","t":"with the words with the deeds, with the libations, and with the"},{"ref":"33.9g","t":"rightly-spoken words."},{"ref":"33.9h","t":"‘Yenhe hatam: All those beings of whom Ahura Mazda...."},{"ref":"33.10","t":"<span class=\"hv-secn\">II.<\/span> ‘Offer up a sacrifice, O Spitama Zarathushtra! unto this spring"},{"ref":"33.10a","t":"of mine, Ardvi Sura Anahita, the wide-expanding and health-giving,"},{"ref":"33.10b","t":"who hates the Daevas and obeys the laws of Ahura, who is worthy"},{"ref":"33.10c","t":"of sacrifice in the material world, worthy of prayer in the material"},{"ref":"33.10d","t":"world; the life-increasing and holy, the herd-increasing and holy,"},{"ref":"33.10e","t":"the fold-increasing and holy, the wealth-increasing and holy,"},{"ref":"33.10f","t":"the country-increasing and holy;"},{"ref":"33.11","t":"‘Who drives forwards on her chariot, holding the reins of"},{"ref":"33.11a","t":"the chariot. She goes, driving, on this chariot, longing for men"},{"ref":"33.11b","t":"and thinking thus in her heart: “Who will praise me? Who"},{"ref":"33.11c","t":"will offer me a sacrifice, with libations cleanly prepared and"},{"ref":"33.11d","t":"well-strained, together with the Haoma and meat? To whom shall"},{"ref":"33.11e","t":"I cleave, who cleaves unto me, and thinks with me, and bestows"},{"ref":"33.11f","t":"gifts unto me, and is of good will unto me?”"},{"ref":"33.11g","t":"‘For her brightness and glory, I will offer her a sacrifice, worth"},{"ref":"33.11h","t":"being heard...."},{"ref":"33.12","t":"<span class=\"hv-secn\">III.<\/span> ‘Offer up a sacrifice, O Spitama Zarathushtra! unto this spring"},{"ref":"33.12a","t":"of mine, Ardvi Sura Anahita...."},{"ref":"33.13","t":"‘Whom four horses carry, all white, of one and the same color,"},{"ref":"33.13a","t":"of the same blood, tall, crushing down the hates of all haters,"},{"ref":"33.13b","t":"of the Daevas and men, of the Yatus and Pairikas, of the oppressors,"},{"ref":"33.13c","t":"of the blind and of the deaf."},{"ref":"33.13d","t":"‘For her brightness and glory, I will offer her a sacrifice...."},{"ref":"33.14","t":"<span class=\"hv-secn\">IV.<\/span> ‘Offer up a sacrifice, O Spitama Zarathushtra! unto this spring"},{"ref":"33.14a","t":"of mine, Ardvi Sura Anahita...."},{"ref":"33.15","t":"‘Strong and bright, tall and beautiful of form, who sends"},{"ref":"33.15a","t":"down by day and by night a flow of motherly waters as large as"},{"ref":"33.15b","t":"the whole of the waters that run along the earth, and who runs"},{"ref":"33.15c","t":"powerfully."},{"ref":"33.15d","t":"‘For her brightness and glory, I will offer her a sacrifice...."},{"ref":"33.16","t":"<span class=\"hv-secn\">V.<\/span> ‘Offer up a sacrifice, O Spitama Zarathushtra! unto this spring"},{"ref":"33.16a","t":"of mine, Ardvi Sura Anahita...."},{"ref":"33.17","t":"‘To her did the Maker Ahura Mazda offer up a sacrifice to"},{"ref":"33.17a","t":"the Airyana Vaejah, by the good river Daitya; with the Haoma and"},{"ref":"33.17b","t":"meat, with the baresma, with the wisdom of the tongue, with the"},{"ref":"33.17c","t":"holy spells, with the words, with the deeds, with the libations,"},{"ref":"33.17d","t":"and with the rightly-spoken words."},{"ref":"33.18","t":"He begged of her a boon, saying: “Grant me this, O good,"},{"ref":"33.18a","t":"most beneficent Ardvi Sura Anahita! that I may bring the son of"},{"ref":"33.18b","t":"Pourushaspa, the holy Zarathushtra, to think after my law, to"},{"ref":"33.18c","t":"speak after my law, to do after my law!”"},{"ref":"33.19","t":"‘Ardvi Sura Anahita granted him that boon, as he was offering"},{"ref":"33.19a","t":"libations, giving gifts, sacrificing, and begging that she would"},{"ref":"33.19b","t":"grant him that boon."},{"ref":"33.19c","t":"‘For her brightness and glory, I will offer her a sacrifice...."},{"ref":"33.20","t":"<span class=\"hv-secn\">VI.<\/span> ‘Offer up a sacrifice, O Spitama Zarathushtra! unto this spring"},{"ref":"33.20a","t":"of mine, Ardvi Sura Anahita...."},{"ref":"33.21","t":"‘To her did Haoshyangha, the Paradhata, offer up a sacrifice"},{"ref":"33.21a","t":"on the enclosure of the Hara, with a hundred male horses, a thousand"},{"ref":"33.21b","t":"oxen, and ten thousand lambs."},{"ref":"33.22","t":"‘He begged of her a boon, saying: “Grant me this, O good,"},{"ref":"33.22a","t":"most beneficent Ardvi Sura Anahita, that I may become the sovereign"},{"ref":"33.22b","t":"lord of all countries, of the Daevas and men, of the Yatus and"},{"ref":"33.22c","t":"Pairikas, of the oppressors, the blind and the deaf; and that"},{"ref":"33.22d","t":"I may smite down two thirds of the Daevas of Mazana and of the"},{"ref":"33.22e","t":"fiends of Varena.”"},{"ref":"33.23","t":"‘Ardvi Sura Anahita granted him that boon, as he was offering"},{"ref":"33.23a","t":"libations, giving gifts, sacrificing, and entreating that she"},{"ref":"33.23b","t":"would grant him that boon."},{"ref":"33.23c","t":"‘For her brightness and glory, I will offer her a sacrifice...."},{"ref":"33.24","t":"<span class=\"hv-secn\">VII.<\/span> ‘Offer up a sacrifice, O Spitama Zarathushtra! unto this spring"},{"ref":"33.24a","t":"of mine, Ardvi Sura Anahita...."},{"ref":"33.25","t":"‘To her did Yima Khshaeta, the good shepherd, offer up a sacrifice"},{"ref":"33.25a","t":"from the height Hukairya, with a hundred male horses, a thousand"},{"ref":"33.25b","t":"oxen, ten thousand lambs."},{"ref":"33.26","t":"‘He begged of her a boon, saying: “Grant me this, O good,"},{"ref":"33.26a","t":"most beneficent Ardvi Sura Anahita! that I may become the sovereign"},{"ref":"33.26b","t":"lord of all countries, of the Daevas and men, of the Yatus and"},{"ref":"33.26c","t":"Pairikas, of the oppressors, the blind and the deaf; and that"},{"ref":"33.26d","t":"I may take from the Daevas both riches and welfare, both fatness"},{"ref":"33.26e","t":"and flocks, both weal and Glory.”"},{"ref":"33.27","t":"‘Ardvi Sura Anahita granted him that boon, as he was offering"},{"ref":"33.27a","t":"libations, giving gifts, sacrificing, and entreating that she"},{"ref":"33.27b","t":"would grant him that boon."},{"ref":"33.27c","t":"‘For her brightness and glory, I will offer her a sacrifice...."},{"ref":"33.28","t":"<span class=\"hv-secn\">VIII.<\/span> ‘Offer up a sacrifice, O Spitama Zarathushtra! unto this spring"},{"ref":"33.28a","t":"of mine, Ardvi Sura Anahita...."},{"ref":"33.29","t":"‘To her did Azi Dahaka, the three-mouthed, offer up a sacrifice"},{"ref":"33.29a","t":"in the land of Bawri, with a hundred male horses, a thousand oxen,"},{"ref":"33.29b","t":"and ten thousand lambs."},{"ref":"33.30","t":"‘He begged of her a boon, saying: “Grant me this boon,"},{"ref":"33.30a","t":"O good, most beneficent Ardvi Sura Anahita! that I may make all"},{"ref":"33.30b","t":"the seven Karshvares of the earth empty of men.”"},{"ref":"33.31","t":"‘Ardvi Sura Anahita did not grant him that boon, although"},{"ref":"33.31a","t":"he was offering libations, giving gifts, sacrificing, and entreating"},{"ref":"33.31b","t":"her that she would grant him that boon."},{"ref":"33.31c","t":"‘For her brightness and glory, I will offer her a sacrifice...."},{"ref":"33.32","t":"<span class=\"hv-secn\">IX.<\/span> ‘Offer up a sacrifice, O Spitama Zarathushtra! unto Ardvi"},{"ref":"33.32a","t":"Sura Anahita...."},{"ref":"33.33","t":"‘To her did Thraetaona, the heir of the valiant Athwya clan,"},{"ref":"33.33a","t":"offer up a sacrifice in the four-cornered Varena, with a hundred"},{"ref":"33.33b","t":"male horses, a thousand oxen, ten thousand lambs."},{"ref":"33.34","t":"‘He begged of her a boon, saying: “Grant me this, O good,"},{"ref":"33.34a","t":"most beneficent Ardvi Sura Anahita! that I may overcome Azi Dahaka,"},{"ref":"33.34b","t":"the three-mouthed, the three-headed, the six-eyed, who has a thousand"},{"ref":"33.34c","t":"senses, that most powerful, fiendish Druj, that demon, baleful"},{"ref":"33.34d","t":"to the world, the strongest Druj that Angra Mainyu created against"},{"ref":"33.34e","t":"the material world, to destroy the world of the good principle;"},{"ref":"33.34f","t":"and that I may deliver his two wives, Savanghavach and Erenavach,"},{"ref":"33.34g","t":"who are the fairest of body amongst women, and the most wonderful"},{"ref":"33.34h","t":"creatures in the world.”"},{"ref":"33.35","t":"‘Ardvi Sura Anahita granted him that boon, as he was offering"},{"ref":"33.35a","t":"libations, giving gifts, sacrificing, and entreating that she"},{"ref":"33.35b","t":"would grant him that boon."},{"ref":"33.35c","t":"‘For her brightness and glory, I will offer her a sacrifice...."},{"ref":"33.36","t":"<span class=\"hv-secn\">X.<\/span> ‘Offer up a sacrifice, O Spitama Zarathushtra! unto Ardvi"},{"ref":"33.36a","t":"Sura Anahita...."},{"ref":"33.37","t":"‘To her did Keresaspa, the manly-hearted, offer up a sacrifice"},{"ref":"33.37a","t":"behind the Vairi Pisanah, with a hundred male horses, a thousand"},{"ref":"33.37b","t":"oxen, ten thousand lambs."},{"ref":"33.38","t":"‘He begged of her a boon, saying: “Grant me this, O good,"},{"ref":"33.38a","t":"most beneficent Ardvi Sura Anahita! that I may overcome the golden-heeled"},{"ref":"33.38b","t":"Gandarewa, though all the shores of the sea Vouru-Kasha are boiling"},{"ref":"33.38c","t":"over; and that I may run up to the stronghold of the fiend on"},{"ref":"33.38d","t":"the wide, round earth, whose ends lie afar.”"},{"ref":"33.39","t":"‘Ardvi Sura Anahita granted him that boon, as he was offering"},{"ref":"33.39a","t":"libations, giving gifts, sacrificing, and entreating that she"},{"ref":"33.39b","t":"would grant him that boon."},{"ref":"33.39c","t":"‘For her brightness and glory, I will offer her a sacrifice...."},{"ref":"33.40","t":"<span class=\"hv-secn\">XI.<\/span> ‘Offer up a sacrifice, O Spitama Zarathushtra! unto this spring"},{"ref":"33.40a","t":"of mine, Ardvi Sara Anahita...."},{"ref":"33.41","t":"‘To her did the Turanian murderer, Frangrasyan, offer up a"},{"ref":"33.41a","t":"sacrifice in his cave under the earth, with a hundred male horses,"},{"ref":"33.41b","t":"a thousand oxen, ten thousand lambs."},{"ref":"33.42","t":"‘He begged of her a boon, saying: “Grant me this, O good,"},{"ref":"33.42a","t":"most beneficent Ardvi Sura Anahita! that I may seize hold of that"},{"ref":"33.42b","t":"Glory, that is waving in the middle of the sea Vouru-Kasha and"},{"ref":"33.42c","t":"that belongs to the Aryan people, to those born and to those not"},{"ref":"33.42d","t":"yet born, and to the holy Zarathushtra.”"},{"ref":"33.43","t":"‘Ardvi Sura Anahita did not grant him that boon."},{"ref":"33.43a","t":"‘For her brightness and glory, I will offer her a sacrifice...."},{"ref":"33.44","t":"<span class=\"hv-secn\">II.<\/span> ‘Offer up a sacrifice, O Spitama Zarathushtra! unto this spring"},{"ref":"33.44a","t":"of mine, Ardvi Sura Anahita...."},{"ref":"33.45","t":"‘To her did the great, most wise Kavi Usa offer up a sacrifice"},{"ref":"33.45a","t":"from Mount Erezifya, with a hundred male horses, a thousand oxen,"},{"ref":"33.45b","t":"ten thousand lambs."},{"ref":"33.46","t":"‘He begged of her a boon, saying: “Grant me, this, O"},{"ref":"33.46a","t":"good, most beneficent Ardvi Sura Anahita! that I may become the"},{"ref":"33.46b","t":"sovereign lord of all countries, of the Daevas and men, of the"},{"ref":"33.46c","t":"Yatus and Pairikas, of the oppressors, the blind and the deaf.”"},{"ref":"33.47","t":"‘Ardvi Sura Anahita granted him that boon, as he was offering"},{"ref":"33.47a","t":"libations, giving gifts, sacrificing, and entreating that she"},{"ref":"33.47b","t":"would grant him that boon."},{"ref":"33.47c","t":"‘For her brightness and glory, I will offer her a sacrifice...."},{"ref":"33.48","t":"<span class=\"hv-secn\">XIII.<\/span> ‘Offer up a sacrifice, O Spitama Zarathushtra! unto this spring"},{"ref":"33.48a","t":"of mine, Ardvi Sura Anahita...."},{"ref":"33.49","t":"‘To her did the gallant Husravah, he who united the Aryan"},{"ref":"33.49a","t":"nations into one kingdom, offer up a sacrifice behind the Chaechasta"},{"ref":"33.49b","t":"lake, the deep lake, of salt waters, with a hundred male horses,"},{"ref":"33.49c","t":"a thousand oxen, ten thousand lambs."},{"ref":"33.50","t":"‘He begged of her a boon, saying: “Grant me this, O good,"},{"ref":"33.50a","t":"most beneficent Ardvi Sura Anahita! that I may become the sovereign"},{"ref":"33.50b","t":"lord of all countries, of Daevas and men, of the Yatus and Pairikas,"},{"ref":"33.50c","t":"of the oppressors, the blind and the deaf; and that I may have"},{"ref":"33.50d","t":"the lead in front of all the teams and that he may not pass through"},{"ref":"33.50e","t":"the forest, he, the murderer, who now is fiercely striving against"},{"ref":"33.50f","t":"me on horseback.”"},{"ref":"33.51","t":"‘Ardvi Sura Anahita granted him that boon, as he was offering"},{"ref":"33.51a","t":"libations, giving gifts, sacrificing, and entreating that she"},{"ref":"33.51b","t":"would grant him that boon."},{"ref":"33.51c","t":"‘For her brightness and glory, I will offer her a sacrifice...."},{"ref":"33.52","t":"<span class=\"hv-secn\">XIV.<\/span> ‘Offer up a sacrifice, O Spitama Zarathushtra! unto this spring"},{"ref":"33.52a","t":"of mine, Ardvi Sura Anahita...."},{"ref":"33.53","t":"‘To her did the valiant warrior Tusa offer worship on the"},{"ref":"33.53a","t":"back of his horse, begging swiftness for his teams, health for"},{"ref":"33.53b","t":"his own body, and that he might watch with full success those"},{"ref":"33.53c","t":"who hated him, smite down his foes, and destroy at one stroke"},{"ref":"33.53d","t":"his adversaries, his enemies, and those who hated him."},{"ref":"33.54","t":"‘He begged of her a boon, saying: “Grant me this, O good,"},{"ref":"33.54a","t":"most beneficent Ardvi Sura Anahita! that I may overcome the gallant"},{"ref":"33.54b","t":"sons of Vaesaka, by the castle Khshathro-saoka, that stands high"},{"ref":"33.54c","t":"up on the lofty, holy Kangha; that I may smite of the Turanian"},{"ref":"33.54d","t":"people their fifties and their hundreds, their hundreds and their"},{"ref":"33.54e","t":"thousands, their thousands and their tens of thousands, their"},{"ref":"33.54f","t":"tens of thousands and their myriads of myriads.”"},{"ref":"33.55","t":"‘Ardvi Sura Anahita granted him that boon, as he was offering"},{"ref":"33.55a","t":"libations, giving gifts, sacrificing, and entreating that she"},{"ref":"33.55b","t":"would grant him that boon."},{"ref":"33.55c","t":"‘For her brightness and glory, I will offer her a sacrifice...."},{"ref":"33.56","t":"<span class=\"hv-secn\">XV.<\/span> ‘Offer up a sacrifice, O Spitama Zarathushtra! unto this spring"},{"ref":"33.56a","t":"of mine, Ardvi Sura Anahita...."},{"ref":"33.57","t":"‘To her did the gallant sons of Vaesaka offer up a sacrifice"},{"ref":"33.57a","t":"in the castle Khshathro-saoka, that stands high up on the lofty,"},{"ref":"33.57b","t":"holy Kangha, with a hundred male horses, a thousand oxen, ten"},{"ref":"33.57c","t":"thousand lambs."},{"ref":"33.58","t":"‘They begged of her a boon, saying: “Grant us this, O"},{"ref":"33.58a","t":"good, most beneficent Ardvi Sura Anahita! that we may overcome"},{"ref":"33.58b","t":"the valiant warrior Tusa, and that we may smite of the Aryan people"},{"ref":"33.58c","t":"their fifties and their hundreds, their hundreds and their thousands,"},{"ref":"33.58d","t":"their thousands and their tens of thousands, their tens of thousands"},{"ref":"33.58e","t":"and their myriads of myriads.”"},{"ref":"33.59","t":"‘Ardvi Sura Anahita did not grant them that boon."},{"ref":"33.59a","t":"‘For her brightness and glory, I will offer her a sacrifice...."},{"ref":"33.60","t":"<span class=\"hv-secn\">XVI.<\/span> ‘Offer up a sacrifice, O Spitama Zarathushtra! unto this spring"},{"ref":"33.60a","t":"of mine, Ardvi Sura Anahita...."},{"ref":"33.61","t":"‘The old Vafra Navaza worshipped her when the strong fiend-smiter,"},{"ref":"33.61a","t":"Thraetaona, flung him up in the air in the shape of a bird, of"},{"ref":"33.61b","t":"a vulture."},{"ref":"33.62","t":"‘He went on flying, for three days and three nights, towards"},{"ref":"33.62a","t":"his own house; but he could not, he could not turn down. At the"},{"ref":"33.62b","t":"end of the third night, when the beneficent dawn came dawning"},{"ref":"33.62c","t":"up, then he prayed unto Ardvi Sura Anahita, saying:"},{"ref":"33.63","t":"‘“Ardvi Sura Anahita! do thou quickly hasten helpfully"},{"ref":"33.63a","t":"and bring me assistance at once. I will offer thee a thousand"},{"ref":"33.63b","t":"libations, cleanly prepared and well strained, along with Haomas"},{"ref":"33.63c","t":"and meat, by the brink of the river Rangha, if I reach alive the"},{"ref":"33.63d","t":"earth made by Ahura and my own house.”"},{"ref":"33.64","t":"‘Ardvi Sura Anahita hastened unto him in the shape of a maid,"},{"ref":"33.64a","t":"fair of body, most strong, tall-formed, high-girdled, pure, nobly"},{"ref":"33.64b","t":"born of a glorious race, wearing shoes up to the ankle wearing"},{"ref":"33.64c","t":"a golden.... and radiant."},{"ref":"33.65","t":"‘She seized him by the arm: quickly was it done, nor was it"},{"ref":"33.65a","t":"long till, speeding, he arrived at the earth made by Mazda and"},{"ref":"33.65b","t":"at his own house, safe, unhurt, unwounded, just as he was before."},{"ref":"33.65c","t":"[66. ‘Ardvi Sura Anahita granted him that boon, as he was offering"},{"ref":"33.65d","t":"up libations, giving gifts, sacrificing, entreating that she would"},{"ref":"33.65e","t":"grant him that boon.]"},{"ref":"33.65f","t":"‘For her brightness and glory, I will offer her a sacrifice...."},{"ref":"33.67","t":"<span class=\"hv-secn\">XVII.<\/span> ‘Offer up a sacrifice, O Spitama Zarathushtra! unto this spring"},{"ref":"33.67a","t":"of mine, Ardvi Sura Anahita...."},{"ref":"33.68","t":"‘To her did Jamaspa offer up a sacrifice, with a hundred horses,"},{"ref":"33.68a","t":"a thousand oxen, ten thousand lambs, when he saw the army of the"},{"ref":"33.68b","t":"wicked, of the worshippers of the Daevas, coming from afar in"},{"ref":"33.68c","t":"battle array."},{"ref":"33.69","t":"‘He asked of her a boon, saying: “Grant me this, O good,"},{"ref":"33.69a","t":"most beneficent Ardvi Sura Anahita! that I may be as constantly"},{"ref":"33.69b","t":"victorious as any one of all the Aryans.”"},{"ref":"33.70","t":"‘Ardvi Sura Anahita granted him that boon, as he was offering"},{"ref":"33.70a","t":"up libations, giving gifts, sacrificing, and entreating that she"},{"ref":"33.70b","t":"would grant him that boon."},{"ref":"33.70c","t":"‘For her brightness and glory, I will offer her a sacrifice...."},{"ref":"33.71","t":"<span class=\"hv-secn\">XVIII.<\/span> ‘Offer up a sacrifice, O Spitama Zarathushtra! unto this spring"},{"ref":"33.71a","t":"of mine, Ardvi Sura Anahita...."},{"ref":"33.72","t":"‘To her did Ashavazdah, the son of Pouru-dhakhshti, and Ashavazdah"},{"ref":"33.72a","t":"and Thrita, the sons of Sayuzhdri, offer up a sacrifice, with"},{"ref":"33.72b","t":"a hundred horses, a thousand oxen, ten thousand lambs, by Apam"},{"ref":"33.72c","t":"Napat, the tall lord, the lord of the females, the bright and"},{"ref":"33.72d","t":"swift-horsed."},{"ref":"33.73","t":"‘They begged of her a boon, saying: “Grant us this, O"},{"ref":"33.73a","t":"good, most beneficent Ardvi Sura Anahita! that we may overcome"},{"ref":"33.73b","t":"the assemblers of the Turanian Danus, Kara Asabana, and Vara Asabana,"},{"ref":"33.73c","t":"and the most mighty Duraekaeta, in the battles of this world."},{"ref":"33.74","t":"‘Ardvi Sura Anahita granted them that boon, as they were offering"},{"ref":"33.74a","t":"up libations, giving gifts, sacrificing, and entreating that she"},{"ref":"33.74b","t":"would grant them that boon."},{"ref":"33.74c","t":"‘For her brightness and glory, l will offer her a sacrifice...."},{"ref":"33.75","t":"<span class=\"hv-secn\">XIX.<\/span> ‘Offer up a sacrifice, O Spitama Zarathushtra! unto this spring"},{"ref":"33.75a","t":"of mine, Ardvi Sura Anahita...."},{"ref":"33.76","t":"‘Vistauru, the son of Naotara, worshipped her by the brink"},{"ref":"33.76a","t":"of the river Vitanghuhaiti, with well-spoken words, speaking thus:"},{"ref":"33.77","t":"‘“This is true, this is truly spoken, that I have smitten"},{"ref":"33.77a","t":"as many of the worshippers of the Daevas as the hairs I bear on"},{"ref":"33.77b","t":"my head. Do thou then, O Ardvi Sura Anahita! leave me a dry passage,"},{"ref":"33.77c","t":"to pass over the good Vitanghuhaiti.”"},{"ref":"33.78","t":"‘Ardvi Sura Anahita hastened unto him in the shape of a maid,"},{"ref":"33.78a","t":"fair of body, most strong, tall-formed, high-girded, pure, nobly"},{"ref":"33.78b","t":"born of a glorious race, wearing shoes up to the ankle, with all"},{"ref":"33.78c","t":"sorts of ornaments and radiant. A part of the waters she made"},{"ref":"33.78d","t":"stand still, a part of the waters she made flow forward, and she"},{"ref":"33.78e","t":"left him a dry passage to pass over the good Vitanghuhaiti."},{"ref":"33.78f","t":"[79. ‘Ardvi Sura Anahita granted him that boon, as he was offering"},{"ref":"33.78g","t":"up libations, giving gifts, sacrificing, and entreating that she"},{"ref":"33.78h","t":"would grant him that boon.]"},{"ref":"33.78i","t":"‘For her brightness and glory, I will offer her a sacrifice...."},{"ref":"33.80","t":"<span class=\"hv-secn\">XX.<\/span> ‘Offer up a sacrifice, O Spitama Zarathushtra! unto this spring"},{"ref":"33.80a","t":"of mine, Ardvi Sura Anahita...."},{"ref":"33.81","t":"‘To her did Yoishta, one of the Fryanas, offer up a sacrifice"},{"ref":"33.81a","t":"with a hundred horses, a thousand oxen, ten thousand lambs on"},{"ref":"33.81b","t":"the Pedvaepa of the Rangha."},{"ref":"33.82","t":"‘He begged of her a boon, saying: “Grant me this, O good,"},{"ref":"33.82a","t":"most beneficent Ardvi Sura Anahita! that I may overcome the evil-doing"},{"ref":"33.82b","t":"Akhtya, the offspring of darkness, and that I may answer the ninety-nine"},{"ref":"33.82c","t":"hard riddles that he asks me maliciously, the evil-doing Akhtya,"},{"ref":"33.82d","t":"the offspring of darkness.”"},{"ref":"33.83","t":"‘Ardvi Sura Anahita granted him that boon, as he was offering"},{"ref":"33.83a","t":"up libations, giving gifts, sacrificing, and entreating that she"},{"ref":"33.83b","t":"would grant him that boon."},{"ref":"33.83c","t":"‘For her brightness and glory, I will offer her a sacrifice...."},{"ref":"33.84","t":"<span class=\"hv-secn\">XXI.<\/span> ‘Offer up a sacrifice, O Spitama Zarathushtra! unto this spring"},{"ref":"33.84a","t":"of mine, Ardvi Sura Anahita...."},{"ref":"33.85","t":"‘Whom Ahura Mazda the merciful ordered thus, saying: “Come,"},{"ref":"33.85a","t":"O Ardvi Sura Anahita, come from those stars down to the earth"},{"ref":"33.85b","t":"made by Ahura, that the great lords may worship thee, the masters"},{"ref":"33.85c","t":"of the countries, and their sons."},{"ref":"33.86","t":"‘“The men of strength will beg of thee swift horses and"},{"ref":"33.86a","t":"supremacy of Glory."},{"ref":"33.86b","t":"‘“The Athravans who read and the pupils of the Athravans"},{"ref":"33.86c","t":"will beg of thee knowledge and prosperity, the Victory made by"},{"ref":"33.86d","t":"Ahura, and the crushing Ascendant."},{"ref":"33.87","t":"‘“The maids of barren womb, longing for a lord, will"},{"ref":"33.87a","t":"beg of thee a strong husband;"},{"ref":"33.87b","t":"‘“Women, on the point of bringing forth, will beg of thee"},{"ref":"33.87c","t":"a good delivery."},{"ref":"33.87d","t":"‘“All this wilt thou grant unto them, as it lies in thy power,"},{"ref":"33.87e","t":"O Ardvi Sura Anahita!”"},{"ref":"33.88","t":"‘Then Ardvi Sura Anahita came forth, O Zarathushtra! down"},{"ref":"33.88a","t":"from those stars to the earth made by Mazda; and Ardvi Sura Anahita"},{"ref":"33.88b","t":"spake thus:"},{"ref":"33.89","t":"‘“O pure, holy Zarathushtra! Ahura Mazda has established"},{"ref":"33.89a","t":"thee as the master of the material world: Ahura Mazda has established"},{"ref":"33.89b","t":"me to keep the whole of the holy creation."},{"ref":"33.89c","t":"‘“Through my brightness and glory flocks and herds and two-legged"},{"ref":"33.89d","t":"men go on, upon the earth: I, forsooth, keep all good things,"},{"ref":"33.89e","t":"made by Mazda, the offspring of the holy principle, just as a"},{"ref":"33.89f","t":"shepherd keeps his flock.”"},{"ref":"33.90","t":"‘Zarathushtra asked Ardvi Sura Anahita: “O Ardvi Sura"},{"ref":"33.90a","t":"Anahita! With what manner of sacrifice shall I worship thee? With"},{"ref":"33.90b","t":"what manner of sacrifice shall I worship and forward thee? So"},{"ref":"33.90c","t":"that Mazda may make thee run down (to the earth), that he may"},{"ref":"33.90d","t":"not make thee run up into the heavens, above the sun; and that"},{"ref":"33.90e","t":"the Serpent may not injure thee with.... with.... with...."},{"ref":"33.90f","t":"and.... poisons.”"},{"ref":"33.91","t":"‘Ardvi Sura Anahita answered: “O pure, holy Spitama!"},{"ref":"33.91a","t":"this is the sacrifice wherewith thou shalt worship me, this is"},{"ref":"33.91b","t":"the sacrifice wherewith thou shalt worship and forward me, from"},{"ref":"33.91c","t":"the time when the sun is rising to the time when the sun is setting."},{"ref":"33.91d","t":"‘“Of this libation of mine thou shalt drink, thou who art"},{"ref":"33.91e","t":"an Athravan, who hast asked and learnt the revealed law, who art"},{"ref":"33.91f","t":"wise, clever, and the Word incarnate."},{"ref":"33.92","t":"‘“Of this libation of mine let no foe drink, no man fever-sick,"},{"ref":"33.92a","t":"no liar, no coward, no jealous one, no woman, no faithful one"},{"ref":"33.92b","t":"who does not sing the Gathas, no leper to be confined."},{"ref":"33.93","t":"‘“I do not accept those libations that are drunk in my"},{"ref":"33.93a","t":"honor by the blind, by the deaf, by the wicked, by the destroyers,"},{"ref":"33.93b","t":"by the niggards, by the.... nor any of those stamped with those"},{"ref":"33.93c","t":"characters which have no strength for the holy Word."},{"ref":"33.93d","t":"‘“Let no one drink of these my libations who is hump-backed"},{"ref":"33.93e","t":"or bulged forward; no fiend with decayed teeth.”"},{"ref":"33.94","t":"‘Then Zarathushtra asked Ardvi Sura Anahita: “O Ardvi"},{"ref":"33.94a","t":"Sura Anahita! What becomes of those libations which the wicked"},{"ref":"33.94b","t":"worshippers of the Daevas bring unto thee after the sun has set?”"},{"ref":"33.95","t":"‘Ardvi Sura Anahita answered: “O pure, holy Spitama Zarathushtra!"},{"ref":"33.95a","t":"howling, clapping, hopping, and shouting, six hundred and a thousand"},{"ref":"33.95b","t":"Daevas, who ought not to receive that sacrifice, receive those"},{"ref":"33.95c","t":"libations that men bring unto me after [the sun has set].”"},{"ref":"33.96","t":"‘I will worship the height Hukairya, of the deep precipices,"},{"ref":"33.96a","t":"made of gold, wherefrom this mine Ardvi Sura Anahita leaps, from"},{"ref":"33.96b","t":"a hundred times the height of a man, while she is possessed of"},{"ref":"33.96c","t":"as much Glory as the whole of the waters that run along the earth,"},{"ref":"33.96d","t":"and she runs powerfully."},{"ref":"33.96e","t":"‘For her brightness and glory, I will offer her a sacrifice...."},{"ref":"33.97","t":"<span class=\"hv-secn\">XXII.<\/span> ‘Offer up a sacrifice, O Spitama Zarathushtra! unto this spring"},{"ref":"33.97a","t":"of mine, Ardvi Sura Anahita...."},{"ref":"33.98","t":"‘Before whom the worshippers of Mazda stand with baresma in"},{"ref":"33.98a","t":"their hands: the Hvovas did worship her, the Naotaras did worship"},{"ref":"33.98b","t":"her; the Hvovas asked for riches, the Naotaras asked for swift"},{"ref":"33.98c","t":"horses. Quickly was Hvova blessed with riches an full prosperity;"},{"ref":"33.98d","t":"quickly became Vishtaspa, the Naotaride, the lord of the swiftest"},{"ref":"33.98e","t":"horses in these countries."},{"ref":"33.99","t":"[‘Ardvi Sura Anahita granted them that boon, as they were"},{"ref":"33.99a","t":"offering up libations, giving gifts, sacrificing, and entreating"},{"ref":"33.99b","t":"that she would grant them that boon.]"},{"ref":"33.99c","t":"‘For her brightness and glory, I will offer her a sacrifice...."},{"ref":"33.100","t":"<span class=\"hv-secn\">XXIII.<\/span> ‘Offer up a sacrifice, O Spitama Zarathushtra! unto this spring"},{"ref":"33.100a","t":"of mine, Ardvi Sura Anahita...."},{"ref":"33.101","t":"‘Who has a thousand cells and a thousand channels: the extent"},{"ref":"33.101a","t":"of each of those cells, of each of those channels, is as much"},{"ref":"33.101b","t":"as a man can ride in forty days, riding on a good horse. In each"},{"ref":"33.101c","t":"channel there stands a palace, well-founded, shining with a hundred"},{"ref":"33.101d","t":"windows, with a thousand columns, well-built, with ten thousand"},{"ref":"33.101e","t":"balconies, and mighty."},{"ref":"33.102","t":"‘In each of those palaces there lies a well-laid, well-scented"},{"ref":"33.102a","t":"bed, covered with pillows, and Ardvi Sura Anahita, O Zarathushtra!"},{"ref":"33.102b","t":"runs down there from a thousand times the height of a man, and"},{"ref":"33.102c","t":"she is possessed of as much Glory as the whole of the waters that"},{"ref":"33.102d","t":"run along the earth, and she runs powerfully."},{"ref":"33.103","t":"<span class=\"hv-secn\">XXIV.<\/span> ‘Offer up a sacrifice, O Spitama Zarathushtra! unto this spring"},{"ref":"33.103a","t":"of mine, Ardvi Sura Anahita...."},{"ref":"33.104","t":"‘Unto her did the holy Zarathushtra offer up a sacrifice in"},{"ref":"33.104a","t":"the Airyana Vaejah, by the good river Daitya; with the Haoma and"},{"ref":"33.104b","t":"meat, with the baresma, with the wisdom of the tongue, with the"},{"ref":"33.104c","t":"holy spells, with the speech, with the deeds, with the libations,"},{"ref":"33.104d","t":"and with the rightly-spoken words."},{"ref":"33.105","t":"‘He begged of her a boon, saying: “Grant me this, O good,"},{"ref":"33.105a","t":"most beneficent Ardvi Sura Anahita! that I may bring the son of"},{"ref":"33.105b","t":"Aurvat-aspa, the valiant Kavi Vistaspa, to think according to"},{"ref":"33.105c","t":"the law, to speak according to the law, to do according to the"},{"ref":"33.105d","t":"law.”"},{"ref":"33.106","t":"‘Ardvi Sura Anahita granted him that boon, as he was"},{"ref":"33.106a","t":"offering up libations, giving gifts, sacrificing, and entreating"},{"ref":"33.106b","t":"that she would grant him that boon."},{"ref":"33.106c","t":"‘For her brightness and glory, I will offer her a sacrifice...."},{"ref":"33.107","t":"<span class=\"hv-secn\">XXV.<\/span> ‘Offer up a sacrifice, O Spitama Zarathushtra! unto this spring"},{"ref":"33.107a","t":"of mine, Ardvi Sura Anahita...."},{"ref":"33.108","t":"‘Unto her did the tall Kavi Vishtaspa offer up a sacrifice"},{"ref":"33.108a","t":"behind Lake Frazdanava, with a hundred male horses, a thousand"},{"ref":"33.108b","t":"oxen, ten thousand lambs."},{"ref":"33.109","t":"‘He begged of her a boon, saying: “Grant me this, O good,"},{"ref":"33.109a","t":"most beneficent Ardvi Sura Anahita! that I may overcome Tathravant,"},{"ref":"33.109b","t":"of the bad law, and Peshana, the worshipper of the Daevas and"},{"ref":"33.109c","t":"the wicked Arejat-aspa, in the battles of this world!”"},{"ref":"33.110","t":"‘Ardvi Sura Anahita granted him that boon, as he was offering"},{"ref":"33.110a","t":"up libations, giving gifts, sacrificing, and entreating that she"},{"ref":"33.110b","t":"would grant him that boon."},{"ref":"33.110c","t":"‘For her brightness and glory, I will offer her a sacrifice...."},{"ref":"33.111","t":"<span class=\"hv-secn\">XXVI.<\/span> ‘Offer up a sacrifice, O Spitama Zarathushtra! unto this spring"},{"ref":"33.111a","t":"of mine, Ardvi Sura Anahita...."},{"ref":"33.112","t":"‘Unto her did Zairi-vairi, who fought on horseback, offer"},{"ref":"33.112a","t":"up a sacrifice behind the river Daitya, with a hundred male horses,"},{"ref":"33.112b","t":"a thousand oxen, ten thousand lambs."},{"ref":"33.113","t":"‘He begged of her a boon, saying: “Grant me this, O good,"},{"ref":"33.113a","t":"most beneficent Ardvi Sura Anahita! that I may overcome Pesho-Changha"},{"ref":"33.113b","t":"the corpse-burier, Humayaka the worshipper of the Daevas, and"},{"ref":"33.113c","t":"the wicked Arejat-aspa, in the battles of this world."},{"ref":"33.114","t":"‘Ardvi Sura Anahita granted him that boon, as he was"},{"ref":"33.114a","t":"offering up libations, giving gifts, sacrificing, and entreating"},{"ref":"33.114b","t":"that she would grant him that boon."},{"ref":"33.114c","t":"‘For her brightness and glory, I will offer her a sacrifice...."},{"ref":"33.115","t":"<span class=\"hv-secn\">XXVII.<\/span> ‘Offer up a sacrifice, O Spitama Zarathushtra! unto this spring"},{"ref":"33.115a","t":"of mine, Ardvi Sura Anahita...."},{"ref":"33.116","t":"‘Unto her did Arejat-aspa and Vandaremaini offer up a sacrifice"},{"ref":"33.116a","t":"by the sea Vouru-Kasha, with a hundred male horses, a thousand"},{"ref":"33.116b","t":"oxen, ten thousand lambs."},{"ref":"33.117","t":"‘They begged of her a boon, saying: “Grant us this, O"},{"ref":"33.117a","t":"good, most beneficent Ardvi Sura Anahita! that we may conquer"},{"ref":"33.117b","t":"the valiant Kavi Vishtaspa and Zairivairi who fights on horseback,"},{"ref":"33.117c","t":"and that we may smite of the Aryan people their fifties and their"},{"ref":"33.117d","t":"hundreds, their hundreds and their thousands, their thousands"},{"ref":"33.117e","t":"and their tens of thousands, their tens of thousands and their"},{"ref":"33.117f","t":"myriads of myriads.”"},{"ref":"33.118","t":"‘Ardvi Sura Anahita did not grant them that favor, though"},{"ref":"33.118a","t":"they were offering up libations, giving gifts, sacrificing, and"},{"ref":"33.118b","t":"entreating that she should grant them that favor."},{"ref":"33.118c","t":"‘For her brightness and glory, I will offer her a sacrifice...."},{"ref":"33.119","t":"<span class=\"hv-secn\">XXVIII.<\/span> ‘Offer up a sacrifice, O Spitama Zarathushtra! unto this spring"},{"ref":"33.119a","t":"of mine, Ardvi Sura Anahita...."},{"ref":"33.120","t":"‘For whom Ahura Mazda has made four horses — the wind,"},{"ref":"33.120a","t":"the rain, the cloud, and the sleet — and thus ever a upon the"},{"ref":"33.120b","t":"earth it is raining, snowing, hailing, and sleeting; and whose"},{"ref":"33.120c","t":"armies are so many and numbered by nine-hundreds and thousands."},{"ref":"33.121","t":"‘I will worship the height Hukairya, of the deep precipices,"},{"ref":"33.121a","t":"made of gold, wherefrom this mine Ardvi Sura Anahita leaps, from"},{"ref":"33.121b","t":"a hundred times the height of a man, while she is possessed of"},{"ref":"33.121c","t":"as much Glory as the whole of the waters that run along the earth,"},{"ref":"33.121d","t":"and she runs powerfully."},{"ref":"33.121e","t":"‘For her brightness and glory, I will offer her a sacrifice...."},{"ref":"33.122","t":"<span class=\"hv-secn\">XXIX.<\/span> ‘Offer up a sacrifice, O Spitama Zarathushtra! unto this spring"},{"ref":"33.122a","t":"of mine, Ardvi Sura Anahita...."},{"ref":"33.123","t":"‘She stands, the good Ardvi Sura Anahita, wearing a golden"},{"ref":"33.123a","t":"mantle, waiting for a man who shall offer her libations and prayers,"},{"ref":"33.123b","t":"and thinking thus in her heart:"},{"ref":"33.124","t":"“‘Who will praise me? Who will offer me a sacrifice,"},{"ref":"33.124a","t":"with libations cleanly prepared and well-strained, together with"},{"ref":"33.124b","t":"the Haoma and meat? To whom shall I cleave, who cleaves unto me,"},{"ref":"33.124c","t":"and thinks with me, and bestows gifts upon, me, and is of good"},{"ref":"33.124d","t":"will unto me?”"},{"ref":"33.124e","t":"‘For her brightness and glory, I will offer her a sacrifice...."},{"ref":"33.125","t":"<span class=\"hv-secn\">XXX.<\/span> ‘Offer up a sacrifice, O Spitama Zarathushtra! unto this spring"},{"ref":"33.125a","t":"of mine, Ardvi Sura Anahita...."},{"ref":"33.126","t":"‘Ardvi Sura Anahita, who stands carried forth in the shape"},{"ref":"33.126a","t":"of a maid, fair of body, most strong, tall-formed, high-girded,"},{"ref":"33.126b","t":"pure, nobly born of a glorious race, wearing along her.... a mantle"},{"ref":"33.126c","t":"fully embroidered with gold;"},{"ref":"33.127","t":"‘Ever holding the baresma in her hand, according to the rules,"},{"ref":"33.127a","t":"she wears square golden earrings on her ears bored, and a golden"},{"ref":"33.127b","t":"necklace around her beautiful neck, she, the nobly born Ardvi"},{"ref":"33.127c","t":"Sura Anahita; and she girded her waist tightly, so that her breasts"},{"ref":"33.127d","t":"may be well-shaped, that they may be tightly pressed."},{"ref":"33.128","t":"‘Upon her head Ardvi Sura Anahita bound a golden crown, with"},{"ref":"33.128a","t":"a hundred stars, with eight rays, a fine.... a well-made crown,"},{"ref":"33.128b","t":"in the shape of a.... with fillets streaming down."},{"ref":"33.129","t":"‘She is clothed with garments of beaver, Ardvi Sura Anahita;"},{"ref":"33.129a","t":"with the skin of thirty beavers of those that bear four young"},{"ref":"33.129b","t":"ones, that are the finest kind of beavers; for the skin of the"},{"ref":"33.129c","t":"beaver that lives in water is the finest-colored of all skins,"},{"ref":"33.129d","t":"and when worked at the right time it shines to the eye with full"},{"ref":"33.129e","t":"sheen of silver and gold."},{"ref":"33.130","t":"‘Here, O good, most beneficent Ardvi Sura Anahita! I beg of"},{"ref":"33.130a","t":"thee this favor: that I, fully blessed, may conquer large kingdoms,"},{"ref":"33.130b","t":"rich in horses, with high tributes, with snorting horses, sounding"},{"ref":"33.130c","t":"chariots, flashing swords, rich in aliments, with stores of food,"},{"ref":"33.130d","t":"with well-scented beds; that I may have at my wish the fullness"},{"ref":"33.130e","t":"of the good things of life and whatever makes a kingdom thrive."},{"ref":"33.131","t":"‘Here, O good, most beneficent Ardvi Sura Anahita! I beg of"},{"ref":"33.131a","t":"thee two gallant companions, one two-legged and one four-legged:"},{"ref":"33.131b","t":"one two-legged, who is swift, quickly rushing, and clever in turning"},{"ref":"33.131c","t":"a chariot round in battle; and one four-legged, who can quickly"},{"ref":"33.131d","t":"turn towards either wing of the host with a wide front, towards"},{"ref":"33.131e","t":"the right wing or the left, towards the left wing or the right."},{"ref":"33.132","t":"‘Through the strength of this sacrifice, of this invocation,"},{"ref":"33.132a","t":"O Ardvi Sura Anahita! come down from those stars, towards the"},{"ref":"33.132b","t":"earth made by Ahura, towards the sacrificing priest, towards the"},{"ref":"33.132c","t":"full boiling [milk]; come to help him who is offering up libations"},{"ref":"33.132d","t":"giving gifts, sacrificing, and entreating that thou wouldst grant"},{"ref":"33.132e","t":"him thy favors; that all those gallant warriors may be strong,"},{"ref":"33.132f","t":"like king Vishtaspa."},{"ref":"33.132g","t":"‘For her brightness and glory, I will offer her a sacrifice...."},{"ref":"33.133","t":"‘Yatha ahu vairya: The will of the Lord is the law of holiness...."},{"ref":"33.133a","t":"‘I bless the sacrifice and prayer, and the strength and vigor"},{"ref":"33.133b","t":"of the holy water-spring Anahita."},{"ref":"33.133c","t":"‘Ashem Vohu: Holiness is the best of all good...."},{"ref":"33.133d","t":"‘[Give] unto that man brightness and glory,... give him the"},{"ref":"33.133e","t":"bright, all-happy, blissful abode of the holy Ones!’"},{"sp":"HDR","t":"6. Khwarshed Yasht (Hymn to the Sun)"},{"ref":"34.0","t":"May Ahura Mazda be rejoiced!...."},{"ref":"34.0a","t":"Ashem Vohu: Holiness is the best of all good...."},{"ref":"34.0b","t":"I confess myself a worshipper of Mazda, a follower of Zarathushtra,"},{"ref":"34.0c","t":"one who hates the Daevas and obeys the laws of Ahura;"},{"ref":"34.0d","t":"For sacrifice, prayer, propitiation, and glorification unto [Havani],"},{"ref":"34.0e","t":"the holy and master of holiness...."},{"ref":"34.0f","t":"Unto the undying, shining, swift-horsed Sun;"},{"ref":"34.0g","t":"Be propitiation, with sacrifice, prayer, propitiation, and glorification."},{"ref":"34.0h","t":"Yatha ahu vairyo: The will of the Lord is the law of holiness...."},{"ref":"34.1","t":"We sacrifice unto the undying, shining, swift-horsed Sun."},{"ref":"34.1a","t":"When the light of the sun waxes warmer, when the brightness of"},{"ref":"34.1b","t":"the sun waxes warmer, then up stand the heavenly Yazatas, by hundreds"},{"ref":"34.1c","t":"and thousands: they gather together its Glory, they make its Glory"},{"ref":"34.1d","t":"pass down, they pour its Glory upon the earth made by Ahura, for"},{"ref":"34.1e","t":"the increase of the world of holiness, for the increase of the"},{"ref":"34.1f","t":"creatures of holiness, for the increase of the undying, shining,"},{"ref":"34.1g","t":"swift-horsed Sun."},{"ref":"34.2","t":"And when the sun rises up, then the earth, made by Ahura,"},{"ref":"34.2a","t":"becomes clean; the running waters become clean, the waters of"},{"ref":"34.2b","t":"the wells become clean, the waters of the sea become clean, the"},{"ref":"34.2c","t":"standing waters become clean; all the holy creatures, the creatures"},{"ref":"34.2d","t":"of the Good Spirit, become clean."},{"ref":"34.3","t":"Should not the sun rise up, then the Daevas would destroy"},{"ref":"34.3a","t":"all the things that are in the seven Karshvares, nor would the"},{"ref":"34.3b","t":"heavenly Yazatas find any way of withstanding or repelling them"},{"ref":"34.3c","t":"in the material world."},{"ref":"34.4","t":"He who offers up a sacrifice unto the undying, shining, swift-horsed"},{"ref":"34.4a","t":"Sun - to withstand darkness, to withstand the Daevas born of darkness,"},{"ref":"34.4b","t":"to withstand the robbers and bandits, to withstand the Yatus and"},{"ref":"34.4c","t":"Pairikas, to withstand death that creeps in unseen - offers it"},{"ref":"34.4d","t":"up to Ahura Mazda, offers it up to the Amesha-Spentas, offers"},{"ref":"34.4e","t":"it up to his own soul. He rejoices all the heavenly and worldly"},{"ref":"34.4f","t":"Yazatas, who offers up a sacrifice unto the undying, shining,"},{"ref":"34.4g","t":"swift-horsed Sun."},{"ref":"34.5","t":"I will sacrifice unto Mithra, the lord of wide pastures, who"},{"ref":"34.5a","t":"has a thousand ears, ten thousand eyes."},{"ref":"34.5b","t":"I will sacrifice unto the club of Mithra, the lord of wide pastures,"},{"ref":"34.5c","t":"well struck down upon the skulls of the Daevas."},{"ref":"34.5d","t":"I will sacrifice unto that friendship, the best of all friendships,"},{"ref":"34.5e","t":"that reigns between the moon and the sun."},{"ref":"34.6","t":"For his brightness and glory, I will offer unto him a sacrifice"},{"ref":"34.6a","t":"worth being heard, namely, unto the undying, shining, swift-horsed"},{"ref":"34.6b","t":"Sun. Unto the undying, shining, swift-horsed Sun we offer up the"},{"ref":"34.6c","t":"libations, the Haoma and meat, the baresma, the wisdom of the"},{"ref":"34.6d","t":"tongue, the holy spells, the speech, the deeds, the libations,"},{"ref":"34.6e","t":"and the rightly-spoken words."},{"ref":"34.6f","t":"Yenghe hatam: All those beings of whom Ahura Mazda...."},{"ref":"34.7","t":"Yatha ahu vairyo: The will of the Lord is the law of holiness...."},{"ref":"34.7a","t":"I bless the sacrifice and the invocation, and the strength and"},{"ref":"34.7b","t":"vigour of the undying, shining, swift-horsed Sun."},{"ref":"34.7c","t":"Ashem Vohu: Holiness is the best of all good...."},{"ref":"34.7d","t":"Give unto that man brightness and glory, give him health of body,"},{"ref":"34.7e","t":".... give him the bright, all-happy, blissful abode of the holy"},{"ref":"34.7f","t":"Ones."},{"sp":"HDR","t":"7. Mah Yasht (Hymn to the Moon)"},{"ref":"35.0","t":"May Ahura Mazda be rejoiced!...."},{"ref":"35.0a","t":"Ashem Vohu: Holiness is the best of all good...."},{"ref":"35.0b","t":"I confess myself a worshipper of Mazda, a follower of Zarathushtra,"},{"ref":"35.0c","t":"one who hates the Daevas and obeys the laws of Ahura;"},{"ref":"35.0d","t":"For sacrifice, prayer, propitiation, and glorification unto [Havani],","hvShift6":[[0,0],[14,15]]},{"ref":"35.0e","t":"the holy and master of holiness...."},{"ref":"35.0f","t":"Unto the Moon that keeps in it the seed of the Bull; unto the"},{"ref":"35.0g","t":"only-created Bull and unto the Bull of many species;"},{"ref":"35.0h","t":"Be propitiation, with sacrifice, prayer, propitiation, and glorification."},{"ref":"35.0i","t":"Yatha ahu vairyo: The will of the Lord is the law of holiness...."},{"ref":"35.1","t":"Hail to Ahura Mazda! Hail to the Amesha-Spentas! Hail to the"},{"ref":"35.1a","t":"Moon that keeps in it the seed of the Bull! Hail to thee when"},{"ref":"35.1b","t":"we look at thee! Hail to thee when thou lookest at us!"},{"ref":"35.2","t":"How does the moon wax? How does the moon wane?"},{"ref":"35.2a","t":"For fifteen days does the moon wax; for fifteen days does the"},{"ref":"35.2b","t":"moon wane. As long as her waxing, so long is the waning; as long"},{"ref":"35.2c","t":"as her waning, so long is the waxing."},{"ref":"35.2d","t":"‘Who is there but thee who makes the moon wax and wane?’"},{"ref":"35.3","t":"We sacrifice unto the Moon that keeps in it the seed of the"},{"ref":"35.3a","t":"Bull, the holy and master of holiness."},{"ref":"35.3b","t":"Here I look at the moon, here I perceive the moon; here I look"},{"ref":"35.3c","t":"at the light of the moon, here I perceive the light of the moon."},{"ref":"35.3d","t":"The Amesha-Spentas stand up holding its glory; the Amesha-Spentas"},{"ref":"35.3e","t":"stand up, pouring its glory upon the earth, made by Mazda."},{"ref":"35.4","t":"And when the light of the moon waxes warmer, golden-hued plants"},{"ref":"35.4a","t":"grow on from the earth during the spring."},{"ref":"35.4b","t":"We sacrifice unto the new moons, the full moons, and the Vishaptathas."},{"ref":"35.4c","t":"We sacrifice unto the new moon, the holy and master of holiness;"},{"ref":"35.4d","t":"We sacrifice unto the full moon, the holy and master of holiness;"},{"ref":"35.4e","t":"We sacrifice unto the Vishaptatha, the holy and master of holiness."},{"ref":"35.5","t":"I will sacrifice unto the Moon, that keeps in it the seed"},{"ref":"35.5a","t":"of the Bull, the liberal, bright, glorious, water-giving, warmth-giving,"},{"ref":"35.5b","t":"wisdom-giving, wealth-giving, riches-giving, thoughtfulness-giving,"},{"ref":"35.5c","t":"weal-giving, freshness-giving, prosperity-giving, the liberal,"},{"ref":"35.5d","t":"the healing."},{"ref":"35.6","t":"For its brightness and glory, I will offer unto it a sacrifice"},{"ref":"35.6a","t":"worth being heard, namely, unto the Moon that keeps in it the"},{"ref":"35.6b","t":"seed of the Bull."},{"ref":"35.6c","t":"Unto the Moon that keeps in it the seed of the Bull, we offer"},{"ref":"35.6d","t":"up the libations, the Haoma and meat, the baresma, the wisdom"},{"ref":"35.6e","t":"of the tongue, the holy spells, the speech, the deeds, the libations,"},{"ref":"35.6f","t":"and the rightly-spoken words."},{"ref":"35.6g","t":"Yenghe hatam: All those beings of whom Ahura Mazda...."},{"ref":"35.7","t":"Yatha ahu vairyo: The will of the Lord is the law of holiness...."},{"ref":"35.7a","t":"I bless the sacrifice and prayer, and the strength and vigour"},{"ref":"35.7b","t":"of the Moon, that keeps in it the seed of the Bull, and of the"},{"ref":"35.7c","t":"only-created Bull, and of the Bull of many species."},{"ref":"35.7d","t":"Ashem Vohu: Holiness is the best of all good."},{"ref":"35.7e","t":"Give unto that man brightness and glory, give him health of body,"},{"ref":"35.7f","t":".... give him the bright, all-happy, blissful abode of the holy"},{"ref":"35.7g","t":"Ones."},{"sp":"HDR","t":"8. Tishtar Yasht (Hymn to the Star Sirius)"},{"ref":"36.1","t":"(Tishtrya is the angel (Yazad) of the star Sirius. Tishtrya also"},{"ref":"36.2","t":"presides over the fourth month and the thirteenth day of each month."},{"ref":"36.3","t":"Sirius also directs the rain.)"},{"ref":"36.0","t":"May Ahura Mazda be rejoiced!...."},{"ref":"36.0a","t":"Ashem Vohu: Holiness is the best of all good...."},{"ref":"36.0b","t":"I confess myself a worshipper of Mazda, a follower of Zarathushtra,"},{"ref":"36.0c","t":"one who hates the Daevas and obeys the laws of Ahura;"},{"ref":"36.0d","t":"For sacrifice, prayer, propitiation, and glorification unto [Havani],"},{"ref":"36.0e","t":"the holy and master of holiness...."},{"ref":"36.0f","t":"Unto Tishtrya, the bright and glorious star, and unto the powerful"},{"ref":"36.0g","t":"Satavaesa, made by Mazda, who pushes waters forward,"},{"ref":"36.0h","t":"Be propitiation, with sacrifice, prayer, propitiation, and glorification."},{"ref":"36.0i","t":"Yatha ahu vairyo: The will of the Lord is the law of holiness...."},{"ref":"36.1a","t":"Ahura Mazda spake unto Spitama Zarathushtra, saying: ‘We worship"},{"ref":"36.1aa","t":"the lordship and mastership [of Tishtrya], whereby he protects"},{"ref":"36.1b","t":"the Moon, the dwelling, the food, when my glorious stars come"},{"ref":"36.1c","t":"along and impart their gifts to men. I will sacrifice unto the"},{"ref":"36.1d","t":"star Tishtrya, that gives the fields their share [of waters]."},{"ref":"36.2a","t":"‘We offer up libations unto Tishtrya, the bright and glorious"},{"ref":"36.2aa","t":"star, that gives happy dwelling and good dwelling; the white,"},{"ref":"36.2b","t":"shining, seen afar, and piercing; the health-bringing, loud-snorting,"},{"ref":"36.2c","t":"and high, piercing from afar with its shining, undefiled rays;"},{"ref":"36.2d","t":"and unto the waters of the wide sea, the Vanguhi of wide renown,"},{"ref":"36.2e","t":"and the species of the Bull, made by Mazda, the awful kingly Glory,"},{"ref":"36.2f","t":"and the Fravashi of the holy Spitama Zarathushtra."},{"ref":"36.3a","t":"‘For his brightness and glory, I will offer unto him a sacrifice"},{"ref":"36.3aa","t":"worth being heard, namely, unto the star Tishtrya."},{"ref":"36.3b","t":"‘Unto Tishtrya, the bright and glorious star, we offer up the"},{"ref":"36.3c","t":"libations, the Haoma and meat, the baresma, the wisdom of the"},{"ref":"36.3d","t":"tongue, the holy spells, the speech, the deeds, the libations,"},{"ref":"36.3e","t":"and the rightly-spoken words."},{"ref":"36.3f","t":"‘Yenhe hatam: All those beings of whom Ahura Mazda...."},{"ref":"36.4","t":"‘We sacrifice unto Tishtrya, the bright and glorious star,"},{"ref":"36.4a","t":"who is the seed of the waters, powerful, tall, and strong, whose"},{"ref":"36.4b","t":"light goes afar; powerful and highly working, through whom the"},{"ref":"36.4c","t":"brightness and the seed of the waters come from the high Apam"},{"ref":"36.4d","t":"Napat."},{"ref":"36.4e","t":"‘For his brightness and glory, I will offer him a sacrifice worth"},{"ref":"36.4f","t":"being heard...."},{"ref":"36.5","t":"‘We sacrifice unto Tishtrya, the bright and glorious star;"},{"ref":"36.5a","t":"for whom long flocks and herds and men, looking forward for him"},{"ref":"36.5b","t":"and deceived in their hope: “When shall we see him rise up,"},{"ref":"36.5c","t":"the bright and glorious star Tishtrya? When will the springs run"},{"ref":"36.5d","t":"with waves as thick as a horse’s size and still thicker? Or will"},{"ref":"36.5e","t":"they never come?”"},{"ref":"36.5f","t":"‘For his brightness and glory, I will offer him a sacrifice worth"},{"ref":"36.5g","t":"being heard...."},{"ref":"36.6","t":"‘We sacrifice unto Tishtrya, the bright and glorious star;"},{"ref":"36.6a","t":"who flies, towards the sea Vouru-Kasha, as swiftly as the arrow"},{"ref":"36.6b","t":"darted through the heavenly space, which Erekhsha, the swift archer,"},{"ref":"36.6c","t":"the Arya amongst the Aryas whose arrow was the swiftest, shot"},{"ref":"36.6d","t":"from Mount Khshaotha to Mount Hvanvant."},{"ref":"36.7","t":"‘For Ahura Mazda gave him assistance; so did the waters and"},{"ref":"36.7a","t":"the plants; and Mithra, the lord of wide pastures, opened a wide"},{"ref":"36.7b","t":"way unto him."},{"ref":"36.7c","t":"‘For his brightness and glory, I will offer him a sacrifice worth"},{"ref":"36.7d","t":"being heard...."},{"ref":"36.8","t":"‘We sacrifice unto Tishtrya, the bright and glorious star,"},{"ref":"36.8a","t":"that afflicts the Pairikas, that vexes the Pairikas, who, in the"},{"ref":"36.8b","t":"shape of worm-stars, fly between the earth and the heavens, in"},{"ref":"36.8c","t":"the sea Vouru-Kasha, the powerful sea, the large-sized, deep sea"},{"ref":"36.8d","t":"of salt waters. He goes to its lake in the shape of a horse, in"},{"ref":"36.8e","t":"a holy shape; and down there he makes the waters boil over, and"},{"ref":"36.8f","t":"the winds flow above powerfully all around."},{"ref":"36.9","t":"‘Then Satavaesa makes those waters flow down to the seven"},{"ref":"36.9a","t":"Karshvares of the earth, and when he has arrived down there, he"},{"ref":"36.9b","t":"stands, beautiful, spreading ease and joy on the fertile countries"},{"ref":"36.9c","t":"(thinking in himself): “How shall the countries of the Aryas"},{"ref":"36.9d","t":"grow fertile?”"},{"ref":"36.9e","t":"‘For his brightness and glory, I will offer him a sacrifice worth"},{"ref":"36.9f","t":"being heard...."},{"ref":"36.10","t":"‘We sacrifice unto Tishtrya, the bright and glorious star,"},{"ref":"36.10a","t":"who spoke unto Ahura Mazda, saying: “Ahura Mazda, most beneficent"},{"ref":"36.10b","t":"Spirit, Maker of the material world, thou Holy One!"},{"ref":"36.11","t":"‘“If men would worship me with a sacrifice in which I"},{"ref":"36.11a","t":"were invoked by my own name, as they worship the other Yazatas"},{"ref":"36.11b","t":"with sacrifices in which they are invoked by their own names,"},{"ref":"36.11c","t":"then I should have come to the faithful at the appointed time;"},{"ref":"36.11d","t":"I should have come in the appointed time of my beautiful, immortal"},{"ref":"36.11e","t":"life, should it be one night, or two nights, or fifty, or a hundred"},{"ref":"36.11f","t":"nights.”"},{"ref":"36.12","t":"‘We sacrifice unto Tishtrya;"},{"ref":"36.12a","t":"‘We sacrifice unto the rains of Tishtrya."},{"ref":"36.12b","t":"‘We sacrifice unto the first star; we sacrifice unto the rains"},{"ref":"36.12c","t":"of the first star."},{"ref":"36.12d","t":"‘I will sacrifice unto the stars Haptoiringa, to oppose the Yatus"},{"ref":"36.12e","t":"and Pairikas."},{"ref":"36.12f","t":"‘We sacrifice unto Vanant, the star made by Mazda; for the well-shapen"},{"ref":"36.12g","t":"strength, for the Victory, made by Ahura, for the crushing Ascendant,"},{"ref":"36.12h","t":"for the destruction of what distresses us, for the destruction"},{"ref":"36.12i","t":"of what persecutes us."},{"ref":"36.12j","t":"‘We sacrifice unto Tishtrya, whose eye-sight is sound."},{"ref":"36.13","t":"‘For ten nights, O Spitama Zarathushtra! Tishtrya, the bright"},{"ref":"36.13a","t":"and glorious star, mingles his shape with light, moving in the"},{"ref":"36.13b","t":"shape of a man of fifteen years of age, bright, with clear eyes,"},{"ref":"36.13c","t":"tall, full of strength, strong, and clever."},{"ref":"36.14","t":"‘He is active as the first man was; he goes on with the strength"},{"ref":"36.14a","t":"of the first man; he has the virility of the first man."},{"ref":"36.15","t":"‘Here he calls for people to assemble, here he asks, saying:"},{"ref":"36.15a","t":"“Who now will offer me the libations with the Haoma and the"},{"ref":"36.15b","t":"holy meat? To whom shall I give wealth of male children, a troop"},{"ref":"36.15c","t":"of male children, and the purification of his own soul? Now I"},{"ref":"36.15d","t":"ought to receive sacrifice and prayer in the material world, by"},{"ref":"36.15e","t":"the law of excellent holiness.”"},{"ref":"36.16","t":"‘The next ten nights, O Spitama Zarathushtra! the bright and"},{"ref":"36.16a","t":"glorious Tishtrya mingles his shape with light, moving in the"},{"ref":"36.16b","t":"shape of a golden-horned bull."},{"ref":"36.17","t":"‘Here he calls for people to assemble, here he asks, saying:"},{"ref":"36.17a","t":"“Who now will offer me the libations with the Haoma and the"},{"ref":"36.17b","t":"holy meat? To whom shall I give wealth of oxen, a herd of oxen,"},{"ref":"36.17c","t":"and the purification of his own soul? Now I ought to receive sacrifice"},{"ref":"36.17d","t":"and prayer in the material world, by the law of excellent holiness.”"},{"ref":"36.18","t":"‘The next ten nights, O Spitama Zarathushtra! the bright and"},{"ref":"36.18a","t":"glorious Tishtrya mingles his shape with light, moving in the"},{"ref":"36.18b","t":"shape of a white, beautiful horse, with golden ears and a golden"},{"ref":"36.18c","t":"caparison."},{"ref":"36.19","t":"‘Here he calls for people to assemble, here he asks, saying:"},{"ref":"36.19a","t":"“Who now will offer me the libations with the Haoma and the"},{"ref":"36.19b","t":"holy meat? To whom shall I give wealth of horses, a troop of horses,"},{"ref":"36.19c","t":"and the purification of his own soul? Now I ought to receive sacrifice"},{"ref":"36.19d","t":"and prayer in the material world, by the law of excellent holiness.”"},{"ref":"36.20","t":"‘Then, O Spitama Zarathushtra! the bright and glorious Tishtrya"},{"ref":"36.20a","t":"goes down to the sea Vouru-Kasha in the shape of a white, beautiful"},{"ref":"36.20b","t":"horse, with golden ears and a golden caparison."},{"ref":"36.21","t":"‘But there rushes down to meet him the Daeva Apaosha, in the"},{"ref":"36.21a","t":"shape of a dark horse, black with black ears, black with a black"},{"ref":"36.21b","t":"back, black with a black tail, stamped with brands of terror."},{"ref":"36.22","t":"‘They meet together, hoof against hoof, O Spitama Zarathushtra!"},{"ref":"36.22a","t":"the bright and glorious Tishtrya and the Daeva Apaosha. They fight"},{"ref":"36.22b","t":"together, O Spitama Zarathushtra! for three days and three nights."},{"ref":"36.22c","t":"And then the Daeva Apaosha proves stronger than the bright and"},{"ref":"36.22d","t":"glorious Tishtrya, he overcomes him."},{"ref":"36.23","t":"‘And Tishtrya flees from the sea Vouru-Kasha, as far as a"},{"ref":"36.23a","t":"Hathra’s length. He cries out in woe and distress, the bright"},{"ref":"36.23b","t":"and glorious Tishtrya: “Woe is me, O Ahura Mazda! I am in"},{"ref":"36.23c","t":"distress, O Waters and Plants! O Fate and thou, Law of the worshippers"},{"ref":"36.23d","t":"of Mazda! Men do not worship me with a sacrifice in which I am"},{"ref":"36.23e","t":"invoked by my own name, as they worship the other Yazatas with"},{"ref":"36.23f","t":"sacrifices in which they are invoked by their own names."},{"ref":"36.24","t":"‘“If men had worshipped me with a sacrifice in which"},{"ref":"36.24a","t":"I had been invoked by my own name, as they worship the other Yazatas"},{"ref":"36.24b","t":"with sacrifices in which they are invoked by their own names,"},{"ref":"36.24c","t":"I should have taken to me the strength of ten horses, the strength"},{"ref":"36.24d","t":"of ten camels, the strength of ten bulls, the strength of ten"},{"ref":"36.24e","t":"mountains, the strength of ten rivers.”"},{"ref":"36.25","t":"‘Then I, Ahura Mazda, offer up to the bright and glorious"},{"ref":"36.25a","t":"Tishtrya a sacrifice in which he is invoked by his own name, and"},{"ref":"36.25b","t":"I bring him the strength of ten horses, the strength of ten camels,"},{"ref":"36.25c","t":"the strength of ten bulls, the strength of ten mountains, the"},{"ref":"36.25d","t":"strength of ten rivers."},{"ref":"36.26","t":"‘Then, O Spitama Zarathushtra! the bright and glorious Tishtrya"},{"ref":"36.26a","t":"goes down to the sea Vouru-Kasha in the shape of a white, beautiful"},{"ref":"36.26b","t":"horse, with golden ears and golden caparison."},{"ref":"36.27","t":"‘But there rushes down to meet him the Daeva Apaosha in the"},{"ref":"36.27a","t":"shape of a dark horse, black with black ears, black with a black"},{"ref":"36.27b","t":"back, black with a black tail, stamped with brands of terror."},{"ref":"36.28","t":"‘They meet together, hoof against hoof, O Spitama Zarathushtra!"},{"ref":"36.28a","t":"the bright and glorious Tishtrya, and the Daeva Apaosha; they"},{"ref":"36.28b","t":"fight together, O Zarathushtra! till the time of noon. Then the"},{"ref":"36.28c","t":"bright and glorious Tishtrya proves stronger than the Daeva Apaosha,"},{"ref":"36.28d","t":"he overcomes him."},{"ref":"36.29","t":"‘Then he goes from the sea Vouru-Kasha as far as a Hathra’s"},{"ref":"36.29a","t":"length: “Hail!” cries the bright and glorious Tishtrya."},{"ref":"36.29b","t":"“Hail unto me, O Ahura Mazda! Hail unto you, O waters and"},{"ref":"36.29c","t":"plants! Hail, O Law of the worshippers of Mazda! Hail will it"},{"ref":"36.29d","t":"be unto you, O lands! The life of the waters will flow down unrestrained"},{"ref":"36.29e","t":"to the big-seeded corn fields, to the small-seeded pasture-fields,"},{"ref":"36.29f","t":"and to the whole of the material world!”"},{"ref":"36.30","t":"Then the bright and glorious Tishtrya goes back down to the"},{"ref":"36.30a","t":"sea Vouru-Kasha, in the shape of a white, beautiful horse, with"},{"ref":"36.30b","t":"golden ears and a golden caparison."},{"ref":"36.31","t":"‘He makes the sea boil up and down; he makes the sea stream"},{"ref":"36.31a","t":"this and that way; he makes the sea flow this and that way: all"},{"ref":"36.31b","t":"the shores of the sea Vouru-Kasha are boiling over, all the middle"},{"ref":"36.31c","t":"of it is boiling over."},{"ref":"36.32","t":"‘And the bright and glorious Tishtrya rises up from the sea"},{"ref":"36.32a","t":"Vouru-Kasha, O Spitama Zarathushtra! the bright and glorious Satavaesa"},{"ref":"36.32b","t":"rises up from the sea Vouru-Kasha; and vapours rise up above Mount"},{"ref":"36.32c","t":"Us-hindu, that stands in the middle of the sea Vouru-Kasha."},{"ref":"36.33","t":"‘Then the vapours push forward, in the regular shape of clouds;"},{"ref":"36.33a","t":"they go following the wind, along the ways which Haoma traverses,"},{"ref":"36.33b","t":"the increaser of the world. Behind him travels the mighty wind,"},{"ref":"36.33c","t":"made by Mazda, and the rain, and the cloud, and the sleet, down"},{"ref":"36.33d","t":"to the several places, down to the fields, down to the seven Karshvares"},{"ref":"36.33e","t":"of the earth."},{"ref":"36.34","t":"‘Apam Napat, O Spitama Zarathushtra! divides the waters amongst"},{"ref":"36.34a","t":"the countries in the material world, in company with the mighty"},{"ref":"36.34b","t":"wind, the Glory, made by the waters, and the Fravashis of the"},{"ref":"36.34c","t":"faithful."},{"ref":"36.34d","t":"‘For his brightness and glory, I will offer him a sacrifice worth"},{"ref":"36.34e","t":"being heard...."},{"ref":"36.35","t":"‘We sacrifice unto Tishtrya, the bright and glorious star,"},{"ref":"36.35a","t":"who from the shining east, moves along his long winding course,"},{"ref":"36.35b","t":"along the path made by the gods, along the way appointed for him"},{"ref":"36.35c","t":"the watery way, at the will of Ahura Mazda, at the will of the"},{"ref":"36.35d","t":"Amesha-Spentas."},{"ref":"36.35e","t":"‘For his brightness and glory, I will offer him a sacrifice worth"},{"ref":"36.35f","t":"being heard...."},{"ref":"36.36","t":"‘We sacrifice unto Tishtrya, the bright and glorious star,"},{"ref":"36.36a","t":"whose rising is watched by men who live on the fruits of the year,"},{"ref":"36.36b","t":"by the chiefs of deep understanding; by the wild beasts in the"},{"ref":"36.36c","t":"mountains, by the tame beasts that run in the plains; they watch"},{"ref":"36.36d","t":"him, as he comes up to the country for a bad year, or for a good"},{"ref":"36.36e","t":"year, (thinking in themselves): “How shall the Aryan countries"},{"ref":"36.36f","t":"be fertile?”"},{"ref":"36.36g","t":"‘For his brightness and glory, I will offer him a sacrifice worth"},{"ref":"36.36h","t":"being heard...."},{"ref":"36.37","t":"‘We sacrifice unto Tishtrya, the bright and glorious star,"},{"ref":"36.37a","t":"swift-flying and swift-moving, who flies towards the sea Vouru-Kasha,"},{"ref":"36.37b","t":"as swiftly as the arrow darted through the heavenly space, which"},{"ref":"36.37c","t":"Erekhsha, the swift archer, the Arya amongst the Aryas whose arrow"},{"ref":"36.37d","t":"was the swiftest, shot from Mount Khshaotha to Mount Hvanvant."},{"ref":"36.38","t":"‘Ahura Mazda gave him assistance, and the Amesha-Spentas and"},{"ref":"36.38a","t":"Mithra, the lord of wide pastures, pointed him the way: behind"},{"ref":"36.38b","t":"him went the tall Ashish Vanguhi and Parendi on her light chariot:"},{"ref":"36.38c","t":"always till, in his course, he reached Mount Hvanvant on the shining"},{"ref":"36.38d","t":"waters."},{"ref":"36.38e","t":"‘For his brightness and glory, I will offer him a sacrifice worth"},{"ref":"36.38f","t":"being heard...."},{"ref":"36.39","t":"‘We sacrifice unto Tishtrya, the bright and glorious star,"},{"ref":"36.39a","t":"who afflicts the Pairikas, who destroys the Pairikas, that Angra"},{"ref":"36.39b","t":"Mainyus flung to stop all the stars that have in them the seed"},{"ref":"36.39c","t":"of the waters."},{"ref":"36.40","t":"’Tishtrya afflicts them, he blows them away from the sea Vouru-Kasha;"},{"ref":"36.40a","t":"then the wind blows the clouds forward, bearing the waters of"},{"ref":"36.40b","t":"fertility, so that the friendly showers spread wide over, they"},{"ref":"36.40c","t":"spread helpingly and friendly over the seven Karshvares."},{"ref":"36.40d","t":"‘For his brightness and glory, I will offer him a sacrifice worth"},{"ref":"36.40e","t":"being heard...."},{"ref":"36.41","t":"‘We sacrifice unto Tishtrya, the bright and glorious star,"},{"ref":"36.41a","t":"for whom long the standing waters, and the running spring-waters,"},{"ref":"36.41b","t":"the stream-waters, and the rain-waters:"},{"ref":"36.42","t":"‘“When will the bright and glorious Tishtrya rise up"},{"ref":"36.42a","t":"for us? When will the springs with a flow and overflow of waters,"},{"ref":"36.42b","t":"thick as a horse’s shoulder, run to the beautiful places and fields,"},{"ref":"36.42c","t":"and to the pastures, even to the roots of the plants, that they"},{"ref":"36.42d","t":"may grow with a powerful growth?”"},{"ref":"36.42e","t":"‘For his brightness and glory, I will offer him a sacrifice worth"},{"ref":"36.42f","t":"being heard...."},{"ref":"36.43","t":"‘We sacrifice unto Tishtrya, the bright and glorious star,"},{"ref":"36.43a","t":"who washes away all things of fear, who stunts the growth of all"},{"ref":"36.43b","t":".... and brings health to all these creations, being most beneficent,"},{"ref":"36.43c","t":"when he has been worshipped with a sacrifice and propitiated,"},{"ref":"36.43d","t":"rejoiced, and satisfied."},{"ref":"36.43e","t":"‘For his brightness and glory, I will offer him a sacrifice worth"},{"ref":"36.43f","t":"being heard...."},{"ref":"36.44","t":"‘I will sacrifice unto Tishtrya, the bright and glorious star,"},{"ref":"36.44a","t":"whom Ahura Mazda has established as a lord and overseer above"},{"ref":"36.44b","t":"all stars, in the same way as he has established Zarathushtra"},{"ref":"36.44c","t":"above men; whom neither Angra Mainyu, nor the Yatus and the Pairikas,"},{"ref":"36.44d","t":"nor the men Yatus can deliver unto death, nor can all the Daevas"},{"ref":"36.44e","t":"together prevail for his death."},{"ref":"36.44f","t":"‘For his brightness and glory, I will offer him a sacrifice worth"},{"ref":"36.44g","t":"being heard...."},{"ref":"36.45","t":"‘We sacrifice unto Tishtrya, the bright and glorious star,"},{"ref":"36.45a","t":"to whom Ahura Mazda has given a thousand senses, and who is the"},{"ref":"36.45b","t":"most beneficent amongst the stars that have in them the seed of"},{"ref":"36.45c","t":"the waters:"},{"ref":"36.46","t":"‘Who moves in light with the stars that have in them the seed"},{"ref":"36.46a","t":"of the waters: he, from the sea Vouru-Kasha, the powerful sea,"},{"ref":"36.46b","t":"the large-sized, deep, and salt of waters, goes to all the lakes,"},{"ref":"36.46c","t":"and to all the beautiful caves, and to all the beautiful channels,"},{"ref":"36.46d","t":"in the shape of a white, beautiful horse, with golden ears and"},{"ref":"36.46e","t":"a golden caparison."},{"ref":"36.47","t":"‘Then, O Spitama Zarathushtra! the waters flow down from the"},{"ref":"36.47a","t":"sea Vouru-Kasha, mother-like, friendly, and healing: he divides"},{"ref":"36.47b","t":"them amongst these countries, being most beneficent, when he has"},{"ref":"36.47c","t":"been worshipped with a sacrifice and propitiated rejoiced, and"},{"ref":"36.47d","t":"satisfied. ‘For his brightness and glory, I will offer him a sacrifice","hvShift6":[[0,0]]},{"ref":"36.47e","t":"worth being heard...."},{"ref":"36.48","t":"‘We sacrifice unto Tishtrya, the bright and glorious star,"},{"ref":"36.48a","t":"for whom long all the creatures of Spenta-Mainyu, those that live"},{"ref":"36.48b","t":"under the ground, and those that live above the ground; those"},{"ref":"36.48c","t":"that live in the waters, and those that live on dry land; those"},{"ref":"36.48d","t":"that fly, and those that run in the plains; and all those that"},{"ref":"36.48e","t":"live within this boundless and endless world of the holy Spirit."},{"ref":"36.48f","t":"‘For his brightness and glory, I will offer him a sacrifice worth"},{"ref":"36.48g","t":"being heard...."},{"ref":"36.49","t":"‘We sacrifice unto Tishtrya, the bright and glorious star,"},{"ref":"36.49a","t":"the healthful, wise, happy, and powerful, who is the lord of a"},{"ref":"36.49b","t":"thousand boons, and grants many boons to that man who has pleased"},{"ref":"36.49c","t":"him, whether begging or not begging for them."},{"ref":"36.50","t":"‘I, O Spitama Zarathushtra! have created that star Tishtrya"},{"ref":"36.50a","t":"as worthy of sacrifice, as worthy of prayer, as worthy of progitiation,"},{"ref":"36.50b","t":"as worthy of glorification as myself, Ahura Mazda;"},{"ref":"36.51","t":"‘In order to withstand, to break asunder, to afflict, to drive"},{"ref":"36.51a","t":"back the malice of that Pairika Duzyairya, whom evil-speaking"},{"ref":"36.51b","t":"people call Huyairya."},{"ref":"36.52","t":"‘Had I not created that star Tishtrya as worthy of sacrifice,"},{"ref":"36.52a","t":"as worthy of prayer, as worthy of propitiation, as worthy of glorification"},{"ref":"36.52b","t":"as myself, Ahura Mazda;"},{"ref":"36.53","t":"‘In order to withstand, to break asunder, to afflict, to drive"},{"ref":"36.53a","t":"back the malice of that Pairika Duzyairya, whom evil-speaking"},{"ref":"36.53b","t":"people call Huyairya;"},{"ref":"36.54","t":"‘Then all day long, all night long, that Pairika Duzyairya"},{"ref":"36.54a","t":"would wage war against this material world of mine, wanting to"},{"ref":"36.54b","t":"extinguish its life, and she goes on, rushing upon and around"},{"ref":"36.54c","t":"it."},{"ref":"36.55","t":"‘But the bright and glorious Tishtrya keeps that Pairika in"},{"ref":"36.55a","t":"bonds, with twofold bonds, with threefold bonds, that cannot be"},{"ref":"36.55b","t":"overcome, with bonds all over the body: it is as if there were"},{"ref":"36.55c","t":"a thousand men keeping one man in bonds, a thousand men of those"},{"ref":"36.55d","t":"who are the strongest in strength."},{"ref":"36.56","t":"‘If the Aryan countries, O Spitama Zarathushtra! would perform"},{"ref":"36.56a","t":"in honour of the bright and glorious Tishtrya the due sacrifice"},{"ref":"36.56b","t":"and invocation, just as that sacrifice and invocation ought to"},{"ref":"36.56c","t":"be performed in the perfection of holiness; never should a hostile"},{"ref":"36.56d","t":"horde enter these Aryan countries, nor any plague, nor leprosy,"},{"ref":"36.56e","t":"nor venomous plants, nor the chariot of a foe, nor the uplifted"},{"ref":"36.56f","t":"spear of a foe.’"},{"ref":"36.57","t":"Zarathushtra asked: ‘What is then, O Ahura Mazda! the sacrifice"},{"ref":"36.57a","t":"and invocation in honour of the bright and glorious Tishtrya,"},{"ref":"36.57b","t":"as it ought to be performed in the perfection of holiness?’"},{"ref":"36.58","t":"Ahura Mazda answered: ‘Let the Aryan nations bring libations"},{"ref":"36.58a","t":"unto him; let the Aryan nations tie bundles of baresma for him;"},{"ref":"36.58b","t":"let the Aryan nations cook for him a head of cattle, either white,"},{"ref":"36.58c","t":"or black, or of any other colour, but all of one and the same"},{"ref":"36.58d","t":"colour."},{"ref":"36.59","t":"‘Let not a murderer take of these offerings, nor a whore,"},{"ref":"36.59a","t":"nor a.... who does not sing the Gathas, who spreads death in"},{"ref":"36.59b","t":"the world and withstands the law of Mazda, the law of Zarathushtra."},{"ref":"36.60","t":"‘If a murderer take of these offerings, or a whore, or a...."},{"ref":"36.60a","t":"who does not sing the Gathas, who spreads death in the world and"},{"ref":"36.60b","t":"withstands the law of Mazda, the law of Zarathushtra, then the"},{"ref":"36.60c","t":"bright and glorious Tishtrya takes back his healing virtues."},{"ref":"36.61","t":"‘Plagues will ever pour upon the Aryan nations; hostile hordes"},{"ref":"36.61a","t":"will ever fall upon the Aryan nations; the Aryans will be smitten,"},{"ref":"36.61b","t":"by their fifties and their hundreds, by their hundreds and their"},{"ref":"36.61c","t":"thousands, by their thousands and their tens of thousands, by","hvShift6":[[0,0]]},{"ref":"36.61d","t":"their tens of thousands and their myriads of myriads."},{"ref":"36.62","t":"‘Yatha ahu vairyo: The will of the Lord is the law of holiness...."},{"ref":"36.62a","t":"‘I bless the sacrifice and prayer, and the strength and vigour"},{"ref":"36.62b","t":"of Tishtrya, the bright and glorious star, and of the powerful"},{"ref":"36.62c","t":"Satavaesa, made by Mazda, who pushes waters forward."},{"ref":"36.62d","t":"‘Ashem Vohu: Holiness is the best of all good...."},{"ref":"36.62e","t":"‘[Give] unto that man brightness and glory,... give him the"},{"ref":"36.62f","t":"bright, all-happy, blissful abode of the holy Ones.’"},{"sp":"HDR","t":"9. Drvasp Yasht"},{"ref":"37.0","t":"May Ahura Mazda be rejoiced! May Angra Mainyu be afflicted!...."},{"ref":"37.0a","t":"Ashem Vohu: Holiness is the best of all good...."},{"ref":"37.0b","t":"I confess myself a worshipper of Mazda, a follower of Zarathushtra,"},{"ref":"37.0c","t":"one who hates the Daevas and obeys the laws of Ahura;"},{"ref":"37.0d","t":"For sacrifice, prayer, satisfaction, and glorification unto Havani,"},{"ref":"37.0e","t":"the holy and master of holiness."},{"ref":"37.0f","t":"Unto the powerful Drvaspa, made by Mazda and holy,"},{"ref":"37.0g","t":"Be propitiation, with sacrifice, prayer, propitiation, and glorification."},{"ref":"37.0h","t":"Yatha ahu vairyo: The will of the Lord is the law of holiness...."},{"ref":"37.1","t":"We sacrifice unto the powerful Drvaspa, made by Mazda and"},{"ref":"37.1a","t":"holy, who heeps the flocks in health, the herds in health, the"},{"ref":"37.1b","t":"grown-up (cattle) in health, the young ones in health; who watches"},{"ref":"37.1c","t":"well from afar, with a wide-spread and long-continued welfare-giving"},{"ref":"37.1d","t":"friendship;"},{"ref":"37.2","t":"Who yokes teams of horses, who makes her chariot turn and"},{"ref":"37.2a","t":"its wheels sound, fat and glistening, strong, tall-formed, weal-possessing,"},{"ref":"37.2b","t":"health-giving, powerful to stand and powerful to turn for assistance"},{"ref":"37.2c","t":"to the faithful."},{"ref":"37.3","t":"To her did Haoshyangha, the Paradhata, offer up a sacrifice"},{"ref":"37.3a","t":"on the enclosure of the Hara, the beautiful height, made by Mazda,"},{"ref":"37.3b","t":"with a hundred male horses, a thousand oxen, and ten thousand"},{"ref":"37.3c","t":"lambs, and with an offering of libations:"},{"ref":"37.4","t":"‘Grant me this boon, O good, most beneficent Drvaspa! that"},{"ref":"37.4a","t":"I may overcome all the Daevas of Mazana; that I may never fear"},{"ref":"37.4b","t":"and bow through terror before the Daevas, but that all the Daevas"},{"ref":"37.4c","t":"may fear and bow in spite of themselves before me, that they may"},{"ref":"37.4d","t":"fear and flee down to darkness.’"},{"ref":"37.5","t":"The powerful Drvaspa, made by Mazda, the holy Drvaspa, the"},{"ref":"37.5a","t":"maintainer, granted him that boon, as he was offering libations,"},{"ref":"37.5b","t":"giving gifts, sacrificing, and entreating that she would grant"},{"ref":"37.5c","t":"him that boon."},{"ref":"37.6","t":"For her brightness and glory, I will offer her a sacrifice"},{"ref":"37.6a","t":"worth being heard; I will offer her a sacrifice well performed,"},{"ref":"37.6b","t":"namely, unto the powerful Drvaspa, made by Mazda and holy. We"},{"ref":"37.6c","t":"offer up libations to the powerful Drvaspa, made by Mazda and"},{"ref":"37.6d","t":"holy; we offer her the Haoma and meat, the baresma, the wisdom"},{"ref":"37.6e","t":"of the tongue, the holy spells, the speech, the deeds, the libations,"},{"ref":"37.6f","t":"and the rightly-spoken words."},{"ref":"37.6g","t":"Yenghe hatam: All those beings of whom Ahura Mazda...."},{"ref":"37.7","t":"We offer up a sacrifice unto the powerful Drvaspa, made by"},{"ref":"37.7a","t":"Mazda and holy, who keeps the flocks in health...."},{"ref":"37.7b","t":"Who yokes teams of horses.... for assistance to the faithful."},{"ref":"37.8","t":"To her did Yima Khshaeta, the good shepherd, offer up a sacrifice"},{"ref":"37.8a","t":"from the height Hukairya, with a hundred male horses, a thousand"},{"ref":"37.8b","t":"oxen, ten thousand lambs, and with an offering of libations:"},{"ref":"37.9","t":"‘Grant me this boon, O good, most beneficent Drvaspa! that"},{"ref":"37.9a","t":"I may bring fatness and flocks down to the world created by Mazda;"},{"ref":"37.9b","t":"that I may bring immortality down to the world created by Mazda;"},{"ref":"37.10","t":"‘That I may take away both hunger and thirst, from the world"},{"ref":"37.10a","t":"created by Mazda; that I may take away both old age and death,"},{"ref":"37.10b","t":"from the world created by Mazda; that I may take away both hot"},{"ref":"37.10c","t":"wind and cold wind, from the world created by Mazda, for a thousand"},{"ref":"37.10d","t":"years.’"},{"ref":"37.11","t":"The powerful Drvaspa, made by Mazda, the holy Drvaspa, the"},{"ref":"37.11a","t":"maintainer, granted him that boon, as he was offering libations,","hvShift6":[[0,0],[57,56]]},{"ref":"37.11b","t":"giving gifts, sacrificing, and entreating that she would grant"},{"ref":"37.11c","t":"him that boon."},{"ref":"37.11d","t":"For her brightness and glory, I will offer her a sacrifice worth"},{"ref":"37.11e","t":"being heard...."},{"ref":"37.12","t":"We offer up a sacrifice unto the powerful Drvaspa, made by"},{"ref":"37.12a","t":"Mazda and holy, who keeps the flocks in health...."},{"ref":"37.12b","t":"Who yokes teams of horses.... for assistance to the faithful."},{"ref":"37.13","t":"To her did Thraetaona, the heir of the valiant Athwya clan,"},{"ref":"37.13a","t":"offer up a sacrifice in the four-cornered Varena, with a hundred"},{"ref":"37.13b","t":"male horses, a thousand oxen, ten thousand lambs, and with an"},{"ref":"37.13c","t":"offering of libations:"},{"ref":"37.14","t":"‘Grant me this boon, O good, most beneficent Drvaspa! that"},{"ref":"37.14a","t":"I may overcome Azhi Dahaka, the three-mouthed, the three-headed,"},{"ref":"37.14b","t":"the six-eyed, who has a thousand senses, that most powerful, fiendish"},{"ref":"37.14c","t":"Druj, that demon, baleful to the world, the strongest Druj that"},{"ref":"37.14d","t":"Angra Mainyu created against the material world, to destroy the"},{"ref":"37.14e","t":"world of the good principle; and that I may deliver his two wives,"},{"ref":"37.14f","t":"Savanghavack and Erenavach, who are the fairest of body amongst"},{"ref":"37.14g","t":"women, and the most wonderful creatures in the world.’"},{"ref":"37.15","t":"The powerful Drvaspa, made by Mazda, the holy Drvasya, the"},{"ref":"37.15a","t":"maintainer, granted him that boon, as he was offering up libations,"},{"ref":"37.15b","t":"giving gifts, sacrificing, and entreating that she would grant"},{"ref":"37.15c","t":"him that boon."},{"ref":"37.15d","t":"For her brightness and glory, I will offer her a sacrifice worth"},{"ref":"37.15e","t":"being heard...."},{"ref":"37.16","t":"We offer up a sacrifice unto the powerful Drvaspa, made by"},{"ref":"37.16a","t":"Mazda and holy, who keeps flocks in health...."},{"ref":"37.16b","t":"Who yokes teams of horses.... for assistance to the faithful."},{"ref":"37.17","t":"To her did Haoma offer up a sacrifice, Haoma, the enlivening,"},{"ref":"37.17a","t":"the healing, the beautiful, the lordly, with golden eyes, upon"},{"ref":"37.17b","t":"the highest height of the Haraiti Bareza. He begged of her a boon"},{"ref":"37.17c","t":"saying:"},{"ref":"37.18","t":"‘Grant me this boon, O good, most beneficent Drvaspa! that"},{"ref":"37.18a","t":"I may bind the Turanian murderer Franghrasyan, that I may drag"},{"ref":"37.18b","t":"him bound, that may bring him bound unto king Husravah, that king"},{"ref":"37.18c","t":"Husravah may kill him, behind the Chaechasta lake, the deep lake"},{"ref":"37.18d","t":"of salt waters, to avenge the murder of his father Syavarshana,"},{"ref":"37.18e","t":"a man, and of Aghraeratha, a semi-man.’"},{"ref":"37.19","t":"The powerful Drvaspa, made by Mazda, the holy Drvaspa, the"},{"ref":"37.19a","t":"maintainer, granted him that boon, as he was offering up libations,"},{"ref":"37.19b","t":"giving gifts, sacrificing, and entreating that she would give"},{"ref":"37.19c","t":"him that boon."},{"ref":"37.19d","t":"For her brightness and glory, I will offer her a sacrifice worth"},{"ref":"37.19e","t":"being heard...."},{"ref":"37.20","t":"We offer up a sacrifice unto the powerful Drvaspa, made by"},{"ref":"37.20a","t":"Mazda and holy, who keeps the flocks in health...."},{"ref":"37.20b","t":"Who yokes teams of horses.... for assistance to the faithful."},{"ref":"37.21","t":"To her did the gallant Husravah, he who united the Arya nations"},{"ref":"37.21a","t":"into one kingdom, offer up a sacrifice, behind the Chaechasta"},{"ref":"37.21b","t":"lake, the deep lake of salt waters, with a hundred male horses,"},{"ref":"37.21c","t":"a thousand oxen, ten thousand lambs, and an offering of libations:"},{"ref":"37.22","t":"‘Grant me this boon, O good, most beneficent Drvaspa! that"},{"ref":"37.22a","t":"I may kill the Turanian murderer, Franghrasyan, behind the Chaechasta"},{"ref":"37.22b","t":"lake, the deep lake of salt waters, to avenge the murder of my"},{"ref":"37.22c","t":"father Syavarshana, a man, and of Aghraeratha, a semi-man.’"},{"ref":"37.23","t":"The powerful Drvaspa, made by Mazda, the holy Drvaspa, the"},{"ref":"37.23a","t":"maintainer, granted him that boon, as he was offering up libations,"},{"ref":"37.23b","t":"giving gifts, sacrificing, and entreating that she would grant"},{"ref":"37.23c","t":"him that boon."},{"ref":"37.23d","t":"For her brightness and glory, I will offer her a sacrifice worth"},{"ref":"37.23e","t":"being heard...."},{"ref":"37.24","t":"We offer up a sacrifice unlo the powerful Drvaspa, made by"},{"ref":"37.24a","t":"Mazda and holy, who keeps the flocks in health...."},{"ref":"37.24b","t":"Who yokes teams of horses.... for assistance to the faithful,"},{"ref":"37.25","t":"To her did the holy Zarathushtra offer up a sacrifice in the"},{"ref":"37.25a","t":"Airyana Vaejah, by the good river Daitya, with the Haoma and meat,"},{"ref":"37.25b","t":"with the baresma, with the wisdom of the tongue, with the holy"},{"ref":"37.25c","t":"spells, with the speech, with the deeds, with the libations, and"},{"ref":"37.25d","t":"with the rightly-spoken words. He begged of her a boon, saying:"},{"ref":"37.26","t":"‘O good, most beneficent Drvaspa! grant me this boon, that"},{"ref":"37.26a","t":"I may bring the good and noble Hutaosa to think according to the"},{"ref":"37.26b","t":"law, to speak according to the law, to do according to the law,"},{"ref":"37.26c","t":"that she may spread my Mazdean law and make it known, and that"},{"ref":"37.26d","t":"she may bestow beautiful praises upon my deeds.’"},{"ref":"37.27","t":"The strong Drvaspa, made by Mazda, the holy Drvaspa, the maintainer,"},{"ref":"37.27a","t":"granted him that boon, as he was offering up libations, giving"},{"ref":"37.27b","t":"gifts, sacrificing, and entreating that she would grant him that"},{"ref":"37.27c","t":"boon."},{"ref":"37.27d","t":"For her brightness and glory, I will offer her a sacrifice worth","hvShift6":[[0,0]]},{"ref":"37.27e","t":"being heard...."},{"ref":"37.28","t":"We offer up a sacrifice unto the powerful Drvaspa, made by"},{"ref":"37.28a","t":"Mazda and holy, who keeps the flocks in health...."},{"ref":"37.28b","t":"Who yokes teams of horses.... for assistance to the faithful."},{"ref":"37.29","t":"To her did the tall Kavi Vistaspa offer up a sacrifice behind"},{"ref":"37.29a","t":"the waters of the river Daitya, with a hundred male horses, a"},{"ref":"37.29b","t":"thousand oxen, ten thousand lambs, and with an offering of libations:"},{"ref":"37.30","t":"‘Grant me this boon, O good, most beneficent Drvaspa! that"},{"ref":"37.30a","t":"I may put to flight Ashta-aurvant, the son of Vispa-thaurvo-asti,"},{"ref":"37.30b","t":"the all-afflicting, of the brazen helmet, of the brazen armour,"},{"ref":"37.30c","t":"of the thick neck, behind whom seven hundred camels....; that"},{"ref":"37.30d","t":"I may put to flight the Hvyaona murderer, Arejat-aspa; that I"},{"ref":"37.30e","t":"may put to flight Darshinika, the worshipper of the Daevas;"},{"ref":"37.31","t":"And that I may smite Tathravant of the bad law; that I may"},{"ref":"37.31a","t":"smite Spinjaurushka, the worshipper of the Daevas; and that I"},{"ref":"37.31b","t":"may bring unto the good law the nations of the Varedhakas and"},{"ref":"37.31c","t":"of the Hvyaonas; and that I may smite of the Huyaona nations their"},{"ref":"37.31d","t":"fifties and their hundreds, their hundreds and their thousands,"},{"ref":"37.31e","t":"their thousands and their tens of thousands, their tens of thousands"},{"ref":"37.31f","t":"and their myriads of myriads."},{"ref":"37.32","t":"The strong Drvaspa, made by Mazda, the holy Drvaspa, the maintainer,"},{"ref":"37.32a","t":"granted him that boon, as he was offering up libations, giving"},{"ref":"37.32b","t":"gifts, sacrificing, and entreating that she would grant him that"},{"ref":"37.32c","t":"boon."},{"ref":"37.32d","t":"For her brightness and glory, I will offer her a sacrifice worth"},{"ref":"37.32e","t":"being heard; I will offer her a sacrifice well performed, namely,"},{"ref":"37.32f","t":"unto the powerful Drvaspa made by Mazda and holy. We offer up"},{"ref":"37.32g","t":"libations to the powerful Drvaspa, made by Mazda and holy; we"},{"ref":"37.32h","t":"offer her the Haoma and meat, the baresma, the wisdom of the tongue,"},{"ref":"37.32i","t":"the holy spells, the speech, the deeds, the libations, and the"},{"ref":"37.32j","t":"rightly-spoken words."},{"ref":"37.32k","t":"Yatha ahu vairyo: The will of the Lord is the law of holiness...."},{"ref":"37.32l","t":"I bless the sacrifice and prayer, and the strength and vigour"},{"ref":"37.32m","t":"of the powerful Drvaspa, made by Mazda and holy."},{"ref":"37.32n","t":"Ashem Vohu: Holiness is the best of all good...."},{"ref":"37.32o","t":"[Give] unto that man brightness and glory, give him health of"},{"ref":"37.32p","t":"body,... give him the bright, all-happy, blissful abode of the"},{"ref":"37.32q","t":"holy Ones."},{"sp":"HDR","t":"10. Mihr Yasht (Hymn to Mithra)"},{"ref":"38.0","t":"May Ahura Mazda be rejoiced!...."},{"ref":"38.0a","t":"Ashem Vohu: Holiness is the best of all good...."},{"ref":"38.0b","t":"I confess myself a worshipper of Mazda, a follower of Zarathushtra,"},{"ref":"38.0c","t":"one who hates the Daevas, and obeys the laws of Ahura;"},{"ref":"38.0d","t":"For sacrifice, prayer, propitiation, and glorification unto [Havani],"},{"ref":"38.0e","t":"the holy and master of holiness...."},{"ref":"38.0f","t":"Unto Mithra, the lord of wide pastures, who has a thousand ears,"},{"ref":"38.0g","t":"ten thousand eyes, a Yazata invoked by his own name, and unto"},{"ref":"38.0h","t":"Rama Hvastra,"},{"ref":"38.0i","t":"Be propitiation, with sacrifice, prayer, propitiation, and glorification."},{"ref":"38.0j","t":"Yatha ahu vairyo: The will of the Lord is the law of holiness...."},{"ref":"38.1","t":"Ahura Mazda spake unto Spitama Zarathushtra, saying: ‘Verily,"},{"ref":"38.1a","t":"when I created Mithra, the lord of wide pastures, O Spitama! I"},{"ref":"38.1b","t":"created him as worthy of sacrifice, as worthy of prayer as myself"},{"ref":"38.1c","t":"Ahura Mazda."},{"ref":"38.2","t":"‘The ruffian who lies unto Mithra brings death unto the whole"},{"ref":"38.2a","t":"country, injuring as much the faithful world as a hundred evil-doers"},{"ref":"38.2b","t":"could do. Break not the contract, O Spitama! neither the one that"},{"ref":"38.2c","t":"thou hadst entered into with one of the unfaithful, nor the one"},{"ref":"38.2d","t":"that thou hadst entered into with one of the faithful who is one"},{"ref":"38.2e","t":"of thy own faith. For Mithra stands for both the faithful and"},{"ref":"38.2f","t":"the unfaithful."},{"ref":"38.3","t":"‘Mithra, the lord of wide pastures, gives swiftness to the"},{"ref":"38.3a","t":"horses of those who lie not unto Mithra."},{"ref":"38.3b","t":"‘Fire, the son of Ahura Mazda, gives the straightest way to those"},{"ref":"38.3c","t":"who lie not unto Mithra."},{"ref":"38.3d","t":"‘The good, strong, beneficent Fravashis of the faithful give a"},{"ref":"38.3e","t":"virtuous offspring to those who lie not unto Mithra."},{"ref":"38.4","t":"‘For his brightness and glory, I will offer unto him a sacrifice"},{"ref":"38.4a","t":"worth being heard, namely, unto Mithra, the lord of wide pastures."},{"ref":"38.4b","t":"‘We offer up libations unto Mithra, the lord of wide pastures,"},{"ref":"38.4c","t":"who gives a happy dwelling and a good dwelling to the Aryan nations."},{"ref":"38.5","t":"‘May he come to us for help! May he come to us for ease! May"},{"ref":"38.5a","t":"he come to us for joy! May he come to us for mercy! May he come"},{"ref":"38.5b","t":"to us for health! May he come to us for victory! May he come to"},{"ref":"38.5c","t":"us for good conscience! May he come to us for bliss! he, the awful"},{"ref":"38.5d","t":"and overpowering, worthy of sacrifice and prayer, not to be deceived"},{"ref":"38.5e","t":"anywhere in the whole of the material world, Mithra, the lord"},{"ref":"38.5f","t":"of wide pastures."},{"ref":"38.6","t":"‘I will offer up libations unto him, the strong Yazata, the"},{"ref":"38.6a","t":"powerful Mithra, most beneficent to the creatures: I will apply"},{"ref":"38.6b","t":"unto him with charity and prayers: I will offer up a sacrifice"},{"ref":"38.6c","t":"worth being heard unto him, Mithra, the lord ofwide pastures,"},{"ref":"38.6d","t":"with the Haoma and meat, with the baresma, with the wisdom of"},{"ref":"38.6e","t":"the tongue, with the holy spells, with the speech, with the deeds,"},{"ref":"38.6f","t":"with the libations, and with the rightly-spoken words. ‘Yenhe"},{"ref":"38.6g","t":"hatam: All those beings of whom Ahura Mazda...."},{"ref":"38.7","t":"‘We sacrifice unto Mithra, the lord of wide pastures, who"},{"ref":"38.7a","t":"is truth-speaking, a chief in assemblies, with a thousand ears,"},{"ref":"38.7b","t":"well-shapen, with ten thousand eyes, high, with full knowledge,"},{"ref":"38.7c","t":"strong, sleepless, and ever awake;"},{"ref":"38.8","t":"‘To whom the chiefs of nations offer up sacrifices, as they"},{"ref":"38.8a","t":"go to the field, against havocking hosts, against enemies coming"},{"ref":"38.8b","t":"in battle array, in the strife of conflicting nations."},{"ref":"38.9","t":"‘On whichever side he has been worshipped first in the fulness"},{"ref":"38.9a","t":"of faith of a devoted heart, to that side turns Mithra, the lord"},{"ref":"38.9b","t":"of wide pastures, with the fiend-smiting wind, with the cursing"},{"ref":"38.9c","t":"thought of the wise."},{"ref":"38.9d","t":"‘For his brightness and glory, I will offer him a sacrifice worth"},{"ref":"38.9e","t":"being heard...."},{"ref":"38.10","t":"‘We sacrifice unto Mithra, the lord of wide pastures,..."},{"ref":"38.10a","t":"sleepless, and ever awake."},{"ref":"38.11","t":"‘Whom the horsemen worship on the back of their horses, begging"},{"ref":"38.11a","t":"swiftness for their teams, health for their own bodies, and that"},{"ref":"38.11b","t":"they may watch with full success those who hate them, smite down"},{"ref":"38.11c","t":"their foes, and destroy at one stroke their adversaries, their"},{"ref":"38.11d","t":"enemies, and those who hate them,","hvShift6":[[0,0],[33,32]]},{"ref":"38.11e","t":"‘For his brightness and glory, I will offer him a sacrifice worth"},{"ref":"38.11f","t":"being heard...."},{"ref":"38.12","t":"‘We sacrifice unto Mithra, the lord of wide pastures,..."},{"ref":"38.12a","t":"sleepless, and ever awake;"},{"ref":"38.13","t":"‘Who first of the heavenly gods reaches over the Hara, before"},{"ref":"38.13a","t":"the undying, swift-horsed sun; who, foremost in a golden array,"},{"ref":"38.13b","t":"takes hold of the beautiful summits, and from thence looks over"},{"ref":"38.13c","t":"the abode of the Aryans with a beneficent eye."},{"ref":"38.14","t":"‘Where the valiant chiefs draw up their many troops in array;"},{"ref":"38.14a","t":"where the high mountains, rich in pastures and waters, yield plenty"},{"ref":"38.14b","t":"to the cattle; where the deep lakes, with salt waters, stand;"},{"ref":"38.14c","t":"where wide-flowing rivers swell and hurry towards Ishkata and"},{"ref":"38.14d","t":"Pouruta, Mouru and Haroyu, the Gava-Sughdha and Hvairizem;"},{"ref":"38.15","t":"‘On Arezahi and Savahi, on Fradadhafshu and Vidadhafshu, on"},{"ref":"38.15a","t":"Vourubareshti and Vourujareshti, on this bright Karshvare of Hvaniratha,"},{"ref":"38.15b","t":"the abode of cattle, the dwelling of cattle, the powerful Mithra"},{"ref":"38.15c","t":"looks with a health-bringing eye;"},{"ref":"38.16","t":"‘He who moves along all the Karshvares, a Yazata unseen, and"},{"ref":"38.16a","t":"brings glory; he who moves along all the Karshvares, a Yazata"},{"ref":"38.16b","t":"unseen, and brings sovereignty; and increases strength for victory"},{"ref":"38.16c","t":"to those who, with a pious intent, holily offer him libations."},{"ref":"38.16d","t":"‘For his brightness and glory, I will offer him a sacrifice worth"},{"ref":"38.16e","t":"being heard...."},{"ref":"38.17","t":"‘We sacrifice unto Mithra, the lord of wide pastures,..."},{"ref":"38.17a","t":"sleepless, and ever awake;"},{"ref":"38.17b","t":"‘Unto whom nobody must lie, neither the master of a house, nor"},{"ref":"38.17c","t":"the lord of a borough, nor the lord of a town, nor the lord of"},{"ref":"38.17d","t":"a province."},{"ref":"38.18","t":"‘If the master of a house lies unto him, or the lord of a"},{"ref":"38.18a","t":"borough, or the lord of a town, or the lord ofa province, then"},{"ref":"38.18b","t":"comes Mithra, angry and offended, and he breaks asunder the house,"},{"ref":"38.18c","t":"the borough, the town, the province; and the masters of the houses,"},{"ref":"38.18d","t":"the lords of the boroughs, the lords of the towns, the lords of"},{"ref":"38.18e","t":"the provinces, and the foremost men of the provinces."},{"ref":"38.19","t":"‘On whatever side there is one who has lied unto Mithra, on"},{"ref":"38.19a","t":"that side Mithra stands forth, angry and offended, and his wrath"},{"ref":"38.19b","t":"is slow to relent."},{"ref":"38.20","t":"‘Those who lie unto Mithra, however swift they may be running,"},{"ref":"38.20a","t":"cannot overtake; riding, cannot....; driving, cannot..... The"},{"ref":"38.20b","t":"spear that the foe of Mithra flings, darts backwards, for the"},{"ref":"38.20c","t":"number of the evil spells that the foe of Mithra works out."},{"ref":"38.21","t":"‘And even though the spear be flung well, even though it reach"},{"ref":"38.21a","t":"the body, it makes no wound, for the number of the evil spells"},{"ref":"38.21b","t":"that the foe of Mithra works out. The wind drives away the spear"},{"ref":"38.21c","t":"that the foe of Mithra flings, for the number of the evil spells"},{"ref":"38.21d","t":"that the foe of Mithra works out."},{"ref":"38.21e","t":"‘For his brightness and glory, I will offer him a sacrifice worth"},{"ref":"38.21f","t":"being heard...."},{"ref":"38.22","t":"‘We sacrifice unto Mithra, the lord of wide pastures,..."},{"ref":"38.22a","t":"sleepless, and ever awake;"},{"ref":"38.22b","t":"‘Who takes out of distress the man who has not lied unto him,"},{"ref":"38.22c","t":"who takes him out of death."},{"ref":"38.23","t":"‘Take us out of distress, take us out of distresses, O Mithra!"},{"ref":"38.23a","t":"as we have not lied unto thee. Thou bringest down terror upon"},{"ref":"38.23b","t":"the bodies of the men who lie unto Mithra; thou takest away the"},{"ref":"38.23c","t":"strength from their arms, being angry and all-powerful; thou takest"},{"ref":"38.23d","t":"the swiftness from their feet, the eye-sight from their eyes,"},{"ref":"38.23e","t":"the hearing from their ears."},{"ref":"38.24","t":"‘Not the wound of the well-sharpened spear or of the flying"},{"ref":"38.24a","t":"arrow reaches that man to whom Mithra comes for help with all"},{"ref":"38.24b","t":"the strength of his soul, he, of the ten thousand spies, the powerful,"},{"ref":"38.24c","t":"all-seeing, undeceivable Mithra."},{"ref":"38.24d","t":"‘For his brightness and glory, I will offer him a sacrifice worth"},{"ref":"38.24e","t":"being heard...."},{"ref":"38.25","t":"‘We sacrifice unto Mithra, the lord of wide pastures,..."},{"ref":"38.25a","t":"sleepless, and ever awake;"},{"ref":"38.25b","t":"‘Who is lordly, deep, strong, and weal-giving; a chief in assemblies,"},{"ref":"38.25c","t":"pleased with prayers, high, holily clever, the incarnate Word,"},{"ref":"38.25d","t":"a warrior with strong arms;"},{"ref":"38.26","t":"‘Who breaks the skulls of the Daevas, and is most cruel in"},{"ref":"38.26a","t":"exacting pains; the punisher of the men who lie unto Mithra, the"},{"ref":"38.26b","t":"withstander of the Pairikas; who, when not deceived, establisheth"},{"ref":"38.26c","t":"nations in supreme strength; who, when not deceived, establisheth"},{"ref":"38.26d","t":"nations in supreme victory;"},{"ref":"38.27","t":"‘Who confounds the ways of the nation that delights in havoc,"},{"ref":"38.27a","t":"who turns away their Glory, takes away their strength for victory,"},{"ref":"38.27b","t":"blows them away helpless, and delivers them unto ten thousand"},{"ref":"38.27c","t":"strokes; he, of the ten thousand spies, the powerful, all-seeing,"},{"ref":"38.27d","t":"undeceivable Mithra."},{"ref":"38.27e","t":"‘For his brightness and glory, I will offer him a sacrifice worth"},{"ref":"38.27f","t":"being heard...."},{"ref":"38.28","t":"‘We sacrifice unto Mithra, the lord of wide pastures,..."},{"ref":"38.28a","t":"sleepless, and ever awake;"},{"ref":"38.28b","t":"‘Who upholds the columns of the lofty house and makes its pillars"},{"ref":"38.28c","t":"solid; who gives herds of oxen and male children to that house"},{"ref":"38.28d","t":"in which he has been satisfied; he breaks to pieces those in which"},{"ref":"38.28e","t":"he has been offended,"},{"ref":"38.29","t":"‘Thou, O Mithra! art both bad and good to nations; thou, O"},{"ref":"38.29a","t":"Mithra! art both bad and good to men; thou, O Mithra! keepest"},{"ref":"38.29b","t":"in thy hands both peace and trouble for nations."},{"ref":"38.30","t":"‘Thou makest houses large, beautiful with women, beautiful"},{"ref":"38.30a","t":"with chariots, with well-laid foundations, and high above their"},{"ref":"38.30b","t":"groundwork; thou makest that house lofty, beautiful with women,"},{"ref":"38.30c","t":"beautiful with chariots, with well-laid foundations, and high"},{"ref":"38.30d","t":"above its groundwork, of which the master, pious and holding libations"},{"ref":"38.30e","t":"in his hand, offers thee a sacrifice, in which thou art invoked"},{"ref":"38.30f","t":"by thy own name and with the proper words."},{"ref":"38.31","t":"‘With a sacrifice, in which thou art invoked by thy own name,"},{"ref":"38.31a","t":"with the proper words will I offer thee libations, O powerful"},{"ref":"38.31b","t":"Mithra!"},{"ref":"38.31c","t":"‘With a sacrifice, in which thou art invoked by thy own name,"},{"ref":"38.31d","t":"with the proper words will I offer thee libations, O most beneficent"},{"ref":"38.31e","t":"Mithra!"},{"ref":"38.31f","t":"‘With a sacrifice, in which thou art invoked by thy own name,"},{"ref":"38.31g","t":"with the proper words will I offer thee libations, O thou undeceivable"},{"ref":"38.31h","t":"Mithra!"},{"ref":"38.32","t":"‘Listen unto our sacrifice, O Mithra! Be thou pleased with"},{"ref":"38.32a","t":"our sacrifice, O Mithra! Come and sit at our sacrifice! Accept"},{"ref":"38.32b","t":"our libations! Accept them as they have been consecrated! Gather"},{"ref":"38.32c","t":"them together with love and lay them in the Garo-nmana!"},{"ref":"38.33","t":"‘Grant us these boons which we beg of thee, O powerful god"},{"ref":"38.33a","t":"I in accordance with the words of revelation, namely, riches,"},{"ref":"38.33b","t":"strength, and victory, good conscience and bliss, good fame and"},{"ref":"38.33c","t":"a good soul; wisdom and the knowledge that gives happiness, the"},{"ref":"38.33d","t":"victorious strength given by Ahura, the crushing Ascendant of"},{"ref":"38.33e","t":"Asha Vahishta, and conversation (with God) on the Holy Word."},{"ref":"38.34","t":"‘Grant that we, in a good spirit and high spirit, exalted"},{"ref":"38.34a","t":"in joy and a good spirit, may smite all our foes; that we, in"},{"ref":"38.34b","t":"a good spirit and high spirit, exalted in joy and a good spirit,"},{"ref":"38.34c","t":"may smite all our enemies; that we, in a good spirit and high"},{"ref":"38.34d","t":"spirit, exalted in joy and a good spirit, may smite all the malice"},{"ref":"38.34e","t":"of Daevas and Men, of the Yatus and Pairikas, of the oppressors,"},{"ref":"38.34f","t":"the blind, and the deaf."},{"ref":"38.34g","t":"‘For his brightness and glory, I will offer him a sacrifice worth"},{"ref":"38.34h","t":"being heard...."},{"ref":"38.35","t":"‘We sacrifice unto Mithra, the lord of wide pastures,..."},{"ref":"38.35a","t":"sleepless, and ever awake;"},{"ref":"38.35b","t":"‘Victory-making, army-governing, endowed with a thousand senses;"},{"ref":"38.35c","t":"power-wielding, power-possessing, and all-knowing;"},{"ref":"38.36","t":"‘Who sets the battle a going, who stands against (armies)"},{"ref":"38.36a","t":"in battle, who, standing against (armies) in battle, breaks asunder"},{"ref":"38.36b","t":"the lines arrayed. The wings of the columns gone to battle shake,"},{"ref":"38.36c","t":"and he throws terror upon the centre of the havocking host."},{"ref":"38.37","t":"‘He can bring and does bring down upon them distress and fear;"},{"ref":"38.37a","t":"he throws down the heads of those who lie to Mithra, he takes"},{"ref":"38.37b","t":"off the heads of those who lie unto Mithra."},{"ref":"38.38","t":"‘Sad is the abode, unpeopled with children, where abide men"},{"ref":"38.38a","t":"who lie unto Mithra, and, verily, the fiendish killer of faithful"},{"ref":"38.38b","t":"men. The grazing cow goes a sad straying way, driven along the"},{"ref":"38.38c","t":"vales of the Mithradrujes: they stand on the road, letting tears"},{"ref":"38.38d","t":"run over their chins."},{"ref":"38.39","t":"‘Their falcon-feathered arrows, shot from the string of the"},{"ref":"38.39a","t":"well-bent bow, fly towards the mark, and hit it not, as Mithra,"},{"ref":"38.39b","t":"the lord of wide pastures, angry, offended, and unsatisfied, comes"},{"ref":"38.39c","t":"and meets them."},{"ref":"38.39d","t":"‘Their spears, well whetted and sharp, their long spears fly from"},{"ref":"38.39e","t":"their hands towards the mark, and hit it not, as Mithra, the lord"},{"ref":"38.39f","t":"of wide pastures, angry, offended, and unsatisfied, comes and"},{"ref":"38.39g","t":"meets them."},{"ref":"38.40","t":"‘Their swords, well thrust and striking at the heads of men,"},{"ref":"38.40a","t":"hit not the mark, as Mithra, the lord of wide pastures, angry,"},{"ref":"38.40b","t":"offended, and unsatisfied, comes and meets them."},{"ref":"38.40c","t":"‘Their clubs, well falling and striking at the heads of men, hit"},{"ref":"38.40d","t":"not the mark, as Mithra, the lord of wide pastures, angry, offended,"},{"ref":"38.40e","t":"and unsatisfied, comes and meets them."},{"ref":"38.41","t":"‘Mithra strikes fear into them; Rashnu strikes a counter-fear"},{"ref":"38.41a","t":"into them; the holy Sraosha blows them away from every side towards"},{"ref":"38.41b","t":"the two Yazatas, the maintainers of the world. They make the ranks"},{"ref":"38.41c","t":"of the army melt away, as Mithra, the lord of wide pastures, angry,"},{"ref":"38.41d","t":"offended, and unsatisfied, comes and meets them."},{"ref":"38.42","t":"‘They cry unto Mithra, the lord of wide pastures, saying:"},{"ref":"38.42a","t":"“O Mithra, thou lord of wide pastures! here are our fiery"},{"ref":"38.42b","t":"horses taking us away, as they flee from Mithra; here are our"},{"ref":"38.42c","t":"sturdy arms cut to pieces by the sword, O Mithra!”"},{"ref":"38.43","t":"‘And then Mithra, the lord of wide pastures, throws them to"},{"ref":"38.43a","t":"the ground, killing their fifties and their hundreds, their hundreds"},{"ref":"38.43b","t":"and their thousands, their thousands and their tens of thousands,"},{"ref":"38.43c","t":"their tens of thousands and their myriads of myriads; as Mithra,"},{"ref":"38.43d","t":"the lord of wide pastures, is angry and offended,"},{"ref":"38.43e","t":"‘For his brightness and glory, I will offer him a sacrifice worth"},{"ref":"38.43f","t":"being heard...."},{"ref":"38.44","t":"‘We sacrifice unto Mithra, the lord of wide pastures,..."},{"ref":"38.44a","t":"sleepless, and ever awake;"},{"ref":"38.44b","t":"‘Whose dwelling, wide as the earth, extends over the material"},{"ref":"38.44c","t":"world, large, unconfined, and bright, a far-and-wide-extending"},{"ref":"38.44d","t":"abode."},{"ref":"38.45","t":"‘Whose eight friends sit as spies for Mithra, on all the heights,"},{"ref":"38.45a","t":"at all the watching-places, observing the man who lies unto Mithra,"},{"ref":"38.45b","t":"looking at those, remembering those who have lied unto Mithra,"},{"ref":"38.45c","t":"but guarding the ways of those whose life is sought by men who"},{"ref":"38.45d","t":"lie unto Mithra, and, verily, by the fiendish killers of faithful"},{"ref":"38.45e","t":"men."},{"ref":"38.46","t":"‘Helping and guarding, guarding behind and guarding in front,"},{"ref":"38.46a","t":"Mithra, the lord of wide pastures, proves an undeceivable spy"},{"ref":"38.46b","t":"and watcher for the man to whom he comes to help with all the"},{"ref":"38.46c","t":"strength of his soul, he of the ten thousand spies, the powerful,"},{"ref":"38.46d","t":"all-knowing, undeceivable god."},{"ref":"38.46e","t":"‘For his brightness and glory, I will offer him a sacrifice worth"},{"ref":"38.46f","t":"being heard...."},{"ref":"38.47","t":"‘We sacrifice unto Mithra, the lord of wide pastures,..."},{"ref":"38.47a","t":"sleepless, and ever awake;"},{"ref":"38.47b","t":"‘A god of high renown and old age, whom wide-hoofed horses carry"},{"ref":"38.47c","t":"against havocking hosts, against enemies coming in battle array,"},{"ref":"38.47d","t":"in the strife of conflicting nations."},{"ref":"38.48","t":"‘And when Mithra drives along towards the havocking hosts,"},{"ref":"38.48a","t":"towards the enemies coming in battle array, in the strife of the"},{"ref":"38.48b","t":"conflicting nations, then he binds the hands of those who have"},{"ref":"38.48c","t":"lied unto Mithra, he confounds their eye-sight, he takes the hearing"},{"ref":"38.48d","t":"from their ears; they can no longer move their feet; they can"},{"ref":"38.48e","t":"no longer withstand those people, those foes, when Mithra, the"},{"ref":"38.48f","t":"lord of wide pastures, bears them ill-will."},{"ref":"38.48g","t":"‘For his brightness and glory, I will offer him a sacrifice worth"},{"ref":"38.48h","t":"being heard...."},{"ref":"38.49","t":"‘We sacrifice unto Mithra, the lord of wide pastures,..."},{"ref":"38.49a","t":"sleepless, and ever awake;"},{"ref":"38.50","t":"‘For whom the Maker, Ahura Mazda, has built up a dwelling"},{"ref":"38.50a","t":"on the Hara Berezaiti, the bright mountain around which the many"},{"ref":"38.50b","t":"(stars) revolve where come neither night nor darkness, no cold"},{"ref":"38.50c","t":"wind and no hot wind, no deathful sickness, no uncleanness made"},{"ref":"38.50d","t":"by the Daevas, and the clouds cannot reach up unto the Haraiti"},{"ref":"38.50e","t":"Bareza;"},{"ref":"38.51","t":"‘A dwelling that all the Amesha-Spentas, in one accord with"},{"ref":"38.51a","t":"the sun, made for him in the fulness of faith of a devoted heart,"},{"ref":"38.51b","t":"and he survevs the whole of the material world from the Haraiti"},{"ref":"38.51c","t":"Bareza."},{"ref":"38.52","t":"‘And when there rushes a wicked worker of evil, swiftly, with"},{"ref":"38.52a","t":"a swift step, Mithra, the lord of wide pastures, goes and yokes"},{"ref":"38.52b","t":"his horses to his chariot, along with the holy, powerful Sraosha"},{"ref":"38.52c","t":"and Nairyo-sangha, who strikes a blow that smites the army, that"},{"ref":"38.52d","t":"smites the strength of the malicious."},{"ref":"38.52e","t":"‘For his brightness and glory, I will offer him a sacrifice worth"},{"ref":"38.52f","t":"being heard...."},{"ref":"38.53","t":"‘We sacrifice unto Mithra, the lord of wide pastures,..."},{"ref":"38.53a","t":"sleepless, and ever awake;"},{"ref":"38.54","t":"‘Who, with hands lifted up, ever cries unto Ahura Mazda, saying:"},{"ref":"38.54a","t":"“I am the kind keeper of all creatures, I am the kind maintainer"},{"ref":"38.54b","t":"of all creatures; yet men worship me not with a sacrifice in which"},{"ref":"38.54c","t":"I am invoked by my own name, as they worship the other gods with"},{"ref":"38.54d","t":"sacrifices in which they are invoked by their own names."},{"ref":"38.55","t":"‘“If men would worship me with a sacrifice in which I"},{"ref":"38.55a","t":"were invoked by my own name, as they worship the other Yazatas"},{"ref":"38.55b","t":"with sacrifices in which they are invoked by their own names,"},{"ref":"38.55c","t":"then I would come to the faithful at the appointed time; I would"},{"ref":"38.55d","t":"come in the appointed time of my beautiful, immortal life.”"},{"ref":"38.56","t":"‘But the pious man, holding libations in his hands, does worship"},{"ref":"38.56a","t":"thee with a sacrifice, in which thou art invoked by thy own ame,"},{"ref":"38.56b","t":"and with the proper words."},{"ref":"38.56c","t":"‘With a sacrifice, in which thou art invoked by thy own name,"},{"ref":"38.56d","t":"with the proper words will I offer thee libations, O powerful"},{"ref":"38.56e","t":"Mithra!"},{"ref":"38.56f","t":"‘With a sacrifice, in which thou art invoked by thy own name,"},{"ref":"38.56g","t":"with the groper words will I offer thee libations, O most beneficent"},{"ref":"38.56h","t":"Mithra!"},{"ref":"38.56i","t":"‘With a sacrifice, in which thou art invoked by thy own name,"},{"ref":"38.56j","t":"with the proper words will I offer thee libations, O thou undeceivable"},{"ref":"38.56k","t":"Mithra!"},{"ref":"38.57","t":"‘Listen unto our sacrifice, ‘O Mithra! Be thou pleased with"},{"ref":"38.57a","t":"our sacrifice, O Mithra! Come and sit at our sacrifice! Accept"},{"ref":"38.57b","t":"our libations! Accept them as they have been consecrated! Gather"},{"ref":"38.57c","t":"them together with love and lay them in the Garo-nmana!"},{"ref":"38.58","t":"‘Grant us these boons which we beg of thee, O powerful god!"},{"ref":"38.58a","t":"in accordance with the words of revelation, namely, riches, strength,"},{"ref":"38.58b","t":"and victory, good conscience and bliss, good fame and a good soul;"},{"ref":"38.58c","t":"wisdom and the knowledge that gives happiness, the victorious"},{"ref":"38.58d","t":"strength given by Ahura, the crushing Ascendant of Asha-Vahishta,"},{"ref":"38.58e","t":"and conversation (with God) on the Holy Word."},{"ref":"38.59","t":"‘Grant that we, in a good spirit and high spirit, exalted"},{"ref":"38.59a","t":"in joy and a good spirit, may smite all our foes; that we, in"},{"ref":"38.59b","t":"a good spirit and high spirit, exalted in joy and a good spirit,"},{"ref":"38.59c","t":"may smite all our enemies; that we, in a good spirit and high"},{"ref":"38.59d","t":"spirit, exalted in joy and a good spirit, may smite all the malice"},{"ref":"38.59e","t":"of Daevas and Men, of the Yatus and Pairikas, of the oppressors,"},{"ref":"38.59f","t":"the blind, and the deaf."},{"ref":"38.59g","t":"‘For his brightness and glory, I will offer him a sacrifice worth"},{"ref":"38.59h","t":"being heard...."},{"ref":"38.60","t":"‘We sacrifice unto Mithra, the lord of wide pastures,..."},{"ref":"38.60a","t":"sleepless, and ever awake;"},{"ref":"38.60b","t":"‘Whose renown is good, whose shape is good, whose glory is good;"},{"ref":"38.60c","t":"who has boons to give at his will, who has pasture-fields to give"},{"ref":"38.60d","t":"at his will; harmless to the tiller of the ground,... beneficent;"},{"ref":"38.60e","t":"he, of the ten thousand spies, the powerful, all-knowing, undeceivable"},{"ref":"38.60f","t":"god."},{"ref":"38.60g","t":"‘For his brightness and glory, I will offer him a sacrifice worth"},{"ref":"38.60h","t":"being heard...."},{"ref":"38.61","t":"‘We sacrifice unto Mithra, the lord of wide pastures,..."},{"ref":"38.61a","t":"sleepless, and ever awake;"},{"ref":"38.61b","t":"‘Firm-legged, a watcher fully awake; valiant, a chief in assemblies;"},{"ref":"38.61c","t":"making the waters flow forward; listening to appeals; making the"},{"ref":"38.61d","t":"waters run and the plants grow up; ruling over the Karshvares;"},{"ref":"38.61e","t":"delivering; happy; undeceivable; endowed with many senses; a creature"},{"ref":"38.61f","t":"of wisdom;"},{"ref":"38.62","t":"‘Who gives neither strength nor vigour to him who has lied"},{"ref":"38.62a","t":"unto Mithra; who gives neither glory nor any boon to him who has"},{"ref":"38.62b","t":"lied unto Mithra."},{"ref":"38.63","t":"‘Thou takest away the strength from their arms, being angry"},{"ref":"38.63a","t":"and all-powerful; thou takest the swiftness from their feet, the"},{"ref":"38.63b","t":"eye-sight from their eyes, the hearing from their ears."},{"ref":"38.63c","t":"‘Not the wound of the well-sharpened spear or of the flying arrow"},{"ref":"38.63d","t":"reaches that man to whom Mithra comes for help with all the strength"},{"ref":"38.63e","t":"of his soul he of the ten-thousand spies, the powerful all-knowing"},{"ref":"38.63f","t":"undeceivable god. ‘For his brightness and glory, I will offer"},{"ref":"38.63g","t":"him a sacrifice worth being heard...."},{"ref":"38.64","t":"‘We sacrifice unto Mithra, the lord of wide pastures,..."},{"ref":"38.64a","t":"sleepless, and ever awake;"},{"ref":"38.64b","t":"‘Who takes possession of the beautiful, wide-expanding law, greatly"},{"ref":"38.64c","t":"and powerfully and whose face looks over all the seven Karshvares"},{"ref":"38.64d","t":"of the earth;"},{"ref":"38.65","t":"‘Who is swift amongst the swift, liberal amongst the liberal,"},{"ref":"38.65a","t":"strong amongst the strong, a chief of assembly amongst the chiefs"},{"ref":"38.65b","t":"of assemblies; increase-giving, fatness-giving, cattle-giving,"},{"ref":"38.65c","t":"sovereignty-giving, son-giving, cheerfulness-giving, and bliss-giving."},{"ref":"38.66","t":"‘With whom proceed Ashi Vanguhi, and Parendi on her light"},{"ref":"38.66a","t":"chariot, the awful Manly Courage, the awful kingly Glory, the"},{"ref":"38.66b","t":"awful sovereign Sky, the awful cursing thought of the wise, the"},{"ref":"38.66c","t":"awful Fravashis of the faithful, and he who keeps united together"},{"ref":"38.66d","t":"the many faithful worshippers of Mazda."},{"ref":"38.66e","t":"‘For his brightness and glory, I will offer him a sacrifice worth"},{"ref":"38.66f","t":"being heard...."},{"ref":"38.67","t":"‘We sacrifice unto Mithra, the lord of wide pastares,..."},{"ref":"38.67a","t":"sleepless, and ever awake;"},{"ref":"38.67b","t":"‘Who drives along on his high-wheeled chariot, made of a heavenly"},{"ref":"38.67c","t":"substance, from the Karshvare of Arezahi to the Karshvare of Hvaniratha,"},{"ref":"38.67d","t":"the bright one; accompanied by the wheel of sovereignty, the Glory"},{"ref":"38.67e","t":"made by Mazda, and the Victory made by Ahura;"},{"ref":"38.68","t":"‘Whose chariot is embraced by the great Ashi Vanguhi; to whom"},{"ref":"38.68a","t":"the Law of Mazda opens a way, that he may go easily; whom four"},{"ref":"38.68b","t":"heavenly steeds, white, shining, seen afar, beneficent, endowed"},{"ref":"38.68c","t":"with knowledge, swiftly carry along the heavenly space, while"},{"ref":"38.68d","t":"the cursing thought of the wise pushes it forward;"},{"ref":"38.69","t":"‘From whom all the Daevas unseen and the Varenya fiends flee"},{"ref":"38.69a","t":"away in fear. Oh! may we never fall across the rush of the angry"},{"ref":"38.69b","t":"lord, who goes and rushes from a thousand sides against his foe,"},{"ref":"38.69c","t":"he, of the ten thousand spies, the powerful, all-knowing, undeceivable"},{"ref":"38.69d","t":"god."},{"ref":"38.69e","t":"‘For his brightness and glory, I will offer him a sacrifice worth"},{"ref":"38.69f","t":"being heard...."},{"ref":"38.70","t":"‘We sacrifice unto Mithra, the lord of wide pastures,..."},{"ref":"38.70a","t":"sleepless, and ever awake;"},{"ref":"38.70b","t":"‘Before whom Verethraghna, made by Ahura, runs opposing the foes"},{"ref":"38.70c","t":"in the shape of a boar, a sharp-toothed he-boar, a sharp-jawed"},{"ref":"38.70d","t":"boar, that kills at one stroke, pursuing, wrathful, with a dripping"},{"ref":"38.70e","t":"face; strong, with iron feet, iron fore-paws, iron weapons, an"},{"ref":"38.70f","t":"iron tail, and iron jaws;"},{"ref":"38.71","t":"‘Who, eagerly clinging to the fleeing foe, along with Manly"},{"ref":"38.71a","t":"Courage, smites the foe in battle, and does not think he has smitten"},{"ref":"38.71b","t":"him, nor does he consider it a blow till he has smitten away the"},{"ref":"38.71c","t":"marrow and the column of life, the marrow and the spring of existence."},{"ref":"38.72","t":"‘He cuts all the limbs to pieces, and mingles, together with"},{"ref":"38.72a","t":"the earth, the bones, hair, brains, and blood of the men who have"},{"ref":"38.72b","t":"lied unto Mithra."},{"ref":"38.72c","t":"‘For his brightness and glory, we offer him a sacrifice worth"},{"ref":"38.72d","t":"being heard...."},{"ref":"38.73","t":"‘We sacrifice unto Mithra, the lord of wide pastures,..."},{"ref":"38.73a","t":"sleepless, and ever awake;"},{"ref":"38.73b","t":"‘Who, with hands lifted up, rejoicing, cries out, speaking thus:"},{"ref":"38.74","t":"‘“O Ahura Mazda, most beneficent spirit! Maker of the"},{"ref":"38.74a","t":"material world, thou Holy One!"},{"ref":"38.74b","t":"‘“If men would worship me with a sacrifice in which I were"},{"ref":"38.74c","t":"invoked by my own name, as they worship the other gods with sacrifices"},{"ref":"38.74d","t":"in which they are invoked by their own names, then I should come"},{"ref":"38.74e","t":"to the faithful at the appointed time; I should come in the appointed"},{"ref":"38.74f","t":"time of my beautiful, immortal life.”"},{"ref":"38.75","t":"‘May we keep our field; may we never be exiles from our field,"},{"ref":"38.75a","t":"exiles from our house, exiles from our borough, exiles from our"},{"ref":"38.75b","t":"town, exiles from our country."},{"ref":"38.76","t":"‘Thou dashest in pieces the malice of the malicious, the malice"},{"ref":"38.76a","t":"of the men of malice: dash thou in pieces the killers of faithful"},{"ref":"38.76b","t":"men!"},{"ref":"38.76c","t":"‘Thou hast good horses, thou hast a good chariot: thou art bringing"},{"ref":"38.76d","t":"help at every appeal, and art powerful."},{"ref":"38.77","t":"‘I will pray unto thee for help, with many consecrations,"},{"ref":"38.77a","t":"with good consecrations of libations; with many offerings, with"},{"ref":"38.77b","t":"good offerings of libations, that we, abiding in thee, may long"},{"ref":"38.77c","t":"inhabit a good abode, full of all the riches that can be wished"},{"ref":"38.77d","t":"for."},{"ref":"38.78","t":"‘Thou keepest those nations that tender a good worship to"},{"ref":"38.78a","t":"Mithra, the lord of wide pastures; thou dashest in pieces those"},{"ref":"38.78b","t":"that delight in havoc. Unto thee will I pray for help: may he"},{"ref":"38.78c","t":"come to us for help, the awful, most powerful Mithra, the worshipful"},{"ref":"38.78d","t":"and praiseworthy, the glorious lord of nations."},{"ref":"38.78e","t":"‘For his brightness and glory, I will offer him a sacrifice worth"},{"ref":"38.78f","t":"being heard...."},{"ref":"38.79","t":"‘We sacrifice unto Mithra, the lord of wide pastures,..."},{"ref":"38.79a","t":"sleepless, and ever awake;"},{"ref":"38.79b","t":"‘Who made a dwelling for Rashnu, and to whom Rashnu gave all his"},{"ref":"38.79c","t":"soul for long friendship;"},{"ref":"38.80","t":"‘Thou art a keeper and protector of the dwelling of those"},{"ref":"38.80a","t":"who lie not: thou art the maintainer of those who lie not. With"},{"ref":"38.80b","t":"thee hath Verethraghna, made by Ahura, contracted the best of"},{"ref":"38.80c","t":"all friendships, and thus it is how so many men who have lied"},{"ref":"38.80d","t":"unto Mithra, even privily, lie smitten down on the ground."},{"ref":"38.80e","t":"‘For his brightness and glory, I will offer him a sacrifice worth"},{"ref":"38.80f","t":"being heard...."},{"ref":"38.81","t":"‘We sacrifice unto Mithra, the lord of wide pastures,..."},{"ref":"38.81a","t":"sleepless, and ever awake;"},{"ref":"38.81b","t":"‘Who made a dwelling for Rashnu, and to whom Rashnu gave all his"},{"ref":"38.81c","t":"soul for long friendship;"},{"ref":"38.82","t":"‘To whom Ahura Mazda gave a thousand senses and ten thousand"},{"ref":"38.82a","t":"eyes to see. With those eyes and those senses, he watches the"},{"ref":"38.82b","t":"man who injures Mithra, the man who lies unto Mithra. Through"},{"ref":"38.82c","t":"those eyes and those senses, he is, undeceivable, he, of the ten"},{"ref":"38.82d","t":"thousand spies, the powerful, all-knowing, undeceivable god."},{"ref":"38.82e","t":"‘For his brightness and glory, I will offer him a sacrifice worth"},{"ref":"38.82f","t":"being heard...."},{"ref":"38.83","t":"‘We sacrifice unto Mithra, the lord of wide pastures,..."},{"ref":"38.83a","t":"sleepless, and ever awake;"},{"ref":"38.83b","t":"‘Whom the lord of the country invokes for help, with hands uplifted;"},{"ref":"38.83c","t":"‘Whom the lord of the town invokes for help, with hands uplifted;"},{"ref":"38.84","t":"‘Whom the lord of the borough invokes for help, with hands"},{"ref":"38.84a","t":"uplifted;"},{"ref":"38.84b","t":"‘Whom the master of the house invokes for help, with hands uplifted;"},{"ref":"38.84c","t":"‘Whom the.... in danger of death invokes for help, with hands"},{"ref":"38.84d","t":"uplifted;"},{"ref":"38.84e","t":"‘Whom the poor man, who follows the good law, when wronged and"},{"ref":"38.84f","t":"deprived of his rights, invokes for help, with hands uplifted."},{"ref":"38.85","t":"‘The voice of his wailing reaches up to the sky, it goes over"},{"ref":"38.85a","t":"the earth all around, it goes over the seven Karshuares, whether"},{"ref":"38.85b","t":"he utters his prayer in a low tone of voice or aloud."},{"ref":"38.86","t":"‘The cow driven astray invokes him for help, longing for the"},{"ref":"38.86a","t":"stables:"},{"ref":"38.86b","t":"‘“When will that bull, Mithra, the lord of wide pastures,"},{"ref":"38.86c","t":"bring us back, and make us reach the stables? when wilt he turn"},{"ref":"38.86d","t":"us back to the right way from the den of the Druj where we were"},{"ref":"38.86e","t":"driven?”"},{"ref":"38.87","t":"‘And to him with whom Mithra, the lord of wide pastures, has"},{"ref":"38.87a","t":"been satisfied, he comes with help; and of him with whom Mithra,"},{"ref":"38.87b","t":"the lord of wide pastures, has been offended, he crushes down"},{"ref":"38.87c","t":"the house, the borough, the town, the province, the country."},{"ref":"38.87d","t":"‘For his brightness and glory, I will offer him a sacrifice worth"},{"ref":"38.87e","t":"being heard...."},{"ref":"38.88","t":"‘We sacrifice unto Mithra, the lord of wide pastures,..."},{"ref":"38.88a","t":"sleepless, and ever awake;"},{"ref":"38.88b","t":"‘To whom the enlivening, healing, fair, lordly golden-eyed Haoma"},{"ref":"38.88c","t":"offered up a sacrifice on the highest of the heights, on the Haraiti"},{"ref":"38.88d","t":"Bareza, he the undefiled to one undefiled, with undefiled baresma,"},{"ref":"38.88e","t":"undefiled libations, and undefiled words;"},{"ref":"38.89","t":"‘Whom the holy Ahura Mazda has established as a priest, quick"},{"ref":"38.89a","t":"in performing the sacrifice and loud in song. He performed the"},{"ref":"38.89b","t":"sacrifice with a loud voice, as a priest quick in sacrifice and"},{"ref":"38.89c","t":"loud in song, a priest to Ahura Mazda, a priest to the Amesha-Spentas."},{"ref":"38.89d","t":"His voice reached up to the sky; went over the earth all around,"},{"ref":"38.89e","t":"went over the seven Karshvares."},{"ref":"38.90","t":"‘Who first lifted up Haomas, in a mortar inlaid with stars"},{"ref":"38.90a","t":"and made of a heavenly substance. Ahura Mazda longed for him,"},{"ref":"38.90b","t":"the Amesha-Spentas longed for him, for the well-slapen body of"},{"ref":"38.90c","t":"him whom the swift-horsed sun awakes for prayer from afar."},{"ref":"38.91","t":"‘Hail to Mithra, the lord of wide pastures, who has a thousand"},{"ref":"38.91a","t":"ears and ten thousand eyes! Thou art worthy of sacrifice and prayer:"},{"ref":"38.91b","t":"mayest thou have sacrifice and prayer in the houses of men! Hail"},{"ref":"38.91c","t":"to the man who shall offer thee a sacrifice, with the holy wood"},{"ref":"38.91d","t":"in his hand, the baresma in his hand, the holy meat in his hand,"},{"ref":"38.91e","t":"the holy mortar in his hand, with his hands well-washed, with"},{"ref":"38.91f","t":"the mortar well-washed, with the bundles of baresma tied up, the"},{"ref":"38.91g","t":"Haoma uplifted, and the Ahuna Vairya sung through."},{"ref":"38.92","t":"‘The holy Ahura Mazda confessed that religion and so did Vohu-Mano,"},{"ref":"38.92a","t":"so did Asha-Vahishta, so did Khshathra-Vairya, so did Spenta-Armaiti,"},{"ref":"38.92b","t":"so did Haurvatat and Ameretat; and all the Amesha-Spentas longed"},{"ref":"38.92c","t":"for and confessed his religion. The kind Mazda conferred upon"},{"ref":"38.92d","t":"him the mastership of the world; and [so did they] who saw thee"},{"ref":"38.92e","t":"amongst all creatures the right lord and master of the world,"},{"ref":"38.92f","t":"the best cleanser of these creatures."},{"ref":"38.93","t":"‘So mayest thou in both worlds, mayest thou keep us in both"},{"ref":"38.93a","t":"worlds, O Mithra, lord of wide pastures! both in this material"},{"ref":"38.93b","t":"world and in the world of the spirit, from the fiend of Death,"},{"ref":"38.93c","t":"from the fiend Aeshma, from the fiendish hordes, that lift up"},{"ref":"38.93d","t":"the spear of havoc, and from the onsets of Aeshma, wherein the"},{"ref":"38.93e","t":"evil-doing Aeshma rushes along with Vidotu, made by the Daevas."},{"ref":"38.94","t":"‘So mayest thou, O Mithra, lord of wide pastures! give swiftness"},{"ref":"38.94a","t":"to our teams, strength to our own bodies, and that we may watch"},{"ref":"38.94b","t":"with full success those who hate us, smite down our foes, and"},{"ref":"38.94c","t":"destroy at one stroke our adversaries, our enemies and those who"},{"ref":"38.94d","t":"hate us."},{"ref":"38.94e","t":"‘For his brightness and glory, I will offer him a sacrifice worth"},{"ref":"38.94f","t":"being heard...."},{"ref":"38.95","t":"‘We sacrifice unto Mithra, the lord of wide pastures,..."},{"ref":"38.95a","t":"sleepless, and ever awake;"},{"ref":"38.95b","t":"‘Who goes over the earth, all her breadth over, after the setting"},{"ref":"38.95c","t":"of the sun, touches both ends of this wide, round earth, whose"},{"ref":"38.95d","t":"ends tie afar, and surveys everything that is between the earth"},{"ref":"38.95e","t":"and the heavens,"},{"ref":"38.96","t":"‘Swinging in his hands a club with a hundred knots, a hundred"},{"ref":"38.96a","t":"edges, that rushes forwards and fells men down; a club cast out"},{"ref":"38.96b","t":"of red brass, of strong, golden brass; the strongest of all weapons,"},{"ref":"38.96c","t":"the most victorious of all weapons;"},{"ref":"38.97","t":"‘From whom Angra Mainyu, who is all death, flees away in fear;"},{"ref":"38.97a","t":"from whom Aeshma, the evil-doing Peshotanu, flees away in fear;"},{"ref":"38.97b","t":"from whom the long-handed Bushyasta flees away in fear; from whom"},{"ref":"38.97c","t":"all the Daevas unseen and the Varenya fiends flee away in fear."},{"ref":"38.98","t":"‘Oh! may we never fall across the rush of Mithra, the lord"},{"ref":"38.98a","t":"of wide pastures, when in anger! May Mithra, the lord of wide"},{"ref":"38.98b","t":"pastures, never smite us in his anger; he who stands up upon this"},{"ref":"38.98c","t":"earth as the strongest of all gods, the most valiant of all gods,"},{"ref":"38.98d","t":"the most energetic of all god, th swiftest of all gods, the most"},{"ref":"38.98e","t":"fiend-smiting of all gods, he, Mithra, the lord of wide pastures."},{"ref":"38.98f","t":"‘For his brightness and glory, I will offer him a sacrifice worth"},{"ref":"38.98g","t":"being heard...."},{"ref":"38.99","t":"‘We sacrifice unto Mithra, the lord of wide pastures,..."},{"ref":"38.99a","t":"sleepless, and ever awake;"},{"ref":"38.99b","t":"‘From whom all the Daevas unseen and the Varenya fiends flee away"},{"ref":"38.99c","t":"in fear."},{"ref":"38.99d","t":"‘The lord of nations, Mithra, the lord of wide pastures, drives"},{"ref":"38.99e","t":"forward at the right-hand side of this wide, round earth, whose"},{"ref":"38.99f","t":"ends lie afar."},{"ref":"38.100","t":"‘At his right hand drives the good, holy Sraosha; at his left"},{"ref":"38.100a","t":"hand drives the tall and strong Rashnu; on all sides around him"},{"ref":"38.100b","t":"drive the waters, the plants, and the Fravashis of the faithful."},{"ref":"38.101","t":"‘In his might, he ever brings to them falcon-feathered arrows,"},{"ref":"38.101a","t":"and, when diiving, he himself comes there, where are nations,"},{"ref":"38.101b","t":"enemy to Mithra, he, first and foremost, strikes blows with his"},{"ref":"38.101c","t":"club on the horse and his rider; he throws fear and fright upon"},{"ref":"38.101d","t":"the horse and his rider."},{"ref":"38.101e","t":"‘For his brightness and glory, I will offer him a sacrifice worth"},{"ref":"38.101f","t":"being heard...."},{"ref":"38.102","t":"‘We sacrifice unto Mithra, the lord of wide pastures,..."},{"ref":"38.102a","t":"sleepless, and ever awake;"},{"ref":"38.102b","t":"‘The warrior of the white horse, of the sharp spear, the tong"},{"ref":"38.102c","t":"spear, the quick arrows; foreseeing and clever;"},{"ref":"38.103","t":"‘Whom Ahura Mazda has established to maintain and look over"},{"ref":"38.103a","t":"all this moving world, and who maintains and looks over all this"},{"ref":"38.103b","t":"moving world; who, never sleeping, wakefully guards the creation"},{"ref":"38.103c","t":"of Mazda; who, never sleeping, wakefully maintains the creation"},{"ref":"38.103d","t":"of Mazda;"},{"ref":"38.103e","t":"‘For his brightness and glory, I will offer him a sacrifice worth"},{"ref":"38.103f","t":"being heard...."},{"ref":"38.104","t":"‘We sacrifice unto Mithra, the lord of wide pastures,..."},{"ref":"38.104a","t":"sleepless, and ever awake;"},{"ref":"38.104b","t":"‘Whose long arms, strong with Mithra-strength, encompass what"},{"ref":"38.104c","t":"he seizes in the easternmost river and what he beats with the"},{"ref":"38.104d","t":"westernmost river, what is by the Sanaka of the Rangha and what"},{"ref":"38.104e","t":"is by the boundary of the earth."},{"ref":"38.105","t":"‘And thou, O Mithra! encompassing all this around, do thou"},{"ref":"38.105a","t":"reach it, all over, with thy arms."},{"ref":"38.105b","t":"‘The man without glory, led astray from the right way, grieves"},{"ref":"38.105c","t":"in his heart; the man without glory thinks thus in himself: “That"},{"ref":"38.105d","t":"careless Mithra does not see all the evil that is done, nor all"},{"ref":"38.105e","t":"the lies that are told.”"},{"ref":"38.106","t":"‘But I think thus in my heart:"},{"ref":"38.106a","t":"‘“Should the evil thoughts of the earthly man be a hundred"},{"ref":"38.106b","t":"times worse, they would not rise so high as the good thoughts"},{"ref":"38.106c","t":"of the heavenly Mithra;"},{"ref":"38.106d","t":"‘“Should the evil words of the earthly man be a hundred times"},{"ref":"38.106e","t":"worse, they would not rise so high as the good words of the heavenly"},{"ref":"38.106f","t":"Mithra;"},{"ref":"38.106g","t":"‘“Should the evil deeds of the earthly man be a hundred times"},{"ref":"38.106h","t":"worse, they would not rise so high as the good deeds of the heavenly"},{"ref":"38.106i","t":"Mithra;"},{"ref":"38.107","t":"‘“Should the heavenly wisdom in the earthly man be a"},{"ref":"38.107a","t":"hundred times greater, it would not rise so high as the heavenly"},{"ref":"38.107b","t":"w’isdom in the heavenly Mithra;"},{"ref":"38.107c","t":"‘‘And thus, should the ears of the earthly man hear a hundred"},{"ref":"38.107d","t":"time better, he would not hear so well as the heavenly Mithra,"},{"ref":"38.107e","t":"whose ear hears well who has a thousand senses, and sees every"},{"ref":"38.107f","t":"man that tells a lie.”"},{"ref":"38.107g","t":"‘Mithra stands up in his strength, he drives in the awfulness"},{"ref":"38.107h","t":"of royalty, and sends from his eyes beautiful looks that shine"},{"ref":"38.107i","t":"from afar, (saying):"},{"ref":"38.108","t":"‘“Who will offer me a sacrifice? Who will lie unto me? Who"},{"ref":"38.108a","t":"thinks me a god worthy of a good sacrifice? Who thinks me worthy"},{"ref":"38.108b","t":"only of a bad sacrifice? To whom shall I, in my might, impart"},{"ref":"38.108c","t":"brightness and glory? To whom bodily health? To whom shall I,"},{"ref":"38.108d","t":"in my might, impart riches and full weal? Whom shall I bless by"},{"ref":"38.108e","t":"raising him a virtuous offspring?"},{"ref":"38.109","t":"‘“To whom shall I give in return, without his thinking"},{"ref":"38.109a","t":"of it, the awful sovereignty, beautifully. arrayed, with many"},{"ref":"38.109b","t":"armies, and most perfect; the sovereignty of an all-powerful tyrant,"},{"ref":"38.109c","t":"who fells down heads, valiant, smiting, and unsmitten; who orders"},{"ref":"38.109d","t":"chastisement to be done and his order is done at once, which he"},{"ref":"38.109e","t":"has ordered in his anger?”"},{"ref":"38.109f","t":"‘O Mithra! when thou art offended and not satisfied, he soothes"},{"ref":"38.109g","t":"thy mind, and makes Mithra satisfied."},{"ref":"38.110","t":"‘“To whom shall I, in my might, impart sickness and death?"},{"ref":"38.110a","t":"To whom shall I impart poverty and sterility? Of whom shall I"},{"ref":"38.110b","t":"at one stroke cut off the offspring!"},{"ref":"38.111","t":"‘“From whom shall I take away, without his thinking of"},{"ref":"38.111a","t":"it, the awful sovereignty, beautifully arrayed, with many armies,"},{"ref":"38.111b","t":"and most perfect; the sovereignty of an all-powerful tyrant, who"},{"ref":"38.111c","t":"fells down heads, valiant, smiting, and unsmitten; who orders"},{"ref":"38.111d","t":"chastisement to be done and his order is done at once, which he"},{"ref":"38.111e","t":"has ordered in his anger.”"},{"ref":"38.111f","t":"‘O Mithra! while thou art satisfied and not angry, he moves thy"},{"ref":"38.111g","t":"heart to anger, and makes Mithra unsatisfied."},{"ref":"38.111h","t":"‘For his brightness and glory, I will offer him a sacrifice worth"},{"ref":"38.111i","t":"being heard...."},{"ref":"38.112","t":"‘We sacrifice unto Mithra, the lord of wide pastures,..."},{"ref":"38.112a","t":"sleepless, and ever awake;"},{"ref":"38.112b","t":"‘A warrior with a silver helm, a golden cuirass, who kills with"},{"ref":"38.112c","t":"the poniard, strong, valiant, lord of the borough. Bright are"},{"ref":"38.112d","t":"the ways of Mithra, by which he goes towards the country, when,"},{"ref":"38.112e","t":"wishing well, he turns its plains and vales to pasture grounds,"},{"ref":"38.113","t":"‘And then cattle and males come to graze, as many as he wants."},{"ref":"38.113a","t":"‘May Mithra and Ahura, the high gods, come to us for help, when"},{"ref":"38.113b","t":"the poniard lifts up its voice aloud, when the nostrils of the"},{"ref":"38.113c","t":"horses quiver, when the poniards.... when the, strings of the"},{"ref":"38.113d","t":"bows whistle and shoot sharp arrows; then the brood of those whose"},{"ref":"38.113e","t":"libations are hated fall smitten to the ground, with their hair"},{"ref":"38.113f","t":"torn off."},{"ref":"38.114","t":"‘So mayest thou, O Mithra, lord of wide pastures! give swiftness"},{"ref":"38.114a","t":"to our teams, strength to our own bodies, and that we may watch"},{"ref":"38.114b","t":"with full success those who hate us, smite down our foes, and"},{"ref":"38.114c","t":"destroy at one stroke our adversaries, our enemies, and those"},{"ref":"38.114d","t":"who hate us."},{"ref":"38.114e","t":"‘For his brightness and glory, I will offer him a sacrifice worth"},{"ref":"38.114f","t":"being heard...."},{"ref":"38.115","t":"‘We sacrifice unto Mithra, the lord of wide pastures,..."},{"ref":"38.115a","t":"sleepless, and ever awake."},{"ref":"38.115b","t":"‘O Mithra, lord of wide pastures! thou master of the house, of"},{"ref":"38.115c","t":"the borough, of the town, of the country, thou Zarathushtrotema!"},{"ref":"38.116","t":"‘Mithra is twentyfold between two friends or two relations;"},{"ref":"38.116a","t":"‘Mithra is thirtyfold between two men of the same group;"},{"ref":"38.116b","t":"‘Mithra is fortyfold between two partners;"},{"ref":"38.116c","t":"‘Mithra is fiftyfold between wife and husband;"},{"ref":"38.116d","t":"‘Mithra is sixtyfold between two pupils (of the same master);"},{"ref":"38.116e","t":"‘Mithra is seventyfold between the pupil and his master;"},{"ref":"38.116f","t":"‘Mithra is eightyfold between the son-in-law and his father-in-law;"},{"ref":"38.116g","t":"‘Mithra is ninetyfold between two brothers;"},{"ref":"38.117","t":"‘Mithra is a hundredfold between the father and the son;"},{"ref":"38.117a","t":"‘Mithra is a thousandfold between two nations;"},{"ref":"38.117b","t":"‘Mithra is ten thousandfold when connected with the Law of Mazda,"},{"ref":"38.117c","t":"and then he will be every day of victorious strength."},{"ref":"38.118","t":"‘May I come unto thee with a prayer that goes lowly or goes"},{"ref":"38.118a","t":"highly! As this sun rises up above the Hara Berezaiti and then"},{"ref":"38.118b","t":"fulfils its career, so may I, O Spitama! with a prayer that goes"},{"ref":"38.118c","t":"lowly or goes highly, rise up above the will of the fiend Angra"},{"ref":"38.118d","t":"Mainyu!"},{"ref":"38.118e","t":"‘For his brightness and glory, I will offer him a sacrifice worth"},{"ref":"38.118f","t":"being heard...."},{"ref":"38.119","t":"‘We sacrifice unto Mithra, the lord of wide pastwes,..."},{"ref":"38.119a","t":"sleepless, and ever awake,"},{"ref":"38.119b","t":"‘Offer up a sacrifice unto Mithra, O Spitama! and order thy pupils"},{"ref":"38.119c","t":"to do the same."},{"ref":"38.119d","t":"‘Let the worshipper of Mazda sacrifice unto thee with small cattle,"},{"ref":"38.119e","t":"with black cattle, with flying birds, gliding forward on wings."},{"ref":"38.120","t":"‘To Mithra all the faithful worshiypers of Mazda must give"},{"ref":"38.120a","t":"strength and energy with offered and proffered Haomas, which the"},{"ref":"38.120b","t":"Zaotar proffers unto him and gives in sacrifice. Let the faithful"},{"ref":"38.120c","t":"man drink of the libations cleanly prepared, which if he does,"},{"ref":"38.120d","t":"if he offers them unto Mithra, the lord of wide pastures, Mithra"},{"ref":"38.120e","t":"will be pleased with him and without anger.’"},{"ref":"38.121","t":"Zarathushtra asked him: ‘O Ahura Mazda! how shall the faithful"},{"ref":"38.121a","t":"man drink the libations cleanly prepared, which if he does and"},{"ref":"38.121b","t":"he offers them unto Mithra, the lord of wide pastures, Mithra"},{"ref":"38.121c","t":"will be pleased with him and without anger?’","hvShift6":[[0,0],[18,17]]},{"ref":"38.122","t":"Ahura Mazda answered: ‘Let them wash their bodies three days"},{"ref":"38.122a","t":"and three nights; let them undergo thirty strokes for the sacrifice"},{"ref":"38.122b","t":"and prayer unto Mithra, the lord of wide pastures. Let them wash"},{"ref":"38.122c","t":"their bodies two days and two nights; let them undergo twenty"},{"ref":"38.122d","t":"strokes for the sacrifice and prayer unto Mithra, the lord of"},{"ref":"38.122e","t":"wide pastures. Let no man drink of these libations who does not"},{"ref":"38.122f","t":"know the staota yesnya: Vispe ratavo."},{"ref":"38.122g","t":"‘For his brightness and glory, I will offer him a sacriace worth"},{"ref":"38.122h","t":"being heard...."},{"ref":"38.123","t":"‘We sacrifice unto Mithra, the lord of wide pastures,..."},{"ref":"38.123a","t":"sleepless, and ever awake;"},{"ref":"38.123b","t":"‘To whom Ahura Mazda offered up a sacrifice in the shining Garo-nmana."},{"ref":"38.124","t":"‘With his arms lifted up towards Immortality, Mithra, the"},{"ref":"38.124a","t":"lord of wide pastures, drives forward from the shining Garo-nmana,"},{"ref":"38.124b","t":"in a beautiful chariot that drives on, ever-swift, adorned with"},{"ref":"38.124c","t":"all sorts of ornaments, and made of gold."},{"ref":"38.125","t":"‘Four stallions draw that chariot, all of the same white colour,"},{"ref":"38.125a","t":"living on heavenly food and undying. The hoofs of their fore-feet"},{"ref":"38.125b","t":"are shod with gold, the hoofs of their hind-feet are shod with"},{"ref":"38.125c","t":"silver; all are yoked to the same pole, and wear the yoke and"},{"ref":"38.125d","t":"the cross-beams of the yoke, fastened with hooks of Khshathra"},{"ref":"38.125e","t":"vairya to a beautiful...."},{"ref":"38.126","t":"‘At his right hand drives Rashnu-Razishta, the most beneficent"},{"ref":"38.126a","t":"and most well-shapen."},{"ref":"38.126b","t":"‘At his left hand drives the most upright Chista, the holy one,"},{"ref":"38.126c","t":"bearing libations in her hands, clothed with white clothes, and"},{"ref":"38.126d","t":"white herself; and the cursing thought of the Law of Mazda."},{"ref":"38.127","t":"‘Close by him drives the strong cursing thought of the wise"},{"ref":"38.127a","t":"man, opposing foes in the shape of a boar, a sharp-toothed he-boar,"},{"ref":"38.127b","t":"a sharp-jawed boar, that kills at one stroke, pursuing, wrathful,"},{"ref":"38.127c","t":"with a dripping face, strong and swift to run, and rushing all"},{"ref":"38.127d","t":"around."},{"ref":"38.127e","t":"‘Behind him drives Atar, all in a blaze, and the awful kingly"},{"ref":"38.127f","t":"Glory."},{"ref":"38.128","t":"‘On a side of the chariot of Mithra, the lord of wide pastures,"},{"ref":"38.128a","t":"stand a thousand bows well-made, with a string of cowgut; they"},{"ref":"38.128b","t":"go through the heavenly space, they fall through the heavenly"},{"ref":"38.128c","t":"space upon the skulls of the Daevas."},{"ref":"38.129","t":"‘On a side of the chariot of Mithra, the lord of wide pastures,"},{"ref":"38.129a","t":"stand a thousand vulture-feathered arrows, with a golden mouth,"},{"ref":"38.129b","t":"with a horn shaft, with a brass tail, and well-made. They go through"},{"ref":"38.129c","t":"the heavenly space, they fall through the heavenly space upon"},{"ref":"38.129d","t":"the skulls of the Daevas."},{"ref":"38.130","t":"‘On a side of the chariot of Mithra, the lord of wide pastures,"},{"ref":"38.130a","t":"stand a thousand spears well-made and sharp-piercing. They go"},{"ref":"38.130b","t":"through the heavenly space, they fall through the heavenly space"},{"ref":"38.130c","t":"upon the skulls of the Daevas."},{"ref":"38.130d","t":"‘On a side of the chariot of Mithra, the lord of wide pastures,"},{"ref":"38.130e","t":"stand a thousand steel-hammers, two-edged, well-made. They go"},{"ref":"38.130f","t":"through the heavenly space, they fall through the heavenly space"},{"ref":"38.130g","t":"upon the skulls of the Daevas."},{"ref":"38.131","t":"‘On a side of the chariot of Mithra, the lord of wide pastures,"},{"ref":"38.131a","t":"stand a thousand swords, two-edged and well-made. They go through"},{"ref":"38.131b","t":"the heavenly space, they fall through the heavenly space upon"},{"ref":"38.131c","t":"the skulls of the Daevas."},{"ref":"38.131d","t":"‘On a side of the chariot of Mithra, the lord of wide pastures,"},{"ref":"38.131e","t":"stand a thousand maces of iron, well-made. They go through the"},{"ref":"38.131f","t":"heavenly space, they fall through the heavenly space upon the"},{"ref":"38.131g","t":"skulls of the Daevas."},{"ref":"38.132","t":"‘On a side of the chariot of Mithra, the lord of wide pastures,"},{"ref":"38.132a","t":"stands a beautiful well-falling club, with a hundred knots, a"},{"ref":"38.132b","t":"hundred edges, that rushes forward and fells men down; a club"},{"ref":"38.132c","t":"cast out of red brass, of strong, golden brass; the strongest"},{"ref":"38.132d","t":"of all weapons, the most victorious of all weapons. It goes through"},{"ref":"38.132e","t":"the heavenly space, it falls through the heavenly space upon the"},{"ref":"38.132f","t":"skulls of the Daevas."},{"ref":"38.133","t":"After he has smitten the Daevas, after he has smitten down"},{"ref":"38.133a","t":"the men who lied unto Mithra, Mithra, the lord of wide pastures,"},{"ref":"38.133b","t":"drives forward through Arezahe and Savahe, through Fradadhafshu"},{"ref":"38.133c","t":"and Vidadhafshu, through Vourubareshti and Vouru-jareshti, through"},{"ref":"38.133d","t":"this our Karshvare, the bright Hvaniratha."},{"ref":"38.134","t":"‘Angra Mainyu, who is all death, flees away in fear; Aeshma,"},{"ref":"38.134a","t":"the evil-doing Peshotanu, flees away in fear; the long-handed"},{"ref":"38.134b","t":"Bushyasta flees away in fear; all the Daevas unseen and the Varenya"},{"ref":"38.134c","t":"fiends flee away in fear."},{"ref":"38.135","t":"‘Oh! may we never fall across the rush of Mithra, the lord"},{"ref":"38.135a","t":"of wide pastures, when in anger! May Mithra, the lord of wide"},{"ref":"38.135b","t":"pastures, never smite us in his anger; he who stands up upon this"},{"ref":"38.135c","t":"earth as the strongest of all gods, the most valiant of all gods,"},{"ref":"38.135d","t":"the most energetic of all gods, the swiftest of all gods, the"},{"ref":"38.135e","t":"most fiend-smiting of all gods, he, Mithra, the lord of wide pastures."},{"ref":"38.135f","t":"‘For his brightness and glory, I will offer him a sacrifice worth"},{"ref":"38.135g","t":"being heard...."},{"ref":"38.136","t":"‘We sacrifice unto Mithra, the lord of wide pastures,..."},{"ref":"38.136a","t":"sleepless, and ever awake;"},{"ref":"38.136b","t":"‘For whom white stallions, yoked to his chariot, draw it, on one"},{"ref":"38.136c","t":"golden wheel, with a full shining axle."},{"ref":"38.137","t":"‘If Mithra takes his libations to his own dwelling, “Happy"},{"ref":"38.137a","t":"that man, I think,” - said Ahura Mazda,- “O holy Zarathra!"},{"ref":"38.137b","t":"for whom a holy priest, as pious as any in the world, who is the"},{"ref":"38.137c","t":"Word incarnate, offers up a sacrifice unto Mithra with bundles"},{"ref":"38.137d","t":"of baresma and with the [proper] words."},{"ref":"38.137e","t":"‘“Straight to that man, I think, will Mithra come, to visit"},{"ref":"38.137f","t":"his dwelling,"},{"ref":"38.138","t":"‘“When Mithra’s boons will come to him, as he follows"},{"ref":"38.138a","t":"God’s teaching, and thinks according to God’s teaching."},{"ref":"38.138b","t":"‘“Woe to that man, I think,” - said Ahura Mazda, - “O"},{"ref":"38.138c","t":"holy Zarathushtra! for whom an unholy priest, not pious, who is"},{"ref":"38.138d","t":"not the Word incarnate, stands behind the baresma, however full"},{"ref":"38.138e","t":"may be the bundles of baresma he ties, however long may be the"},{"ref":"38.138f","t":"sacrifice he performs.”"},{"ref":"38.139","t":"‘He does not delight Ahura Mazda, nor the other Amesha-Spentas,"},{"ref":"38.139a","t":"nor Mithra, the lord of wide pastures, he who thus scorns Mazda,"},{"ref":"38.139b","t":"and the other Amesha-Spentas, and Mithra, the lord of wide pastures,"},{"ref":"38.139c","t":"and the Law, and Rashnu, and Arstat, who makes the world grow,"},{"ref":"38.139d","t":"who makes the world increase."},{"ref":"38.139e","t":"‘For his brightness and glory, I will offer him a sacrifice worth"},{"ref":"38.139f","t":"being heard...."},{"ref":"38.140","t":"‘We sacrifice unto Mithra, the lord of wide pastures,..."},{"ref":"38.140a","t":"sleepless, and ever awake."},{"ref":"38.140b","t":"‘I will offer up a sacrifice unto the good Mithra, O Spitama!"},{"ref":"38.140c","t":"unto the strong, heavenly god, who is foremost, highly merciful,"},{"ref":"38.140d","t":"and peerless; whose house is above, a stout and strong warrior;"},{"ref":"38.141","t":"‘Victorious and armed with a well-fashioned weapon, watchful"},{"ref":"38.141a","t":"in darkness and undeceivable. He is the stoutest of the stoutest,"},{"ref":"38.141b","t":"he is the strongest of the strongest, he is the most intelligent"},{"ref":"38.141c","t":"of the gods, he is victorious and endowed with Glory: he, of the"},{"ref":"38.141d","t":"ten thousand eyes, of the ten thousand spies, the powerful, all-knowing,"},{"ref":"38.141e","t":"undeceivable god."},{"ref":"38.141f","t":"‘For his brightness and glory, I will offer him a sacrifice worth"},{"ref":"38.141g","t":"being heard...."},{"ref":"38.142","t":"‘We sacrifice unto Mithra, the lord of wide pastures,..."},{"ref":"38.142a","t":"sleepless, and ever awake;"},{"ref":"38.142b","t":"‘Who, with his manifold knowledge, powerfully increases the creation"},{"ref":"38.142c","t":"of Spenta Mainyu, and is a well-created and most great Yazata,"},{"ref":"38.142d","t":"self-shining like the moon, when he makes his own body shine;"},{"ref":"38.143","t":"‘Whose face is flashing with light like the face of the star"},{"ref":"38.143a","t":"Tistrya; whose chariot is embraced by that goddess who is foremost"},{"ref":"38.143b","t":"amongst those who have no deceit in them, O Spitama! who is fairer"},{"ref":"38.143c","t":"than any creature in the world, and full of light to shine. I"},{"ref":"38.143d","t":"will worship that chariot, wrought by the Maker, Ahura Mazda,"},{"ref":"38.143e","t":"inlaid with stars and made of a heavenly substance; (the chariot)"},{"ref":"38.143f","t":"of Mithra, who has ten thousand spies, the powerful, all-knowing,"},{"ref":"38.143g","t":"undeceivable god."},{"ref":"38.143h","t":"‘For his brightness and glory, I will offer him a sacrifice worth"},{"ref":"38.143i","t":"being heard...."},{"ref":"38.144","t":"‘We sacrifice unto Mithra, the lord of wide pastures, who"},{"ref":"38.144a","t":"is truth-speaking, a chief in assemblies, with a thousand ears,"},{"ref":"38.144b","t":"well-shapen, with a thousand eyes, high, with full knowledge,"},{"ref":"38.144c","t":"strong, sleepless, and ever awake."},{"ref":"38.144d","t":"‘We sacrifice unto the Mithra around countries;"},{"ref":"38.144e","t":"‘We sacrifice unto the Mithra within countries;"},{"ref":"38.144f","t":"‘We sacrifice unto the Mithra in this country;"},{"ref":"38.144g","t":"‘We sacrifice unto the Mithra above countries;"},{"ref":"38.144h","t":"‘We sacrifice unto the Mithra under countries;"},{"ref":"38.144i","t":"‘We sacrifice unto the Mithra before countries;"},{"ref":"38.144j","t":"‘We sacrifice unto the Mithra behind countries."},{"ref":"38.145","t":"‘We sacrifice unto Mithra and Ahura, the two great, imperishable,"},{"ref":"38.145a","t":"holy gods; and unto the stars, and the moon, and the sun, with"},{"ref":"38.145b","t":"the trees that yield up baresma. We sacrifice unto Mithra, the"},{"ref":"38.145c","t":"lord of all countries."},{"ref":"38.145d","t":"‘For his brightness and glory, I will offer unto him a sacrifice"},{"ref":"38.145e","t":"worth being heard, namely, unto Mithra, the lord of wide pastures."},{"ref":"38.145f","t":"‘Yatha ahu vairyo: The will of the Lord is the law of holiness...."},{"ref":"38.145g","t":"‘I bless the sacrifice and p yer, and the strength and vigour"},{"ref":"38.145h","t":"of Mithra, the lord of wide pastures, who has a thousand ears,"},{"ref":"38.145i","t":"ten thousand eyes, a Yazata invoked by his own name; and that"},{"ref":"38.145j","t":"of Rama Hvastra."},{"ref":"38.145k","t":"‘Ashem Vohu: Holiness is the best of all good...."},{"ref":"38.145l","t":"‘[Give] unto that man brightness and glory,... give him the"},{"ref":"38.145m","t":"bright, all-happy, blissful abode of the holy Ones!’"},{"sp":"HDR","t":"11. Srosh Yasht Hadokht"},{"ref":"39.0","t":"May Ahura Mazda be rejoiced!...."},{"ref":"39.0a","t":"Ashem Vohu: Holiness is the best of all good...."},{"ref":"39.0b","t":"I confess myself a worshipper of Mazda, a follower of Zarathushtra,"},{"ref":"39.0c","t":"one who hates the Daevas and obeys the laws of Ahura;"},{"ref":"39.0d","t":"For sacrifice, prayer, propitiation, and glorification unto [Havani],"},{"ref":"39.0e","t":"the holy and master of holiness...."},{"ref":"39.0f","t":"Unto the holy, strong Sraosha, who is the incarnate Word, a mighty-speared"},{"ref":"39.0g","t":"and lordly god,"},{"ref":"39.0h","t":"Be propitiation, with sacrifice, prayer, propitiation, and glorification."},{"ref":"39.0i","t":"Yatha ahu vairyo: The will of the Lord is the law of holiness...."},{"ref":"39.1","t":"We sacrifice unto the holy, tall-formed, fiend-smiting Sraosha,"},{"ref":"39.1a","t":"who makes the world increase, the holy and master of holiness."},{"ref":"39.1b","t":"Good prayer, excellent prayer to the worlds, O Zarathushtra!"},{"ref":"39.2","t":"This it is that takes away the friendship of the fiend and"},{"ref":"39.2a","t":"fiends, of the he-fiend and of the she-fiend; it turns away in"},{"ref":"39.2b","t":"giddiness their eyes, minds, ears, hands, feet, mouths, and tongues;"},{"ref":"39.2c","t":"as good prayer, without deceit and without harm, is Manly Courage,"},{"ref":"39.2d","t":"and turns away the Druj."},{"ref":"39.3","t":"The holy Sraosha, the best protector ofthe poor, is fiend-smiting;"},{"ref":"39.3a","t":"he is the best smiter of the Druj."},{"ref":"39.3b","t":"The faithful one who pronounces most words of blessing is the"},{"ref":"39.3c","t":"most victorious in victory; the Mathra Spenta takes best the unseen"},{"ref":"39.3d","t":"Druj way. The Ahuna Vairya is the best fiend-smiter among all"},{"ref":"39.3e","t":"spells; the word of truth is the fighter that is the best of all"},{"ref":"39.3f","t":"fiend-smiters."},{"ref":"39.3g","t":"The Law of the worshippers of Mazda is the truest giver of all"},{"ref":"39.3h","t":"the good things of all those that are the offspring of the good"},{"ref":"39.3i","t":"principle; and so is the Law of Zarathushtra."},{"ref":"39.4","t":"And he who should pronounce that word, O Zarathushtra! either"},{"ref":"39.4a","t":"a man or a woman with a mind all intent on holiness, with words"},{"ref":"39.4b","t":"all intent on holiness, with deeds all intent on holiness, when"},{"ref":"39.4c","t":"he is in fear either of high waters or of the darkness of a rainy"},{"ref":"39.4d","t":"night;"},{"ref":"39.4e","t":"Or at the fords of a river, or at the branching-off of roads;"},{"ref":"39.4f","t":"Or in the meeting together of the faithful, or the rushing together"},{"ref":"39.4g","t":"of the worshippers of the Daevas;"},{"ref":"39.5","t":"Whether on the road or in the law he has to fear, not in that"},{"ref":"39.5a","t":"day nor in that night shall the tormenting fiend, who wants to"},{"ref":"39.5b","t":"torment him, prevail to throw upon him the look of his evil eye,"},{"ref":"39.5c","t":"and the malice of the thief who carries off cattle shall not reach"},{"ref":"39.5d","t":"him."},{"ref":"39.6","t":"Pronounce then that word, O Zarathushtra! that word to be"},{"ref":"39.6a","t":"spoken, when thou fall upon the idolaters and thieves and Daevas"},{"ref":"39.6b","t":"rushing together. Then the malice of the wicked worshippers of"},{"ref":"39.6c","t":"the Daevas, of the Yatus and their followers, of the Pairikas"},{"ref":"39.6d","t":"and their followers, will be affrighted and rush away. Down are"},{"ref":"39.6e","t":"the Daevas! Down are the Daeva-worshippers, and they take back"},{"ref":"39.6f","t":"their mouths from biting."},{"ref":"39.7","t":"And therefore we take around us the holy-natured Sraosha,"},{"ref":"39.7a","t":"the holy, the fiend-smiter, as one does with shepherds’ dogs;"},{"ref":"39.7b","t":"therefore we sacrifice unto the holy-natured Sraosha, the holy,"},{"ref":"39.7c","t":"the fiend-smiter, with good thoughts, good words, and good deeds."},{"ref":"39.8","t":"For his brightness and glory, for his strength and victorious"},{"ref":"39.8a","t":"power, for his offering sacrifices unto the gods, I will offer"},{"ref":"39.8b","t":"him a sacrifice worth being heard. I will offer up libations unto"},{"ref":"39.8c","t":"the holy Sraosha, unto the great Ashi Vanguhi, and unto Nairyo-sangha,"},{"ref":"39.8d","t":"the tall-formed."},{"ref":"39.8e","t":"So may the holy Sraosha, the fiend-smiter, come to us for help!"},{"ref":"39.9","t":"We worship the holy Sraosha; we worship the great master,"},{"ref":"39.9a","t":"Ahura Mazda, who is supreme in holiness, who is the foremost to"},{"ref":"39.9b","t":"do deeds of holiness."},{"ref":"39.9c","t":"We worship all the words of Zarathushtra, and all the good deeds,"},{"ref":"39.9d","t":"those done and those to be done."},{"ref":"39.9e","t":"Yenhe hatam: All those beings of whom Ahura Mazda...."},{"ref":"39.10","t":"We sacrifice unto the holy, tall-formed fiend-smiting Sraosha,"},{"ref":"39.10a","t":"who makes the world increase, the holy and master of holiness;"},{"ref":"39.10b","t":"Who strikes the evil-doing man, who strikes the evil-doing woman;"},{"ref":"39.10c","t":"who smites the fiendish Druj, and is most strong and world-destroying;"},{"ref":"39.10d","t":"who maintains and looks over all this moving world;"},{"ref":"39.11","t":"Who, never sleeping, wakefully guards the creation of Mazda;"},{"ref":"39.11a","t":"who, never sleeping, wakefully maintains the creation of Mazda;"},{"ref":"39.11b","t":"who protects all the material world with his club uplifted, from"},{"ref":"39.11c","t":"the hour when the sun is down;"},{"ref":"39.12","t":"Who never more did enjoy sleep from the time when the two"},{"ref":"39.12a","t":"Spirits made the world, namely, the good Spirit and the evil One;"},{"ref":"39.12b","t":"who every day, every night, fights with the Mazainya Daevas."},{"ref":"39.13","t":"He bows not for fear and fright before the Daevas: before"},{"ref":"39.13a","t":"him all the Daevas bow for fear and fright reluctantly, and rush"},{"ref":"39.13b","t":"away to darkness."},{"ref":"39.13c","t":"For his brightness and glory, for his strength and victorious"},{"ref":"39.13d","t":"power...."},{"ref":"39.14","t":"Yatha ahu vairyo: The will of the Lord is the law of holiness...."},{"ref":"39.14a","t":"We sacrifice unto the holy, tall-formed, fiend-smiting Sraosha,"},{"ref":"39.14b","t":"who makes the world increase, the holy and master of holiness;"},{"ref":"39.14c","t":"Who with peace and friendship watches the Druj and the most beneficent"},{"ref":"39.14d","t":"Spirit: so that the Amesha-Spentas may go along the seven Karshvares"},{"ref":"39.14e","t":"of the earth; who is the teacher of the Law: he himself was taught"},{"ref":"39.14f","t":"it by Ahura Mazda, the holy One."},{"ref":"39.14g","t":"For his brightness and glory, for his strength and victorious"},{"ref":"39.14h","t":"power...."},{"ref":"39.15","t":"Yatha ahu vairyo: The will of the Lord is the law of holiness...."},{"ref":"39.15a","t":"We sacrifice unto the holy, tall-formed, fiend-smiting Sraosha,"},{"ref":"39.15b","t":"who makes the world increase, the holy and master of holiness;"},{"ref":"39.15c","t":"Whom the holy Ahura Mazda has created to withstand Aeshma, the"},{"ref":"39.15d","t":"fiend of the wounding spear; we sacrifice unto Peace, whose breath"},{"ref":"39.15e","t":"is friendly, and unto the two withstanders of sin and guilt,"},{"ref":"39.16","t":"The friends of the holy Sraosha;"},{"ref":"39.16a","t":"The friends of Rashnu Razista;"},{"ref":"39.16b","t":"The friends of the good Law of the worshippers of Mazda;"},{"ref":"39.16c","t":"The friends of Arstat, who makes the world grow, who makes the"},{"ref":"39.16d","t":"world increase, who makes the world prosper;"},{"ref":"39.16e","t":"The friends of Ashi Vanguhi;"},{"ref":"39.16f","t":"The friends of the good Chisti;"},{"ref":"39.16g","t":"The friends of the most right Chista;"},{"ref":"39.17","t":"The friends of all gods;"},{"ref":"39.17a","t":"The friends of the Mathra Spenta;"},{"ref":"39.17b","t":"The friends of the fiend-destrqying Law;"},{"ref":"39.17c","t":"The friends of the long-traditional teaching;"},{"ref":"39.17d","t":"The friends of the Amesha-Spentas;"},{"ref":"39.17e","t":"The friends of ourselves, the Saoshyants, the two-footed part"},{"ref":"39.17f","t":"of the holy creation;"},{"ref":"39.17g","t":"The friends of all the beings of the holy world."},{"ref":"39.17h","t":"For his brightness and glory, for his strength and victorious"},{"ref":"39.17i","t":"power...."},{"ref":"39.18","t":"Yatha ahu vairyo: The will of the Lord is the law of holiness...."},{"ref":"39.18a","t":"We sacrifice unto the holy, tall-formed, fiend-smiting Sraosha,"},{"ref":"39.18b","t":"who makes the world increase, the holy and master of holiness;"},{"ref":"39.18c","t":"The first [Sraosha], the next, the middle, and the highest; with"},{"ref":"39.18d","t":"the first sacrifice, with the next, with the middle, and with"},{"ref":"39.18e","t":"the highest. We sacrifice unto all [the moments] of the holy and"},{"ref":"39.18f","t":"strong Sraosha, who is the incarnate Word;"},{"ref":"39.19","t":"The strong Sraosha, of the manly courage, the warrior of the"},{"ref":"39.19a","t":"strong arms, who breaks the skulls of the Daevas; who smites with"},{"ref":"39.19b","t":"heavy blows and is strong to smite; the holy Sraosha, who smites"},{"ref":"39.19c","t":"with heavy blows; we sacrifice unto the crushing Ascendant of"},{"ref":"39.19d","t":"both the holy Sraosha and Arshti."},{"ref":"39.20","t":"We sacrifice for all the houses protected by Sraosha, where"},{"ref":"39.20a","t":"the holy Sraosha is dear and friendly treated and satisfied, as"},{"ref":"39.20b","t":"well as the faithful man, rich in good thoughts, rich in good"},{"ref":"39.20c","t":"words, rich in good deeds."},{"ref":"39.21","t":"We sacrifice unto the body of the holy Sraosha;"},{"ref":"39.21a","t":"We sacrifice unto the body of Rashnu Razishta;"},{"ref":"39.21b","t":"We sacrifice unto the body of Mithra, the lord of wide pastures;"},{"ref":"39.21c","t":"We sacrifice unto the body of the holy wind;"},{"ref":"39.21d","t":"We sacrifice unto the body of the good Law of the worshippers"},{"ref":"39.21e","t":"of Mazda;"},{"ref":"39.21f","t":"We sacrifice unto the body of Arshtat, who makes the world grow,"},{"ref":"39.21g","t":"who makes the world increase, who makes the world prosper;"},{"ref":"39.21h","t":"We sacrifice unto the body of Ashi Vanguhi;"},{"ref":"39.21i","t":"We sacrifice unto the body of the good Chisti;"},{"ref":"39.21j","t":"We sacrifice unto the body of the most right Chista;"},{"ref":"39.21k","t":"We sacrifice unto the bodies of all the gods;"},{"ref":"39.22","t":"We sacrifice unto the body of the Mathra Spenta;"},{"ref":"39.22a","t":"We sacrifice unto the body of the fiend-destroying Law;"},{"ref":"39.22b","t":"We sacrifice unto the body of the long-traditional teaching;"},{"ref":"39.22c","t":"We sacrifice unto the bodies of the Amesha-Spentas;"},{"ref":"39.22d","t":"We sacrifice unto the bodies of ourselves, the Saoshyants, the"},{"ref":"39.22e","t":"two-footed part of the holy creation;"},{"ref":"39.22f","t":"We sacrifice unto the bodies of all the beings of the holy world."},{"ref":"39.22g","t":"For his brightness and glory, for his strength and victorious"},{"ref":"39.22h","t":"power...."},{"ref":"39.23","t":"Yatha ahu vairyo: The will of the Lord is the law of holiness...."},{"ref":"39.23a","t":"I bless the sacrifice and prayer, the strength and vigour of the"},{"ref":"39.23b","t":"holy, strong Sraosha, who is the incarnate Word, a mighty-speared"},{"ref":"39.23c","t":"and lordly god"},{"ref":"39.23d","t":"[Give] unto that man brightness and glory,.. give him the bright,"},{"ref":"39.23e","t":"all-happy, blissful abode of the holy Ones!"},{"sp":"HDR","t":"11a. Srosh Yasht"},{"ref":"40.1","t":"(SEE YASNA, CHAPTER 57)"},{"sp":"HDR","t":"12. Rashn Yasht","hvShift6":[[0,0]]},{"ref":"41.0","t":"May Ahura Mazda be rejoiced!...."},{"ref":"41.0a","t":"Ashem Vohu: Holiness is the best of all good...."},{"ref":"41.0b","t":"I confess myself a worshipper of Mazda, a follower of Zarathushtra,"},{"ref":"41.0c","t":"one who hates the Daevas and obeys the laws of Ahura;"},{"ref":"41.0d","t":"For sacrifice, prayer, propitiation, and glorification unto [Havani],"},{"ref":"41.0e","t":"the holy and master of holiness."},{"ref":"41.0f","t":"Unto Rashnu Razishta; unto Arshtat, who makes the world grow,"},{"ref":"41.0g","t":"who makes the world increase; unto the true-spoken speech, that"},{"ref":"41.0h","t":"makes the world grow;"},{"ref":"41.0i","t":"Be propitiation, with sacrifice, prayer, propitiation, and glorification."},{"ref":"41.0j","t":"Yatha ahu vairyo: The will of the Lord is the law of holiness...."},{"ref":"41.1","t":"The holy (Zarathushtra) asked him: ‘O holy Ahura Mazda! I"},{"ref":"41.1a","t":"ask thee; answer me with words of truth, thou who knowest the"},{"ref":"41.1b","t":"truth. Thou art undeceivable, thou hast an undeceivable understanding;"},{"ref":"41.1c","t":"thou art undeceivable, as thou knowest everything."},{"ref":"41.1d","t":"‘What of the Holy Word is created true? what is created progress-making?"},{"ref":"41.1e","t":"what is fit to discern? what is healthful? what is wise? what"},{"ref":"41.1f","t":"is happy and more powerful to destroy than all other creatures?’"},{"ref":"41.2","t":"Ahura Mazda answered: ‘I will declare that unto thee, O pure,"},{"ref":"41.2a","t":"holy Spitama!"},{"ref":"41.2b","t":"‘The most glorious Holy Word (itself), this is what in the Holy"},{"ref":"41.2c","t":"Word is created true, what is created progress making, what is"},{"ref":"41.2d","t":"fit to discern, what is healthful, wise, and happy, what is more"},{"ref":"41.2e","t":"powerful to destroy than all other creatures.’"},{"ref":"41.3","t":"Ahura Mazda said: ‘Bind up a three-twigged baresma against"},{"ref":"41.3a","t":"the way of the sun. [Address] unto me, Ahura Mazda, these words:"},{"ref":"41.3b","t":"“We invoke, we bless [Ahura]; I invoke the friendship [of"},{"ref":"41.3c","t":"Ahura] towards this var (ordeal) prepared, towards the fire and"},{"ref":"41.3d","t":"the baresma, towards the full boiling [milk], towards the var"},{"ref":"41.3e","t":"of oil and the sap of the plants.”"},{"ref":"41.4","t":"‘Then I, Ahura Mazda, shall come for help unto thee, towards"},{"ref":"41.4a","t":"this var prepared, towards the fire and the baresma, towards the"},{"ref":"41.4b","t":"full boiling [milk], towards the var of oil and the sap of the"},{"ref":"41.4c","t":"plants;"},{"ref":"41.4d","t":"‘Along with the fiend-smiting Wind, along with the cursing thought"},{"ref":"41.4e","t":"of the wise, along with the kingly Glory, along with Saoka, made"},{"ref":"41.4f","t":"by Mazda."},{"ref":"41.5","t":"‘We invoke, we bless Rashnu, the strong; I invoke his friendship"},{"ref":"41.5a","t":"towards this var prepared, towards the fire and the baresma, towards"},{"ref":"41.5b","t":"the full boiling [milk], towards the var of oil and the sap of:"},{"ref":"41.5c","t":"the plants."},{"ref":"41.6","t":"‘Then Rashnu the tall, the strong, will come for help unto"},{"ref":"41.6a","t":"thee, towards this var prepared, towards the fire and the baresma,"},{"ref":"41.6b","t":"towards the full boiling [milk], towards the var of oil and the"},{"ref":"41.6c","t":"sap of the plants:"},{"ref":"41.6d","t":"‘Along with the fiend-smiting Wind, along with the cursing thought"},{"ref":"41.6e","t":"of the wise, along with the kingly Glory, along with Saoka, made"},{"ref":"41.6f","t":"by Mazda."},{"ref":"41.7","t":"‘O thou, holy Rashnu! O most true Rashnu! most beneficent"},{"ref":"41.7a","t":"Rashnu! most knowing Rashnu! most discerning Rashnu I most fore-knowing"},{"ref":"41.7b","t":"Rashnu! most far-seeing Rashnu I Rashnu, the best doer of justice!"},{"ref":"41.7c","t":"Rashnu, the best smiter of thieves;"},{"ref":"41.8","t":"‘The uninjured, the best killer, smiter, destroyer of thieves"},{"ref":"41.8a","t":"and bandits! in whatever part of the world thou art watching the"},{"ref":"41.8b","t":"doings of men and making the account... (obscure)."},{"ref":"41.9","t":"‘Whether thou, O holy Rashnu! art in the Karshvare Arezahi,","hvShift6":[[0,0]]},{"ref":"41.9a","t":"we invoke, we bless Rashnu, the strong. I invoke his friendship"},{"ref":"41.9b","t":"towards this var prepared.... in whatever part of the world thou"},{"ref":"41.9c","t":"art."},{"ref":"41.10","t":"‘Whether thou, O holy Rashnu! art in the Karshvare Savahi,"},{"ref":"41.10a","t":"we invoke, we bless Rashnu. I invoke his friendship towards this"},{"ref":"41.10b","t":"var prepared... in whatever part of the world thou art."},{"ref":"41.11","t":"‘Whether thou, O holy Rashnu! art in the Karshvare Fradadhafshu,"},{"ref":"41.11a","t":"we invoke, we bless Rashnu, the strong. I invoke his friendship"},{"ref":"41.11b","t":"towards this var prepared.... in whatever part of the world thou"},{"ref":"41.11c","t":"art."},{"ref":"41.12","t":"‘Whether thou, O holy Rashnu! art in the Karshvare Vidadhafshu,"},{"ref":"41.12a","t":"we invoke, we bless Rashnu, the strong. I invoke his friendship"},{"ref":"41.12b","t":"towards this var prepared.... in whatever part of the world thou"},{"ref":"41.12c","t":"art."},{"ref":"41.13","t":"‘Whether thou, O holy Rashnu! art in the Karshvare Vouru-bareshti,"},{"ref":"41.13a","t":"we invoke, we bless Rashnu, the strong. I invoke his friendship"},{"ref":"41.13b","t":"towards this var prepared.... in whatever part of the world thou"},{"ref":"41.13c","t":"art."},{"ref":"41.14","t":"‘Whether thou, O holy Rashnu! art in the Karshvare Vouru-jareshti,"},{"ref":"41.14a","t":"we invoke, we bless Rashnu, the strong. I invoke his friendship"},{"ref":"41.14b","t":"towards this var prepared.... in whatever part of the world thou"},{"ref":"41.14c","t":"art."},{"ref":"41.15","t":"‘Whether thou, O holy Rashnu! art in this Karshvare, the bright"},{"ref":"41.15a","t":"Hvaniratha, we invoke, we bless Rashnu, the strong. I invoke his"},{"ref":"41.15b","t":"friendship towards this var prepared.... in whatever part of"},{"ref":"41.15c","t":"the world thou art."},{"ref":"41.16","t":"‘Whether thou, O holy Rashnu! art in the sea Vouru-Kasha,"},{"ref":"41.16a","t":"we invoke, we bless Rashnu, the strong. I invoke his friendship"},{"ref":"41.16b","t":"towards this var prepared.... in whatever part of the world thou"},{"ref":"41.16c","t":"art."},{"ref":"41.17","t":"‘Whether thou, O holy Rashnu! art on the tree of the eagle,"},{"ref":"41.17a","t":"that stands in the middle of the sea Vouru-Kasha, that is called"},{"ref":"41.17b","t":"the tree of good remedies, the tree of powerful remedies, the"},{"ref":"41.17c","t":"tree of all remedies, and on which rest the seeds of all plants;"},{"ref":"41.17d","t":"we invoke, we bless Rashnu, the strong. I invoke his friendship"},{"ref":"41.17e","t":"towards this var prepared...."},{"ref":"41.18","t":"‘Whether thou, O holy Rashnu! art on the Aodhas of the Rangha,"},{"ref":"41.18a","t":"we invoke, we bless Rashnu, the strong. I invoke his friendship"},{"ref":"41.18b","t":"towards this var prepared...."},{"ref":"41.19","t":"‘Whether thou, O holy Rashnu! art on the Sanaka of the Rangha,"},{"ref":"41.19a","t":"we invoke, we bless Rashnu, the strong. I invoke his friendship"},{"ref":"41.19b","t":"towards this var prepared...."},{"ref":"41.20","t":"‘Whether thou, O holy Rashnu! art at one of the angles of"},{"ref":"41.20a","t":"this earth, we invoke we bless Rashnu. I invoke his friendship"},{"ref":"41.20b","t":"towards this var prepared...."},{"ref":"41.21","t":"‘Whether thou, O holy Rashnu! art at the boundary of this"},{"ref":"41.21a","t":"earth, we invoke, we bless Rashnu. I invoke his friendship towards"},{"ref":"41.21b","t":"this var prepared...."},{"ref":"41.22","t":"‘Whether thou, O holy Rashnu! art in any place of this earth,"},{"ref":"41.22a","t":"we invoke, we bless Rashnu. I invoke his friendship towards this"},{"ref":"41.22b","t":"var prepared...."},{"ref":"41.23","t":"‘Whether thou, O holy Rashnu! art on the Hara Berezaiti, the"},{"ref":"41.23a","t":"bright mountain around which the many (stars) revolve, where come"},{"ref":"41.23b","t":"neither night nor darkness, no cold wind and no hot wind, no deathful"},{"ref":"41.23c","t":"sickness, no uncleanness made by the Daevas, and the clouds cannot"},{"ref":"41.23d","t":"reach up unto the Haraiti Bareza; we invoke, we bless Rashnu."},{"ref":"41.23e","t":"I invoke his friendship towards this var prepared...."},{"ref":"41.24","t":"‘Whether thou, O holy Rashnu! art upon the highest Hukairya,"},{"ref":"41.24a","t":"of the deep precipices, made of gold, where from this river of"},{"ref":"41.24b","t":"mine, Ardvi Sura Anahita, leaps from a thousand times the height"},{"ref":"41.24c","t":"of a man, we invoke, we bless Rashnu, the strong. I invoke his"},{"ref":"41.24d","t":"friendship towards this var prepared...."},{"ref":"41.25","t":"‘Whether thou, O holy Rashnu! art upon the Taera of the height"},{"ref":"41.25a","t":"Haraiti, around which the stars, the moon, and the sun revolve,"},{"ref":"41.25b","t":"we invoke, we bless Rashnu, the strong. I invoke his friendship"},{"ref":"41.25c","t":"towards this var prepared...."},{"ref":"41.26","t":"‘Whether thou, O holy Rashnu! art in the star Vanant, made"},{"ref":"41.26a","t":"by Mazda, we invoke, we bless Rashnu, the strong. I invoke his"},{"ref":"41.26b","t":"friendship towards this var prepared...."},{"ref":"41.27","t":"‘Whether thou, O holy Rashnu! art in the bright and glorious"},{"ref":"41.27a","t":"star Tishtrya, we invoke, we bless Rashnu, the strong. I invoke"},{"ref":"41.27b","t":"his friendship towards the var prepared...."},{"ref":"41.28","t":"‘Whether thou, O holy Rashnu! art in the group of the Haptoiringa"},{"ref":"41.28a","t":"stars, we invoke, we bless Rashnu, the strong. I invoke his friendship"},{"ref":"41.28b","t":"towards this var prepared...."},{"ref":"41.29","t":"‘Whether thou, O holy Rashnu! art in those stars that have"},{"ref":"41.29a","t":"the seed of the waters in them, we invoke, we bless Rashnu, the"},{"ref":"41.29b","t":"strong. I invoke his friendship towards this var prepared...."},{"ref":"41.30","t":"‘Whether thou, O holy Rashnu! art in those stars that have"},{"ref":"41.30a","t":"the seed of the earth in them, we invoke, we bless Rashnu, the"},{"ref":"41.30b","t":"strong. I invoke his friendship towards this var prepared...."},{"ref":"41.31","t":"‘Whether thou, O holy Rashnu! art in those stars that have"},{"ref":"41.31a","t":"the seed of the plants in them, we invoke, we bless Rashnu, the"},{"ref":"41.31b","t":"strong. I invoke his friendship towards this var prepared...."},{"ref":"41.32","t":"‘Whether thou, O holy Rashnu! art in the stars that belong"},{"ref":"41.32a","t":"to the Good Spirit, we invoke, we bless Rashnu, the strong. I"},{"ref":"41.32b","t":"invoke his friendship towards this var prepared...."},{"ref":"41.33","t":"‘Whether thou, O holy Rashnu! art in the moon which has the"},{"ref":"41.33a","t":"seed of the Bull in it, we invoke, we bless Rashnu, the strong."},{"ref":"41.33b","t":"I invoke his friendship towards this var prepared...."},{"ref":"41.34","t":"‘Whether thou, O holy Rashnu! art in the swift-horsed sun,"},{"ref":"41.34a","t":"we invoke, we bless Rashnu, the strong. I invoke his friendship"},{"ref":"41.34b","t":"towards this var prepared...."},{"ref":"41.35","t":"‘Whether thou, O holy Rashnu! art in the sovereign endless"},{"ref":"41.35a","t":"Light, we invoke, we bless Rashnu, the strong. I invoke his friendship"},{"ref":"41.35b","t":"towards this var prepared...."},{"ref":"41.36","t":"‘Whether thou, O holy Rashnu! art in the bright, all-happy,"},{"ref":"41.36a","t":"blissful abode of the holy Ones, we invoke, we bless Rashnu, the"},{"ref":"41.36b","t":"strong. I invoke his friendship towards this var prepared...."},{"ref":"41.37","t":"‘Whether thou, O holy Rashnu! art in the shining Garo-demana,"},{"ref":"41.37a","t":"we invoke, we bless Rashnu, the strong. I invoke his friendship"},{"ref":"41.37b","t":"towards this var prepared...."},{"ref":"41.38","t":"‘Whether thou, O holy Rashnu! art,.. (obscure) we invoke,"},{"ref":"41.38a","t":"we bless Rashnu, the strong. I invoke his friendship towards this"},{"ref":"41.38b","t":"var prepared...."},{"ref":"41.39","t":"‘For his brightness and glory, I will offer unto him a sacrifice"},{"ref":"41.39a","t":"worth being heard...."},{"ref":"41.39b","t":"‘Yenhe hatam: All those beings of whom Ahura Mazda...."},{"ref":"41.40","t":"‘Yatha ahu vairyo: The will of the Lord is the law of holiness...."},{"ref":"41.40a","t":"‘I bless the sacrifice and prayer, and the strength and vigour"},{"ref":"41.40b","t":"of Rashnu Razishta; of Arshtat, who makes the world grow, who"},{"ref":"41.40c","t":"makes the world increase; and of the true-spoken speech that makes"},{"ref":"41.40d","t":"the world grow."},{"ref":"41.40e","t":"‘Ashem Vohu: Holiness is the best of all good...."},{"ref":"41.40f","t":"‘[Give] unto that man brightness and glory, give him health of"},{"ref":"41.40g","t":"body,... give him the bright, all-happy, blissful abode of the"},{"ref":"41.40h","t":"holy Ones.’"},{"sp":"HDR","t":"13. Frawardin Yasht (Hymn to the Fravashis)"},{"ref":"42.0","t":"May Ahura Mazda be rejoiced!...."},{"ref":"42.0a","t":"Ashem Vohu: Holiness is the best of all good...."},{"ref":"42.0b","t":"I confess myself a worshipper of Mazda, a follower of Zarathushtra,"},{"ref":"42.0c","t":"one who hates the Daevas and obeys the laws of Ahura;"},{"ref":"42.0d","t":"For sacrifice, prayer, propitiation, and glorification unto [Havani],"},{"ref":"42.0e","t":"the holy and master of holiness."},{"ref":"42.0f","t":"Unto the awful, overpowering Fravashis of the faithful; unto the"},{"ref":"42.0g","t":"Fravashis of the men of the primitive law; unto the Fravashis"},{"ref":"42.0h","t":"of the next-of-kin,"},{"ref":"42.0i","t":"Be propitiation, with sacrifice, prayer, propitiation, and glorification."},{"ref":"42.0j","t":"Yatha ahu vairyo: The will of the Lord is the law of holiness...."},{"ref":"42.1","t":"Ahura Mazda spake unto Spitama Zarathushtra, saying: ‘Do thou"},{"ref":"42.1a","t":"proclaim, O pure Zarathushtra! the vigour and strength, the glory,"},{"ref":"42.1b","t":"the help and the joy that are in the Fravashis of the faithful,"},{"ref":"42.1c","t":"the awful and overpowering Fravashis; do thou tell how they come"},{"ref":"42.1d","t":"to help me, how they bring assistance unto me, the awful Fravashis"},{"ref":"42.1e","t":"of the faithful."},{"ref":"42.2","t":"‘Through their brightness and glory, O Zarathushtra! I maintain"},{"ref":"42.2a","t":"that sky, there above, shining and seen afar, and encompassing"},{"ref":"42.2b","t":"this earth all around."},{"ref":"42.3","t":"‘It looks like a palace, that stands built of a heavenly substance,"},{"ref":"42.3a","t":"firmly established, with ends that lie afar, shining in its body"},{"ref":"42.3b","t":"of ruby over the three-thirds (of the earth)”; it is like"},{"ref":"42.3c","t":"a garment inlaid with stars, made of a heavenly substance, that"},{"ref":"42.3d","t":"Mazda puts on, along with Mithra and Rashnu and Spenta-Armaiti,"},{"ref":"42.3e","t":"and on no side can the eye perceive the end of it."},{"ref":"42.4","t":"‘Through their brightness and glory, O Zarathushtra! I maintain"},{"ref":"42.4a","t":"Ardvi Sura Anahita, the wide-expanding and health-giving, who"},{"ref":"42.4b","t":"hates the Daevas and obeys the laws of Ahura who is worthy of"},{"ref":"42.4c","t":"sacrifice in the material world, worthy of prayer in the material"},{"ref":"42.4d","t":"world, the life-increasing and holy, the flocks-increasing and"},{"ref":"42.4e","t":"holy, the fold-increasing and holy, the wealth increasing and"},{"ref":"42.4f","t":"holy, the country increasing and holy;"},{"ref":"42.5","t":"‘Who makes the seed of all males pure, who makes the womb"},{"ref":"42.5a","t":"of all females pure for bringing forth, who makes all females"},{"ref":"42.5b","t":"bring forth in safety, who puts milk in the breasts of all females"},{"ref":"42.5c","t":"in the right measure and the right quality;"},{"ref":"42.6","t":"‘The large river, known afar, that is as large as the whole"},{"ref":"42.6a","t":"of all the waters that run along the earth; that runs powerfully"},{"ref":"42.6b","t":"from the height Hukairya down to the sea Vouru-kasha."},{"ref":"42.7","t":"‘All the shores of the sea Vouru-kasha are boiling over, all"},{"ref":"42.7a","t":"the middle of it is boiling over, when she runs down there, when"},{"ref":"42.7b","t":"she streams down there, she, Ardvi Sura Anahita, who has a thousand"},{"ref":"42.7c","t":"cells and a thousand channels; the extent of each of those cells,"},{"ref":"42.7d","t":"of each of those channels, is as much as a man can ride in forty"},{"ref":"42.7e","t":"days, riding on a good horse."},{"ref":"42.8","t":"‘From this river of mine alone flow all the waters that spread"},{"ref":"42.8a","t":"all over the seven Karshvares; this river of mine alone goes on"},{"ref":"42.8b","t":"bringing waters, both in summer and in winter. This river of mine"},{"ref":"42.8c","t":"purifies the seed in males, the womb in females, the milk in females’"},{"ref":"42.8d","t":"breasts."},{"ref":"42.9","t":"‘Through their brightness and glory, O Zarathushtra! I maintain"},{"ref":"42.9a","t":"the wide earth made by Ahura, the large and broad earth, that"},{"ref":"42.9b","t":"bears so much that is fine, that bears all the bodily world, the"},{"ref":"42.9c","t":"live and the dead, and the high mountains, rich in pastures and"},{"ref":"42.9d","t":"waters;"},{"ref":"42.10","t":"‘Upon which run the many streams and rivers; upon which the"},{"ref":"42.10a","t":"many kinds of plants grow up from the ground, to nourish animals"},{"ref":"42.10b","t":"and men, to nourish the Aryan nations, to nourish the five kinds"},{"ref":"42.10c","t":"of animals, and to help the faithful."},{"ref":"42.11","t":"‘Through their brightness and glory, O Zarathushtra! I maintain"},{"ref":"42.11a","t":"in the womb the child that has been conceived, so that it does"},{"ref":"42.11b","t":"not die from the assaults of Vidotu, and I develop in it the bones,"},{"ref":"42.11c","t":"the hair, the... the entrails, the feet, and the sexual organs."},{"ref":"42.12","t":"‘Had not the awful Fravashis of the faithful given help unto"},{"ref":"42.12a","t":"me, those animals and men of mine, of which there are such excellent"},{"ref":"42.12b","t":"kinds, would not subsist; strength would belong to the Druj, the"},{"ref":"42.12c","t":"dominion would belong to the Druj, the material world would belong"},{"ref":"42.12d","t":"to the Druj."},{"ref":"42.13","t":"‘Between the earth and the sky the immaterial creatures would"},{"ref":"42.13a","t":"be harassed by the Druj; between the earth and the sky the immaterial"},{"ref":"42.13b","t":"creatures would be smitten by the Druj; and never afterwards would"},{"ref":"42.13c","t":"Angra-Mainyu give way to the blows of Spenta-Mainyu."},{"ref":"42.14","t":"‘Through their brightness and glory the waters run and flow"},{"ref":"42.14a","t":"forward from the never-failing springs; through their brightness"},{"ref":"42.14b","t":"and glory the plants grow up from the earth, by the never-failing"},{"ref":"42.14c","t":"springs; through their brightness and glory the winds blow, driving"},{"ref":"42.14d","t":"down the clouds towards the never-failing springs."},{"ref":"42.15","t":"‘Through their brightness and glory the females conceive offspring;"},{"ref":"42.15a","t":"through their brightness and glory they bring forth in safety;"},{"ref":"42.15b","t":"it is through their brightness and glory when they become blessed"},{"ref":"42.15c","t":"with children."},{"ref":"42.16","t":"‘Through their brightness and glory a man is born who is a"},{"ref":"42.16a","t":"chief in assemblies and meetings, who listens well to the (holy)"},{"ref":"42.16b","t":"words, whom Wisdom holds dear, and who returns a victor from discussions"},{"ref":"42.16c","t":"with Gaotema, the heretic."},{"ref":"42.16d","t":"‘Through their brightness and glory the sun goes his way; through"},{"ref":"42.16e","t":"their brightness and glory the moon goes her way; through their"},{"ref":"42.16f","t":"brightness and glory the stars go their way."},{"ref":"42.17","t":"‘In fearful battles they are the wisest for help, the Fravashis"},{"ref":"42.17a","t":"of the faithful."},{"ref":"42.17b","t":"‘The most powerful amongst the Fravashis of the faithful, O Spitama!"},{"ref":"42.17c","t":"are those of the men of the primitive law or those of the Saoshyants"},{"ref":"42.17d","t":"not yet born, who are to restore the world. Of the others, the"},{"ref":"42.17e","t":"Fravashis of the living faithful are more powerful, O Zarathushtra!"},{"ref":"42.17f","t":"than those of the dead, O Spitama!"},{"ref":"42.18","t":"‘And the man who in life shall treat the Fravashis of the"},{"ref":"42.18a","t":"faithful well, will become a ruler of the country with full power,"},{"ref":"42.18b","t":"and a chief most strong; so shall any man of you become, who shall"},{"ref":"42.18c","t":"treat Mithra well, the lord of wide pastures, and Arshtat, who"},{"ref":"42.18d","t":"makes the world grow, who makes the world increase."},{"ref":"42.19","t":"‘Thus do I proclaim unto thee, O pure Spitama! the vigour"},{"ref":"42.19a","t":"and strength, the glory, the help, and the joy that are in the"},{"ref":"42.19b","t":"Fravashis of the faithful, the awful and overpowering Fravashis;"},{"ref":"42.19c","t":"and how they come to help me, how they bring assistance unto me,"},{"ref":"42.19d","t":"the awful Fravashis of the faithful.’"},{"ref":"42.20","t":"Ahura Mazda spake unto Spitama Zarathushtra, saying: ‘If in"},{"ref":"42.20a","t":"this material world, O Spitama Zarathushtra! thou happenest to"},{"ref":"42.20b","t":"come upon frightful roads, full of dangers and fears, O Zarathushtra!"},{"ref":"42.20c","t":"and thou fearest for thyself, then do thou recite these words,"},{"ref":"42.20d","t":"then proclaim these fiend-smiting words, O Zarathushtra!"},{"ref":"42.21","t":"‘“I praise, I invoke, I meditate upon, and we sacrifice"},{"ref":"42.21a","t":"unto the good, strong, beneficent Fravashis of the faithful. We"},{"ref":"42.21b","t":"worship the Fravashis of the masters of the houses, those of the"},{"ref":"42.21c","t":"lords of the boroughs, those of the lords of the towns, those"},{"ref":"42.21d","t":"of the lords of the countries, those of the Zarathustrotemas;"},{"ref":"42.21e","t":"the Fravashis of those that are, the Fravashis of those that have"},{"ref":"42.21f","t":"been, the Fravashis of those that will be; all the Fravashis of"},{"ref":"42.21g","t":"all nations, and most friendly the Fravashis of the friendly nations;"},{"ref":"42.22","t":"‘“Who maintain the sky, who maintain the waters, who"},{"ref":"42.22a","t":"maintain the earth, who maintain the cattle, who maintain in the"},{"ref":"42.22b","t":"womb the child that has been conceived, so that it does not die"},{"ref":"42.22c","t":"from the assaults of Vidotu, and develop in it the bones, the"},{"ref":"42.22d","t":"hair, the.... the entrails, the feet, and the sexual organs;"},{"ref":"42.23","t":"‘“Who are much-bringing, who move with awfulness, well-moving,"},{"ref":"42.23a","t":"swiftly moving, quickly moving, who move when invoked; who are"},{"ref":"42.23b","t":"to be invoked in the conquest of good, who are to be invoked in"},{"ref":"42.23c","t":"fights against foes, who are to be invoked in battles;"},{"ref":"42.24","t":"‘“Who give victory to their invoker, who give boons to"},{"ref":"42.24a","t":"their lover, who give health to the sick man, who give good Glory"},{"ref":"42.24b","t":"to the faithful man that brings libations and invokes them with"},{"ref":"42.24c","t":"a sacrifice and words of propitiation,"},{"ref":"42.25","t":"‘“Who turn to that side where are faithful men, most"},{"ref":"42.25a","t":"devoted to holiness, and where is the greatest piety, where the"},{"ref":"42.25b","t":"faithful man is rejoiced, and where the faithful man is not ill-treated.”’"},{"ref":"42.26","t":"We worship the good, strong, beneficent Fravashis of the faithful,"},{"ref":"42.26a","t":"who are the mightiest of drivers, the lightest of those driving"},{"ref":"42.26b","t":"forwards, the slowest of the retiring, the safest of all bridges,"},{"ref":"42.26c","t":"the least-erring of all weapons and arms, and who never turn their"},{"ref":"42.26d","t":"backs."},{"ref":"42.27","t":"At once, wherever they come, we worship them, the good ones,"},{"ref":"42.27a","t":"the excellent ones, the good, the strong, the beneficent Fravashis"},{"ref":"42.27b","t":"of the faithful. They are to be invoked when the bundles of baresma"},{"ref":"42.27c","t":"are tied; they are to be invoked in fights against foes, in battles,"},{"ref":"42.27d","t":"and there where gallant men strive to conquer foes."},{"ref":"42.28","t":"Mazda invoked them for help, when he fixed the sky and the"},{"ref":"42.28a","t":"waters and the earth and the plants; when Spenta-Mainyu fixed"},{"ref":"42.28b","t":"the sky, when he fixed the waters, when the earth, when the cattle,"},{"ref":"42.28c","t":"when the plants, when the child conceived in the womb, so that"},{"ref":"42.28d","t":"it should not die from the assaults of Vidotu, and developed in"},{"ref":"42.28e","t":"it the bones, the hair, the.... the entrails, the feet, and"},{"ref":"42.28f","t":"the sexual organs."},{"ref":"42.29","t":"Spenta-Mainyu maintained the sky, and they sustained it from"},{"ref":"42.29a","t":"below, they, the strong Fravashis, who sit in silence, gazing"},{"ref":"42.29b","t":"with sharp looks; whose eyes and ears are powerful, who bring"},{"ref":"42.29c","t":"long joy, high and high-girded; well-moving and moving afar, loud-snorting,"},{"ref":"42.29d","t":"possessing riches and a high renown."},{"ref":"42.30","t":"We worship the good, strong, beneficent Fravashis of the faithful;"},{"ref":"42.30a","t":"whose friendship is good, and who know how to benefit; whose friendship"},{"ref":"42.30b","t":"lasts long; who like to stay in the abode where they are not harmed"},{"ref":"42.30c","t":"by its dwellers; who are good, beautiful afar, health-giving,"},{"ref":"42.30d","t":"of high renown, conquering in battle, and who never do harm first."},{"ref":"42.31","t":"We worship the good, strong, beneficent Fravashis of the faithful;"},{"ref":"42.31a","t":"whose will is dreadful unto those who vex them; powerfully working"},{"ref":"42.31b","t":"and most beneficent; who in battle break the dread arms of their"},{"ref":"42.31c","t":"foes and haters."},{"ref":"42.32","t":"We worship the good, strong, beneficent Fravashis of the faithful;"},{"ref":"42.32a","t":"liberal, valiant, and full of strength, not to be seized by thought,"},{"ref":"42.32b","t":"welfare-giving, kind, and health-giving, following with Ashi’s"},{"ref":"42.32c","t":"remedies, as far as the earth extends, as the rivers stretch,"},{"ref":"42.32d","t":"as the sun rises."},{"ref":"42.33","t":"We worship the good, strong, beneficent Fravashis of the faithful,"},{"ref":"42.33a","t":"who gallantly and bravely fight, causing havoc, wounding, breaking"},{"ref":"42.33b","t":"to pieces all the malice of the malicious, Daevas and men, and"},{"ref":"42.33c","t":"smiting powerfully in battle, at their wish and will."},{"ref":"42.34","t":"You kindly deliver the Victory made by Ahura, and the crushing"},{"ref":"42.34a","t":"Ascendant, most beneficently, to those countries where you, the"},{"ref":"42.34b","t":"good ones, unharmed and rejoiced, unoppressed and unoffended,"},{"ref":"42.34c","t":"have been held worthy of sacrifice and prayer, and proceed the"},{"ref":"42.34d","t":"way of your wish."},{"ref":"42.35","t":"We worship the good, strong, beneficent Fravashis of the faithful,"},{"ref":"42.35a","t":"of high renown, smiting in battle, most strong, shield-bearing"},{"ref":"42.35b","t":"and harmless to those who are true, whom both the pursuing and"},{"ref":"42.35c","t":"the fleeing invoke for help: the pursuer invokes them for a swift"},{"ref":"42.35d","t":"race, and for a swift race does the fleer invoke them;"},{"ref":"42.36","t":"Who turn to that side where are faithful men, most devoted"},{"ref":"42.36a","t":"to holiness, and where is the greatest piety, where the faithful"},{"ref":"42.36b","t":"man is rejoiced, and where the faithful man is not ill-treated."},{"ref":"42.37","t":"We worship the good, strong, beneficent Fravashis of the faithful,"},{"ref":"42.37a","t":"who form many battalions, girded with weapons, lifting up spears,"},{"ref":"42.37b","t":"and full of sheen; who in fearful battles come rushing along where"},{"ref":"42.37c","t":"the gallant heroes go and assail the Danus."},{"ref":"42.38","t":"There you destroy the victorious strength of the Turanian"},{"ref":"42.38a","t":"Danus; there you destroy the malice of the Turanian Danus; through"},{"ref":"42.38b","t":"you the chiefs are of high intellect and most successful; they,"},{"ref":"42.38c","t":"the gallant heroes, the gallant Saoshyants, the gallant conquerors"},{"ref":"42.38d","t":"of the offspring of the Danus chiefs of myriads, who wound with"},{"ref":"42.38e","t":"stones."},{"ref":"42.39","t":"We worship the good, strong, beneficent Fravashis of the faithful,"},{"ref":"42.39a","t":"who rout the two wings of an army standing in battle array, who"},{"ref":"42.39b","t":"make the centre swerve, and swiftly pursue onwards, to help the"},{"ref":"42.39c","t":"faithful and to distress the doers of evil deeds."},{"ref":"42.40","t":"We worship the good, strong, beneficent Fravashis of the faithful;"},{"ref":"42.40a","t":"awful, overpowering, and victorious, smiting in battle, sorely"},{"ref":"42.40b","t":"wounding, blowing away (the foes), moving along to and fro, of"},{"ref":"42.40c","t":"good renown, fair of body, godly of soul, and holy; who give victory"},{"ref":"42.40d","t":"to their invoker, who give boons to their lover, who give health"},{"ref":"42.40e","t":"to the sick man;"},{"ref":"42.41","t":"Who give good glory to him who worships them with a sacrifice,"},{"ref":"42.41a","t":"as that man did worship them, the holy Zarathushtra, the chief"},{"ref":"42.41b","t":"of the material world, the head of the two-footed race, in whatever"},{"ref":"42.41c","t":"struggle he had to enter, in whatever distress he did fear;"},{"ref":"42.42","t":"Who, when well invoked, enjoy bliss in the heavens; who, when"},{"ref":"42.42a","t":"well invoked, come forward from the heavens, who are the heads"},{"ref":"42.42b","t":"of that sky above, possessing the well-shapen Strength, the Victory"},{"ref":"42.42c","t":"made by Ahura, the crushing Ascendant, and Welfare, the wealth-bringing,"},{"ref":"42.42d","t":"boon-bringing, holy, well fed, worthy of sacrifice and prayer"},{"ref":"42.42e","t":"in the perfection of holiness."},{"ref":"42.43","t":"They shed Satavaesa between the earth and the sky, him to"},{"ref":"42.43a","t":"whom the waters belong, who listens to appeals and makes the waters"},{"ref":"42.43b","t":"flow and the plants grow up, to nourish animals and men, to nourish"},{"ref":"42.43c","t":"the Aryan nations, to nourish the five kinds of animals and to"},{"ref":"42.43d","t":"help the faithful."},{"ref":"42.44","t":"Satavaesa comes down and flows between the earth and the sky,"},{"ref":"42.44a","t":"he to whom the waters belong, who listens to appeals and makes"},{"ref":"42.44b","t":"the waters and the plants grow up, fair, radiant, and full of"},{"ref":"42.44c","t":"light, to nourish animals and men, to nourish the Aryan nations,"},{"ref":"42.44d","t":"to nourish the five kinds of animals, and to help the faithful."},{"ref":"42.45","t":"We worship the good, strong, beneficent Fravashis of the faithful;"},{"ref":"42.45a","t":"with helms of brass, with weapons of brass, with armour of brass;"},{"ref":"42.45b","t":"who struggle in the fights for victory in garments of light, arraying"},{"ref":"42.45c","t":"the battles and bringing them forwards, to kill thousands of Daevas."},{"ref":"42.45d","t":"When the wind blows from behind them and brings their breath unto"},{"ref":"42.45e","t":"men,"},{"ref":"42.46","t":"Then men know where blows the breath of victory: and they"},{"ref":"42.46a","t":"pay pious homage unto the good, strong, beneficent Fravashis of"},{"ref":"42.46b","t":"the faithful, with their hearts prepared and their arms uplifted."},{"ref":"42.47","t":"Whichever side they have been first worshipped in the fulness"},{"ref":"42.47a","t":"of faith of a devoted heart, to that side turn the awful Fravashis"},{"ref":"42.47b","t":"of the faithful, along with Mithra and Rashnu and the awful cursing"},{"ref":"42.47c","t":"thought of the wise and the victorious wind."},{"ref":"42.48","t":"And those nations are smitten at one stroke by their fifties"},{"ref":"42.48a","t":"and their hundreds, by their hundreds and their thousands, by"},{"ref":"42.48b","t":"their thousands and their tens of thousands, by their tens of"},{"ref":"42.48c","t":"thousands and their myriads of myriads, against which turn the"},{"ref":"42.48d","t":"awful Fravashis of the faithful, along with Mithra and Rashnu,"},{"ref":"42.48e","t":"and the awful cursing thought of the wise and the victorious wind."},{"ref":"42.49","t":"We worship the good, strong, beneficent Fravashis of the faithful,"},{"ref":"42.49a","t":"who come and go through the borough at the time of the Hamaspathmaidyem;"},{"ref":"42.49b","t":"they go along there for ten nights, asking thus:"},{"ref":"42.50","t":"‘Who will praise us? Who will offer us a sacrifice? Who will"},{"ref":"42.50a","t":"meditate upon us? Who will bless us? Who will receive us with"},{"ref":"42.50b","t":"meat and clothes in his hand and with a prayer worthy of bliss?"},{"ref":"42.50c","t":"Of which of us will the name be taken for invocation? Of which"},{"ref":"42.50d","t":"of you will the soul be worshipped by you with a sacrifice? To"},{"ref":"42.50e","t":"whom will this gift of ours be given, that he may have never-failing"},{"ref":"42.50f","t":"food for ever and ever?’"},{"ref":"42.51","t":"And the man who offers them up a sacrifice, with meat and"},{"ref":"42.51a","t":"clothes in his hand, with a prayer worthy of bliss, the awful"},{"ref":"42.51b","t":"Fravashis of the faithful, satisfied, unharmed, and unoffended,"},{"ref":"42.51c","t":"bless thus:"},{"ref":"42.52","t":"‘May there be in this house flocks of animals and men! May"},{"ref":"42.52a","t":"there be a swift horse and a solid chariot! May there be a man"},{"ref":"42.52b","t":"who knows how to praise God and rule in an assembly, who will"},{"ref":"42.52c","t":"offer us sacrifices with meat and clothes in his hand, and with"},{"ref":"42.52d","t":"a prayer worthy of bliss.’"},{"ref":"42.53","t":"We worship the good, strong, beneficent Fravashis of the faithful,"},{"ref":"42.53a","t":"who show beautiful paths to the waters, made by Mazda, which had"},{"ref":"42.53b","t":"stood before for a long time in the same place without flowing:"},{"ref":"42.54","t":"And now they flow along the path made by Mazda, along the"},{"ref":"42.54a","t":"way made by the gods, the watery way appointed to them, at the"},{"ref":"42.54b","t":"wish of Ahura Mazda, at the wish of the Amesha-Spentas."},{"ref":"42.55","t":"We worship the good, strong, beneficent Fravashis of the faithful,"},{"ref":"42.55a","t":"who show a beautiful growth to the fertile plants, which had stood"},{"ref":"42.55b","t":"before for a long time in the same place without growing;"},{"ref":"42.56","t":"And now they grow up along the path made by Mazda, along the"},{"ref":"42.56a","t":"way made by the gods, in the time appointed to them, at the wish"},{"ref":"42.56b","t":"of Ahura Mazda, at the wish of the Amesha-Spentas."},{"ref":"42.57","t":"We worship the good, strong, beneficent Fravashis of the faithful,"},{"ref":"42.57a","t":"who showed their paths to the stars, the moon, the sun, and the"},{"ref":"42.57b","t":"endless lights, that had stood before for a long time in the same"},{"ref":"42.57c","t":"place, without moving forwards, through the oppression of the"},{"ref":"42.57d","t":"Daevas and the assaults of the Daevas."},{"ref":"42.58","t":"And now they move around in their far-revolving circle for"},{"ref":"42.58a","t":"ever, till they come to the time of the good restoration of the"},{"ref":"42.58b","t":"world."},{"ref":"42.59","t":"We worship the good, strong, beneficent Fravashis of the faithful,"},{"ref":"42.59a","t":"who watch over the bright sea Vouru-Kasha, to the number of ninety"},{"ref":"42.59b","t":"thousand, and nine thousand, and nine hundred, and ninety-nine."},{"ref":"42.60","t":"We worship the good, strong, beneficent Fravashis of the faithful,"},{"ref":"42.60a","t":"who watch over the stars Haptoiringa, to the number of ninety"},{"ref":"42.60b","t":"thousand, and nine thousand, and nine hundred, and ninety-nine."},{"ref":"42.61","t":"We worship the good, strong, beneficent Fravashis of the faithful,"},{"ref":"42.61a","t":"who watch over the body of Keresaspa, the son of Sama, the club-bearer"},{"ref":"42.61b","t":"with plaited hair, to the number of ninety thousand, and nine"},{"ref":"42.61c","t":"thousand, and nine hundred, and ninety-nine."},{"ref":"42.62","t":"We worship the good, strong, beneficent Fravashis of the faithful,"},{"ref":"42.62a","t":"who watch over the seed of the holy Zarathushtra, to the number"},{"ref":"42.62b","t":"of ninety thousand, and nine thousand, and nine hundred, and ninety-nine."},{"ref":"42.63","t":"We worship the good, strong, beneficent Fravashis of the faithful,"},{"ref":"42.63a","t":"who fight at the right hand of the reigning lord, if he rejoices"},{"ref":"42.63b","t":"the faithful and if the awful Fravashis of the faithful are not"},{"ref":"42.63c","t":"hurt by him, if they are rejoiced by him, unharmed and unoffended."},{"ref":"42.64","t":"We worship the good, strong, beneficent Fravashis of the faithful,"},{"ref":"42.64a","t":"who are greater, who are stronger, who are swifter, who are more"},{"ref":"42.64b","t":"powerful, who are more victorious, who are more healing, who are"},{"ref":"42.64c","t":"more effective than can be expressed by words; who run by tens"},{"ref":"42.64d","t":"of thousands into the midst of the Myazdas."},{"ref":"42.65","t":"And when the waters come up from the sea Vouru-Kasha, O Spitama"},{"ref":"42.65a","t":"Zarathushtra! along with the Glory made by Mazda, then forwards"},{"ref":"42.65b","t":"come the awful Fravashis of the faithful, many and many hundreds,"},{"ref":"42.65c","t":"many and many thousands, many and many tens of thousands,"},{"ref":"42.66","t":"Seeking water for their own kindred, for their own borough,"},{"ref":"42.66a","t":"for their own town, for their own country, and saying thus: ‘May"},{"ref":"42.66b","t":"our own country have a good store and full joy!’"},{"ref":"42.67","t":"They fight in the battles that are fought in their own place"},{"ref":"42.67a","t":"and land, each according to the place and house where he dwelt"},{"ref":"42.67b","t":"(of yore): they look like a gallant warrior who, girded up and"},{"ref":"42.67c","t":"watchful, fights for the hoard he has treasured up."},{"ref":"42.68","t":"And those of them who win bring waters to their own kindred,"},{"ref":"42.68a","t":"to their own borough, to their own town, to their own country,"},{"ref":"42.68b","t":"saying thus: ‘May my country grow and increase!’"},{"ref":"42.69","t":"And when the all-powerful sovereign of a country has been"},{"ref":"42.69a","t":"surprised by his foes and haters, he invokes them, the awful Fravashis"},{"ref":"42.69b","t":"of the faithful."},{"ref":"42.70","t":"And they come to his help, if they have not been hurt by him,"},{"ref":"42.70a","t":"if they have been rejoiced by him, if they have not been harmed"},{"ref":"42.70b","t":"nor offended, the awful Fravashis of the faithful: they come flying"},{"ref":"42.70c","t":"unto him, it seems as if they were well-winged birds."},{"ref":"42.71","t":"They come in as a weapon and as a shield, to keep him behind"},{"ref":"42.71a","t":"and to keep him in front, from the Druj unseen, from the female"},{"ref":"42.71b","t":"Varenya fiend, from the evil-doer bent on mischief, and from that"},{"ref":"42.71c","t":"fiend who is all death, Angra Mainyu. It will be as if there were"},{"ref":"42.71d","t":"a thousand men watching over one man;"},{"ref":"42.72","t":"So that neither the sword well-thrust, neither the club well-falling,"},{"ref":"42.72a","t":"nor the arrow well-shot, nor the spear well-darted, nor the stones"},{"ref":"42.72b","t":"flung from the arm shall destroy him."},{"ref":"42.73","t":"They come on this side, they come on that side, never resting,"},{"ref":"42.73a","t":"the good, powerful, beneficent Fravashis of the faithful, asking"},{"ref":"42.73b","t":"for help thus: ‘Who will praise us? Who will offer us a sacrifice?"},{"ref":"42.73c","t":"Who will meditate upon us? Who will bless us? Who will receive"},{"ref":"42.73d","t":"us with meat and clothes in his hand and with a prayer worthy"},{"ref":"42.73e","t":"of bliss? Of which of us will the name be taken for invocation?"},{"ref":"42.73f","t":"Of which of you will the soul be worshipped by you with a sacrifice?"},{"ref":"42.73g","t":"To whom will that gift of ours be given, that he may have never-failing"},{"ref":"42.73h","t":"food for ever and ever?’"},{"ref":"42.74","t":"We worship the perception; we worship the intellect; we worship"},{"ref":"42.74a","t":"the conscience; we worship those of the Saoshyants;"},{"ref":"42.74b","t":"We worship the souls; those of the tame animals; those of the"},{"ref":"42.74c","t":"wild animals; those of the animals that live in the waters; those"},{"ref":"42.74d","t":"of the animals that live under the ground; those of the flying"},{"ref":"42.74e","t":"ones; those of the running ones; those of the grazing ones."},{"ref":"42.74f","t":"We worship their Fravashis."},{"ref":"42.75","t":"We worship the Fravashis."},{"ref":"42.75a","t":"We worship them, the liberal;"},{"ref":"42.75b","t":"We worship them, the valiant; we worship them, the most valiant;"},{"ref":"42.75c","t":"We worship them, the beneficent; we worship them, the most beneficent;"},{"ref":"42.75d","t":"We worship them, the powerful;"},{"ref":"42.75e","t":"We worship them, the most strong;"},{"ref":"42.75f","t":"We worship them, the light; we worship them, the most light;"},{"ref":"42.75g","t":"We worship them, the effective; we worship them, the most effective."},{"ref":"42.76","t":"They are the most effective amongst the creatures of the two"},{"ref":"42.76a","t":"Spirits, they the good, strong, beneficent Fravashis of the faithful,"},{"ref":"42.76b","t":"who stood holding fast when the two Spirits created the world,"},{"ref":"42.76c","t":"the Good Spirit and the Evil One."},{"ref":"42.77","t":"When Angra Mainyu broke into the creation of the good holiness,"},{"ref":"42.77a","t":"then came in across Vohu Mano and Atar."},{"ref":"42.78","t":"They destroyed the malice of the fiend Angra Mainyu, so that"},{"ref":"42.78a","t":"the waters did not stop flowing nor did the plants stop growing;"},{"ref":"42.78b","t":"but at once the most beneficent waters of the creator and ruler,"},{"ref":"42.78c","t":"Ahura Mazda, flowed forward and his plants went on growing."},{"ref":"42.79","t":"We worship all the waters;"},{"ref":"42.79a","t":"We worship all the plants;"},{"ref":"42.79b","t":"We worship all the good, strong, beneficent Fravashis of the faithful."},{"ref":"42.79c","t":"We worship the waters by their names;"},{"ref":"42.79d","t":"We worship the plants by their names;"},{"ref":"42.79e","t":"We worship the good, strong, beneficent Fravashis of the faithful"},{"ref":"42.79f","t":"by their names."},{"ref":"42.80","t":"Of all those ancient Fravashis, we worship the Fravashi of"},{"ref":"42.80a","t":"Ahura Mazda; who is the greatest, the best, the fairest, the most"},{"ref":"42.80b","t":"solid, the wisest, the finest of body and supreme in holiness;"},{"ref":"42.81","t":"Whose soul is the Mathra Spenta, who is white, shining, seen"},{"ref":"42.81a","t":"afar; and we worship the beautiful forms, the active forms wherewith"},{"ref":"42.81b","t":"he clothes the Amesha-Spentas; we worship the swift-horsed sun."},{"ref":"42.82","t":"We worship the good, strong, beneficent Fravashis of the Amesha-Spentas,"},{"ref":"42.82a","t":"the bright ones, whose looks perform what they wish, the tall,"},{"ref":"42.82b","t":"quickly coming to do, strong, and lordly, who are undecaying and"},{"ref":"42.82c","t":"holy;"},{"ref":"42.83","t":"Who are all seven of one thought, who are all seven of one"},{"ref":"42.83a","t":"speech, who are all seven of one deed; whose thought is the same,"},{"ref":"42.83b","t":"whose speech is the same, whose deed is the same, whose father"},{"ref":"42.83c","t":"and commander is the same, namely, the Maker, Ahura Mazda;"},{"ref":"42.84","t":"Who see one another’s soul thinking of good thoughts, thinking"},{"ref":"42.84a","t":"of good words, thinking of good deeds, thinking of Garo-nmana,"},{"ref":"42.84b","t":"and whose ways are shining as they go down towards the libations."},{"ref":"42.85","t":"We worship the good, strong, beneficent Fravashis: that of"},{"ref":"42.85a","t":"the most rejoicing fire, the beneficent and assembly-making; and"},{"ref":"42.85b","t":"that of the holy, strong Sraosha, who is the incarnate Word, a"},{"ref":"42.85c","t":"mighty-speared and lordly god; and that of Nairyo-sangha."},{"ref":"42.86","t":"And that of Rashnu Razishta;"},{"ref":"42.86a","t":"That of Mithra, the lord of wide pastures;"},{"ref":"42.86b","t":"That of the Mathra-Spenta;"},{"ref":"42.86c","t":"That of the sky;"},{"ref":"42.86d","t":"That of the waters;"},{"ref":"42.86e","t":"That of the earth;"},{"ref":"42.86f","t":"That of the plants;"},{"ref":"42.86g","t":"That of the Bull;"},{"ref":"42.86h","t":"That of the living man;"},{"ref":"42.86i","t":"That of the holy creation."},{"ref":"42.87","t":"We worship the Fravashi of Gaya Maretan, who first listened"},{"ref":"42.87a","t":"unto the thought and teaching of Ahura Mazda; of whom Ahura formed"},{"ref":"42.87b","t":"the race of the Aryan nations, the seed of the Aryan nations."},{"ref":"42.87c","t":"We worship the piety and the Fravashi of the holy Zarathushtra;"},{"ref":"42.88","t":"Who first thought what is good, who first spoke what is good,"},{"ref":"42.88a","t":"who first did what is good; who was the first Priest, the first"},{"ref":"42.88b","t":"Warrior, the first Plougher of the ground; who first knew and"},{"ref":"42.88c","t":"first taught; who first possessed and first took possession of"},{"ref":"42.88d","t":"the Bull, of Holiness, of the Word, the obedience to the Word,"},{"ref":"42.88e","t":"and dominion, and all the good things made by Mazda, that are"},{"ref":"42.88f","t":"the offspring of the good Principle;"},{"ref":"42.89","t":"Who was the first Priest, the first Warrior, the first Plougher"},{"ref":"42.89a","t":"of the ground; who first took the turning of the wheel from the"},{"ref":"42.89b","t":"hands of the Daeva and of the cold-hearted man; who first in the"},{"ref":"42.89c","t":"material world pronounced the praise of Asha, thus bringing the"},{"ref":"42.89d","t":"Daevas to naught, and confessed himself a worshipper of Mazda,"},{"ref":"42.89e","t":"a follower of Zarathushtra, one who hates the Daevas, and obeys"},{"ref":"42.89f","t":"the laws of Ahura."},{"ref":"42.90","t":"Who first in the material world said the word that destroys"},{"ref":"42.90a","t":"the Daevas, the law of Ahura; who first in the material world"},{"ref":"42.90b","t":"proclaimed the word that destroys the Daevas, the law of Ahura;"},{"ref":"42.90c","t":"who first in the material world declared all the creation of the"},{"ref":"42.90d","t":"Daevas unworthy of sacrifice and prayer; who was strong, giving"},{"ref":"42.90e","t":"all the good things of life, the first bearer of the Law amongst"},{"ref":"42.90f","t":"the nations;"},{"ref":"42.91","t":"In whom was heard the whole Mathra, the word of holiness;"},{"ref":"42.91a","t":"who was the lord and master of the world, the praiser of the most"},{"ref":"42.91b","t":"great, most good and most fair Asha; who had a revelation of the"},{"ref":"42.91c","t":"Law, that most excellent of all beings;"},{"ref":"42.92","t":"For whom the Amesha-Spentas longed, in one accord with the"},{"ref":"42.92a","t":"sun, in the fulness of faith of a devoted heart; they longed for"},{"ref":"42.92b","t":"him, as the lord and master of the world, as the praiser of the"},{"ref":"42.92c","t":"most great, most good, and most fair Asha, as having a revelation"},{"ref":"42.92d","t":"of the Law, that most excellent of all beings;"},{"ref":"42.93","t":"In whose birth and growth the waters and the plants rejoiced;"},{"ref":"42.93a","t":"in whose birth and growth the waters and the plants grew; in whose"},{"ref":"42.93b","t":"birth and growth all the creatures of the good creations cried"},{"ref":"42.93c","t":"out, Hail!"},{"ref":"42.94","t":"‘Hail to us! for he is born, the Athravan, Spitama Zarathushtra."},{"ref":"42.94a","t":"Zarathushtra will offer us sacrifices with libations and bundles"},{"ref":"42.94b","t":"of baresma; and there will the good Law of the worshippers of"},{"ref":"42.94c","t":"Mazda come and spread through all the seven Karshvares of the"},{"ref":"42.94d","t":"earth."},{"ref":"42.95","t":"‘There will Mithra, the lord of wide pastures, increase all"},{"ref":"42.95a","t":"the excellences of our countries, and allay their troubles; there"},{"ref":"42.95b","t":"will the powerful Apam-Napat increase all the excellences of our"},{"ref":"42.95c","t":"countries, and allay their troubles.’"},{"ref":"42.95d","t":"We worship the piety and Fravashi of Maidhyo-maungha, the son"},{"ref":"42.95e","t":"of Arasti, who first listened unto the word and teaching of Zarathushtra."},{"ref":"42.96","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Asmo-hvanvant;"},{"ref":"42.96a","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Asan-hvanvant."},{"ref":"42.96b","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Gavayan."},{"ref":"42.96c","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Parshat-gaush. the son of"},{"ref":"42.96d","t":"Frata;"},{"ref":"42.96e","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Vohvasti, the son of Snaoya;"},{"ref":"42.96f","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Isvat, the son of Varaza."},{"ref":"42.97","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Saena, the son of Ahum-stut,"},{"ref":"42.97a","t":"who first appeared upon this earth with a hundred pupils."},{"ref":"42.97b","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Fradhidaya."},{"ref":"42.97c","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Usmanara, the son of Paeshata."},{"ref":"42.97d","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Vohu-raochah, the son of Franya;"},{"ref":"42.97e","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Asho-raochah, the son of Franya;"},{"ref":"42.97f","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Varesmo-raochah, the son of"},{"ref":"42.97g","t":"Franya."},{"ref":"42.98","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Isat-vastra, the son of"},{"ref":"42.98a","t":"Zarathushtra;"},{"ref":"42.98b","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Urvatat-nara, the son of Zarathushtra;"},{"ref":"42.98c","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Hvare-chithra, the son of"},{"ref":"42.98d","t":"Zarathushtra."},{"ref":"42.98e","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Daevo-tbis, the son of Takhma."},{"ref":"42.98f","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Thrimithwant, the son of Spitama."},{"ref":"42.98g","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Daungha, the son of Zairita."},{"ref":"42.99","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy king Vistaspa; the gallant"},{"ref":"42.99a","t":"one, who was the incarnate Word, the mighty-speared, and lordly"},{"ref":"42.99b","t":"one; who, driving the Druj before him, sought wide room for the"},{"ref":"42.99c","t":"holy religion; who, driving the Druj before him, made wide room"},{"ref":"42.99d","t":"for the holy religion, who made himself the arm and support of"},{"ref":"42.99e","t":"this law of Ahura, of this law of Zarathushtra."},{"ref":"42.100","t":"Who took her, standing bound, from the hands of the Hunus,"},{"ref":"42.100a","t":"and established her to sit in the middle [of the world], high"},{"ref":"42.100b","t":"ruling, never falling back, holy, nourished with plenty of cattle"},{"ref":"42.100c","t":"and pastures, blessed with plenty of cattle and pastures."},{"ref":"42.101","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Zairi-vairi;"},{"ref":"42.101a","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Yukhta-vairi;"},{"ref":"42.101b","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Sriraokhshan;"},{"ref":"42.101c","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Keresaokhshan;"},{"ref":"42.101d","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Vanara;"},{"ref":"42.101e","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Varaza;"},{"ref":"42.101f","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Bujisravah;"},{"ref":"42.101g","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Berezyarshti;"},{"ref":"42.101h","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Tizyarshti;"},{"ref":"42.101i","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Perethu-arshti;"},{"ref":"42.101j","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Vizhyarshti."},{"ref":"42.102","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Naptya;"},{"ref":"42.102a","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Vazhaspa;"},{"ref":"42.102b","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Habaspa."},{"ref":"42.102c","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Vistauru, the son of Naotara."},{"ref":"42.102d","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Frash-ham-vareta;"},{"ref":"42.102e","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Frasho-kareta."},{"ref":"42.102f","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Atare-vanu;"},{"ref":"42.102g","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Atare-pata;"},{"ref":"42.102h","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Atare-data;"},{"ref":"42.102i","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Atare-chithra;"},{"ref":"42.102j","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Atare-hvarenah;"},{"ref":"42.102k","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Atare-savah;"},{"ref":"42.102l","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Atare-zantu;"},{"ref":"42.102m","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Atare-danghu."},{"ref":"42.103","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Hushkyaothna;"},{"ref":"42.103a","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Pishkyaothna;"},{"ref":"42.103b","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy and gallant Spento-data."},{"ref":"42.103c","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Basta-vairi;"},{"ref":"42.103d","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Kava-razem."},{"ref":"42.103e","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Frashaoshtra, the son of Hvova;"},{"ref":"42.103f","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Jamaspa, the son of Hvova;"},{"ref":"42.103g","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Avaraoshtri."},{"ref":"42.104","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Hushkyaothna, the son"},{"ref":"42.104a","t":"of Frashaoshtra;"},{"ref":"42.104b","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Hvadaena, the son of Frashaoshtra."},{"ref":"42.104c","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Hanghaurvaungh, the son of"},{"ref":"42.104d","t":"Jamaspa;"},{"ref":"42.104e","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Vareshna, the son of Hanghaurvaungh."},{"ref":"42.104f","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Vohu-nemah, the son of Avaraoshtri,"},{"ref":"42.104g","t":"To withstand evil dreams, to withstand evil visions, to withstand"},{"ref":"42.104h","t":"evil....(?), to withstand the evil Pairikas."},{"ref":"42.105","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Mathravaka, the son of"},{"ref":"42.105a","t":"Simaezhi, the Aethrapati, the Hamidhpati, who was able to smite"},{"ref":"42.105b","t":"down most of the evil, unfaithful Ashemaoghas, that shout the"},{"ref":"42.105c","t":"hymns, and acknowledge no lord and no master, the dreadful ones"},{"ref":"42.105d","t":"whose Fravashis are to be broken; to withstand the evil done by"},{"ref":"42.105e","t":"the faithful."},{"ref":"42.106","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Asha-stu, the son of Maidhyo-maungha."},{"ref":"42.106a","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Avarethrabah, the son of Rastare-vaghant."},{"ref":"42.106b","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Bujra, the son of Dazgaraspa."},{"ref":"42.106c","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Zbaurvant;"},{"ref":"42.106d","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy and gallant Karesna, the son"},{"ref":"42.106e","t":"of Zbaurvant; who was the incarnate Word, mighty-speared and lordly;"},{"ref":"42.107","t":"In whose house did walk the good, beautiful, shining Ashi"},{"ref":"42.107a","t":"Vanguhi, in the shape of a maid fair of body, most strong, tall-formed,"},{"ref":"42.107b","t":"high-up girded, pure, nobly born of a glorious seed; who, rushing"},{"ref":"42.107c","t":"to the battle, knew how to make room for himself with his own"},{"ref":"42.107d","t":"arms; who, rushing to the battle, knew how to fight the foe with"},{"ref":"42.107e","t":"his own arms."},{"ref":"42.108","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Viraspa, the son of Karesna;"},{"ref":"42.108a","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Azata, the son of Karesna:"},{"ref":"42.108b","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Frayaodha, the son of Karesna."},{"ref":"42.108c","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy and good Arshya; Arshya, the"},{"ref":"42.108d","t":"chief in assemblies, the most energetic of the worshippers of"},{"ref":"42.108e","t":"Mazda."},{"ref":"42.108f","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Darayat-ratha;"},{"ref":"42.108g","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Frayat-ratha;"},{"ref":"42.108h","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Skarayat-ratha."},{"ref":"42.109","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Arshvant;"},{"ref":"42.109a","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Vyarshvant;"},{"ref":"42.109b","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Paityarshvant."},{"ref":"42.109c","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Amru;"},{"ref":"42.109d","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Chamru."},{"ref":"42.109e","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Dratha;"},{"ref":"42.109f","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Paiti-dratha;"},{"ref":"42.109g","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Paiti-vangha."},{"ref":"42.109h","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Frasha-vakhsha."},{"ref":"42.109i","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Nemo-vanghu, the son of Vaedhayangha."},{"ref":"42.110","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Visadha."},{"ref":"42.110a","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Asha-vanghu, the son of Bivandangha;"},{"ref":"42.110b","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Jaro-danghu, the son of Pairishtira;"},{"ref":"42.110c","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Neremyazdana, the son of Athwyoza."},{"ref":"42.110d","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Berezishnu, the son of Ara;"},{"ref":"42.110e","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Kasupatu, the son of Ara."},{"ref":"42.110f","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Frya."},{"ref":"42.110g","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy ASTVAT-ERETA."},{"ref":"42.111","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Gaopi-vanghu."},{"ref":"42.111a","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy and gallant Ham-baretar vanghvam."},{"ref":"42.111b","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Staotar-Vahishtahe-Ashyehe."},{"ref":"42.111c","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Pouru-dhakhshti, the son of"},{"ref":"42.111d","t":"Khshtavaenya;"},{"ref":"42.111e","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Khshoi-wraspa, the son of"},{"ref":"42.111f","t":"Khshtavaenya."},{"ref":"42.112","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Ayo-asti, the son of Pouru-dhakhshti;"},{"ref":"42.112a","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Vohv-asti, the son of Pount-dhakhshti;"},{"ref":"42.112b","t":"We-worship the Fravashi of the holy Gaya-dhasti, the son of Pouru-dhakhshti;"},{"ref":"42.112c","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Asha-vazdah, the son of Pouru-dhakhshti;"},{"ref":"42.112d","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Urudhu, the son of Pouru-dhakhshti."},{"ref":"42.112e","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Khshathro-chinah, the son"},{"ref":"42.112f","t":"of Khshvoiwraspa."},{"ref":"42.113","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Ashahura, the son of Jishti."},{"ref":"42.113a","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Fraya-zanta;"},{"ref":"42.113b","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Frenah, the son of Frayazanta;"},{"ref":"42.113c","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Jaro-vanghu, the son of Frayazanta."},{"ref":"42.113d","t":"We worship the Fravashis of the holy Asha-vazdah and Thrita, the"},{"ref":"42.113e","t":"sons of Sayuzhdri."},{"ref":"42.113f","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Vohu-raochah, the son of Varakasa."},{"ref":"42.113g","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Arejan-ghant, the Turanian."},{"ref":"42.113h","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Usinemah."},{"ref":"42.114","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Yukhtaspa."},{"ref":"42.114a","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Asha-skyaothna, the son of"},{"ref":"42.114b","t":"Gayadhasti."},{"ref":"42.114c","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Vohu-nemah, the son of Katu;"},{"ref":"42.114d","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Vohu-vazdah, the son of Katu."},{"ref":"42.114e","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Asha-saredha, the son of Asha-sairyach;"},{"ref":"42.114f","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Asha-saredha, the son of Zairyach."},{"ref":"42.114g","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Chakhshni."},{"ref":"42.114h","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Syavaspi."},{"ref":"42.114i","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Pourushti, the son of Kavi."},{"ref":"42.115","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Varesmapa, the son of"},{"ref":"42.115a","t":"Janara."},{"ref":"42.115b","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Nanarasti, the son of Paeshatah;"},{"ref":"42.115c","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Zarazdati, the son of Paeshatah."},{"ref":"42.115d","t":"We worship tke Fravashi of the holy Gaevani, the son of Vohu-nemah."},{"ref":"42.115e","t":"We worship the Fravashis of the holy Arezva and Sruta-spadha"},{"ref":"42.115f","t":"We worship the Fravashis Of the holy Zrayah and Spento-khratu."},{"ref":"42.115g","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Varshni, the son of Vagereza."},{"ref":"42.115h","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Frachya, the son of Taurvati."},{"ref":"42.115i","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Vahmae-data, the son of Mathravaka,"},{"ref":"42.115j","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Ushtra, the son of Sadhanah."},{"ref":"42.116","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Danghu-sruta;"},{"ref":"42.116a","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Danghu-fradhah."},{"ref":"42.116b","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Aspo-padho-makhshti;"},{"ref":"42.116c","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Payanghro-makhshti."},{"ref":"42.116d","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Ushtazanta."},{"ref":"42.116e","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Asha-savah,"},{"ref":"42.116f","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Asho-urvatha."},{"ref":"42.116g","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Haomo-hvarenah."},{"ref":"42.117","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Frava."},{"ref":"42.117a","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Usnaka."},{"ref":"42.117b","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Hvanvant."},{"ref":"42.117c","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Daeno-vazah."},{"ref":"42.117d","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Arejaona."},{"ref":"42.117e","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Aiwi-hvarenah."},{"ref":"42.117f","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Huyazata."},{"ref":"42.117g","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Hare-dhaspa."},{"ref":"42.117h","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Pazinah."},{"ref":"42.117i","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Hvakhshathra."},{"ref":"42.117j","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Asho-paoirya,"},{"ref":"42.117k","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy ASTVAT-ERETA."},{"ref":"42.118","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Hugau."},{"ref":"42.118a","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Anghuyu."},{"ref":"42.118b","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Gauri;"},{"ref":"42.118c","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Yushta, the son of Gauri."},{"ref":"42.118d","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Mazdra-vanghu;"},{"ref":"42.118e","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Srira-vanghu."},{"ref":"42.118f","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Ayuta."},{"ref":"42.118g","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Suro-yazata."},{"ref":"42.119","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Eredhwa"},{"ref":"42.119a","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Kavi."},{"ref":"42.119b","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Ukhshan, the son of the great"},{"ref":"42.119c","t":"Vidi-sravah, known afar."},{"ref":"42.119d","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Vanghu-dhata, the son of Hvadhata;"},{"ref":"42.119e","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Uzya, the son of Vanghu-dhata;"},{"ref":"42.119f","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Frya."},{"ref":"42.120","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy one whose name is Ashem-yenhe-raochau;"},{"ref":"42.120a","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy one whose name is Ashem-yenhe-vereza;"},{"ref":"42.120b","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy one whose name is Ashem-yahmai-ushta."},{"ref":"42.120c","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Yoishta, of the Fryana house."},{"ref":"42.120d","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Usmanara, the son of Paeshatah"},{"ref":"42.120e","t":"Paitisrira, to withstand the evil done by one’s kindred."},{"ref":"42.121","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Spiti, the son of Uspasnu;"},{"ref":"42.121a","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Erezraspa, the son of Uspasnu."},{"ref":"42.121b","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Usadhan, the son of Mazdayasna."},{"ref":"42.121c","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Fradat-vanghu, the son of"},{"ref":"42.121d","t":"Stivant."},{"ref":"42.121e","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Raochas-chaeshman;"},{"ref":"42.121f","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Hvare-chaeshman"},{"ref":"42.121g","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Frasrutara;"},{"ref":"42.121h","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Visrutara."},{"ref":"42.121i","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Baremna. We worship the Fravashi"},{"ref":"42.121j","t":"of the holy Visruta."},{"ref":"42.122","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Hvaspa;"},{"ref":"42.122a","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Chathwaraspa."},{"ref":"42.122b","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Dawra-maeshi."},{"ref":"42.122c","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Fraora-ostra, the son of Kaosha."},{"ref":"42.122d","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Frinaspa, the son of Kaeva."},{"ref":"42.122e","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Fradat-nara, the son of Gravaratu."},{"ref":"42.122f","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Vohu-ushtra, the son of Akhnangha."},{"ref":"42.122g","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Vivare-shvant, the son of"},{"ref":"42.122h","t":"Ainyu."},{"ref":"42.123","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Frarazi, the son of Tura."},{"ref":"42.123a","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Stipi, the son of Ravant."},{"ref":"42.123b","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Parshanta, the son of Gandarewa."},{"ref":"42.123c","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Avahya, the son of Spenta."},{"ref":"42.123d","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Aeta, the son of Mayu;"},{"ref":"42.123e","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Yaetush-gau, the son of Vyatana."},{"ref":"42.123f","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Garshta, the son of Kavi."},{"ref":"42.124","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Pouru-bangha, the son"},{"ref":"42.124a","t":"of Zaosha."},{"ref":"42.124b","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Vohu-data, the son of Kata."},{"ref":"42.124c","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Baungha, the son of Saungha."},{"ref":"42.124d","t":"We worship the Fravashis of the holy Hvareza and Ankasa."},{"ref":"42.124e","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Aravaoshtra, the son of Erezvat-danghu."},{"ref":"42.124f","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Frachithra, the son of Berezvant."},{"ref":"42.124g","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Vohu-peresa, the son of Ainyu."},{"ref":"42.125","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Paro-dasma, the son of"},{"ref":"42.125a","t":"Dashtaghni, a Miza man of the Miza land."},{"ref":"42.125b","t":"We worship the Fravashis of the holy Fratira and Baeshatastira."},{"ref":"42.125c","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy and pure Avare-gau, the son"},{"ref":"42.125d","t":"of Aoighimatastira."},{"ref":"42.125e","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Gaomant, the son of Zavan,"},{"ref":"42.125f","t":"a Raozhdya man of the Raozhdya land."},{"ref":"42.125g","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Thrit, the son of Aevo-saredha-fyaeshta,"},{"ref":"42.125h","t":"a Tanya man of the Tanya land."},{"ref":"42.126","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Tiro-nakathwa, of the"},{"ref":"42.126a","t":"Uspaeshta-Saena house."},{"ref":"42.126b","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Utayuti Vit-kavi, the son"},{"ref":"42.126c","t":"of Zighri, of the Saena house;"},{"ref":"42.126d","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Frohakafra, the son of Merezishmya,"},{"ref":"42.126e","t":"of the Saena house."},{"ref":"42.126f","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Varesmo-raochah, the son of"},{"ref":"42.126g","t":"Perethu-afzem."},{"ref":"42.127","t":"We worship the Fravashis of the holy Asha-nemah and Vidat-gau,"},{"ref":"42.127a","t":"of this country."},{"ref":"42.127b","t":"We worship the Fravashis of the holy Par-shat-gau and Dazgara-gau,"},{"ref":"42.127c","t":"of the Apakhshira country."},{"ref":"42.127d","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Hufra-vakhsh, of the Kahrkana"},{"ref":"42.127e","t":"house."},{"ref":"42.127f","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Akayadha, of the Pidha house."},{"ref":"42.127g","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Jamaspa, the younger."},{"ref":"42.127h","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Maidhyo-maungha, the younger."},{"ref":"42.127i","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Urvatat-nara, the younger."},{"ref":"42.128","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Raochas-chaeshman;"},{"ref":"42.128a","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Hvare-chaeshman;"},{"ref":"42.128b","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Fradat-hvarenah;"},{"ref":"42.128c","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Varedat-hvarenah;"},{"ref":"42.128d","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Vouru-nemah;"},{"ref":"42.128e","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Vouru-savah;"},{"ref":"42.128f","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Ukhshyat-ereta;"},{"ref":"42.128g","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Ukhshyat-nemah;"},{"ref":"42.128h","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy ASTVAT-ERETA;"},{"ref":"42.129","t":"Whose name will be the victorious SAOSHYANT and whose name"},{"ref":"42.129a","t":"will be Astvat-ereta. He will be SAOSHYANT (the Beneficent One),"},{"ref":"42.129b","t":"because he will benefit the whole bodily world; he will be ASTVAT-ERETA"},{"ref":"42.129c","t":"(he who makes the bodily creatures rise up), because as a bodily"},{"ref":"42.129d","t":"creature and as a living creature he will stand against the destruction"},{"ref":"42.129e","t":"of the bodily creatures, to withstand the Druj of the two-footed"},{"ref":"42.129f","t":"brood, to withstand the evil done by the faithful."},{"ref":"42.130","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Yima, the son of Vivanghant;"},{"ref":"42.130a","t":"the valiant Yima, who had flocks at his wish; to stand against"},{"ref":"42.130b","t":"the oppression caused by the Daevas, against the drought that"},{"ref":"42.130c","t":"destroys pastures, and against death that creeps unseen."},{"ref":"42.131","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Thraetaona, of the Athwya"},{"ref":"42.131a","t":"house; to stand against itch, hot fever, humours, cold fever,"},{"ref":"42.131b","t":"and incontinency, to stand against the evil done by the Serpent."},{"ref":"42.131c","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Aoshnara, the son of Pouru-jira."},{"ref":"42.131d","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Uzava, the son of Tumaspa."},{"ref":"42.131e","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Aghraeratha, the demi-man."},{"ref":"42.131f","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Manushchithra, the son of"},{"ref":"42.131g","t":"Airyu."},{"ref":"42.132","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy king Kavata;"},{"ref":"42.132a","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy king Aipivanghu;"},{"ref":"42.132b","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy king Usadhan;"},{"ref":"42.132c","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Arshan;"},{"ref":"42.132d","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Pisanah;"},{"ref":"42.132e","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy king Byarshan;"},{"ref":"42.132f","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy king Syavarshan;"},{"ref":"42.132g","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy king Husravah;"},{"ref":"42.133","t":"For the well-shapened Strength, for the Victory made by Ahura,"},{"ref":"42.133a","t":"for the crushing Ascendant for the righteousness of the law, for"},{"ref":"42.133b","t":"the innocence of the law, for the unconquerable power of the law;"},{"ref":"42.133c","t":"for the extermination of the enemies at one stroke;"},{"ref":"42.134","t":"And for the vigour of health, for the Glory made by Mazda,"},{"ref":"42.134a","t":"for the health of the body, and for a good, virtuous offspring,"},{"ref":"42.134b","t":"wise, chief in assemblies, bright, and clear-eyed, that frees"},{"ref":"42.134c","t":"[their father] from the pangs [of hell], of good intellect; and"},{"ref":"42.134d","t":"for that part in the blessed world that falls to wisdom and to"},{"ref":"42.134e","t":"those who do not follow impiety;"},{"ref":"42.135","t":"For a dominion full of splendour, for a long, long life, and"},{"ref":"42.135a","t":"for all boons and remedies; to withstand the Yatus and Pairikas,"},{"ref":"42.135b","t":"the oppressors, the blind, and the deaf; to withstand the evil"},{"ref":"42.135c","t":"done by oppressors."},{"ref":"42.136","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Keresaspa, the Sama, the"},{"ref":"42.136a","t":"club-bearer with plaited hair; to withstand the dreadful arm and"},{"ref":"42.136b","t":"the hordes with the wide battle array, with the many spears, with"},{"ref":"42.136c","t":"the straight spears, with the spears uplifted, bearing the spears"},{"ref":"42.136d","t":"of havoc; to withstand the dreadful brigand who works destruction,"},{"ref":"42.136e","t":"the man-slayer who has no mercy; to withstand the evil done by"},{"ref":"42.136f","t":"the brigand."},{"ref":"42.137","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Akhrura, the son of Husravah;"},{"ref":"42.137a","t":"To withstand the wicked one that deceives his friend and the niggard"},{"ref":"42.137b","t":"that causes the destruction of the world."},{"ref":"42.137c","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy and gallant Haoshyangha;"},{"ref":"42.137d","t":"To withstand tke Mazainya Daevas and the Varenya fiends; to withstand"},{"ref":"42.137e","t":"the evil done by the Daevas."},{"ref":"42.138","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Fradhakhshti, the son"},{"ref":"42.138a","t":"of the jar,"},{"ref":"42.138b","t":"To withstand Aeshma, the fiend of the wounding spear, and the"},{"ref":"42.138c","t":"Daevas that grow through Aeshma; to withstand the evil done by"},{"ref":"42.138d","t":"Aeshma."},{"ref":"42.139","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Hvovi."},{"ref":"42.139a","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Freni;"},{"ref":"42.139b","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Thriti;"},{"ref":"42.139c","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Pouruchista."},{"ref":"42.139d","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Hutaosa;"},{"ref":"42.139e","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Huma."},{"ref":"42.139f","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Zairichi."},{"ref":"42.139g","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Vispa-taurvashi."},{"ref":"42.139h","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Ushtavaiti."},{"ref":"42.139i","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Tushnamaiti."},{"ref":"42.140","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Freni, the wife of Usenemah;"},{"ref":"42.140a","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Freni, the wife of the son"},{"ref":"42.140b","t":"of Frayazanta;"},{"ref":"42.140c","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Freni, the wife of the son"},{"ref":"42.140d","t":"of Khshoiwraspa;"},{"ref":"42.140e","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Freni, the wife of Gayadhasti."},{"ref":"42.140f","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Asabani, the wife of Pourudhakhsti."},{"ref":"42.140g","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Ukhshyeinti, the wife of Staotar-Vahishtahe-Ashyehe."},{"ref":"42.141","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy maid Vadhut."},{"ref":"42.141a","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy maid Jaghrudh."},{"ref":"42.141b","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy maid Franghadh."},{"ref":"42.141c","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy maid Urudhayant."},{"ref":"42.141d","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy maid Paesanghanu."},{"ref":"42.141e","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Hvaredhi."},{"ref":"42.141f","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Huchithra."},{"ref":"42.141g","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy Kanuka."},{"ref":"42.141h","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy maid Srutat-fedhri."},{"ref":"42.142","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy maid Vanghu-fedhri;"},{"ref":"42.142a","t":"We worship the Fravashi of the holy maid Eredat-fedhri, who is"},{"ref":"42.142b","t":"called Vispa-taurvairi. She is Vispa-taurvairi (the all-destroying)"},{"ref":"42.142c","t":"because she will bring him forth, who will destroy the malice"},{"ref":"42.142d","t":"of Daevas and men, to withstand the evil done by the Jahi."},{"ref":"42.143","t":"We worship the Fravashis of the holy men in the Aryan countries;"},{"ref":"42.143a","t":"We worship the Fravashis of the holy women in the Aryan countries."},{"ref":"42.143b","t":"We worship the Fravashis of the holy men in the Turanian countries;"},{"ref":"42.143c","t":"We worship the Fravashis of the holy women in the Turanian countries."},{"ref":"42.143d","t":"We worship the Fravashis of the holy men in the Sairimyan countries;"},{"ref":"42.143e","t":"We worship the Fravashis of the holy women in the Sairimyan countries."},{"ref":"42.144","t":"We worship the Fravashis of the holy men in the Sairimyan"},{"ref":"42.144a","t":"countries;"},{"ref":"42.144b","t":"We worship the Fravashis of the holy women in the Saini countries."},{"ref":"42.144c","t":"We worship the Fravashis of the holy men in the Dahi countries;"},{"ref":"42.144d","t":"We worship the Fravashis of the holy women in the Dahi countries."},{"ref":"42.144e","t":"We worship the Fravashis of the holy men in all countries;"},{"ref":"42.144f","t":"We worship the Fravashis of the holy women in all countries."},{"ref":"42.145","t":"We worship all the good, awful, beneficent Fravashis of the"},{"ref":"42.145a","t":"faithful, from Gaya Mareta down to the victorious Saoshyant. May"},{"ref":"42.145b","t":"the Fravashis of the faithful come quickly to us! May they come"},{"ref":"42.145c","t":"to our help!"},{"ref":"42.146","t":"They protect us when in distress with manifest assistance,"},{"ref":"42.146a","t":"with the assistance of Ahura Mazda and of the holy, powerful Sraosha,"},{"ref":"42.146b","t":"and with the Mathra-Spenta, the all-knowing, who hates the Daevas"},{"ref":"42.146c","t":"with a mighty hate, a friend of Ahura Mazda, whom Zarathushtra"},{"ref":"42.146d","t":"worshipped so greatly in the material world."},{"ref":"42.147","t":"May the good waters and the plants and the Fravashis of the"},{"ref":"42.147a","t":"faithful abide down here! May you be rejoiced and well received"},{"ref":"42.147b","t":"in this house! Here are the Athravans of the countries, thinking"},{"ref":"42.147c","t":"of good holiness. Our hands are lifted up for asking help, and"},{"ref":"42.147d","t":"for offering a sacrifice unto you, O most beneficent Fravashis!"},{"ref":"42.148","t":"We worship the Fravashis of all the holy men and holy women"},{"ref":"42.148a","t":"whose souls are worthy of sacrifice, whose Fravashis are worthy"},{"ref":"42.148b","t":"of invocation."},{"ref":"42.148c","t":"We worship the Fravashis of all the holy men and holy women, our"},{"ref":"42.148d","t":"sacrificing to whom makes us good in the eyes of Akura Mazda:"},{"ref":"42.148e","t":"of all of those we have heard that Zarathushtra is the first and"},{"ref":"42.148f","t":"best, as a follower of Ahura and as a performer of the law."},{"ref":"42.149","t":"We worship the spirit, conscience, perception, soul, and Fravashi"},{"ref":"42.149a","t":"of men of the primitive law, of the first who listened to the"},{"ref":"42.149b","t":"teaching (of Ahura), holy men and holy women, who struggled for"},{"ref":"42.149c","t":"holiness; we worship the spirit, conscience, perception, soul,"},{"ref":"42.149d","t":"and Fravashi of our next-of-kin, holy men and holy women, who"},{"ref":"42.149e","t":"struggled for holiness."},{"ref":"42.150","t":"We worship the men of the primitive law who will be in these"},{"ref":"42.150a","t":"houses, boroughs, towns, and countries;"},{"ref":"42.150b","t":"We worship the men of the primitive law who have been in these"},{"ref":"42.150c","t":"houses, boroughs, towns, and countries;"},{"ref":"42.150d","t":"We worship the men of the primitive law who are in these houses,"},{"ref":"42.150e","t":"boroughs, towns, and countries."},{"ref":"42.151","t":"We worship the men of the primitive law in all houses, boroughs,"},{"ref":"42.151a","t":"towns, and countries, who obtained these houses, who obtained"},{"ref":"42.151b","t":"these boroughs, who obtained these towns, who obtained these countries,"},{"ref":"42.151c","t":"who obtained holiness, who obtained the Mathra, who obtained the"},{"ref":"42.151d","t":"[blessedness of the] soul, who obtained all the perfections of"},{"ref":"42.151e","t":"goodness."},{"ref":"42.152","t":"We worship Zarathushtra, the lord and master of all the material"},{"ref":"42.152a","t":"world, the man of the primitive law; the wisest of all-beings,"},{"ref":"42.152b","t":"the best-ruling of all beings, the brightest of all beings, the"},{"ref":"42.152c","t":"most glorious of all beings, the most worthy of sacrifice amongst"},{"ref":"42.152d","t":"all beings, the most worthy of prayer amongst all beings, the"},{"ref":"42.152e","t":"most worthy of propitiation amongst all beings, the most worthy"},{"ref":"42.152f","t":"of glorification amongst all beings, whom we call well-desired"},{"ref":"42.152g","t":"and worthy of sacrifice and prayer as much as any being can be,"},{"ref":"42.152h","t":"in the perfection of his holiness."},{"ref":"42.153","t":"We worship this earth; we worship those heavens;"},{"ref":"42.153a","t":"We worship those good things that stand between (the earth and"},{"ref":"42.153b","t":"the heavens) and that are worthy of sacrifice and prayer and are"},{"ref":"42.153c","t":"to be worshipped by the faithful man."},{"ref":"42.154","t":"We worship the souls of the wild beasts and of the tame."},{"ref":"42.154a","t":"We worship the souls of the holy men and women, born at any time,"},{"ref":"42.154b","t":"whose consciences struggle, or will struggle, or have. struggled,"},{"ref":"42.154c","t":"for the good."},{"ref":"42.155","t":"We worship the spirit, conscience, perception, soul, and Fravashi"},{"ref":"42.155a","t":"of the holy men and holy women who struggle, will struggle, or"},{"ref":"42.155b","t":"have struggled, and teach the Law and who have struggled for holiness."},{"ref":"42.155c","t":"Yenhe hatam: All those beings to whom Ahura Mazda..."},{"ref":"42.155d","t":"Yatha ahu vairyo: The will of the Lord is the law of holiness...."},{"ref":"42.156","t":"The Fravashis of the faithful, awful and overpowering, awful"},{"ref":"42.156a","t":"and victorious; the Fravashis of the men of the primitive law;"},{"ref":"42.156b","t":"the Fravashis of the next-of-kin; may these Fravashis come satisfied"},{"ref":"42.156c","t":"into this house, may they walk satisfied through this house!"},{"ref":"42.157","t":"May they, being satisfied, bless this house with the presence"},{"ref":"42.157a","t":"of the kind Ashi Vanguhi! May they leave this house satisfied!"},{"ref":"42.157b","t":"May they carry back from here hymns and worship to the Maker,"},{"ref":"42.157c","t":"Ahura Mazda, and the Amesha-Spentas! May they not leave this house"},{"ref":"42.157d","t":"of us, the worshippers of Mazda, complaining!"},{"ref":"42.158","t":"Yatha ahu vairyo: The will of the Lord is the law of holiness...."},{"ref":"42.158a","t":"I bless the sacrifice and prayer, and the strength and vigour"},{"ref":"42.158b","t":"of the awful, overpowering Fravashis of the faithful; of the Fravashis"},{"ref":"42.158c","t":"of the men of the primitive law; of the Fravashis of the next-of-kin."},{"ref":"42.158d","t":"Ashem Vohu: Holiness is the best of all good...."},{"ref":"42.158e","t":"[Give] unto that man brightness and glory,... give him the bright,"},{"ref":"42.158f","t":"all-happy, blissful abode of the holy Ones."},{"sp":"HDR","t":"14. Warharan Yasht"},{"ref":"43.0","t":"May Ahura Mazda be rejoiced!.... Ashem Vohu: Holiness is the"},{"ref":"43.0a","t":"best of all good...."},{"ref":"43.0b","t":"I confess myself a worshipper of Mazda, a follower of Zarathushtra,"},{"ref":"43.0c","t":"one who hates the Daevas and obeys the laws of Ahura;"},{"ref":"43.0d","t":"For sacrifice, prayer, propitiation, and glorification unto (Havani],"},{"ref":"43.0e","t":"the holy and master of holiness...."},{"ref":"43.0f","t":"Unto Verethraghna, made by Mazda, and unto the crushing Ascendant;"},{"ref":"43.0g","t":"Be propitiation, with sacrifice, prayer, propitiation, and glorification."},{"ref":"43.0h","t":"Yatha ahu vairyo: The will of the Lord is the law of holiness...."},{"ref":"43.1","t":"We sacrifice unto Verethraghna, made by Ahura."},{"ref":"43.1a","t":"Zarathushtra asked Ahura Mazda: ‘Ahura Mazda, most beneficent"},{"ref":"43.1b","t":"Spirit, Maker of the material world, thou Holy One! ‘Who is the"},{"ref":"43.1c","t":"best-armed of the heavenly gods?’"},{"ref":"43.1d","t":"Ahura Mazda answered: ‘It is Verethraghna, made by Ahura, O Spitama"},{"ref":"43.1e","t":"Zarathushtra!’"},{"ref":"43.2","t":"Verethraghna, made by Ahura, came to him first, running in"},{"ref":"43.2a","t":"the shape of a strong, beautiful wind, made by Mazda; he bore"},{"ref":"43.2b","t":"the good Glory, made by Mazda, the Glory made by Mazda, that is"},{"ref":"43.2c","t":"both health and strength."},{"ref":"43.3","t":"Then he, who is the strongest, said unto him: ‘I am the strongest"},{"ref":"43.3a","t":"in strength; I am the most victorious in victory; I am the most"},{"ref":"43.3b","t":"glorious in glory; I am the most favouring in favour; I am the"},{"ref":"43.3c","t":"best giver of welfare: I am the best-healing in health-giving."},{"ref":"43.4","t":"‘And I shall destroy the malice of all the malicious, the"},{"ref":"43.4a","t":"malice of Daevas and men, of the ‘Yatus and Pairikas, of the oppressors,"},{"ref":"43.4b","t":"the blind, and the deaf."},{"ref":"43.5","t":"‘For his brightness and glory, I will offer unto him a sacrifice"},{"ref":"43.5a","t":"worth being heard; namely, unto Verethraghna, made by Ahura. We"},{"ref":"43.5b","t":"worship Verethraghna, made by Ahura, with an offering of libations,"},{"ref":"43.5c","t":"according to the primitive ordinances of Ahura; with the Haoma"},{"ref":"43.5d","t":"and meat, the baresma, the wisdom of the tongue, the holy spells,"},{"ref":"43.5e","t":"the speech, the deeds, the libations, and the rightly-spoken words."},{"ref":"43.5f","t":"‘Yenhe hatam: All those beings of whom Ahura Mazda...."},{"ref":"43.6","t":"‘We sacrifice unto Verethraghna, made by Ahura.’"},{"ref":"43.6a","t":"Zarathushtra asked Ahura Mazda: ‘Ahura Mazda, most beneficent"},{"ref":"43.6b","t":"Spirit, Maker of the material world, thou Holy One!"},{"ref":"43.6c","t":"Who is the best-armed of the heavenly gods?’"},{"ref":"43.6d","t":"Ahura Mazda answered: ‘It is Verethraghna, made by Ahura, O Spitama"},{"ref":"43.6e","t":"Zarathushtra!’"},{"ref":"43.7","t":"Verethraghna, made by Ahura, came to him the second time,"},{"ref":"43.7a","t":"running in the shape of a beautiful bull, with yellow ears and"},{"ref":"43.7b","t":"golden horns; upon whose horns floated the well-shapen Strength,"},{"ref":"43.7c","t":"and Victory, beautiful of form, made by Ahura: thus did he come,"},{"ref":"43.7d","t":"bearing the good Glory, made by Mazda, the Glory made by Mazda,"},{"ref":"43.7e","t":"that is both health and strength."},{"ref":"43.7f","t":"Then he, who is the strongest, said unto him: ‘I am the strongest"},{"ref":"43.7g","t":"in strength...."},{"ref":"43.7h","t":"‘And I shall destroy the malice of all malicious...."},{"ref":"43.7i","t":"For his brightness and glory, I will offer unto him a sacrifice"},{"ref":"43.7j","t":"worth being heard...."},{"ref":"43.8","t":"We sacrifice unto Verethraghna, made by Ahura."},{"ref":"43.8a","t":"Zarathushtra asked Ahura Mazda: ‘Ahura Mazda, most beneficent"},{"ref":"43.8b","t":"Spirit, Maker of the material world, thou Holy One!"},{"ref":"43.8c","t":"‘Who is the best-armed of the heavenly gods?’"},{"ref":"43.8d","t":"Ahura Mazda answered: ‘It is Verethraghna, made by Ahura, O Spitama"},{"ref":"43.8e","t":"Zarathushtra!’"},{"ref":"43.9","t":"Verethraghna, made by Ahura, came to him the third time, running"},{"ref":"43.9a","t":"in the shape of a white, beautiful horse, with yellow ears and"},{"ref":"43.9b","t":"a golden caparison; upon whose forehead floated the well-shapen"},{"ref":"43.9c","t":"Strength, and Victory, beautiful of form, made by Ahura: thus"},{"ref":"43.9d","t":"did he come, bearing the good Glory, made by Mazda, that is both"},{"ref":"43.9e","t":"health and strength."},{"ref":"43.9f","t":"Then he, who is the strongest, said unto him: ‘I am the strongest"},{"ref":"43.9g","t":"in strength...."},{"ref":"43.9h","t":"‘And I shall destroy the malice of all malicious....’"},{"ref":"43.9i","t":"For his brightness and glory, I will offer unto him a sacrifice"},{"ref":"43.9j","t":"worth being heard...."},{"ref":"43.10","t":"We sacrifice unto Verethraghna, made by Ahura."},{"ref":"43.10a","t":"Zarathushtra asked Ahura Mazda: ‘Ahura Mazda, most beneficent"},{"ref":"43.10b","t":"Spirit, Maker of the material world, ‘Who is the best-armed of"},{"ref":"43.10c","t":"the heavenly gods?’"},{"ref":"43.10d","t":"Ahura Mazda answered: ‘It is Verethraghna, made by Ahura, O Spitama"},{"ref":"43.10e","t":"Zarathushtra!’"},{"ref":"43.11","t":"Verethraghna, made by Ahura, came to him the fourth time,"},{"ref":"43.11a","t":"running in the shape of a burden-bearing camel, sharp-toothed,"},{"ref":"43.11b","t":"swift.... stamping forwards, long-haired, and living in the"},{"ref":"43.11c","t":"abodes of men;"},{"ref":"43.12","t":"Who of all males in rut shows greatest strength and greatest"},{"ref":"43.12a","t":"fire, when he goes to his females. Of all females those are best"},{"ref":"43.12b","t":"kept whom a burden-bearing camel keeps, who has thick forelegs"},{"ref":"43.12c","t":"and large humps,... quick-eyed, long-headed, bright, tall,"},{"ref":"43.12d","t":"and strong;"},{"ref":"43.13","t":"Whose piercing look goes afar.... even in the dark of the"},{"ref":"43.13a","t":"night; who throws white foam along his mouth; well-kneed, well-footed,"},{"ref":"43.13b","t":"standing with the countenance of an all-powerful master: Thus"},{"ref":"43.13c","t":"did Verethraghna come, bearing the good Glory made by Mazda, the"},{"ref":"43.13d","t":"Glory made by Mazda"},{"ref":"43.14","t":"We sacrifice unto Verethraghna, made by Ahura."},{"ref":"43.14a","t":"Zarathushtra asked Ahura Mazda: ‘Ahura Mazda, most beneficent"},{"ref":"43.14b","t":"Spirit, Maker of the material world, thou Holy One! ‘Who is the"},{"ref":"43.14c","t":"best-armed of the heavenly gods?’ Ahura Mazda answered: ‘It is"},{"ref":"43.14d","t":"Verethraghna, made by Ahura, O Spitama Zarathushtra!’"},{"ref":"43.15","t":"‘Verethraghna, made by Ahura, came to him the fifth time,"},{"ref":"43.15a","t":"running in the shape of a boar, opposing the foes, a sharp-toothed"},{"ref":"43.15b","t":"he-boar, a sharp-jawed boar, that kills at one stroke, pursuing,"},{"ref":"43.15c","t":"wrathful, with a dripping face, strong, and swift to run, and"},{"ref":"43.15d","t":"rushing all around."},{"ref":"43.15e","t":"Thus did Verethraghna come, bearing the good Glory made by Mazda,"},{"ref":"43.15f","t":"the Glory made by Mazda."},{"ref":"43.16","t":"We sacrifice unto Verethragna, made by..... Zarathushtra"},{"ref":"43.16a","t":"asked Ahura Mazda: ‘Ahura Mazda, most beneficent Spirit, Maker"},{"ref":"43.16b","t":"of the material world, thou Holy One!"},{"ref":"43.16c","t":"‘Who is the best-armed of the heavenly gods?’"},{"ref":"43.16d","t":"Ahura Mazda answered: ‘It is Verethraghna, made by Ahura, O Spitama"},{"ref":"43.16e","t":"Zarathushtra!’"},{"ref":"43.17","t":"Verethraghna, made by Ahura, came to him the sixth time, running"},{"ref":"43.17a","t":"in the shape of a beautiful youth of fifteen, shining, clear-eyed,"},{"ref":"43.17b","t":"thin-heeled."},{"ref":"43.17c","t":"Thus did Verethraghna come, bearing the good Glory made by Mazda,"},{"ref":"43.17d","t":"the Glory made by Mazda...."},{"ref":"43.18","t":"We sacrifice unto Verethraghna, made by Ahura."},{"ref":"43.18a","t":"Zarathushtra asked Ahura Mazda: ‘Ahura Mazda, most beneficent"},{"ref":"43.18b","t":"Spirit, Maker of the material world, thou Holy One!"},{"ref":"43.18c","t":"‘Who is the best-armed of the heavenly gods?’"},{"ref":"43.18d","t":"Ahura Mazda answered: ‘It is Verethraghna, made by Ahura, O Spitama"},{"ref":"43.18e","t":"Zarathushtra!’"},{"ref":"43.19","t":"Verethraghna, made by Ahura, came to him the seventh time,"},{"ref":"43.19a","t":"running in the shape of a raven that... below and... above,"},{"ref":"43.19b","t":"and that is the swiftest of all birds, the lightest of the flying"},{"ref":"43.19c","t":"creatures."},{"ref":"43.20","t":"He alone of living things, - he or none, - overtakes the flight"},{"ref":"43.20a","t":"of an arrow, however well it has been shot. He flies up joyfully"},{"ref":"43.20b","t":"at the first break of dawn, wishing the night to be no more, wishing"},{"ref":"43.20c","t":"the dawn, that has not yet come, to come."},{"ref":"43.21","t":"He grazes the hidden ways of the mountains, he grazes the"},{"ref":"43.21a","t":"tops of the mountains, he grazes the depths of the vales, he grazes"},{"ref":"43.21b","t":"the summits of the trees, listening to the voices of the birds."},{"ref":"43.21c","t":"Thus did Verethraghna come, bearing the good Glory made by Mazda,"},{"ref":"43.21d","t":"the Glory made by Mazda."},{"ref":"43.22","t":"We sacrifice unto Verethraghna, made by Ahura."},{"ref":"43.22a","t":"Zarathushtra asked Ahura Mazda: ‘Ahura Mazda, most beneficent"},{"ref":"43.22b","t":"Spirit, Maker of the material world. thou Holy One! Who is the"},{"ref":"43.22c","t":"best-armed of the heavenly gods?’"},{"ref":"43.22d","t":"Ahura Mazda answered: ‘It is Verethraghna, made by Ahura, O Spitama"},{"ref":"43.22e","t":"Zarathushtra!’"},{"ref":"43.23","t":"Verethraghna, made by Ahura, came to him the eighth time,"},{"ref":"43.23a","t":"running in the shape of a wild, beautiful ram, with horns bent"},{"ref":"43.23b","t":"round."},{"ref":"43.23c","t":"Thus did Verethraghna come, bearing the good Glory made by Mazda,"},{"ref":"43.23d","t":"the Glory made by Mazda...."},{"ref":"43.24","t":"We sacrifice unto Verethraghna, made by Ahura."},{"ref":"43.24a","t":"Zarathushtra asked Ahura Mazda: ‘Ahura Mazda, most beneficent"},{"ref":"43.24b","t":"Spirit, Maker of the material world, thou Holy One! ‘Who is the"},{"ref":"43.24c","t":"best-armed of the heavenly gods?’ Ahura Mazda answered: ‘It is"},{"ref":"43.24d","t":"Verethraghna, made by Ahura, O Spitama Zarathushtra!’"},{"ref":"43.25","t":"Verethraghna, made by Ahura, came to him the ninth time, running"},{"ref":"43.25a","t":"in the shape of a beautiful, fighting buck, with sharp horns."},{"ref":"43.25b","t":"Thus did Verethraghna come, bearing the good Glory made by Mazda,"},{"ref":"43.25c","t":"the Glory made by Mazda...."},{"ref":"43.26","t":"We sacrifice unto Verethraghna, made by Ahura."},{"ref":"43.26a","t":"Zarathushtra asked Ahura Mazda: ‘Ahura Mazda, most beneficent"},{"ref":"43.26b","t":"Spirit, Maker of the material world, thou Holy One! ‘Who is the"},{"ref":"43.26c","t":"best-armed of the heavenly gods?’"},{"ref":"43.26d","t":"Ahura Mazda answered: ‘It is Verethraghna, made by Ahura, O Spitama"},{"ref":"43.26e","t":"Zarathushtra!’"},{"ref":"43.27","t":"Verethraghna, made by Ahura, came to him the tenth time, running"},{"ref":"43.27a","t":"in the shape of a man, bright and beautiful, made by Mazda: he"},{"ref":"43.27b","t":"held a sword with a golden blade, inlaid with all sorts of ornaments."},{"ref":"43.27c","t":"Thus did Verethraghna come, bearing the good Glory made by Mazda,"},{"ref":"43.27d","t":"the Glory made by Mazda."},{"ref":"43.28","t":"We sacrifice unto Verethraghna, made by Ahura, who makes virility,"},{"ref":"43.28a","t":"who makes death, who makes resurrection, who possesses peace,"},{"ref":"43.28b","t":"who has a free way."},{"ref":"43.28c","t":"Unto him did the holy Zarathushtra offer up a sacrifice, [asking]"},{"ref":"43.28d","t":"for victorious thinking, victorious speaking, victorious doing,"},{"ref":"43.28e","t":"victorious addressing, and victorious answering."},{"ref":"43.29","t":"Verethraghna, made by Ahura, gave him the fountains of manliness,"},{"ref":"43.29a","t":"the strength of the arms, the health of the whole body, the sturdiness"},{"ref":"43.29b","t":"of the whole body, and the eye-sight of the Kara fish, that lives"},{"ref":"43.29c","t":"beneath the waters and can measure a rippling of the water, not"},{"ref":"43.29d","t":"thicker than a hair, in the Rangha whose ends lie afar, whose"},{"ref":"43.29e","t":"depth is a thousand times the height of a man."},{"ref":"43.29f","t":"For his brightness and glory, I will offer unto him a sacrifice"},{"ref":"43.29g","t":"worth being heard...."},{"ref":"43.30","t":"We sacrifice unto Verethraghna, made by Ahura, who makes virility,"},{"ref":"43.30a","t":"who makes death, who makes resurrection, who possesses peace,"},{"ref":"43.30b","t":"who has a free way."},{"ref":"43.30c","t":"Unto him did the holy Zarathushtra offer up a sacrifice, [asking]"},{"ref":"43.30d","t":"for victorious thinking, victorious speaking, victorious doing,"},{"ref":"43.30e","t":"victorious addressing, and victorious answering."},{"ref":"43.31","t":"Verethraghna, made by Ahura, gave him the fountains of manliness,"},{"ref":"43.31a","t":"the strength of the arms, the health of the whole body, the sturdiness"},{"ref":"43.31b","t":"of the whole body, and the eye-sight of the male horse, that,"},{"ref":"43.31c","t":"in the dark of the night, in its first half and through the rain,"},{"ref":"43.31d","t":"can perceive a horse’s hair lying on the ground and knows whether"},{"ref":"43.31e","t":"it is from the head or from the tail."},{"ref":"43.31f","t":"For his brightness and glory, I will offer unto him a sacrifice"},{"ref":"43.31g","t":"worth being heard...."},{"ref":"43.32","t":"We sacrifice unto Verethraghna, made by Ahura, who makes virility,"},{"ref":"43.32a","t":"who makes death, who makes resurrection, who possesses peace,"},{"ref":"43.32b","t":"who has a free way."},{"ref":"43.32c","t":"Unto him did the holy Zarathushtra sacrifice, [asking] for victorious"},{"ref":"43.32d","t":"thinking, victorious speaking, victorious doing, victorious addressing,"},{"ref":"43.32e","t":"and victorious answering."},{"ref":"43.33","t":"Verethraghna, made by Ahura, gave him the fountains of virility,"},{"ref":"43.33a","t":"the strength of the arms, the health of the whole body, the sturdiness"},{"ref":"43.33b","t":"of the whole body, and the eye-sight of the vulture with a golden"},{"ref":"43.33c","t":"collar, that, from as far as nine districts, can perceive a piece"},{"ref":"43.33d","t":"of flesh not thicker than the fist, giving just as much light"},{"ref":"43.33e","t":"as a needle gives, as the point of a needle gives."},{"ref":"43.33f","t":"For his brightness and glory, I will offer unto him a sacrifice"},{"ref":"43.33g","t":"worth being heard...."},{"ref":"43.34","t":"We sacrifice unto Verethraghna, made by Ahura."},{"ref":"43.34a","t":"Zarathushtra asked Ahura Mazda: ‘Ahura Mazda, most beneficent"},{"ref":"43.34b","t":"Spirit, Maker of the material world, thou Holy One!"},{"ref":"43.34c","t":"‘If I have a curse thrown upon me, a spell told upon me by the"},{"ref":"43.34d","t":"many men who hate me, what is the remedy for it?’"},{"ref":"43.35","t":"Ahura Mazda answered: ‘Take thou a feather of that bird with"},{"ref":"43.35a","t":"... feathers, the Varenjana, O Spitama Zarathushtra! With that"},{"ref":"43.35b","t":"feather thou shalt rub thy own body, with that feather thou shalt"},{"ref":"43.35c","t":"curse back thy enemies."},{"ref":"43.36","t":"‘If a man holds a bone of that strong bird, or a feather of"},{"ref":"43.36a","t":"that strong bird, no one can smite or turn to flight that fortunate"},{"ref":"43.36b","t":"man. The feather of that bird of birds brings him help; it brings"},{"ref":"43.36c","t":"unto him the homage of men, it maintains in him his glory."},{"ref":"43.37","t":"‘Then the sovereign, the lord of countries, will no longer"},{"ref":"43.37a","t":"kill his hundreds, though he is a killer of men; the.... will"},{"ref":"43.37b","t":"not kill at one stroke; he alone smites and goes forwards."},{"ref":"43.38","t":"‘All tremble before him who holds the feather, they tremble"},{"ref":"43.38a","t":"therefore before me; all my enemies tremble before me and fear"},{"ref":"43.38b","t":"my strength and victorious force and the fierceness established"},{"ref":"43.38c","t":"in my body."},{"ref":"43.39","t":"‘He carries the chariot of the lords; he carries the chariots"},{"ref":"43.39a","t":"of the lordly ones, the chariots of the sovereigns. He carried"},{"ref":"43.39b","t":"the chariot of Kavi Usa; upon his wings runs the male horse, runs"},{"ref":"43.39c","t":"the burden-bearing camel, runs the water of the river."},{"ref":"43.40","t":"‘Him rode the gallant Thraetaona, who smote Azhi Dahaka, the"},{"ref":"43.40a","t":"three-mouthed, the three-headed, the six-eyed, who had a thousand"},{"ref":"43.40b","t":"senses; that most powerful, fiendish Druj, that demon, baleful"},{"ref":"43.40c","t":"to the world, the strongest Druj that Angra Mainyu created against"},{"ref":"43.40d","t":"the material world, to destroy the world of the good principle."},{"ref":"43.40e","t":"‘For his brightness and glory, I will offer unto him a sacrifice"},{"ref":"43.40f","t":"worth being heard...."},{"ref":"43.41","t":"‘We sacrifice to Verethraghna, made by Ahura."},{"ref":"43.41a","t":"‘Verethraghna confounds the glory of this house with its wealth"},{"ref":"43.41b","t":"in cattle. He is like that great bird, the Saena; he is like the"},{"ref":"43.41c","t":"big clouds, full of water, that beat the mountains."},{"ref":"43.41d","t":"‘For his brightness and glory, I will offer unto him a sacrifice"},{"ref":"43.41e","t":"worth being heard...."},{"ref":"43.42","t":"‘We sacrifice to Verethraghna, made by Ahura.’"},{"ref":"43.42a","t":"Zarathushtra asked Ahura Mazda: ‘Ahura Mazda, most beneficent"},{"ref":"43.42b","t":"Spirit, Maker of the material world thou Holy One! ‘Where is it"},{"ref":"43.42c","t":"that we must invoke the name of Verethraghna, made by Ahura? Where"},{"ref":"43.42d","t":"is it that we must praise him? That we must humbly praise him?’"},{"ref":"43.43","t":"Ahura Mazda answered: ‘When armies meet together in full array,"},{"ref":"43.43a","t":"O Spitama Zarathushtra! (asking) which of the two is the party"},{"ref":"43.43b","t":"that conquers and is not crushed, that smites and is not smitten;"},{"ref":"43.44","t":"‘Do thou throw four feathers in the way. Whichever of the"},{"ref":"43.44a","t":"two will first worship the well-shapen Strength, and Verethraghna,"},{"ref":"43.44b","t":"beautiful of form. made by Mazda, on his side will victory stand."},{"ref":"43.45","t":"‘I will bless Strength and Victory, the two keepers, the two"},{"ref":"43.45a","t":"good keepers, the two maintainers; the two who... the two who"},{"ref":"43.45b","t":"... the two who...; the two who forgive, the two who strike off,"},{"ref":"43.45c","t":"the two who forget."},{"ref":"43.46","t":"‘O Zarathushtra! let not that spell be shown to any one, except"},{"ref":"43.46a","t":"by the father to his son, or by the brother to his brother from"},{"ref":"43.46b","t":"the same womb, or by the Athravan to his pupil. These are words"},{"ref":"43.46c","t":"that are awful and powerful, awful and assembly-ruling, awful"},{"ref":"43.46d","t":"and victorious, awful and healing: these are words that save the"},{"ref":"43.46e","t":"head that was lost and chant away the uplifted weapon.’"},{"ref":"43.47","t":"We sacrifice to Verethraghna, made by Ahura: who goes along"},{"ref":"43.47a","t":"the armies arrayed, and goes here and there asking, along with"},{"ref":"43.47b","t":"Mithra and Rashnu: ‘Who is it who lies unto Mithra? Who is it"},{"ref":"43.47c","t":"who thrusts [his oath] against Rashnu? To whom shall I, in my"},{"ref":"43.47d","t":"might, impart illness and death?’"},{"ref":"43.48","t":"Ahura Mazda said: ‘If men sacrifice unto Verethraghna, made"},{"ref":"43.48a","t":"by Ahura, if the due sacrifice and prayer is offered unto him"},{"ref":"43.48b","t":"just as it ought to be performed in the perfection of holiness,"},{"ref":"43.48c","t":"never will a hostile horde enter the Aryan countries, nor any"},{"ref":"43.48d","t":"plague, nor leprosy, nor venomous plants, nor the chariot of a"},{"ref":"43.48e","t":"foe, nor the uplifted spear of a foe."},{"ref":"43.49","t":"Zarathushtra asked: ‘What is then, O Ahura Mazda! the sacrifice"},{"ref":"43.49a","t":"and invocation in honour of Verethraghna, made by Ahura, as it"},{"ref":"43.49b","t":"ought to be performed in the perfection of holiness?’"},{"ref":"43.50","t":"Ahura Mazda answered: ‘Let the Aryan nations bring libations"},{"ref":"43.50a","t":"unto him; let the Aryan nations tie bundles of baresma for him;"},{"ref":"43.50b","t":"let the Aryan nations cook for him a head of cattle, either white,"},{"ref":"43.50c","t":"or black, or of any other colour, but all of one and the same"},{"ref":"43.50d","t":"colour."},{"ref":"43.51","t":"‘Let not a murderer take of those offerings, nor a whore,"},{"ref":"43.51a","t":"nor a.... who does not sing the Gathas, who spreads death in"},{"ref":"43.51b","t":"the world and withstands the law of Mazda, the law of Zarathushtra."},{"ref":"43.52","t":"‘If a murderer take of those offerings, or a whore, or a...."},{"ref":"43.52a","t":"who does not sing the Gathas, then Verethraghna, made by Ahura,"},{"ref":"43.52b","t":"takes back his healing virtues."},{"ref":"43.53","t":"‘Plagues will ever pour upon the Aryan nations; hostile hordes"},{"ref":"43.53a","t":"will ever fall upon the Aryan nations; the Aryans will be smitten"},{"ref":"43.53b","t":"by their fifties and their hundreds, by their hundreds and their"},{"ref":"43.53c","t":"thousands, by their thousands and their tens of thousands, by"},{"ref":"43.53d","t":"their tens of thousands and their myriads of myriads.’"},{"ref":"43.54","t":"There Verethraghna, made by Ahura, proclaimed thus: ‘The Soul"},{"ref":"43.54a","t":"of the Bull, the wise creature, does not receive from man due"},{"ref":"43.54b","t":"sacrifice and prayer; for now the Daevas and the worshippers of"},{"ref":"43.54c","t":"the Daevas make blood flow and spill it like water;"},{"ref":"43.55","t":"‘For now the... Daevas and the worshippers of the Daevas"},{"ref":"43.55a","t":"bring to the fire the plant that is called Haperesi, the wood"},{"ref":"43.55b","t":"that is called Nemetka;"},{"ref":"43.56","t":"‘(Therefore) when the (?Vyambura) Daevas and the worshippers"},{"ref":"43.56a","t":"of the Daevas bow their backs, bend their waists, and arrange"},{"ref":"43.56b","t":"all their limbs, they think they will smite and smite not, they"},{"ref":"43.56c","t":"think they will kill and kill not; and then the (?Vyambura) Daevas"},{"ref":"43.56d","t":"and the worshippers of the Daevas have their minds confounded"},{"ref":"43.56e","t":"and their eyes made giddy.’"},{"ref":"43.56f","t":"For his brightness and glory, I will offer unto him a sacrifice"},{"ref":"43.56g","t":"worth being heard...."},{"ref":"43.57","t":"We sacrifice to Verethraghna, made by Ahura."},{"ref":"43.57a","t":"I offer up Haoma, who saves one’s head; I offer up the victorious"},{"ref":"43.57b","t":"Haoma; I offer him up, the good protector; I offer up Haoma, who"},{"ref":"43.57c","t":"is a protector to my body, as a man who shall drink of him shall"},{"ref":"43.57d","t":"win and prevail over his enemies in battle;"},{"ref":"43.58","t":"That I may smite this army, that I may smite down this army,"},{"ref":"43.58a","t":"that I may cut in pieces this army that is coming behind me."},{"ref":"43.58b","t":"For his brightness and glory, I will offer unto him a sacrifice"},{"ref":"43.58c","t":"worth being heard...."},{"ref":"43.59","t":"We sacrifice to Verethraghna, made by Ahura."},{"ref":"43.59a","t":"The prince and his son and his sons who are chiefs of myriads"},{"ref":"43.59b","t":"offer him up a bright...(?) [saying]: ‘He is strong, and Victorious"},{"ref":"43.59c","t":"is his name; he is victorious, and Strong is his name;’"},{"ref":"43.60","t":"That I may be as constantly victorious as any one of all the"},{"ref":"43.60a","t":"Aryans; that I may smite this army, that I may smite down this"},{"ref":"43.60b","t":"army, that I may cut in pieces this army that is coming behind"},{"ref":"43.60c","t":"me."},{"ref":"43.60d","t":"For his brightness and glory, I will offer unto him a sacrifice"},{"ref":"43.60e","t":"worth being heard...."},{"ref":"43.61","t":"We sacrifice to Verethraghna, made by Ahura."},{"ref":"43.61a","t":"Yatha ahu vairyo: The will of the Lord is the law of holiness...."},{"ref":"43.61b","t":"In the ox is our strength, in the ox is our need; in the ox is"},{"ref":"43.61c","t":"our speech, in the ox is our victory; in the ox is our food, in"},{"ref":"43.61d","t":"the ox is our clothing; in the ox is tillage, that makes food"},{"ref":"43.61e","t":"grow for us."},{"ref":"43.61f","t":"For his brightness and glory, I will offer unto him a sacrifice"},{"ref":"43.61g","t":"worth being heard...."},{"ref":"43.62","t":"We sacrifice to Verethraghna, made by Ahura;"},{"ref":"43.62a","t":"Who breaks the columns asunder, who cuts the columns to pieces,"},{"ref":"43.62b","t":"who wounds the columns, who makes the columns shake; who comes"},{"ref":"43.62c","t":"and breaks the columns asunder, who comes and cuts the columns"},{"ref":"43.62d","t":"to pieces, who comes and wounds the columns, who comes and makes"},{"ref":"43.62e","t":"the columns shake, both of Daevas and men, of the Yatus and Pairikas,"},{"ref":"43.62f","t":"of the oppressors, the blind, and the deaf."},{"ref":"43.62g","t":"For his brightness and glory, I will offer unto him a sacrifice"},{"ref":"43.62h","t":"worth being heard...."},{"ref":"43.63","t":"We sacrifice to Verethraghna, made by Ahura."},{"ref":"43.63a","t":"When Verethraghna, made by Ahura, binds the hands, confounds the"},{"ref":"43.63b","t":"eye-sight, takes the hearing from the ears of the Mithradrujes"},{"ref":"43.63c","t":"marching in columns, allied by cities, they can no longer move"},{"ref":"43.63d","t":"their feet, they can no longer-withstand."},{"ref":"43.63e","t":"For his brightness and glory I will offer unto him a sacrifice"},{"ref":"43.63f","t":"worth being heard...."},{"ref":"43.64","t":"Yatha ahu vairyo: The will of the Lord is the law of holiness...."},{"ref":"43.64a","t":"I bless the sacrifice and prayer, and the strength and vigour"},{"ref":"43.64b","t":"of Verethraghna, made by Mazda; and of the crushing Ascendant."},{"ref":"43.64c","t":"Ashem Vohu: Holiness is the best of all good...."},{"ref":"43.64d","t":"[Give] unto that man brightness and glory,... give him the bright,"},{"ref":"43.64e","t":"all-happy, blissful abode of the holy Ones."},{"sp":"HDR","t":"15. Ram Yasht"},{"ref":"44.0","t":"May Ahura Mazda be rejoiced!...."},{"ref":"44.0a","t":"Ashem Vohu: Holiness is the best of all good...."},{"ref":"44.0b","t":"I confess myself a worshipper of Mazda, a follower of Zarathushtra,"},{"ref":"44.0c","t":"one who hates the Daevas, and obeys the laws of Ahura;"},{"ref":"44.0d","t":"For sacrifice, prayer, propitiation, and glorification unto [Havani]"},{"ref":"44.0e","t":"the holy and master of holiness...."},{"ref":"44.0f","t":"Unto Rama Hvastra, unto Vayu who works highly and is more powerful"},{"ref":"44.0g","t":"to afflict than all other creatures,"},{"ref":"44.0h","t":"Be propitiation from me, for sacrifice, prayer, propitiation and"},{"ref":"44.0i","t":"glorification."},{"ref":"44.0j","t":"Yatha ahu vairyo: The will of the Lord is the law of holiness...."},{"ref":"44.1","t":"I will sacrifice to the Waters and to Him who divides them."},{"ref":"44.1a","t":"I will sacrifice to Peace, whose breath is friendly, and to Weal,"},{"ref":"44.1b","t":"both of them."},{"ref":"44.1c","t":"To this Vayu do we sacrifice, this Vayu do we invoke, for this"},{"ref":"44.1d","t":"house, for the master of this house, and for the man here who"},{"ref":"44.1e","t":"is offering libations and giving gifts. To this excellent God"},{"ref":"44.1f","t":"do we sacrifice, that he may accept our meat and our prayers,"},{"ref":"44.1g","t":"and grant us in return to crush our enemies at one stroke."},{"ref":"44.2","t":"To him did the Maker, Ahura Mazda, offer up a sacrifice in"},{"ref":"44.2a","t":"the Airyana Vaejah, on a golden throne, under golden beams and"},{"ref":"44.2b","t":"a golden canopy, with bundles of baresma and offerings of full-boiling"},{"ref":"44.2c","t":"[milk]."},{"ref":"44.3","t":"He begged of him a boon, saying: ‘Grant me this, O Vayu! who"},{"ref":"44.3a","t":"dost work highly, that I may smite the creation of Angra Mainyu,"},{"ref":"44.3b","t":"and that nobody may smite this creation of the Good Spirit!’"},{"ref":"44.4","t":"Vayu, who works highly, granted him that boon, as the Maker,"},{"ref":"44.4a","t":"Ahura Mazda, did pursue it."},{"ref":"44.5","t":"We sacrifice to the holy Vayu: we sacrifice to Vayu, who works"},{"ref":"44.5a","t":"highly."},{"ref":"44.5b","t":"To this part of thee do we sacrifice, O Vayu! that belongs to"},{"ref":"44.5c","t":"Spenta Mainyu."},{"ref":"44.5d","t":"For his brightness and glory, I will offer unto him a sacrifice"},{"ref":"44.5e","t":"worth being heard, namely, unto the awful Vayu, who works highly."},{"ref":"44.5f","t":"We offer up a sacrifice unto the awful Vayu, who works highly,"},{"ref":"44.5g","t":"with the libations, with the Haoma and meat, with the baresma,"},{"ref":"44.5h","t":"with the wisdom of the tongue, with the holy spells, the words,"},{"ref":"44.5i","t":"the deeds, the libations, and the well-spoken words."},{"ref":"44.5j","t":"Yenhe hatam: All those beings of whom Ahura Mazda...."},{"ref":"44.6","t":"I will sacrifice to the Waters and to Him who divides them...."},{"ref":"44.6a","t":"To this Vayu do we sacrifice, this Vayu do we invoke...."},{"ref":"44.7","t":"To him did Haoshyangha, the Paradhata, offer up a sacrifice"},{"ref":"44.7a","t":"on the Taera of the Hara, bound with iron, on a golden throne,","hvShift6":[[0,0]]},{"ref":"44.7b","t":"under golden beams and a golden canopy, with bundles of baresma"},{"ref":"44.7c","t":"and offerings of full-boiling [milk]."},{"ref":"44.8","t":"He begged of him a boon, saying: ‘Grant me, O Vayu! who dost"},{"ref":"44.8a","t":"work highly, that I may smite two-thirds of the Daevas of Mazana"},{"ref":"44.8b","t":"and of the fiends of Varena.’"},{"ref":"44.9","t":"Vayu, who works highly, granted him that boon, as the Maker,"},{"ref":"44.9a","t":"Ahura Mazda, did pursue it."},{"ref":"44.9b","t":"We sacrifice to the holy Vayu...."},{"ref":"44.9c","t":"For his brightness and glory, I will offer unto him a sacrifice"},{"ref":"44.9d","t":"worth being heard...."},{"ref":"44.10","t":"I will sacrifice to the Waters and to Him who divides them...."},{"ref":"44.10a","t":"To this Vayu do we sacrifice, this Vayu do we invoke...."},{"ref":"44.11","t":"To him did Takhma Urupa, the well-armed, offer up a sacrifice"},{"ref":"44.11a","t":"on a golden throne, under golden beams and a golden canopy, with"},{"ref":"44.11b","t":"bundles of baresma and offerings of full-boiling [milk]."},{"ref":"44.12","t":"He begged of him a boon, saying: ‘Grant me this, O Vayu! who"},{"ref":"44.12a","t":"dost work highly, that I may conquer all Daevas and men, all the"},{"ref":"44.12b","t":"Yatus and Pairikas, and that I may ride Angra Mainyu, turned into"},{"ref":"44.12c","t":"the shape of a horse, all around the earth from one end to the"},{"ref":"44.12d","t":"other, for thirty years.’"},{"ref":"44.13","t":"Vayu, who works highly, granted him that boon, as the Maker,"},{"ref":"44.13a","t":"Ahura Mazda, did pursue it."},{"ref":"44.13b","t":"‘We sacrifice to the holy Vayu...."},{"ref":"44.13c","t":"For his brightness and glory, I will offer unto him a sacrifice"},{"ref":"44.13d","t":"worth being heard...."},{"ref":"44.14","t":"I will sacrifice to the Waters and to Him who divides them....."},{"ref":"44.14a","t":"To this Vayu do we sacrifice, this Vayu do we invoke...."},{"ref":"44.15","t":"Unto him did the bright Yima, the good shepherd, sacrifice"},{"ref":"44.15a","t":"from the height Hukairya, the all-shining and golden, on a golden"},{"ref":"44.15b","t":"throne, under golden beams and a golden canopy, with bundles of"},{"ref":"44.15c","t":"baresma and offerings of full-boiling [milk]."},{"ref":"44.16","t":"He begged of him a boon, saying: ‘Grant me this, O Vayu! who"},{"ref":"44.16a","t":"dost work highly, that I may become the most glorious of the men"},{"ref":"44.16b","t":"born to behold the sun: that I may make in my reign both animals"},{"ref":"44.16c","t":"and men undying, waters and plants undrying, and the food for"},{"ref":"44.16d","t":"eating creatures never-failing.’"},{"ref":"44.16e","t":"In the reign of the valiant Yima there was neither cold wind nor"},{"ref":"44.16f","t":"hot wind, neither old age nor death, nor envy made by the Daevas."},{"ref":"44.17","t":"Vayu, who works highly, granted him that boon, as the Maker,"},{"ref":"44.17a","t":"Ahura Mazda, did pursue it."},{"ref":"44.17b","t":"We sacrifice to the holy Vayu...."},{"ref":"44.17c","t":"For his brightness and glory, I will offer unto him a sacrifice"},{"ref":"44.17d","t":"worth being heard...."},{"ref":"44.18","t":"I will sacrifice to the Waters and to Him who divides them...."},{"ref":"44.18a","t":"To this Vayu do we sacrifice, this Vayu do we invoke...."},{"ref":"44.19","t":"Unto him did the three-mouthed Azhi Dahaka offer up a sacrifice"},{"ref":"44.19a","t":"in his accursed palace of Kvirinta, on a golden throne, under"},{"ref":"44.19b","t":"golden beams and a golden canopy, with bundles of baresma and"},{"ref":"44.19c","t":"offerings of full-boiling [milk]."},{"ref":"44.20","t":"He begged of him a boon, saying: ‘Grant me this, O Vayu! who"},{"ref":"44.20a","t":"dost work highly, that I may make all the seven Karshvares of"},{"ref":"44.20b","t":"the earth empty of men.’"},{"ref":"44.21","t":"In vain did he sacrifice, in vain did he beg, in vain did"},{"ref":"44.21a","t":"he invoke, in vain did he give gifts, in vain did he bring libations;"},{"ref":"44.21b","t":"Vayu did not grant him that boon."},{"ref":"44.21c","t":"For his brightness and glory, I will offer unto him a sacrifice"},{"ref":"44.21d","t":"worth being heard...."},{"ref":"44.22","t":"I will sacrifice to the Waters and to Him who divides them...."},{"ref":"44.22a","t":"To this Vayu do we sacrifice, this Vayu do we invoke...."},{"ref":"44.23","t":"Unto him did Thraetaona, the heir of the valiant Athwya clan,"},{"ref":"44.23a","t":"offer up a sacrifice in the four-cornered Varena, on a golden"},{"ref":"44.23b","t":"throne, under golden beams and a golden canopy, with bundles of"},{"ref":"44.23c","t":"baresma and offerings of full-boiling [milk]."},{"ref":"44.24","t":"He begged of him a boon, saying: ‘Grant me this, O Vayu! who"},{"ref":"44.24a","t":"dost work highly, that I may overcome Azhi Dahaka, the three-mouthed,"},{"ref":"44.24b","t":"the three-headed, the six-eyed, who has a thousand senses, that"},{"ref":"44.24c","t":"most powerful, fiendish Druj, that demon baleful to the world,"},{"ref":"44.24d","t":"the strongest Druj that Angra Mainyu created against the material"},{"ref":"44.24e","t":"world, to destroy the world of the good principle; and that I"},{"ref":"44.24f","t":"may deliver his two wives, Savanghavach and Erena-vach, who are"},{"ref":"44.24g","t":"the fairest of body amongst women, and the most wonderful creatures"},{"ref":"44.24h","t":"in the world.’"},{"ref":"44.25","t":"Vayu, who works highly, granted him that boon, as the Maker,"},{"ref":"44.25a","t":"Ahura Mazda, did pursue it."},{"ref":"44.25b","t":"We sacrifice to the holy Vayu...."},{"ref":"44.25c","t":"For his brightness and glory I will offer unto him a sacrifice"},{"ref":"44.25d","t":"worth being heard...."},{"ref":"44.26","t":"I will sacrifice to the Waters and to Him who divides them...."},{"ref":"44.26a","t":"To this Vayu do we sacrifice, this Vayu do we invoke...."},{"ref":"44.27","t":"To him did the manly-hearted Keresaspa offer up a sacrifice"},{"ref":"44.27a","t":"by the Gudha, a channel of the Rangha, made by Mazda, upon a golden"},{"ref":"44.27b","t":"throne, under golden beams and a golden canopy, with bundles of"},{"ref":"44.27c","t":"baresma and offerings of full-boiling [milk]."},{"ref":"44.28","t":"He begged of him a boon, saying: ‘Grant me this, O Vayu! who"},{"ref":"44.28a","t":"dost work highly, that I may succeed in avenging my brother Urvakhshaya,"},{"ref":"44.28b","t":"that I may smite Hitaspa and yoke him to my chariot.’"},{"ref":"44.28c","t":"The Gandarewa, who lives beneath the waters, is the son of Ahura"},{"ref":"44.28d","t":"in the deep, he is the only master of the deep."},{"ref":"44.29","t":"Vayu, who works highly, granted him that boon, as the Maker,"},{"ref":"44.29a","t":"Ahura Mazda, did pursue it."},{"ref":"44.29b","t":"We sacrifice to the holy Vayu...."},{"ref":"44.29c","t":"For his brightness and glory, I will offer unto him a sacrifice"},{"ref":"44.29d","t":"worth being heard...."},{"ref":"44.30","t":"I will sacrifice to the Waters and to Him who divides them...."},{"ref":"44.30a","t":"To this Vayu do we sacrifice, this Vayu do we invoke...."},{"ref":"44.31","t":"To him did Aurvasara, the lord of the country, offer up a"},{"ref":"44.31a","t":"sacrifice, towards the White Forest, by the White Forest, on the"},{"ref":"44.31b","t":"border of the White Forest, on a golden throne, under golden beams"},{"ref":"44.31c","t":"and a golden canopy, with bundles of baresma and offerings of"},{"ref":"44.31d","t":"full-boiling [milk]."},{"ref":"44.32","t":"He begged of him a boon, saying: ‘Grant me this, O Vayu! who"},{"ref":"44.32a","t":"dost work highly, that the gallant Husravah, he who unites the"},{"ref":"44.32b","t":"Aryan nations into one kingdom, may not smite us; that I may flee"},{"ref":"44.32c","t":"from king Husravah;...."},{"ref":"44.32d","t":"‘That king Husravah and all the Aryans in the forest may smite"},{"ref":"44.32e","t":"him.’"},{"ref":"44.33","t":"Vayu, who works highly, granted him that boon, as the Maker,"},{"ref":"44.33a","t":"Ahura Mazda, did pursue it."},{"ref":"44.33b","t":"We sacrifice to the holy Vayu...."},{"ref":"44.33c","t":"For his brightness and glory, I will offer unto him a sacrifice"},{"ref":"44.33d","t":"Worth being heard...."},{"ref":"44.34","t":"I will sacrifice to the Waters and to Him who divides them...."},{"ref":"44.34a","t":"To this Vayu do we sacrifice, this Vayu do we invoke...."},{"ref":"44.35","t":"To him did Hutaosa, she of the many brothers, of the Naotara"},{"ref":"44.35a","t":"house, offer up a sacrifice, on a golden throne, under golden"},{"ref":"44.35b","t":"beams and a golden canopy, with bundles of baresma and offerings"},{"ref":"44.35c","t":"of boiling milk."},{"ref":"44.36","t":"She begged of him a boon, saying: ‘Grant me this, O Vayu!"},{"ref":"44.36a","t":"who dost work highly, that I may be dear and loved and well-received"},{"ref":"44.36b","t":"in the house of King Vishtaspa.’"},{"ref":"44.37","t":"Vayu, who works highly, granted her that boon, as the Maker,"},{"ref":"44.37a","t":"Ahura Mazda, did pursue it."},{"ref":"44.37b","t":"We sacrifice to the holy Vayu...."},{"ref":"44.37c","t":"For his brightness and glory, I will offer unto him a sacrifice"},{"ref":"44.37d","t":"worth being heard...."},{"ref":"44.38","t":"I will sacrifice to the Waters and to Him who divides them...."},{"ref":"44.38a","t":"To this Vayu do we sacrifice, this Vayu do we invoke...."},{"ref":"44.39","t":"To him did the maids, whom no man had known, offer up a sacrifice"},{"ref":"44.39a","t":"on a golden throne, under golden beams and a golden canopy, with"},{"ref":"44.39b","t":"bundles of baresma and offerings of boiling milk."},{"ref":"44.40","t":"They begged of him a boon, saying: ‘Grant us this, O Vayu!"},{"ref":"44.40a","t":"who dost work highly, that we may find a husband, young and beautiful","hvShift6":[[0,0]]},{"ref":"44.40b","t":"of body, who will treat us well, all life long, and give us offspring;"},{"ref":"44.40c","t":"a wise, learned, ready-tongued husband.’"},{"ref":"44.41","t":"Vayu, who works highly, granted them that boon, as the Maker,"},{"ref":"44.41a","t":"Ahura Mazda, did pursue it."},{"ref":"44.41b","t":"We sacrifice to the holy Vayu...."},{"ref":"44.41c","t":"For his brightness and glory, I will offer unto him a sacrifice"},{"ref":"44.41d","t":"worth being heard...."},{"ref":"44.42","t":"I will sacrifice to the Waters and to Him who divides them...."},{"ref":"44.42a","t":"To this Vayu do we sacrifice, this Vayu do we invoke...."},{"ref":"44.42b","t":"We sacrifice to that Vayu that belongs to the Good Spirit, the"},{"ref":"44.42c","t":"bright and glorious Vayu."},{"ref":"44.43","t":"My name is Vayu, O holy Zarathushtra! My name is Vayu, because"},{"ref":"44.43a","t":"I go through (vyemi) the two worlds, the one which the Good Spirit"},{"ref":"44.43b","t":"has made and the one which the Evil Spirit has made."},{"ref":"44.43c","t":"My name is the Overtaker (apaeta), O holy Zarathushtra! My name"},{"ref":"44.43d","t":"is the Overtaker, because I can overtake the creatures of both"},{"ref":"44.43e","t":"worlds, the one that the Good Spirit has made and the one that"},{"ref":"44.43f","t":"the Evil Spirit has made."},{"ref":"44.44","t":"My name is the All-smiting, O holy Zarathushtra! My name is"},{"ref":"44.44a","t":"the All-smiting, because I can smite the creatures of both worlds,"},{"ref":"44.44b","t":"the one that the Good Spirit has made and the one that the Evil"},{"ref":"44.44c","t":"Spirit has made."},{"ref":"44.44d","t":"My name is the Worker of Good, O holy Zarathushtra! My name is"},{"ref":"44.44e","t":"the Worker of Good, because I work the good of the Maker, Ahura"},{"ref":"44.44f","t":"Mazda and of the Amesha-Spentas."},{"ref":"44.45","t":"My name is He that goes forwards."},{"ref":"44.45a","t":"My name is He that goes backwards."},{"ref":"44.45b","t":"My name is He that bends backwards."},{"ref":"44.45c","t":"My name is He that hurls away."},{"ref":"44.45d","t":"My name is He that hurls down."},{"ref":"44.45e","t":"My name is He that destroys."},{"ref":"44.45f","t":"My name is He that takes away."},{"ref":"44.45g","t":"My name is He that finds out."},{"ref":"44.45h","t":"My name is He that finds out the Glory (Hvareno)."},{"ref":"44.46","t":"My name is the Valiant; my name is the Most Valiant."},{"ref":"44.46a","t":"My name is the Strong; my name is the Strongest."},{"ref":"44.46b","t":"My name is the Firm; my name is the Firmest."},{"ref":"44.46c","t":"My name is the Stout; my name is the Stoutest."},{"ref":"44.46d","t":"My name is He that crosses over easily."},{"ref":"44.46e","t":"My name is He that goes along hurling away."},{"ref":"44.46f","t":"My name is He that crushes at one stroke."},{"ref":"44.46g","t":"My name is (?Ainiva)."},{"ref":"44.46h","t":"My name is He that works against the Daevas."},{"ref":"44.46i","t":"My name is (?Keredharisha)."},{"ref":"44.47","t":"My name is He that prevails over malice; my name is He that"},{"ref":"44.47a","t":"destroys malice."},{"ref":"44.47b","t":"My name is He that unites; my name is He that reunites; my name"},{"ref":"44.47c","t":"is He that separates."},{"ref":"44.47d","t":"My name is the Burning; my name is the Quick of intelligence,"},{"ref":"44.47e","t":"My name is Deliverance; my name is Welfare."},{"ref":"44.47f","t":"My name is the Burrow; my name is He who destroys the burrows;"},{"ref":"44.47g","t":"my name is He who spits upon the burrows."},{"ref":"44.48","t":"My name is Sharpness of spear; my name is He of the sharp"},{"ref":"44.48a","t":"spear."},{"ref":"44.48b","t":"My name is Length of spear; my name is He of the long spear."},{"ref":"44.48c","t":"My name is Piercingness of spear; my name is He of the piercing"},{"ref":"44.48d","t":"spear."},{"ref":"44.48e","t":"My name is the Glorious; my name is the Over-glorious."},{"ref":"44.49","t":"Invoke these names of mine, O holy Zarathushtra! in the midst"},{"ref":"44.49a","t":"of the havocking hordes, in the midst of the columns moving forwards,"},{"ref":"44.49b","t":"in the strife of the conflicting nations."},{"ref":"44.50","t":"Invoke these names of mine, O holy Zarathushtra! when the"},{"ref":"44.50a","t":"all-powerful tyrant of a country falls upon thee, rushes upon"},{"ref":"44.50b","t":"thee, deals wounds hpon thee, or hurls his chariot against thee,"},{"ref":"44.50c","t":"to rob thee of thy wealth, to rob thee of thy health."},{"ref":"44.51","t":"Invoke these names of mine, O holy Zarathushtra! when the"},{"ref":"44.51a","t":"unholy Ashemaogha falls upon thee, rushes upon thee, deals wounds"},{"ref":"44.51b","t":"upon thee, or hurls his chariot against thee, to rob thee of thy"},{"ref":"44.51c","t":"strength, to rob thee of thy health, to rob thee of thy health."},{"ref":"44.52","t":"Invoke these names of mine, O holy Zarathushtra! when a man"},{"ref":"44.52a","t":"stands in bonds, when a man is being thrown into bonds, or when"},{"ref":"44.52b","t":"a man is being dragged in bonds: thus the prisoners flee from"},{"ref":"44.52c","t":"the hands of those who carry them, they flee away out of the prison."},{"ref":"44.53","t":"0 thou Vayu! who strikest fear upon all men and horses, who"},{"ref":"44.53a","t":"in all creatures workest against the Daevas, both into the lowest"},{"ref":"44.53b","t":"places and into those a thousand times deep dost thou enter with"},{"ref":"44.53c","t":"equal power."},{"ref":"44.54","t":"‘With what manner of sacrifice shall I worship thee? With"},{"ref":"44.54a","t":"what manner of sacrifice shall I forward and worship thee? With"},{"ref":"44.54b","t":"what manner of sacrifice will be achieved thy adoration, O great"},{"ref":"44.54c","t":"Vayu! thou who art high-up girded, firm, swift-moving, high-footed,","hvShift6":[[0,0]]},{"ref":"44.54d","t":"wide-breasted, wide-thighed, with untrembling eyes, as powerful"},{"ref":"44.54e","t":"in sovereignty as any absolute sovereign in the world?’"},{"ref":"44.55","t":"‘Take thou a baresma, O holy Zarathushtra! turn it upwards"},{"ref":"44.55a","t":"or downwards, according as it is full day or dawning; upwards"},{"ref":"44.55b","t":"during the day, downwards at the dawn."},{"ref":"44.56","t":"‘If thou makest me worshipped with a sacrifice, then I shall"},{"ref":"44.56a","t":"say unto thee with my own voice things of health, made by Mazda"},{"ref":"44.56b","t":"and full of glory, so that Angra Mainyu may never do harm unto"},{"ref":"44.56c","t":"thee, nor the Yatus, nor those addicted to the works of the Yatu,"},{"ref":"44.56d","t":"whether Daevas or men.’"},{"ref":"44.57","t":"We sacrifice unto thee, O great Vayu! we sacrifice unto thee,"},{"ref":"44.57a","t":"O strong Vayu!"},{"ref":"44.57b","t":"We sacrifice unto Vayu, the greatest of the great; we sacrifice"},{"ref":"44.57c","t":"unto Vayu, the strongest of the strong."},{"ref":"44.57d","t":"We sacrifice unto Vayu, of the golden helm."},{"ref":"44.57e","t":"We sacrifice unto Vayu, of the golden crown."},{"ref":"44.57f","t":"We sacrifice unto Vayu, of the golden necklace."},{"ref":"44.57g","t":"We sacrifice unto Vayu, of the golden chariot."},{"ref":"44.57h","t":"We sacrifice unto Vayu, of the golden wheel."},{"ref":"44.57i","t":"We sacrifice unto Vayu, of the golden weapons."},{"ref":"44.57j","t":"We sacrifice unto Vayu, of the golden garment."},{"ref":"44.57k","t":"We sacrifice unto Vayu, of the golden shoe."},{"ref":"44.57l","t":"We sacrifice unto Vayu, of the golden girdle."},{"ref":"44.57m","t":"We sacrifice unto the holy Vayu; we sacrifice unto Vayu, who works"},{"ref":"44.57n","t":"highly."},{"ref":"44.57o","t":"To this part of thee do we sacrifice, O Vayu! that belongs to"},{"ref":"44.57p","t":"the Good Spirit."},{"ref":"44.57q","t":"For his brightness and glory, I will offer unto him a sacrifice"},{"ref":"44.57r","t":"worth being heard, namely, unto the awful Vayu, who works highly...."},{"ref":"44.58","t":"Yatha ahu vairyo: The will of the Lord is the law of holiness...."},{"ref":"44.58a","t":"I bless the sacrifice and invocation unto, and the strength and"},{"ref":"44.58b","t":"vigour of Rama Hvastra, and Vayu, who works highly, more powerful"},{"ref":"44.58c","t":"to amict than all the other creatures: this part of thee that"},{"ref":"44.58d","t":"belongs to the Good Spirit."},{"ref":"44.58e","t":"Ashem Vohu: Holiness is the best of all good...."},{"ref":"44.58f","t":"[Give] unto that man brightness and glory,... give him the bright,"},{"ref":"44.58g","t":"all-happy, blissful abode of the holy Ones."},{"sp":"HDR","t":"16. Den Yasht"},{"ref":"45.0","t":"May Ahura Mazda be rejoiced!...."},{"ref":"45.0a","t":"Ashem Vohu: Holiness is the best of all good...."},{"ref":"45.0b","t":"I confess myself a worshipper of Mazda, a follower of Zarathushtra,"},{"ref":"45.0c","t":"one who hates the Daevas and obeys the laws of Ahura;"},{"ref":"45.0d","t":"For sacrifice, prayer, propitiation, and glorification unto [Havani],"},{"ref":"45.0e","t":"the holy and master of holiness...."},{"ref":"45.0f","t":"To the most right Chista, made by Mazda and holy, and to the good"},{"ref":"45.0g","t":"Law of the worshippers of Mazda."},{"ref":"45.0h","t":"Be propitiation from me, for sacrifice, prayer, propitiation,"},{"ref":"45.0i","t":"and glorification."},{"ref":"45.0j","t":"Yatha ahu vairyo: The will of the Lord is the law of holiness....."},{"ref":"45.1","t":"We sacrifice to the most right Chista, made by Mazda and holy:"},{"ref":"45.1a","t":"we sacrifice to the good Law of the worshippers of Mazda, the"},{"ref":"45.1b","t":"supplier of good stores, who runs quickly to the goal and frees"},{"ref":"45.1c","t":"one best from dangers, who brings libations, who is holy, clever,"},{"ref":"45.1d","t":"and renowned, speedy to work and quick of work; who goes quickly"},{"ref":"45.1e","t":"and cleanses well; the good Law of the worshippers of Mazda;"},{"ref":"45.2","t":"To whom Zarathushtra did sacrifice, saying: ‘Rise up from"},{"ref":"45.2a","t":"thy seat, come forward from the Abode, thou most right Chista,"},{"ref":"45.2b","t":"made by Mazda and holy. If thou art before me, stay for me; if"},{"ref":"45.2c","t":"thou art behind me, overtake me."},{"ref":"45.3","t":"‘Let everything be as friendly to us as anything can be: may"},{"ref":"45.3a","t":"we go smoothly along the roads, find good pathways in the mountains,"},{"ref":"45.3b","t":"run easily through the forests, and cross happily the rivers!’"},{"ref":"45.4","t":"For her brightness and glory, I will offer unto her a sacrifice"},{"ref":"45.4a","t":"worth being heard, namely, unto the most right Chista, made by"},{"ref":"45.4b","t":"Mazda and holy. I will offer up a sacrifice unto the most right"},{"ref":"45.4c","t":"Chista, made by Mazda and holy, with the libations, with the Haoma"},{"ref":"45.4d","t":"and meat, with the baresma, with the wisdom of the tongue, with"},{"ref":"45.4e","t":"the holy spells, with the words and deeds, with the libations,"},{"ref":"45.4f","t":"with the well spoken words."},{"ref":"45.4g","t":"Yenhe hatam: All those beings of whom Ahura Mazda...."},{"ref":"45.5","t":"We sacrifice to the most right Chista, made by Mazda and holy:"},{"ref":"45.5a","t":"we sacrifice to the good Law of the worshippers of Mazda.... (repeat"},{"ref":"45.5b","t":"verse 1)."},{"ref":"45.6","t":"To whom Zarathushtra did sacrifice for righteousness of thought,"},{"ref":"45.6a","t":"for righteousness of speech, for righteousness of deed, and for"},{"ref":"45.6b","t":"this boon,"},{"ref":"45.7","t":"That the most right Chista, made by Mazda and holy, would"},{"ref":"45.7a","t":"give him the swiftness of the feet, the quick hearing of the ears,"},{"ref":"45.7b","t":"the strength of the arms, the health of the whole body, the sturdiness"},{"ref":"45.7c","t":"of the whole body, and the eye-sight of the Kara fish, that lives"},{"ref":"45.7d","t":"beneath the waters, and can measure a rippling of the waters not"},{"ref":"45.7e","t":"thicker than a hair, in the Rangha, whose ends lie afar and whose"},{"ref":"45.7f","t":"depth is a thousand times the height of a man."},{"ref":"45.7g","t":"For her brightness and glory, I will offer unto her a sacrifice"},{"ref":"45.7h","t":"worth being heard...."},{"ref":"45.8","t":"We sacrifice to the most right Chista, made by Mazda and holy:"},{"ref":"45.8a","t":"we sacrifice to the good Law of the worshippers of Mazda...."},{"ref":"45.9","t":"To whom Zarathushtra did sacrifice for righteousness of thought,"},{"ref":"45.9a","t":"for righteousness of speech, for righteousness of deed, and for"},{"ref":"45.9b","t":"this boon,"},{"ref":"45.10","t":"That the most right Chista, made by Mazda and holy, would"},{"ref":"45.10a","t":"give him the swiftness of the feet, the quick hearing of the ears,"},{"ref":"45.10b","t":"the strength of the arms, the health of the whole body, the sturdiness"},{"ref":"45.10c","t":"of the whole body, and the eye-sight of the male horse, that,"},{"ref":"45.10d","t":"in the dark of the night, through the rain, the snow, the hail,"},{"ref":"45.10e","t":"or the sleet, from as far as nine districts, can perceive a horse’s"},{"ref":"45.10f","t":"hair, mingled with the earth, and knows whether it is from the"},{"ref":"45.10g","t":"head or from the tail."},{"ref":"45.10h","t":"For her brightness and glory, I will offer unto her a sacrifice"},{"ref":"45.10i","t":"worth being heard...."},{"ref":"45.11","t":"We sacrifice to the most right Chista, made by Mazda and holy:"},{"ref":"45.11a","t":"we sacrifice to the good Law of the worshippers of Mazda...."},{"ref":"45.12","t":"To whom Zarathushtra did sacrifice for righteousness of thought,"},{"ref":"45.12a","t":"for righteousness of speech, for righteousness of deed, and for"},{"ref":"45.12b","t":"this boon,"},{"ref":"45.13","t":"That the most right Chista, made by Mazda and holy, would"},{"ref":"45.13a","t":"give him the swiftness of the feet, the quick hearing of the ears,"},{"ref":"45.13b","t":"the strength of the arms, the health of the whole body, the sturdiness"},{"ref":"45.13c","t":"of the whole body, and the eye-sight of the vulture with a golden"},{"ref":"45.13d","t":"collar, that, from as far as nine districts, can perceive a piece"},{"ref":"45.13e","t":"of flesh, not thicker than a fist, giving just as much light as"},{"ref":"45.13f","t":"a needle gives, as the point of a needle gives."},{"ref":"45.13g","t":"For her brightness and glory, I will offer unto her a sacrifice"},{"ref":"45.13h","t":"worth being heard...."},{"ref":"45.14","t":"We sacrifice to the most right Chista, made by Mazda and holy:"},{"ref":"45.14a","t":"we sacrifice to the good Law of the worshippers of Mazda...."},{"ref":"45.15","t":"To whom the holy Hvovi did sacrifice with full knowledge,"},{"ref":"45.15a","t":"wishing that the holy Zarathushtra would give her his good narcotic,"},{"ref":"45.15b","t":"that she might think according to the law, speak according to"},{"ref":"45.15c","t":"the law, and do according to the law."},{"ref":"45.15d","t":"For her brightness and glory, I will offer unto her a sacrifice"},{"ref":"45.15e","t":"worth being heard...."},{"ref":"45.16","t":"We sacrifice to the most right Chista, made by Mazda and holy:"},{"ref":"45.16a","t":"we sacrifice to the good Law of the worshippers of Mazda...."},{"ref":"45.17","t":"To whom the Athravans, sent afar, did sacrifice, wishing a"},{"ref":"45.17a","t":"good memory to preach the law, and wishing strength for their"},{"ref":"45.17b","t":"own body."},{"ref":"45.17c","t":"For her brightness and glory, I will offer unto her a sacrifice"},{"ref":"45.17d","t":"worth being heard...."},{"ref":"45.18","t":"We sacrifice to the most right Chista, made by Mazda and holy:"},{"ref":"45.18a","t":"we sacrifice to the good Law of the worshippers of Mazda...."},{"ref":"45.19","t":"To whom the king of the country, the lord of the country does"},{"ref":"45.19a","t":"sacrifice, wishing peace for his country, wishing strength for"},{"ref":"45.19b","t":"his own body."},{"ref":"45.19c","t":"For her brightness and glory, I will offer unto her a sacrifice"},{"ref":"45.19d","t":"worth being heard...."},{"ref":"45.20","t":"Yatha ahu vairyo: The will of the Lord is the law of holiness...."},{"ref":"45.20a","t":"I bless the sacrifice and prayer, and the strength and vigour"},{"ref":"45.20b","t":"of the most right Chista, made by Mazda and holy, and of the good"},{"ref":"45.20c","t":"Law of the worshippers of Mazda."},{"ref":"45.20d","t":"Ashem Vohu: Holiness is the best of all good...."},{"ref":"45.20e","t":"[Give] unto that man brightness and glory,... give him long,"},{"ref":"45.20f","t":"long life, give him the bright, all-happy, blissful abode of the"},{"ref":"45.20g","t":"holy Ones."},{"sp":"HDR","t":"17. Ard Yasht"},{"ref":"46.1","t":"We sacrifice to Ashi Vanguhi, who is shining, high, tall-formed,"},{"ref":"46.1a","t":"well worthy of sacrifice, with a loud-sounding chariot, strong,"},{"ref":"46.1b","t":"welfare-giving, healing, with fulness of intellect, and powerful;"},{"ref":"46.2","t":"The daughter of Ahura Mazda, the sister of the Amesha-Spentas,"},{"ref":"46.2a","t":"who endows all the Saoshyants with the enlivening intelligence;"},{"ref":"46.2b","t":"she also brings heavenly wisdom at her wish, and comes to help"},{"ref":"46.2c","t":"him who invokes her from near and him who invokes her from afar,"},{"ref":"46.2d","t":"and worships her with offerings of libations."},{"ref":"46.3","t":"For her brightness and glory, I will offer her a sacrifice"},{"ref":"46.3a","t":"worth being heard; I will offer up unto Ashi Vanguhi a good sacrifice"},{"ref":"46.3b","t":"with an offering of libations. We sacrifice unto Ashi Vanguhi"},{"ref":"46.3c","t":"with the libations, with the Haoma and meat, with the baresma,"},{"ref":"46.3d","t":"with the wisdom of the tongue, with the holy spells, with the"},{"ref":"46.3e","t":"words, with the deeds, with the libations, and with the rightly-spoken"},{"ref":"46.3f","t":"words."},{"ref":"46.3g","t":"Yenhe-hatam: All those beings of whom Ahura Mazda...."},{"ref":"46.4","t":"We sacrifice to Ashi Vanguhi, who is shining, high, tall-formed,"},{"ref":"46.4a","t":"well worthy of sacrifice, with a loud-sounding chariot, strong,"},{"ref":"46.4b","t":"welfare-giving, healing, with fulness of intellect, and powerful."},{"ref":"46.5","t":"Homage unto Haoma, and unto the Mathra, and unto the holy"},{"ref":"46.5a","t":"Zarathushtra!"},{"ref":"46.5b","t":"Homage unto Haoma, because all other drinks are attended with"},{"ref":"46.5c","t":"Aeshma, the fiend of the wounding spear: but the drinking of Haoma"},{"ref":"46.5d","t":"is attended with Asha and with Ashi Vanguhi herself."},{"ref":"46.6","t":"Ashi is fair; Ashi is radiant with joy; she is far-piercing"},{"ref":"46.6a","t":"with her rays. Ashi gives good Glory unto those men whom thou"},{"ref":"46.6b","t":"dost follow, O Ashi! Full of perfumes is the house in which the"},{"ref":"46.6c","t":"good, powerful Ashi Vanguhi puts her....(obscure) feet, for long"},{"ref":"46.6d","t":"friendship."},{"ref":"46.7","t":"Those men whom thou dost attend, O Ashi! are kings of kingdoms,"},{"ref":"46.7a","t":"that are rich in horses, with large tributes, with snorting horses,"},{"ref":"46.7b","t":"sounding chariots, flashing swords, rich in aliments and in stores"},{"ref":"46.7c","t":"of food; well-scented where the beds are spread and full of all"},{"ref":"46.7d","t":"the other riches that may be wished for. Happy the man whom thou"},{"ref":"46.7e","t":"dost attend! do thou attend me, thou rich in all sorts of desirable"},{"ref":"46.7f","t":"things and strong!"},{"ref":"46.8","t":"Those men whom thou dost attend, O Ashi Vanguhi! have houses"},{"ref":"46.8a","t":"that stand well laid up, rich in cattle, foremost in Asha, and"},{"ref":"46.8b","t":"long-supported. Happy the man whom thou dost attend! Do thou attend"},{"ref":"46.8c","t":"me, thou rich in all sorts of desirable things and strong!"},{"ref":"46.9","t":"The men whom thou dost attend, O Ashi Vanguhi! have beds that"},{"ref":"46.9a","t":"stand well-spread, well-adorned, well-made, provided with cushions"},{"ref":"46.9b","t":"and with feet inlaid with gold. Happy the man whom thou dost attend!"},{"ref":"46.9c","t":"Do thou attend me, thou rich in all sorts of desirable things"},{"ref":"46.9d","t":"and strong!"},{"ref":"46.10","t":"The men whom thou dost attend, O Ashi Vanguhi! have their"},{"ref":"46.10a","t":"ladies that sit on their beds, waiting for them: they lie on the"},{"ref":"46.10b","t":"cushions, adorning themselves,...(obscure), with square bored"},{"ref":"46.10c","t":"ear-rings and a necklace of gold: ‘When will our lord come? when"},{"ref":"46.10d","t":"shall we enjoy in our bodies the joys of love?’ Happy the man"},{"ref":"46.10e","t":"whom thou dost attend! Do thou attend me, thou rich in all sorts"},{"ref":"46.10f","t":"of desirable things and strong!"},{"ref":"46.11","t":"The men whom thou dost attend, O Ashi Vanguhi! have daughters"},{"ref":"46.11a","t":"that sit....(obscure); thin is their waist, beautiful is their"},{"ref":"46.11b","t":"body, long are their fingers; they are as fair of shape as those"},{"ref":"46.11c","t":"who look on can wish. Happy the man whom thou dost attend! Do"},{"ref":"46.11d","t":"thou attend me, thou rich in all sorts of desirable things and"},{"ref":"46.11e","t":"strong!"},{"ref":"46.12","t":"The men whom thou dost attend, O Ashi Vanguhi! have horses"},{"ref":"46.12a","t":"swift and loud-neighing; they drive the chariot lightly, they"},{"ref":"46.12b","t":"take it to the battle, they bear a gallant praiser (of the gods),"},{"ref":"46.12c","t":"who has many horses, a solid chariot, a sharp spear, a long spear,"},{"ref":"46.12d","t":"and swift arrows, who hits his aim, pursuing after his enemies,"},{"ref":"46.12e","t":"and smiting his foes. Happy the man whom thou dost attend! Do"},{"ref":"46.12f","t":"thou attend me, thou rich in all sorts of desirable things and"},{"ref":"46.12g","t":"strong!"},{"ref":"46.13","t":"The men whom thou dost attend, O Ashi Vanguhi! have large-humped,"},{"ref":"46.13a","t":"burden-bearing camels, flying from the ground or fighting with"},{"ref":"46.13b","t":"holy fieriness. Happy the man whom thou dost attend! Do thou attend"},{"ref":"46.13c","t":"me, thou rich in all sorts of desirable things and strong!"},{"ref":"46.14","t":"The men whom thou dost attend, O Ashi Vanguhi! have hoards"},{"ref":"46.14a","t":"of silver and gold brought together from far distant regions;"},{"ref":"46.14b","t":"and garments of splendid make. Happy the man whom thou dost attend!"},{"ref":"46.14c","t":"Do thou attend me, thou rich in all sorts of desirable things"},{"ref":"46.14d","t":"and strong!"},{"ref":"46.15","t":"Do not turn thy look from me! turn thy mercy towards me, O"},{"ref":"46.15a","t":"great Ashi! thou art well-made and of a noble seed; thou art sovereign"},{"ref":"46.15b","t":"at thy wish; thou art Glory in a bodily form."},{"ref":"46.16","t":"Thy father is Ahura Mazda, the greatest of all gods, the best"},{"ref":"46.16a","t":"of all gods; thy mother is Armaiti Spenta; thy brothers are Sraosha,"},{"ref":"46.16b","t":"a god of Asha, and Rashnu, tall and strong, and Mithra, the lord"},{"ref":"46.16c","t":"of wide pastures, who has ten thousand spies and a thousand ears;"},{"ref":"46.16d","t":"thy sister is the Law of the worshippers of Mazda."},{"ref":"46.17","t":"Praised of the gods, unoffended by the righteous, the great"},{"ref":"46.17a","t":"Ashi Vanguhi stood up on her chariot, thus speaking: ‘Who art"},{"ref":"46.17b","t":"thou who dost invoke me, whose voice is to my ear the sweetest"},{"ref":"46.17c","t":"of all that invoked me most?’"},{"ref":"46.18","t":"And he said aloud: ‘I am Spitama Zarathushtra, who, first"},{"ref":"46.18a","t":"of mortals, recited the praise of the excellent Asha and offered"},{"ref":"46.18b","t":"up sacrifice unto Ahura Mazda and the Amesha-Spentas; in whose"},{"ref":"46.18c","t":"birth and growth the waters and the plants rejoiced; in whose"},{"ref":"46.18d","t":"birth and growth the waters and the plants grew; in whose birth"},{"ref":"46.18e","t":"and growth all the creatures of the good creation cried out, Hail!"},{"ref":"46.19","t":"‘In whose birth and growth Angra Mainyu rushed away from this"},{"ref":"46.19a","t":"wide, round earth, whose ends lie afar, and he, the evil-doing"},{"ref":"46.19b","t":"Angra Mainyu, who is all death, said: “All the gods together"},{"ref":"46.19c","t":"have not been able to smite me down in spite of myself, and Zarathushtra"},{"ref":"46.19d","t":"alone can reach me in spite of myself."},{"ref":"46.20","t":"‘“He smites me with the Ahuna Vairya, as strong a weapon"},{"ref":"46.20a","t":"as a stone big as a house; he burns me with Asha-Vahishta, as"},{"ref":"46.20b","t":"if it were melting brass. He makes it better for me that I should"},{"ref":"46.20c","t":"leave this earth, he, Spitama Zarathushtra, the only one who can"},{"ref":"46.20d","t":"daunt me.”’"},{"ref":"46.21","t":"And the great Ashi Vanguhi exclaimed: ‘Come nearer unto me,"},{"ref":"46.21a","t":"thou pure, holy Spitama! lean against my chariot!’"},{"ref":"46.21b","t":"Spitama Zarathushtra came nearer unto her, he leant against her"},{"ref":"46.21c","t":"chariot."},{"ref":"46.22","t":"And she caressed him with the left arm and the right, with"},{"ref":"46.22a","t":"the right arm and the left, thus speaking: ‘Thou art beautiful,"},{"ref":"46.22b","t":"O Zarathushtra! thou art well-shapen, O Spitama! strong are thy"},{"ref":"46.22c","t":"legs and long are thy arms: Glory is given to thy body and long"},{"ref":"46.22d","t":"cheerfulness to thy soul, as sure as I proclaim it unto thee.’"},{"ref":"46.23","t":"We sacrifice to Ashi Vanguhi, who is shining, high, tall-formed,"},{"ref":"46.23a","t":"well worthy of sacrifice, with a loud-sounding chariot, strong,"},{"ref":"46.23b","t":"welfare-giving, healing, with fulness of intellect and powerful."},{"ref":"46.24","t":"To her did Haoshyangha, the Paradhata, offer up a sacrifice,"},{"ref":"46.24a","t":"upon the enclosure of the Hara, the beautiful height, made by"},{"ref":"46.24b","t":"Mazda."},{"ref":"46.25","t":"He begged of her a boon, saying: ‘Grant me this, O great Ashi"},{"ref":"46.25a","t":"Vanguhi! that I may overcome all the Daevas of Mazana; that I"},{"ref":"46.25b","t":"may never fear and bow through terror before the Daevas, but that"},{"ref":"46.25c","t":"all the Daevas may fear and bow in spite of themselves before"},{"ref":"46.25d","t":"me, that they may fear and flee down to darkness.’"},{"ref":"46.26","t":"The great Ashi Vanguhi ran and came to his side: Haoshyangha,"},{"ref":"46.26a","t":"the Paradhata, obtained that boon."},{"ref":"46.26b","t":"For her brightness and glory, I will offer her a sacrifice...."},{"ref":"46.27","t":"We sacrifice to Ashi Vanguhi, who is shining, high.... and"},{"ref":"46.27a","t":"powerful."},{"ref":"46.28","t":"To her did Yima Khshaeta, the good shepherd, offer up a sacrifice"},{"ref":"46.28a","t":"from the height Hukairya."},{"ref":"46.29","t":"He begged of her a boon, saying: ‘Grant me this, O great Ashi"},{"ref":"46.29a","t":"Vanguhi! that I may bring fatness and flocks down to the world"},{"ref":"46.29b","t":"created by Mazda; that I may bring immortality down to the world"},{"ref":"46.29c","t":"created by Mazda;"},{"ref":"46.30","t":"‘That I may take away both hunger and thirst, from the world"},{"ref":"46.30a","t":"created by Mazda; that I may take away both old age and death,"},{"ref":"46.30b","t":"from the world created by Mazda; that I may take away both hot"},{"ref":"46.30c","t":"wind and cold wind, from the world created by Mazda, for a thousand"},{"ref":"46.30d","t":"years.’"},{"ref":"46.31","t":"Then great Ashi Vanguhi ran and came to his side: Yima Khshaeta,"},{"ref":"46.31a","t":"the good shepherd, obtained that boon."},{"ref":"46.31b","t":"For her brightness and glory, I will offer her a sacrifice...."},{"ref":"46.32","t":"We sacrifice to Ashi Vanguhi, who is shining, high.... and"},{"ref":"46.32a","t":"powerful."},{"ref":"46.33","t":"To her did Thraetaona, the heir of the valiant Athwya clan,"},{"ref":"46.33a","t":"offer up a sacrifice in the four-cornered Varena."},{"ref":"46.34","t":"He begged of her a boon, saying: ‘Grant me this, O great Ashi"},{"ref":"46.34a","t":"Vanguhi! that I may overcome Azhi Dahaka, the three-mouthed, the"},{"ref":"46.34b","t":"three-headed, the six-eyed, who has a thousand senses, that most"},{"ref":"46.34c","t":"powerful, fiendish Druj, that demon, baleful to the world, the"},{"ref":"46.34d","t":"strongest Druj that Angra Mainyu created against the material"},{"ref":"46.34e","t":"world, to destroy the world of the good principle; and that I"},{"ref":"46.34f","t":"may deliver his two wives, Savanghavak and Erenavak, who are the"},{"ref":"46.34g","t":"fairest of body amongst women, and the most wonderful creatures"},{"ref":"46.34h","t":"in the world.’"},{"ref":"46.35","t":"The great Ashi Vanguhi ran and came to his side. Thraetaona,"},{"ref":"46.35a","t":"the heir of the valiant Athwya clan, obtained that boon."},{"ref":"46.35b","t":"For her brightness and glory, I will offer her a sacrifice...."},{"ref":"46.36","t":"We sacrifice to Ashi Vanguhi, who is shining, high.... and"},{"ref":"46.36a","t":"powerful."},{"ref":"46.37","t":"To her did Haoma offer up a sacrifice, Haoma, the enlivening,"},{"ref":"46.37a","t":"the healing, the beautiful, the lordly, with golden eyes, upon"},{"ref":"46.37b","t":"the highest height of the Haraiti Bareza."},{"ref":"46.38","t":"He begged of her a boon, saying: ‘Grant me this, O great Ashi"},{"ref":"46.38a","t":"Vanguhi! that I may bind the Turanian murderer, Franghrasyan,"},{"ref":"46.38b","t":"that I may drag him bound, that I may bring him bound unto king"},{"ref":"46.38c","t":"Husravah, that king Husravah may kill him, behind the Chaechasta"},{"ref":"46.38d","t":"lake, the deep lake of salt waters, to avenge the murder of his"},{"ref":"46.38e","t":"father Syavarshana, a man, and of Aghraeratha, a semi-man.’"},{"ref":"46.39","t":"The great Ashi Vanguhi ran and came to his side. Haoma, the"},{"ref":"46.39a","t":"enlivening, the healing, the beautiful, the lordly, with golden"},{"ref":"46.39b","t":"eyes, obtained that boon."},{"ref":"46.39c","t":"For her brightness and glory, I will offer her a sacrifice...."},{"ref":"46.40","t":"We sacrifice to Ashi Vanguhi, who is shining, high.... and"},{"ref":"46.40a","t":"powerful."},{"ref":"46.41","t":"To her did the gallant Husravah, he who united the Aryan nations"},{"ref":"46.41a","t":"into one kingdom, offer up a sacrifice, behind the Chaechasta"},{"ref":"46.41b","t":"lake, the deep lake of salt waters."},{"ref":"46.42","t":"He begged of her a boon, saying: ‘Grant me this, O great Ashi"},{"ref":"46.42a","t":"Vanguhi! that I may kill the Turanian murderer, Franghrasyan,"},{"ref":"46.42b","t":"behind the Chaechasta lake, the deep lake of salt waters, to avenge"},{"ref":"46.42c","t":"the murder of my father Syavarshana, a man, and of Aghraeratha,"},{"ref":"46.42d","t":"a semi-man.’"},{"ref":"46.43","t":"The great Ashi Vanguhi ran and came to his side. The gallant"},{"ref":"46.43a","t":"Husravah, he who united the Aryan nations into one kingdom, obtained"},{"ref":"46.43b","t":"that boon."},{"ref":"46.43c","t":"For her brightness and glory, I will offer her a sacrifice worth"},{"ref":"46.43d","t":"being heard...."},{"ref":"46.44","t":"We sacrifice to Ashi Vanguhi, who is shining, high.... and"},{"ref":"46.44a","t":"powerful."},{"ref":"46.45","t":"To her did the holy Zarathushtra offer up a sacrifice in the"},{"ref":"46.45a","t":"Airyana Vaejah, by the good river Daitya, with the Haoma and meat,"},{"ref":"46.45b","t":"with the baresma, with the wisdom of the tongue, with the holy"},{"ref":"46.45c","t":"spells, with the speech, with the deeds, with the libations, and"},{"ref":"46.45d","t":"with the rightly-spoken words."},{"ref":"46.46","t":"He begged of her a boon, saying: ‘Grant me this, O great Ashi"},{"ref":"46.46a","t":"Vanguhi! that I may bring the good and noble Hutaosa to think"},{"ref":"46.46b","t":"according to the law, to speak according to the law, to do according"},{"ref":"46.46c","t":"to the law, that she may spread my law and make it known, that"},{"ref":"46.46d","t":"she may bestow beautiful praises upon my deeds.’"},{"ref":"46.47","t":"The great Ashi Vanguhi ran and came to his side: the holy"},{"ref":"46.47a","t":"Zarathushtra obtained that boon."},{"ref":"46.47b","t":"For her brightness, and glory, I will offer her a sacrifice worth"},{"ref":"46.47c","t":"being heard...."},{"ref":"46.48","t":"We sacrifice to Ashi Vanguhi, who is shining, high.... and"},{"ref":"46.48a","t":"powerful."},{"ref":"46.49","t":"To her did the tall Kavi Vishtaspa offer up a sacrifice behind"},{"ref":"46.49a","t":"the waters of the river Daitya."},{"ref":"46.50","t":"He begged of her a boon, saying: ‘Grant me this, O great Ashi"},{"ref":"46.50a","t":"Vanguhi! that I may put to flight Asta-aurvant, the son of Vispo-thaurvo-asti,"},{"ref":"46.50b","t":"the all-afflicting, of the brazen helmet, of the brazen armour,"},{"ref":"46.50c","t":"of the thick neck, behind whom seven hundred camels....; that"},{"ref":"46.50d","t":"I may put to flight the Hvyaona murderer, Arejat-aspa; that I"},{"ref":"46.50e","t":"may put to flight Darshinika, the worshipper of the Daevas;"},{"ref":"46.51","t":"‘And that I may smite Tathravant of the bad law; that I may"},{"ref":"46.51a","t":"smite Spinjaurushka, the worshipper of the Daevas; and that I"},{"ref":"46.51b","t":"may bring unto the good law the nations of the Varedhakas and"},{"ref":"46.51c","t":"of the Hvyaonas; and that I may smite of the Hvyaona nations their"},{"ref":"46.51d","t":"fifties and their hundreds, their hundreds and their thousands,"},{"ref":"46.51e","t":"their thousands and their tens of thousands, their tens of thousands"},{"ref":"46.51f","t":"and their myriads of myriads.’"},{"ref":"46.52","t":"The great Ashi Vanguhi ran and came to his side: the tall"},{"ref":"46.52a","t":"Kavi Vishtaspa obtained that boon."},{"ref":"46.52b","t":"For her brightness and glory, I will offer her a sacrifice worth"},{"ref":"46.52c","t":"being heard...."},{"ref":"46.53","t":"We sacrifice to Ashi Vanguhi, who is shining, high.... and"},{"ref":"46.53a","t":"powerful."},{"ref":"46.54","t":"And the great Ashi Vanguhi said: ‘None of those libations"},{"ref":"46.54a","t":"will be accepted by me, which are sent to me either by a man whose"},{"ref":"46.54b","t":"seed is dried out, or by the courtezan who produces untimely issues,"},{"ref":"46.54c","t":"or by young boys, or by girls who have known no man."},{"ref":"46.54d","t":"‘When the Turanians and the swift-horsed Naotaras, clapping their"},{"ref":"46.54e","t":"hands, ran after me,"},{"ref":"46.55","t":"‘I hid myself under the foot of a bull walking under his burden;"},{"ref":"46.55a","t":"then young boys, and girls who had known no man, discovered me,"},{"ref":"46.55b","t":"even while the Turanians and the swift-horsed Naotaras, clapping"},{"ref":"46.55c","t":"their hands, were running after me."},{"ref":"46.56","t":"‘Even I hid myself under the throat of a ram of hundredfold"},{"ref":"46.56a","t":"energy: then again young boys, and girls who had known no man,"},{"ref":"46.56b","t":"discovered me, even while the Turanians and the swift-horsed Naotaras,"},{"ref":"46.56c","t":"clapping their hands, were running after me.’"},{"ref":"46.57","t":"The first wailing of the great Ashi Vanguhi is her wailing"},{"ref":"46.57a","t":"about the courtezan who destroys her fruit: ‘Stand thou not near"},{"ref":"46.57b","t":"her, sit thou not on her bed!’ - ‘What shall I do? Shall I go"},{"ref":"46.57c","t":"back to the heavens? Shall I sink into the earth?’"},{"ref":"46.58","t":"The second wailing of the great Ashi Vanguhi is her wailing"},{"ref":"46.58a","t":"about the courtezan who brings forth a child conceived of a stranger"},{"ref":"46.58b","t":"and presents it to her husband: ‘What shall I do? Shall I go back"},{"ref":"46.58c","t":"to the heavens? Shall I sink into the earth?’"},{"ref":"46.59","t":"This is the third wailing of the great Ashi Vanguhi: ‘This"},{"ref":"46.59a","t":"is the worst deed that men and tyrants do, namely, when they deprive"},{"ref":"46.59b","t":"maids, that have been barren for a long time, of marrying and"},{"ref":"46.59c","t":"bringing forth children. What shall I do? Shall I go back to the"},{"ref":"46.59d","t":"heavens? Shall I sink into the earth?’"},{"ref":"46.60","t":"Ahura Mazda answered: ‘O fair and wise Ashi, go not back to"},{"ref":"46.60a","t":"the heavens, sink not into the earth! Stay here and walk inside"},{"ref":"46.60b","t":"the fine kingly palace.’"},{"ref":"46.61","t":"I shall worship thee with such a sacrifice, I shall worship"},{"ref":"46.61a","t":"and forward thee with such a sacrifice as Vishtaspa offered unto"},{"ref":"46.61b","t":"thee, behind the river Daitya. The Zaotar lifted up a loud voice,"},{"ref":"46.61c","t":"with baresma before him. With that sort of sacrifice shall I worship"},{"ref":"46.61d","t":"thee? With that sort of sacrifice shall I worship and forward"},{"ref":"46.61e","t":"thee, O fair and wise Ashi?"},{"ref":"46.61f","t":"For her brightness and glory, I will offer her a sacrifice worth"},{"ref":"46.61g","t":"being heard...."},{"ref":"46.62","t":"Yatha ahu vairyo: The will of the Lord is the law of holiness...."},{"ref":"46.62a","t":"I bless the sacrifice and prayer, and the strength and vigour"},{"ref":"46.62b","t":"of Ashi Vanguhi; of the good Chisti; of the good Erethe; of the"},{"ref":"46.62c","t":"good Rasastat; of the Glory and Weal, made by Mazda."},{"ref":"46.62d","t":"Ashem Vohu: Holiness is the best of all good...."},{"ref":"46.62e","t":"[Give] unto that man brightness and glory, give him health of"},{"ref":"46.62f","t":"body,... give him the bright, all-happy, blissful abode of the"},{"ref":"46.62g","t":"holy Ones."},{"sp":"HDR","t":"18. Ashtad Yasht"},{"ref":"47.0","t":"May Ahura Mazda be rejoiced!...."},{"ref":"47.0a","t":"Ashem Vohu: Holiness is the best of all good...."},{"ref":"47.0b","t":"I confess myself a worshipper of Mazda, a follower of Zarathushtra."},{"ref":"47.0c","t":"one who hates the Daevas and obeys the laws of Ahura;"},{"ref":"47.0d","t":"For sacrifice, prayer, propitiation, and glorification unto [Havani],"},{"ref":"47.0e","t":"the holy and master of holiness...."},{"ref":"47.0f","t":"Unto the Glory of the Aryans, made by Mazda,"},{"ref":"47.0g","t":"Be propitiation, with sacrifice, prayer, propitiation, and glorification."},{"ref":"47.0h","t":"Yatha ahu vairyo: The will of the Lord is the law of holiness...."},{"ref":"47.1","t":"Ahura Mazda spake unto Spitama Zarathushtra, saying: ‘I made"},{"ref":"47.1a","t":"the Aryan Glory, rich in food, rich in flocks, rich in wealth,"},{"ref":"47.1b","t":"rich in Glory; provided with full store of intelligence, with"},{"ref":"47.1c","t":"full store of money, to withstand Need, and to withstand enemies."},{"ref":"47.2","t":"‘It destroys Angra Mainyu, who is all death; it destroys Aeshma,"},{"ref":"47.2a","t":"the fiend of the wounding spear; it destroys the yellow Bushyasta;"},{"ref":"47.2b","t":"it destroys the contagion of Aekha; it destroys the fiend of death,"},{"ref":"47.2c","t":"Apaosha; it destroys the non-Aryan nations."},{"ref":"47.3","t":"‘And I made the great Ashi Vanguhi; she comes in, amid the"},{"ref":"47.3a","t":"family; she comes in, inside the fine royal palace."},{"ref":"47.4","t":"‘Let Ashi, with fulness of welfare, follow the man who gladdens"},{"ref":"47.4a","t":"the faithful with his gifts! she comes in, inside his family;"},{"ref":"47.4b","t":"she comes in, inside his fine royal palace."},{"ref":"47.4c","t":"‘With all sorts of flocks, with all victory, with all intelligence,"},{"ref":"47.4d","t":"with all Glory, the great Ashi Vanguhi puts one foot inside his"},{"ref":"47.4e","t":"family; she comes in, inside his fine royal palace."},{"ref":"47.5","t":"‘Horses multiply a thousandfold, flocks multiply a thousandfold;"},{"ref":"47.5a","t":"and so does his virtuous offspring, (as) the bright, glorious"},{"ref":"47.5b","t":"star Tishtrya moves on equally, and so does the strong wind made"},{"ref":"47.5c","t":"by Mazda, and so does the Glory of the Aryas."},{"ref":"47.6","t":"‘And they bring increase on the tops of all mountains, down"},{"ref":"47.6a","t":"the depths of all vales; they bring increase to all the growing"},{"ref":"47.6b","t":"plants, the fair, the golden-hued. And they bring (away) the contagion"},{"ref":"47.6c","t":"of Aekha, they bring (away) the fiend of death, Apaosha."},{"ref":"47.7","t":"‘Hail to the bright and glorious star Tishtrya Hail to the"},{"ref":"47.7a","t":"strong wind, made by Mazda! Hail to the Glory of the Aryas!"},{"ref":"47.7b","t":"‘Yatha ahu vairyo: The will of the Lord is the law of holiness...."},{"ref":"47.7c","t":"‘Ashem Vohu: Holiness is the best of all good...."},{"ref":"47.8","t":"‘We worship the Ahuna Vairya."},{"ref":"47.8a","t":"‘We worship Asha-Vahishta, the fairest Amesha-Spenta."},{"ref":"47.8b","t":"‘We worship the rightly-spoken Words, fiend-smiting and healing."},{"ref":"47.8c","t":"‘We worship the healing, well-spoken Words, the fiend-smiting."},{"ref":"47.8d","t":"‘We worship the Mathra Spenta and the Law of Mazda, and (piety)"},{"ref":"47.8e","t":"that delights in Haoma."},{"ref":"47.8f","t":"‘We worship the Glory of the Aryas."},{"ref":"47.8g","t":"‘Yenhe hatam: All those beings of whom Ahura Mazda...."},{"ref":"47.9","t":"‘Yatha ahu vairyo: The will of the Lord is the law of holiness...."},{"ref":"47.9a","t":"‘I bless the sacrifice and prayer, and the strength and vigour"},{"ref":"47.9b","t":"of the Glory of the Aryas, made by Mazda."},{"ref":"47.9c","t":"‘Ashem Vohu: Holiness is the best of all good...."},{"ref":"47.9d","t":"‘[Give] unto that man brightness and glory,... give him the"},{"ref":"47.9e","t":"bright, all-happy, blissful abode of the holy Ones.’"},{"sp":"HDR","t":"19. Zam Yasht"},{"ref":"48.1","t":"(This Yasht, inscribed to the Genius of the Earth, is devoted to"},{"ref":"48.2","t":"a description of the mountains and the kingly Glory (kavaem Hvareno),"},{"ref":"48.3","t":"which are invoked, together with the Earth, in the corresponding"},{"ref":"48.4","t":"formula of he Sirozah (par. 28) there is no Yasht devoted to the"},{"ref":"48.5","t":"Earth itself.)"},{"ref":"48.6","t":"The mountains are simply enumerated (pars. 1-8). The rest of the"},{"ref":"48.7","t":"Yasht is devoted to the praise of the Hvareno, or, more precisely,"},{"ref":"48.8","t":"to that of those who possessed it, whose powers or feats are described."},{"ref":"48.9","t":"The list begins with Ahura Mazda (par. 10), and closes with Saoshyant"},{"ref":"48.10","t":"(par. 89); that is to say, it begins with the beginning of the"},{"ref":"48.11","t":"world, and closes with its end. It includes the Amesha-Spentas"},{"ref":"48.12","t":"(par. 15), Haoshyangha (par. 26), Takhma Urupa (par. 28), Yima"},{"ref":"48.13","t":"(par. 31), Mithra (par. 35), Thraetaona (par. 36), Keresaspa (par."},{"ref":"48.14","t":"38), the kings of the Kaianyan dynasty (pars. 66-72), Kavi Husravah"},{"ref":"48.15","t":"(par. 74), Zarathushtra (par. 79), Vishtaspa (par. 84). The unsuccessful"},{"ref":"48.16","t":"efforts of Franghrasyan to take possession of it are described"},{"ref":"48.17","t":"at length (pars. 56-64)."},{"ref":"48.18","t":"This Yasht would serve as a short history of the Iranian monarchy,"},{"ref":"48.19","t":"an abridged Shah Namah.)"},{"ref":"48.0","t":"May Ahura Mazda be rejoiced!...."},{"ref":"48.0a","t":"Ashem Vohu: Holiness is the best of all good...."},{"ref":"48.0b","t":"I confess myself a worshipper of Mazda, a follower of Zarathushtra,"},{"ref":"48.0c","t":"one who hates the Daevas and obeys the laws of Ahura;"},{"ref":"48.0d","t":"For sacrifice, prayer, propitiation, and glorification unto [Havani],"},{"ref":"48.0e","t":"the holy and master of holiness...."},{"ref":"48.0f","t":"Unto Mount Ushi-darena, made by Mazda, the seat of holy happiness;"},{"ref":"48.0g","t":"unto the kingly Glory, made by Mazda; unto that Glory that cannot"},{"ref":"48.0h","t":"be forcibly seized, made by Mazda,"},{"ref":"48.0i","t":"Be propitiation, with sacrifice, prayer, propitiation, and glorification."},{"ref":"48.0j","t":"Yatha ahu vairyo: The will of the Lord is the law of holiness...."},{"ref":"48.1a","t":"The first mountain that rose up out of the earth, O Spitama"},{"ref":"48.1aa","t":"Zarathushtra! was the Haraiti Barez. That mountain stretches all"},{"ref":"48.1b","t":"along the shores of the land washed by waters towards the east."},{"ref":"48.1c","t":"The second mountain was Mount Zeredho, outside Mount Manusha:"},{"ref":"48.1d","t":"this mountain too stretches all along the shores of the land washed"},{"ref":"48.1e","t":"by waters towards the east."},{"ref":"48.2a","t":"From there grew up Mount Ushi-dhau, Ushi-darena, Mount Erezifya,"},{"ref":"48.2aa","t":"and Mount Fraorepa. The sixth was Mount Erezura. The seventh was"},{"ref":"48.2b","t":"Mount Bumya. The eighth was Mount Raoidhita. The ninth was Mount"},{"ref":"48.2c","t":"Mazishishvau. The tenth was Mount Antare-danghu. The eleventh"},{"ref":"48.2d","t":"was Mount Erezisha. The twelfth was Mount Vaiti-gaesa."},{"ref":"48.3a","t":"And Mount Adarana, Mount Bayana, Mount Ishkata Upairi-saena,"},{"ref":"48.3aa","t":"with the.... snows; the two Hamankuna mountains, the eight Vasna"},{"ref":"48.3b","t":"mountains, the eight powerful Fravanku, the four Vidhvana summits;"},{"ref":"48.4a","t":"Mount Aezakha, Mount Maenakha, Mount Vakhedrakae, Mount Asaya,"},{"ref":"48.4aa","t":"Mount Tudhaskae, Mount Isavae, Mount Draoshishvau, Mount Sairivau,"},{"ref":"48.4b","t":"Mount Nanghushmau, Mount Kakahyu, Mount Antare-Kangha;"},{"ref":"48.5a","t":"Mount Sichidava, Mount Ahuna, Mount Raemana, Mount Asha-stembana,"},{"ref":"48.5aa","t":"Mount Urunyo-vaidhkae, Mount Asnavant, Mount Ushaoma, Mount Ushta-hvarenah,"},{"ref":"48.5b","t":"Mount Syamaka, Mount Vafrayau, Mount Vourusha;"},{"ref":"48.6a","t":"Amongst which stand Mount Jatara, Mount Adhutavau, Mount Spitavarena,"},{"ref":"48.6aa","t":"Mount Spento-data, Mount Kadrva-aspa, Mount Kaoirisa, Mount Taera,"},{"ref":"48.6b","t":"Mount Bara-srayana, Mount Barana, Mount Frapayau, Mount Udrya,"},{"ref":"48.6c","t":"and Mount Raevant, and all those heights to which men have given"},{"ref":"48.6d","t":"the name of mount,"},{"ref":"48.7a","t":"To the number of two thousand mountains, and two hundred and"},{"ref":"48.7aa","t":"forty and four, O Spitama Zarathushtra!"},{"ref":"48.8a","t":"For its brightness and glory, I will offer it a sacrifice"},{"ref":"48.8aa","t":"worth being heard, namely, unto the awful kingly Glory. Unto the"},{"ref":"48.8b","t":"awful kingly Glory we offer up the libations, the Haoma and meat,"},{"ref":"48.8c","t":"the baresma, the wisdom of the tongue, the holy spells, the speech,"},{"ref":"48.8d","t":"the deeds, the libations, and the rightly-spoken words."},{"ref":"48.8e","t":"Yenhe hatam: All those beings of whom Ahura Mazda...."},{"ref":"48.9a","t":"We sacrifice unto the awful kingly Glory, made by Mazda; most"},{"ref":"48.9aa","t":"conquering, highly working, that possesses health. wisdom, and"},{"ref":"48.9b","t":"happiness, and is more powerful to destroy than all other creatures;"},{"ref":"48.10a","t":"That belongs to Ahura Mazda, as (through it) Ahura Mazda made"},{"ref":"48.10aa","t":"the creatures, many and good, many and fair, many and wonderful,"},{"ref":"48.10b","t":"many and prosperous, many and bright;"},{"ref":"48.11a","t":"So that they may restore the world, which will (thenceforth)"},{"ref":"48.11aa","t":"never grow old and never die, never decaying and never rotting,"},{"ref":"48.11b","t":"ever living and ever increasing, and master of its wish, when"},{"ref":"48.11c","t":"the dead will rise, when life and immortality will come, and the"},{"ref":"48.11d","t":"world will be restored at its wish;"},{"ref":"48.12a","t":"When the creation will grow deathless, - the prosperous creation"},{"ref":"48.12aa","t":"of the Good Spirit, - and the Druj shall perish, though she may"},{"ref":"48.12b","t":"rush on every side to kill the holy beings; she and her hundredfold"},{"ref":"48.12c","t":"brood shall perish, as it is the will of the Lord."},{"ref":"48.12d","t":"For its brightness and glory, I will offer it a sacrifice...."},{"ref":"48.14a","t":"We sacrifice unto the awful kingly Glory, made by Mazda...."},{"ref":"48.15a","t":"That belongs to the Amesha-Spentas, the bright ones, whose"},{"ref":"48.15aa","t":"looks perform their wish, tall, quickly coming to do, strong,"},{"ref":"48.15b","t":"lordly, who are undecaying and holy;"},{"ref":"48.16a","t":"Who are all seven of one thought, who are all seven of one"},{"ref":"48.16aa","t":"speech, who are all seven of one deed; whose thought is the same,"},{"ref":"48.16b","t":"whose speech is the same, whose deed is the same, whose father"},{"ref":"48.16c","t":"and commander is the same, namely, the Maker, Ahura Mazda."},{"ref":"48.17a","t":"Who see one another’s soul thinking of good thoughts, thinking"},{"ref":"48.17aa","t":"of good words, thinking of good deeds, thinking of Garo-nmana,"},{"ref":"48.17b","t":"and whose ways are shining as they go down to the libations;"},{"ref":"48.18a","t":"Who are the makers and governors, the shapers and overseers,"},{"ref":"48.18aa","t":"the keepers and preservers of these creations of Ahura Mazda."},{"ref":"48.19a","t":"It is they who shall restore the world, which will (thenceforth)"},{"ref":"48.19aa","t":"never grow old and never die, never decaying and never rotting,"},{"ref":"48.19b","t":"ever living and ever increasing, and master of its wish, when"},{"ref":"48.19c","t":"the dead will rise, when life and immortality will come, and the"},{"ref":"48.19d","t":"world will be restored at its wish;"},{"ref":"48.20","t":"When the creation will grow deathless, - the prosperous creation"},{"ref":"48.20a","t":"of the Good Spirit, - and the Druj shall perish, though she may"},{"ref":"48.20b","t":"rush on every side to kill the holy beings; she and her hundredfold"},{"ref":"48.20c","t":"brood shall perish, as it is the will of the Lord."},{"ref":"48.20d","t":"For its brightness and glory, I will offer it a sacrifice...."},{"ref":"48.21","t":"We sacrifice unto the awful kingly Glory, made by Mazda...."},{"ref":"48.22","t":"That belongs to the gods in the heavens and to those in the"},{"ref":"48.22a","t":"material world, and to the blessed ones, born or not yet born,"},{"ref":"48.22b","t":"who are to perform the restoration of the world."},{"ref":"48.23","t":"It is they who shall restore the world, which will (thenceforth)"},{"ref":"48.23a","t":"never grow old and never die, never decaying and never rotting,"},{"ref":"48.23b","t":"ever living and ever increasing, and master of its wish, when"},{"ref":"48.23c","t":"the dead will rise, when life and immortality will come, and the"},{"ref":"48.23d","t":"world will be restored at its wish;"},{"ref":"48.24","t":"When the creation will grow deathless, - the prosperous creation"},{"ref":"48.24a","t":"of the Good Spirit, - and the Druj shall perish, though she may"},{"ref":"48.24b","t":"rush on every side to kill the holy beings; she and her hundredfold"},{"ref":"48.24c","t":"brood shall perish, as it is the will of the Lord."},{"ref":"48.24d","t":"For its brightness and glory, I will offer it a sacrifice...."},{"ref":"48.25","t":"We sacrifice unto the awful kingly Glory, made by Mazda...."},{"ref":"48.26","t":"That clave unto Haoshyangha, the Paradhata, for a long time,"},{"ref":"48.26a","t":"when he ruled over the seven Karshvares of the earth, over the"},{"ref":"48.26b","t":"Daevas and men, over the Yatus and the Pairikas, over the oppressors,"},{"ref":"48.26c","t":"the blind, and the deaf; he who smote two-thirds of the Daevas"},{"ref":"48.26d","t":"of Mazana and of the Varenya fiends."},{"ref":"48.26e","t":"For its brightness and glory, I will offer it a sacrifice...."},{"ref":"48.27","t":"We sacrifice unto the awful kingly Glory, made by Mazda...."},{"ref":"48.28","t":"That clave unto Takhma Urupa, the well-armed, while he ruled"},{"ref":"48.28a","t":"over the seven Karshvares of the earth, over the paevas and men,"},{"ref":"48.28b","t":"the Yatus and Pairikas, the oppressors, the blind, and the deaf;"},{"ref":"48.29","t":"When he conquered all Daevas and men, all the Yatus and Pairikas,"},{"ref":"48.29a","t":"and rode Angra Mainyu, turned into the shape of a horse, all around"},{"ref":"48.29b","t":"the earth from one end to the other, for thirty years."},{"ref":"48.29c","t":"For its brightness and glory, I win offer it a sacrifice...."},{"ref":"48.30","t":"We sacrifice unto the awful kingly Glory, made by Mazda...."},{"ref":"48.31","t":"That clave unto the bright Yima, the good shepherd, for a"},{"ref":"48.31a","t":"long time, while he ruled over the seven Karshvares of the earth,"},{"ref":"48.31b","t":"over the Daevas and men, the Yatus and Pairikas, the oppressors,"},{"ref":"48.31c","t":"the blind, and the deaf;"},{"ref":"48.32","t":"He who took from the Daevas both riches and welfare, both"},{"ref":"48.32a","t":"fatness and flocks, both weal and Glory;"},{"ref":"48.32b","t":"In whose reign both aliments were never failing for feeding creatures,"},{"ref":"48.32c","t":"flocks and men were undying, waters and plants were undrying;"},{"ref":"48.33","t":"In whose reign there was neither cold wind nor hot wind, neither"},{"ref":"48.33a","t":"old age nor death, nor envy made by the Daevas, in the times before"},{"ref":"48.33b","t":"his lie, before he began to have delight in words of falsehood"},{"ref":"48.33c","t":"and untruth."},{"ref":"48.34","t":"But when he began to find delight in words of falsehood and"},{"ref":"48.34a","t":"untruth, the Glory was seen to flee away from him in the shape"},{"ref":"48.34b","t":"of a bird. When his Glory had disappeared, then the great Yima"},{"ref":"48.34c","t":"Khshaeta, the good shepherd, trembled and was in sorrow before"},{"ref":"48.34d","t":"his foes; he was confounded, and laid him down on the ground."},{"ref":"48.35","t":"The first time when the Glory departed from the bright Yima,"},{"ref":"48.35a","t":"the Glory went from Yima, the son of Vivanghant, in the shape"},{"ref":"48.35b","t":"of a Varaghna bird."},{"ref":"48.35c","t":"Then Mithra seized that Glory, Mithra, the lord of wide pastures,"},{"ref":"48.35d","t":"whose ear is quick to hear, who has a thousand senses. We sacrifice"},{"ref":"48.35e","t":"unto Mithra, the lord of all countries, whom Ahura Mazda has created"},{"ref":"48.35f","t":"the most glorious of all the gods in the heavens."},{"ref":"48.36","t":"The second time when the Glory departed from the bright Yima,"},{"ref":"48.36a","t":"the Glory went from Yima, the son of Vivanghant, in the shape"},{"ref":"48.36b","t":"of a Varaghna bird."},{"ref":"48.36c","t":"Then Thraetaona seized that Glory, he, the heir of the valiant"},{"ref":"48.36d","t":"Athwya clan, who was the most victorious of all victorious men"},{"ref":"48.36e","t":"next to Zarathushtra;"},{"ref":"48.37","t":"Who smote Azhi Dahaka, the three-mouthed, the three-headed,"},{"ref":"48.37a","t":"the six-eyed, who had a thousand senses, that most powerful, fiendish"},{"ref":"48.37b","t":"Druj, that demon baleful to the world, the strongest Druj that"},{"ref":"48.37c","t":"Angra Mainyu created against the material world, to destroy the"},{"ref":"48.37d","t":"world of the good principle."},{"ref":"48.38","t":"The third time when the Glory departed from the bright Yima,"},{"ref":"48.38a","t":"that Glory went from Yima, the son of Vivanghant, in the shape"},{"ref":"48.38b","t":"of a Varaghna bird."},{"ref":"48.38c","t":"Then the manly-hearted Keresaspa seized that Glory; he who was"},{"ref":"48.38d","t":"the sturdiest of the men of strength, next to Zarathushtra, for"},{"ref":"48.38e","t":"his manly courage."},{"ref":"48.39","t":"For Manly Courage clave unto him. We worship Manly Courage,"},{"ref":"48.39a","t":"firm of foot, unsleeping, quick to rise, and fully awake, that"},{"ref":"48.39b","t":"clave unto Keresaspa;"},{"ref":"48.40","t":"Who killed the snake Srvara, the horse-devouring, men-devouring,"},{"ref":"48.40a","t":"yellow, poisonous snake, over which yellow poison flowed a thumb’s"},{"ref":"48.40b","t":"breadth thick. Upon him Keresaspa was cooking his food in a brass"},{"ref":"48.40c","t":"vessel: at the time of noon, the fiend felt the heat, and stood"},{"ref":"48.40d","t":"upon his feet: he rushed from under the brass vessel and upset"},{"ref":"48.40e","t":"the boiling water: the manly-hearted Keresaspa fell back affrighted;"},{"ref":"48.41","t":"Who killed the golden-heeled Gandarewa, that was rushing with"},{"ref":"48.41a","t":"open jaws, eager to destroy the living world of the good principle;"},{"ref":"48.41b","t":"Who killed the brood of Pathana, all the nine; and the brood of"},{"ref":"48.41c","t":"Nivika, and the brood of Dashtayana;"},{"ref":"48.41d","t":"Who killed the golden-crowned Hitaspa, and Vareshava, the son"},{"ref":"48.41e","t":"of Dana and Pitaona, attended by many Pairikas;"},{"ref":"48.42","t":"Who killed Arezo-shamana, him of the manly courage, who was"},{"ref":"48.42a","t":"strong, well-beloved, hail, energetically rushing, fully awake,"},{"ref":"48.42b","t":"never falling back....;"},{"ref":"48.43","t":"Who killed Snavidhaka, him who killed with his nails, the"},{"ref":"48.43a","t":"stone-handed: thus did he exclaim to all around: ‘I am an infant"},{"ref":"48.43b","t":"still, I am not yet of age: if I ever grow of age, I shall make"},{"ref":"48.43c","t":"the earth a wheel, I shall make the heavens a chariot;"},{"ref":"48.44","t":"‘I shall bring down the Good Spirit from the shining Garo-nmana;"},{"ref":"48.44a","t":"I shall make the Evil Spirit rush up from the dreary Hell. They"},{"ref":"48.44b","t":"will carry my chariot, both the Good Spirit and the Evil One,"},{"ref":"48.44c","t":"unless the manly-hearted Keresaspa kill me.’"},{"ref":"48.44d","t":"The manly-hearted Keresaspa killed him, his life went away, his"},{"ref":"48.44e","t":"spirit vanished."},{"ref":"48.44f","t":"For its brightness and glory, I will offer it a sacrifice...."},{"ref":"48.45","t":"We sacrifice unto the awful Glory, that cannot be forcibly"},{"ref":"48.45a","t":"seized, made by Mazda...."},{"ref":"48.46","t":"For which the Good Spirit and the Evil One did struggle with"},{"ref":"48.46a","t":"one another: for that Glory that cannot be forcibly seized they"},{"ref":"48.46b","t":"flung each of them their darts most swift."},{"ref":"48.46c","t":"The Good Spirit flung a dart, and so did Vohu-Mano, and Asha-Vahishta"},{"ref":"48.46d","t":"and Atar, the son of Ahura Mazda."},{"ref":"48.46e","t":"The Evil Spirit flung a dart, and so did Akem-Mano, and Aeshma"},{"ref":"48.46f","t":"of the wounding spear and Azhi Dahaka and Spityura, he who sawed"},{"ref":"48.46g","t":"Yima in twain."},{"ref":"48.47","t":"Then forward came Atar, the son of Ahura Mazda, thinking thus"},{"ref":"48.47a","t":"in his heart: ‘I want to seize that Glory that cannot be forcibly"},{"ref":"48.47b","t":"seized.’"},{"ref":"48.47c","t":"But Azhi Dahaka, the three-mouthed, he of the evil law, rushed"},{"ref":"48.47d","t":"on his back, thinking of extinguishing it:"},{"ref":"48.48","t":"‘Here give it up to me; O Atar, son of Ahura Mazda: if thou"},{"ref":"48.48a","t":"seizest that Glory that cannot be forcibly seized, I shall rush"},{"ref":"48.48b","t":"upon thee, so that thou mayest never more blaze on the earth made"},{"ref":"48.48c","t":"by Ahura and protect the world of the good principle.’"},{"ref":"48.48d","t":"And Atar took back his hands, as the instinct of life prevailed,"},{"ref":"48.48e","t":"so much had Azhi affrighted him."},{"ref":"48.49","t":"Then Azhi, the three-mouthed, he of the evil law, rushed forward,"},{"ref":"48.49a","t":"thinking thus in his heart: ‘I want to seize that Glory that cannot"},{"ref":"48.49b","t":"be forcibly seized.’"},{"ref":"48.49c","t":"But Atar, the son of Ahura Mazda, advanced behind him, speaking"},{"ref":"48.49d","t":"in these words:"},{"ref":"48.50","t":"‘There give it up to me, thou three-mouthed Azhi Dahaka. If"},{"ref":"48.50a","t":"thou seizest that Glory that cannot be forcibly seized, then I"},{"ref":"48.50b","t":"will enter thy hinder part, I will blaze up in thy jaws, so that"},{"ref":"48.50c","t":"thou mayest never more rush upon the earth made by Mazda and destroy"},{"ref":"48.50d","t":"the world of the good principle.’"},{"ref":"48.50e","t":"Then Azhi took back his hands, as the instinct of life prevailed,"},{"ref":"48.50f","t":"so much had Atar affrighted him."},{"ref":"48.51","t":"That Glory swells up and goes to the sea Vouru-Kasha. The"},{"ref":"48.51a","t":"swift-horsed Son of the Waters seizes it at once: this is the"},{"ref":"48.51b","t":"wish of the Son of the Waters, the swift-horsed: ‘I want to seize"},{"ref":"48.51c","t":"that Glory that cannot be forcibly seized, down to the bottom"},{"ref":"48.51d","t":"of the sea Vouru-Kasha, in the bottom of the deep rivers.’"},{"ref":"48.52","t":"We sacrifice unto the Son of the Waters, the swift-horsed,"},{"ref":"48.52a","t":"the tall and shining lord, the lord of females; the male god,"},{"ref":"48.52b","t":"who helps one at his appeal; who made man, who shaped man, a god"},{"ref":"48.52c","t":"who lives beneath waters, and whose ear is the quickest to hear"},{"ref":"48.52d","t":"when he is worshipped."},{"ref":"48.53","t":"‘And whosoever of you, O men,’ - thus said Ahura Mazda, -"},{"ref":"48.53a","t":"‘O holy Zarathushtra! shall seize that Glory that cannot be forcibly"},{"ref":"48.53b","t":"seized, he has the gifts of an Athravan; whosoever shall long"},{"ref":"48.53c","t":"for the illumination of knowledge, he has the gifts of an Athravan;"},{"ref":"48.53d","t":"whosoever shall long for fulness of knowledge, he has the gifts"},{"ref":"48.53e","t":"of an Athravan;"},{"ref":"48.54","t":"‘And Riches will cleave unto him, giving him full welfare,"},{"ref":"48.54a","t":"holding a shield before him, powerful, rich of cattle and garments;"},{"ref":"48.54b","t":"and Victory will cleave unto him, day after day; and likewise"},{"ref":"48.54c","t":"Strength, that smites more than a year. Attended by that Victory,"},{"ref":"48.54d","t":"he will conquer the havocking hordes; attended by that Victory,"},{"ref":"48.54e","t":"he will conquer all those who hate him.’ For its brightness and"},{"ref":"48.54f","t":"glory, I will offer it a sacrifice...."},{"ref":"48.55","t":"We sacrifice unto the awful Glory, that cannot be forcibly"},{"ref":"48.55a","t":"seized, made by Mazda...."},{"ref":"48.56","t":"Which the Turanian ruffian Frangrasyan tried to seize in the"},{"ref":"48.56a","t":"sea Vouru-Kasha. He stripped himself naked, wishing to seize that"},{"ref":"48.56b","t":"Glory that belongs to the Aryan nations, born and unborn, and"},{"ref":"48.56c","t":"to the holy Zarathushtra. But the Glory escaped, the Glory fled"},{"ref":"48.56d","t":"away, the Glory changed its seat, and an arm of the sea Vouru-Kasha"},{"ref":"48.56e","t":"was produced, namely, that lake that is called Lake Husravah."},{"ref":"48.57","t":"Then the most crafty Turanian Frangrasyan rushed out of the"},{"ref":"48.57a","t":"sea Vouru-Kasha, O Spitama Zarathushtra! thinking evil thoughts:"},{"ref":"48.57b","t":"‘.... I have not been able to conquer the Glory that belongs to"},{"ref":"48.57c","t":"the Aryan nations, born and unborn, and to the holy Zarathushtra."},{"ref":"48.58","t":"‘Then I will defile all corn and liquors, as to greatness,"},{"ref":"48.58a","t":"goodness, and fairness.’"},{"ref":"48.58b","t":"‘Ahura Mazda will come against thee, ever eager to create new"},{"ref":"48.58c","t":"creatures.’"},{"ref":"48.58d","t":"Then the most crafty Turania Frangrasyan rushed down into the"},{"ref":"48.58e","t":"sea Vouru-Kasha, O Spitama Zarathushtra!"},{"ref":"48.59","t":"A second time he stripped himself naked, wishing to seize"},{"ref":"48.59a","t":"that Glory that belongs to the Aryan nations, born and unborn,"},{"ref":"48.59b","t":"and to the holy Zarathushtra. But the Glory escaped, the Glory"},{"ref":"48.59c","t":"fled away, the Glory changed its seat, and an arm of the sea Vouru-Kasha"},{"ref":"48.59d","t":"was produced, namely, that lake that is called Lake Vanghazdau."},{"ref":"48.60","t":"Then the most crafty Turanian Frangrasyan rushed out of the"},{"ref":"48.60a","t":"sea Vouru-Kasha, O Spitama Zarathushtra! thinking evil thoughts:"},{"ref":"48.60b","t":"‘.... I have not been able to conquer the Glory that belongs to"},{"ref":"48.60c","t":"the Aryan nations, born and unborn, and to the holy Zarathushtra."},{"ref":"48.61","t":"‘Then I will defile all corn and liquors, as to greatness,"},{"ref":"48.61a","t":"goodness, and fairness.’"},{"ref":"48.61b","t":"‘Ahura Mazda will come against thee, ever eager to create new"},{"ref":"48.61c","t":"creatures.’"},{"ref":"48.61d","t":"Then the most crafty Turanian Frangrasyan rushed down into the"},{"ref":"48.61e","t":"sea Vouru-Kasha."},{"ref":"48.62","t":"A third time he stripped himself naked, wishing to seize the"},{"ref":"48.62a","t":"Glory that belongs to the Aryan nations, born and unborn, and"},{"ref":"48.62b","t":"to the holy Zarathushtra. But the Glory escaped, the Glory fled"},{"ref":"48.62c","t":"away, the Glory changed its seat, and an arm was produced in the"},{"ref":"48.62d","t":"sea Vouru-Kasha, namely, the water that is called Awzh-danva."},{"ref":"48.63","t":"Then the most crafty Turanian Frangrasyan rushed out of the"},{"ref":"48.63a","t":"sea Vouru-Kasha, O Spitama Zarathushtra! thinking evil thought:"},{"ref":"48.63b","t":"‘.... I have not been able to conquer the Glory that belongs to"},{"ref":"48.63c","t":"the Aryan nations, born and unborn, and to the holy Zarathushtra!’"},{"ref":"48.64","t":"He was not able to seize the Glory that belongs to the Aryan"},{"ref":"48.64a","t":"nations, born and unborn, and to the holy Zarathushtra."},{"ref":"48.64b","t":"For its brightness and glory, I will offer it a sacrifice...."},{"ref":"48.65","t":"We sacrifice unto the awful Glory that cannot be forcibly"},{"ref":"48.65a","t":"seized, made by Mazda...."},{"ref":"48.66","t":"That cleaves unto him who grows up there, where lies Lake"},{"ref":"48.66a","t":"Kasava, along with the Haetumant river; there where stands Mount"},{"ref":"48.66b","t":"Ushidhau, surrounded by waters, that run from the mountain."},{"ref":"48.67","t":"It runs unto him, it flows and swells unto him, bringing good"},{"ref":"48.67a","t":"pastures and fine horses, bringing plenty, full of glory; with"},{"ref":"48.67b","t":"beauty and weal; powerful and friendly, rich of pastures, prolific"},{"ref":"48.67c","t":"and golden. It runs unto him, it flows and swells unto him, bright"},{"ref":"48.67d","t":"and glorious, making the white.... grow, smiting away all plagues."},{"ref":"48.68","t":"And there comes with him a horse’s strength, there comes with"},{"ref":"48.68a","t":"him a camel’s strength, there comes with him a man’s strength,"},{"ref":"48.68b","t":"there comes with him the kingly Glory: and there is in him, O"},{"ref":"48.68c","t":"holy Zarathushtra! so much of kingly Glory as might extinguish"},{"ref":"48.68d","t":"at once all the non-Aryan nations."},{"ref":"48.69","t":"And then (through it) living creatures may keep away hunger"},{"ref":"48.69a","t":"and death, living creatures (may keep away) cold and heat. Such"},{"ref":"48.69b","t":"is the kingly Glory, the keeper of the Aryan nations and of the"},{"ref":"48.69c","t":"five kinds of animals, made to help the faithful and the Law of"},{"ref":"48.69d","t":"the worshippers of Mazda."},{"ref":"48.69e","t":"For its brightness and glory, I will offer it a sacrifice...."},{"ref":"48.70","t":"We sacrifice unto the awful kingly Glory, made by Mazda...."},{"ref":"48.71","t":"That clave unto Kavi Kavata, and unto Kavi Aipivohu, and unto"},{"ref":"48.71a","t":"Kavi Usadha, and unto Kavi Arshan, and unto Kavi Pisina, and unto"},{"ref":"48.71b","t":"Kavi Byarshan, and unto Kavi Syavarshan;"},{"ref":"48.72","t":"So that they were all of them brave, all of them strong, all"},{"ref":"48.72a","t":"of them healthful, all of them wise, all of them happy in their"},{"ref":"48.72b","t":"wishes, all of them powerful kings."},{"ref":"48.72c","t":"For its brightness and glory, I will offer it a sacrifice...."},{"ref":"48.73","t":"We sacrifice unto the awful kingly Glory, made by Mazda...."},{"ref":"48.74","t":"That clave unto Kavi Husravah for the well-shapen Strength,"},{"ref":"48.74a","t":"for the Victory made by Ahura, for the crushing Ascendant; for"},{"ref":"48.74b","t":"the righteousness of the law, for the innocence of the law, for"},{"ref":"48.74c","t":"the unconquerable power of the law; for the extermination of the"},{"ref":"48.74d","t":"enemies at one stroke;"},{"ref":"48.75","t":"And for the vigour of health, for the Glory made by Mazda,"},{"ref":"48.75a","t":"for the health of the body, and for a good, virtuous offspring,"},{"ref":"48.75b","t":"wise, chief in assemblies, bright, and clear-eyed, that frees"},{"ref":"48.75c","t":"[their father] from the pangs [of hell], of good intellect; and"},{"ref":"48.75d","t":"for that part in the blessed world that falls to wisdom and to"},{"ref":"48.75e","t":"those who do not follow impiety;"},{"ref":"48.76","t":"And for a dominion full of splendour, for a long, long life,"},{"ref":"48.76a","t":"and for all boons and remedies; 77. So that king Husravah [had"},{"ref":"48.76b","t":"the lead] all along the long race, and he could not pass through"},{"ref":"48.76c","t":"the forest, he, the murderer, who was fiercely striving against"},{"ref":"48.76d","t":"him on horseback; the lord Kavi Husravah prevailed over all; he"},{"ref":"48.76e","t":"put in bonds Frangrasyan and Keresavazda, to avenge the murder"},{"ref":"48.76f","t":"of his father Syavarshana, a man, and of Aghraeratha, a semi-man."},{"ref":"48.76g","t":"For its brightness and glory, I will offer it a sacrifice...."},{"ref":"48.78","t":"We sacrifice unto the awful kingly Glory, made by Mazda...."},{"ref":"48.79","t":"That clave unto the holy Zarathushtra, so that he thought"},{"ref":"48.79a","t":"according to the Law, spake according to the Law, and did according"},{"ref":"48.79b","t":"to the Law; so that he was the holiest in holiness in all the"},{"ref":"48.79c","t":"living world, the best-ruling in exercising rule, the brightest"},{"ref":"48.79d","t":"in brightness, the most glorious in glory, the most victorious"},{"ref":"48.79e","t":"in victory."},{"ref":"48.80","t":"At his sight the Daevas rushed away; at his sight the (demoniac)"},{"ref":"48.80a","t":"malices were extinguished; at his sight the Jainis drew hack their"},{"ref":"48.80b","t":"ways from the mortals and, lamenting and wailing, laid violent"},{"ref":"48.80c","t":"hands on the Daevas."},{"ref":"48.81","t":"And that one prayer, the Ahuna Vairya, which the holy Zarathushtra"},{"ref":"48.81a","t":"sang and repeated four times, with a song that waxed louder and"},{"ref":"48.81b","t":"louder, drove back all the Daevas beneath the earth, and took"},{"ref":"48.81c","t":"off from them sacrifice and prayer."},{"ref":"48.82","t":"It was it, the Glory of Zarathushtra, that the Turanian ruffian"},{"ref":"48.82a","t":"Frangrasyan tried to seize to rule over all the Karshvares; round"},{"ref":"48.82b","t":"about the seven Karshvares did that ruffian Frangrasyan rush,"},{"ref":"48.82c","t":"trying to seize the Glory of Zarathushtra. But that Glory escaped"},{"ref":"48.82d","t":"to hidden inlets of the sea; and there those two made my will"},{"ref":"48.82e","t":"roll on; they entered my will, as it was my wish, Ahura Mazda’s,"},{"ref":"48.82f","t":"and as it was the wish of the Law of Mazda."},{"ref":"48.82g","t":"For its brightness and glory, I will offer it a sacrifice...."},{"ref":"48.83","t":"We sacrifice unto the awful kingly Glory, made by Mazda...."},{"ref":"48.84","t":"That clave unto king Vistaspa, so that he thought according"},{"ref":"48.84a","t":"to the Law, spake according to the Law, and did according to the"},{"ref":"48.84b","t":"Law; so that he professed that Law, destroying his foes and causing"},{"ref":"48.84c","t":"the Daevas to retire."},{"ref":"48.85","t":"Who, driving the Druj before him, sought wide room for the"},{"ref":"48.85a","t":"holy religion; who, driving the Druj before him, made wide room"},{"ref":"48.85b","t":"for the holy religion; who made himself the arm and support of"},{"ref":"48.85c","t":"this law of Ahura, of this law of Zarathushtra;"},{"ref":"48.86","t":"Who took her, standing bound, from the hands of the Hunus,"},{"ref":"48.86a","t":"and established her to sit in the middle [of the world], high"},{"ref":"48.86b","t":"ruling, never falling back, holy, nourished with plenty of cattle"},{"ref":"48.86c","t":"and pastures, blessed with plenty of cattle and pastures."},{"ref":"48.87","t":"The valiant king Vishtaspa conquered all enemies, Tathravant"},{"ref":"48.87a","t":"of the evil law, Peshana, the worshipper of the Daevas, and the"},{"ref":"48.87b","t":"fiendish wicked Arejat-aspa and the other wicked Hvyaonas."},{"ref":"48.87c","t":"For its brightness and glory, I will offer it a sacrifice...."},{"ref":"48.88","t":"We sacrifice unto the awful kingly Glory, made by Mazda...."},{"ref":"48.89","t":"That will cleave unto the victorious Saoshyant and his helpers,"},{"ref":"48.89a","t":"when he shall restore the world, which will (thenceforth) never"},{"ref":"48.89b","t":"grow old and never die, never decaying and never rotting, ever"},{"ref":"48.89c","t":"living and ever increasing, and master of its wish, when the dead"},{"ref":"48.89d","t":"will rise, when life and immortality will come, and the world"},{"ref":"48.89e","t":"will be restored at its wish;"},{"ref":"48.90","t":"When the creation will grow deathless, - the prosperous creation"},{"ref":"48.90a","t":"of the Good Spirit, - and the Druj shall perish, though she may"},{"ref":"48.90b","t":"rush on every side to kill the holy beings; she and her hundredfold"},{"ref":"48.90c","t":"brood shall perish, as it is the will of the Lord."},{"ref":"48.90d","t":"For its brightness and glory, I will offer it a sacrifice...."},{"ref":"48.91","t":"We sacrifice unto the awful kingly Glory, made by Mazda...."},{"ref":"48.92","t":"When Astvat-ereta shall rise up from Lake Kasava, a friend"},{"ref":"48.92a","t":"of Ahura Mazda, a son of Vispa-taurvairi, knowing the victorious"},{"ref":"48.92b","t":"knowledge."},{"ref":"48.92c","t":"It was that Glory that Thraetaona bore with him when Azhi Dahaka"},{"ref":"48.92d","t":"was killed;"},{"ref":"48.93","t":"That Frangrasyan, the Turanian, bore when Drvau was killed,"},{"ref":"48.93a","t":"when the Bull was killed;"},{"ref":"48.93b","t":"That king Husravah bore when Frangrasyan, the Turanian, was killed;"},{"ref":"48.93c","t":"That king Vishtaspa bore, when he victoriously maintained Holiness"},{"ref":"48.93d","t":"against the host of the fiends and took off the Druj from the"},{"ref":"48.93e","t":"world of the good principle."},{"ref":"48.94","t":"He, with the eye of intelligence, shall look down upon all"},{"ref":"48.94a","t":"the creatures of the Paeshish, her of the evil seed: he shall"},{"ref":"48.94b","t":"look upon the whole living world with the eye of plenty, and his"},{"ref":"48.94c","t":"look shall deliver to immortality the whole of the living creatures."},{"ref":"48.95","t":"And there shall his friends come forward, the friends of Astvat-ereta,"},{"ref":"48.95a","t":"who are fiend-smiting, well-thinking, well-speaking, well-doing,"},{"ref":"48.95b","t":"following the good law, and whose tongues have never uttered a"},{"ref":"48.95c","t":"word of falsehood."},{"ref":"48.95d","t":"Before them shall Aeshma of the wounding spear, who has no Glory,"},{"ref":"48.95e","t":"bow and flee; he shall smite the most wicked Druj, her of the"},{"ref":"48.95f","t":"evil seed, born of darkness."},{"ref":"48.96","t":"Akem-Mano smites, but Vohu-Mano shall smite him; the Word"},{"ref":"48.96a","t":"of falsehood smites, but the Word of truth shall smite it. Haurvatat"},{"ref":"48.96b","t":"and Ameretat shall smite both hunger and thirst: Haurvatat and"},{"ref":"48.96c","t":"Ameretat shall smite the evil hunger and the evil thirst. The"},{"ref":"48.96d","t":"evil-doing Angra Mainyu bows and flees, becoming powerless."},{"ref":"48.96e","t":"For its brightness and glory, I will offer it a sacrifice...."},{"ref":"48.97","t":"Yatha ahu vairya: The will of the Lord is the law of holiness"},{"ref":"48.97a","t":"...."},{"ref":"48.97b","t":"I bless the sacrifice and prayer, and the strength and vigour"},{"ref":"48.97c","t":"of Mount Ushi-darena, made by Mazda, the seat of holy happiness;"},{"ref":"48.97d","t":"of the kingly Glory, made by Mazda; of the Glory that cannot be"},{"ref":"48.97e","t":"forcibly seized, made by Mazda."},{"ref":"48.97f","t":"Ashem Vohu: Holiness is the best of all good...."},{"ref":"48.97g","t":"[Give] unto that man brightness and glory,... give him the bright,"},{"ref":"48.97h","t":"all-happy, blissful abode of the holy Ones."},{"sp":"HDR","t":"20. Hom Yasht"},{"ref":"49.1","t":"(SEE YASNA, CHAPTERS 9-11.)"},{"sp":"HDR","t":"21. Vanand Yasht"},{"ref":"50.0","t":"May Ahura Mazda be rejoiced!...."},{"ref":"50.0a","t":"Ashem Vohu: Holiness is the best of all good...."},{"ref":"50.0b","t":"I confess myself a worshipper of Mazda, a follower of Zarathushtra,"},{"ref":"50.0c","t":"one who hates the Daevas and obeys the laws of Ahura;"},{"ref":"50.0d","t":"For sacrifice, prayer, propitiation, and glorification unto [Havani],"},{"ref":"50.0e","t":"the holy and master of holiness...."},{"ref":"50.0f","t":"Unto the star Vanant, made by Mazda,"},{"ref":"50.0g","t":"Be propitiation, with sacrifice, prayer, propitiation, and glorification."},{"ref":"50.0h","t":"Yatha ahu vairyo: The will of the Lord is the law of holiness...."},{"ref":"50.1","t":"We sacrifice unto the star Vanant, made by Mazda, the holy"},{"ref":"50.1a","t":"and master of holiness."},{"ref":"50.1b","t":"I will sacrifice unto Vanant, strong, invoked by his own name,"},{"ref":"50.1c","t":"healing, in order to withstand the accursed and most foul Khrafstras"},{"ref":"50.1d","t":"of the most abominable Angra Mainyu."},{"ref":"50.2","t":"Yatha ahu vairyo: The will of the Lord is the law of holiness...."},{"ref":"50.2a","t":"I bless the sacrifice and prayer, and the strength and vigour"},{"ref":"50.2b","t":"of the star Vanant, made by Mazda."},{"ref":"50.2c","t":"Ashem Vohu: Holiness is the best of all good...."},{"ref":"50.2d","t":"[Give] unto that man brightness and glory,... give him the bright,"},{"ref":"50.2e","t":"all-happy, blissful abode of the holy Ones."},{"sp":"HDR","t":"Siroza 1"},{"ref":"52.1","t":"OHRMAZD."},{"ref":"52.1a","t":"To Ahura Mazda, bright and glorious, and to the Amesha-Spentas."},{"ref":"52.2","t":"Vohuman."},{"ref":"52.2a","t":"To Vohu-Mano; to Peace, whose breath is friendly, and who is more"},{"ref":"52.2b","t":"powerful to destroy than all other creatures; to the heavenly"},{"ref":"52.2c","t":"Wisdom, made by Mazda; and to the Wisdom acquired through the"},{"ref":"52.2d","t":"ear, made by Mazda."},{"ref":"52.3","t":"Ardwahisht."},{"ref":"52.3a","t":"To Asha-Vahishta, the fairest; to the much-desired Airyaman, made"},{"ref":"52.3b","t":"by Mazda; to the instrument made by Mazda; and to the good Saoka,"},{"ref":"52.3c","t":"with eyes of love, made by Mazda and holy."},{"ref":"52.4","t":"Shahrewar."},{"ref":"52.4a","t":"To Khshathra-vairya; to the metals; to Mercy and Charity."},{"ref":"52.5","t":"Spandarmad."},{"ref":"52.5a","t":"To the good Spenta-Armaiti, and to the good Rata, with eyes of"},{"ref":"52.5b","t":"love, made by Mazda and holy."},{"ref":"52.6","t":"Hordad."},{"ref":"52.6a","t":"To Haurvatat, the master; to the prosperity of the seasons and"},{"ref":"52.6b","t":"to the years, the masters of holiness."},{"ref":"52.7","t":"Amurdad."},{"ref":"52.7a","t":"To Ameretat, the master; to fatness and flocks; to the plenty"},{"ref":"52.7b","t":"of corn; and to the powerful Gaokerena, made by Mazda."},{"ref":"52.7c","t":"(At the gah Hawan):"},{"ref":"52.7d","t":"to Mithra, the lord of wide pastures and to Rama Hvastra."},{"ref":"52.7e","t":"(At the gah Rapithwin):"},{"ref":"52.7f","t":"to Asha-Vahishta and to Atar, the son of Ahura Mazda."},{"ref":"52.7g","t":"(At the gah Uzerin):"},{"ref":"52.7h","t":"to Apam Napat, the tall lord, and to the water made by Mazda."},{"ref":"52.7i","t":"(At the gah Aiwisruthrem):"},{"ref":"52.7j","t":"to the Fravashis of the faithful, and to the females that"},{"ref":"52.7k","t":"bring forth flocks of males; to the prosperity of the seasons;"},{"ref":"52.7l","t":"to the well-shapen and tall-formed Strength, to Verethraghna,"},{"ref":"52.7m","t":"made by Ahura, and to the crushing Ascendant."},{"ref":"52.7n","t":"(At the gah Ushahin):"},{"ref":"52.7o","t":"to the holy, devout, fiend-smiting Sraosha, who makes the"},{"ref":"52.7p","t":"world grow; to Rashnu Razishta, and to Arshtat, who makes the"},{"ref":"52.7q","t":"world grow, who makes the world increase."},{"ref":"52.8","t":"Dai-pa-Adar."},{"ref":"52.8a","t":"To the Maker Ahura Mazda, bright and glorious, and to the Amesha-Spentas."},{"ref":"52.9","t":"Adar."},{"ref":"52.9a","t":"To Atar, the son of Ahura Mazda; to the Glory and to the Weal,"},{"ref":"52.9b","t":"made by Mazda; to the Glory of the Aryas, made by Mazda; to the"},{"ref":"52.9c","t":"awful Glory of the Kavis, made by Mazda."},{"ref":"52.9d","t":"To Atar, the son of Ahura Mazda; to king Husravah; to the lake"},{"ref":"52.9e","t":"of Husravah; to Mount Asnavant, made by Mazda; to Lake Chaechasta,"},{"ref":"52.9f","t":"made by Mazda; to the Glory of the Kavis, made by Mazda."},{"ref":"52.9g","t":"To Atar, the son of Ahura Mazda; to Mount Raevant, made by Mazda;"},{"ref":"52.9h","t":"to the Glory of the Kavis, made by Mazda."},{"ref":"52.9i","t":"To Atar, the beneficent, the warrior; the God who is a full source"},{"ref":"52.9j","t":"of Glory, the God who is a full source of healing."},{"ref":"52.9k","t":"To Atar, the son of Ahura Mazda, with all Atars; to the God Nairyo-Sangha,"},{"ref":"52.9l","t":"who dwells in the navel of kings."},{"ref":"52.10","t":"Aban."},{"ref":"52.10a","t":"To the good Waters, made by Mazda; to the holy water-spring Ardvi"},{"ref":"52.10b","t":"Anahita; to all waters made by Mazda; to all plants made by Mazda."},{"ref":"52.11","t":"Khwarshed."},{"ref":"52.11a","t":"To the undying, shining, swift-horsed Sun."},{"ref":"52.12","t":"Mah."},{"ref":"52.12a","t":"To the Moon that keeps in it the seed of the Bull; to the only-created"},{"ref":"52.12b","t":"bull; to the Bull of many species."},{"ref":"52.13","t":"Tishtar."},{"ref":"52.13a","t":"To Tistrya, the bright and glorious star; to the powerful Satavaesa,"},{"ref":"52.13b","t":"made by Mazda, who pushes waters forward; to the stars, made by"},{"ref":"52.13c","t":"Mazda, that have in them the seed of the waters, the seed of the"},{"ref":"52.13d","t":"earth, the seed of the plants; to the star Vanant, made by Mazda:"},{"ref":"52.13e","t":"to those stars that are seven in number, the Haptoiringas, made"},{"ref":"52.13f","t":"by Mazda, glorious and healing."},{"ref":"52.14","t":"Goshorun."},{"ref":"52.14a","t":"To the body of the Cow, to the soul of the Cow, to the powerful"},{"ref":"52.14b","t":"Drvaspa, made by Mazda and holy."},{"ref":"52.15","t":"Dai-pa-Mihr."},{"ref":"52.15a","t":"To the Maker Ahura Mazda, bright and glorious, and to the Amesha-Spentas."},{"ref":"52.16","t":"Mihr."},{"ref":"52.16a","t":"To Mithra, the lord of wide pastures, who has a thousand ears"},{"ref":"52.16b","t":"and ten thousand eyes, a God invoked by his own name; to Rama"},{"ref":"52.16c","t":"Hvastra."},{"ref":"52.17","t":"Srosh."},{"ref":"52.17a","t":"To the holy, strong Sraosha, who is the incarnate Word, a mighty-speared"},{"ref":"52.17b","t":"and lordly God."},{"ref":"52.18","t":"Rashn."},{"ref":"52.18a","t":"To Rashnu Razishta; to Arstat, who makes the world grow, who makes"},{"ref":"52.18b","t":"the world increase; to the true-spoken speech, that makes the"},{"ref":"52.18c","t":"world grow."},{"ref":"52.19","t":"Frawardin."},{"ref":"52.19a","t":"To the awful, overpowering Fravashis of the holy ones."},{"ref":"52.20","t":"Warharan."},{"ref":"52.20a","t":"To the well-shapen, tall-formed Strength; to Verethraghna, made"},{"ref":"52.20b","t":"by Ahura; to the crushing Ascendant."},{"ref":"52.21","t":"Ram."},{"ref":"52.21a","t":"To Rama Hvastra; to Vayu, who works highly and is more powerful"},{"ref":"52.21b","t":"to destroy than all other creatures: to that part of thee, O Vayu,"},{"ref":"52.21c","t":"that belongs to Spenta-Mainyu; to the sovereign Sky, to the Boundless"},{"ref":"52.21d","t":"Time, to the sovereign Time of the long Period."},{"ref":"52.22","t":"Wad."},{"ref":"52.22a","t":"To the bounteous Wind, that blows below, above, before, and behind;"},{"ref":"52.22b","t":"to the manly Courage."},{"ref":"52.23","t":"Dai-pa-Den."},{"ref":"52.23a","t":"To the Maker, Ahura Mazda, bright and glorious; to the Amesha-Spentas."},{"ref":"52.24","t":"Den."},{"ref":"52.24a","t":"To the most right Chista, made by Mazda and holy; to the good"},{"ref":"52.24b","t":"Law of the worshippers of Mazda."},{"ref":"52.25","t":"Ard."},{"ref":"52.25a","t":"To Ashi Vanguhi; to the good Chisti; to the good Erethe; to the"},{"ref":"52.25b","t":"good Rasastat; to the Weal and Glory, made by Mazda; to Parendi,"},{"ref":"52.25c","t":"of the light chariot; to the Glory of the Aryas made by Mazda;"},{"ref":"52.25d","t":"to the kingly Glory made by Mazda; to that Glory that cannot be"},{"ref":"52.25e","t":"forcibly seized, made by Mazda; to the Glory of Zarathustra, made"},{"ref":"52.25f","t":"by Mazda."},{"ref":"52.26","t":"Ashtad."},{"ref":"52.26a","t":"To Arstat, who makes the world grow; to Mount Ushi-darena, made"},{"ref":"52.26b","t":"by Mazda, the seat of holy happiness."},{"ref":"52.27","t":"Asman."},{"ref":"52.27a","t":"To the high, powerful Heavens; to the bright all-happy, blissful"},{"ref":"52.27b","t":"abode of the holy ones."},{"ref":"52.28","t":"Zam."},{"ref":"52.28a","t":"To the bounteous Earth; to these places, to these fields; to Mount"},{"ref":"52.28b","t":"Ushi-darena, made by Mazda, the seat of holy happiness; to all"},{"ref":"52.28c","t":"the mountains made by Mazda, that are seats of holy happiness,"},{"ref":"52.28d","t":"of full happiness; to the kingly Glory made by Mazda; to that"},{"ref":"52.28e","t":"Glory that cannot be forcibly seized, made by Mazda."},{"ref":"52.29","t":"Mahraspand."},{"ref":"52.29a","t":"To the holy, righteousness-performing Mathra Spenta; to the Law"},{"ref":"52.29b","t":"opposed to the Daevas, the Law of Zarathushtra; to the long-traditional"},{"ref":"52.29c","t":"teaching; to the good Law of the worshippers of Mazda; to the"},{"ref":"52.29d","t":"Devotion to the Mathra Spenta; to the understanding that keeps"},{"ref":"52.29e","t":"the Law of the worshippers of Mazda; to the knowledge of the Mathra"},{"ref":"52.29f","t":"Spenta; to the heavenly Wisdom made by Mazda; to the Wisdom acquired"},{"ref":"52.29g","t":"through the ear and made by Mazda."},{"ref":"52.30","t":"Anagran."},{"ref":"52.30a","t":"To the eternal and sovereign luminous space; to the bright Garo-nmana;"},{"ref":"52.30b","t":"to the sovereign place of eternal Weal; to the Chinvat-bridge,"},{"ref":"52.30c","t":"made by Mazda; to the tall lord Apam Napat and to the water made"},{"ref":"52.30d","t":"by Mazda; to Haoma, of holy birth; to the pious and good Blessing;"},{"ref":"52.30e","t":"to the awful cursing thought of the wise; to all the holy Gods"},{"ref":"52.30f","t":"of the heavenly world and of the material one; to the awful, overpowering"},{"ref":"52.30g","t":"Fravashis of the faithful, to the Fravashis of the first men of"},{"ref":"52.30h","t":"the law, to the Fravashis of the next-of-kin; to every God invoked"},{"ref":"52.30i","t":"by his own name."},{"sp":"HDR","t":"Siroza 2"},{"ref":"53.1","t":"OHRMAZD."},{"ref":"53.1a","t":"We sacrifice unto the bright and glorious Ahura Mazda; we"},{"ref":"53.1b","t":"sacrifice unto the Amesha-Spentas, the all-ruling, the"},{"ref":"53.1c","t":"all-beneficent."},{"ref":"53.2","t":"Vohuman."},{"ref":"53.2a","t":"We sacrifice unto Vohu-Mano, the Amesha-Spenta; we sacrifice"},{"ref":"53.2b","t":"unto Peace, whose breath is friendly, and who is more powerful to"},{"ref":"53.2c","t":"destroy than all other creatures. We sacrifice unto the heavenly"},{"ref":"53.2d","t":"Wisdom, made by Mazda; we sacrifice unto the Wisdom acquired"},{"ref":"53.2e","t":"through the ear, made by Mazda."},{"ref":"53.3","t":"Ardwahisht."},{"ref":"53.3a","t":"We sacrifice unto Asha-Vahista, the fairest, the"},{"ref":"53.3b","t":"Amesha-Spenta; we sacrifice unto the much-desired Airyaman; we"},{"ref":"53.3c","t":"sacrifice unto the instrument made by Mazda; we sacrifice unto"},{"ref":"53.3d","t":"the good Saoka, with eyes of love, made by Mazda and holy."},{"ref":"53.4","t":"Shahrewar."},{"ref":"53.4a","t":"We sacrifice unto Khshathra-Vairya, the Amesha-Spenta; we"},{"ref":"53.4b","t":"sacrifice unto the metals; we sacrifice unto Mercy and Charity."},{"ref":"53.5","t":"Spandarmad."},{"ref":"53.5a","t":"We sacrifice unto the good Spenta Armaiti; we sacrifice unto"},{"ref":"53.5b","t":"the good Rata, with eyes of love, made by Mazda and holy."},{"ref":"53.6","t":"Hordad."},{"ref":"53.6a","t":"We sacrifice unto Haurvatat, the Amesha-Spenta; we sacrifice"},{"ref":"53.6b","t":"unto the prosperity of the seasons. We sacrifice unto the years,"},{"ref":"53.6c","t":"the holy and masters of holiness."},{"ref":"53.7","t":"Amurdad."},{"ref":"53.7a","t":"We sacrifice unto Ameretat, the Amesha-Spenta; we sacrifice"},{"ref":"53.7b","t":"unto fatness and flocks; we sacrifice unto the plenty of corn; we"},{"ref":"53.7c","t":"sacrifice unto the powerful Gaokerena, made by Mazda."},{"ref":"53.7d","t":"(At the gah Hawan): We sacrifice unto Mithra, the lord of"},{"ref":"53.7e","t":"wide pastures; we sacrifice unto Rama Hvastra."},{"ref":"53.7f","t":"(At the gah Rapithwin): We sacrifice unto Asha-Vahista and"},{"ref":"53.7g","t":"unto Atar, the son of Ahura Mazda."},{"ref":"53.7h","t":"(At the gah Uzerin): We sacrifice unto Apam Napat, the"},{"ref":"53.7i","t":"swift-horsed, the tall and shining lord, the lord of the females;"},{"ref":"53.7j","t":"we sacrifice unto the water made by Mazda and holy."},{"ref":"53.7k","t":"(At the gah Aiwisruthrem): We sacrifice unto the good,"},{"ref":"53.7l","t":"powerful, beneficent Fravashis of the holy ones; we sacrifice"},{"ref":"53.7m","t":"unto the females that bring forth flocks of males; we sacrifice"},{"ref":"53.7n","t":"unto the thrift of the seasons; we sacrifice unto the well-shapen"},{"ref":"53.7o","t":"and tall-formed Strength; we sacrifice unto Verethraghna, made by"},{"ref":"53.7p","t":"Mazda; we sacrifice unto the crushing Ascendant."},{"ref":"53.7q","t":"(At the gah Ushahin): We sacrifice unto the holy,"},{"ref":"53.7r","t":"tall-formed, fiend-smiting Sraosha, who makes the world grow, the"},{"ref":"53.7s","t":"holy and master of holiness; we sacrifice unto Rashnu Razishta;"},{"ref":"53.7t","t":"we sacrifice unto Arstat, who makes the world grow, who makes the"},{"ref":"53.7u","t":"world increase."},{"ref":"53.8","t":"Dai-pa-Adar."},{"ref":"53.8a","t":"We sacrifice unto the Maker Ahura Mazda, the bright and"},{"ref":"53.8b","t":"glorious; we sacrifice unto the Amesha-Spentas, the all-ruling,"},{"ref":"53.8c","t":"the all-beneficent."},{"ref":"53.9","t":"Adar."},{"ref":"53.9a","t":"We sacrifice unto Atar, the son of Ahura Mazda; we sacrifice"},{"ref":"53.9b","t":"unto the Glory, made by Mazda; we sacrifice unto the Weal, made"},{"ref":"53.9c","t":"by Mazda; we sacrifice unto the Glory of the Aryas, made by"},{"ref":"53.9d","t":"Mazda; we sacrifice unto the awful Glory of the Kavis, made by"},{"ref":"53.9e","t":"Mazda."},{"ref":"53.9f","t":"We sacrifice unto Atar, the son of Ahura Mazda; we sacrifice"},{"ref":"53.9g","t":"unto king Husravah; we sacrifice unto the lake of Husravah; we"},{"ref":"53.9h","t":"sacrifice unto Mount Asnavant, made by Mazda; we sacrifice unto"},{"ref":"53.9i","t":"Lake Chaechasta, made by Mazda; we sacrifice unto the awful Glory"},{"ref":"53.9j","t":"of the Kavis, made by Mazda."},{"ref":"53.9k","t":"We sacrifice unto Atar, the son of Ahura Mazda; we sacrifice"},{"ref":"53.9l","t":"unto Mount Raevant, made by Mazda; we sacrifice unto the awful"},{"ref":"53.9m","t":"Glory of the Kavis, made by Mazda."},{"ref":"53.9n","t":"We sacrifice unto Atar, the son of Ahura Mazda; we sacrifice"},{"ref":"53.9o","t":"unto Atar, the beneficent, the warrior. We sacrifice unto that"},{"ref":"53.9p","t":"God, who is a full source of glory. We sacrifice unto that God,"},{"ref":"53.9q","t":"who is a full source of healing."},{"ref":"53.9r","t":"We sacrifice unto Atar, the son of Ahura Mazda; we sacrifice"},{"ref":"53.9s","t":"unto all Fires; we sacrifice unto the God, Nairyo-Sangha, who"},{"ref":"53.9t","t":"dwells in the navel of kings."},{"ref":"53.10","t":"Aban."},{"ref":"53.10a","t":"We sacrifice unto the good Waters, made by Mazda and holy;"},{"ref":"53.10b","t":"we sacrifice unto the holy water-spring Ardvi Anahita; we"},{"ref":"53.10c","t":"sacrifice unto all waters, made by Mazda and Holy; we sacrifice"},{"ref":"53.10d","t":"unto all plants, made by Mazda and holy."},{"ref":"53.11","t":"Khwarshed."},{"ref":"53.11a","t":"We sacrifice unto the bright, undying, shining, swift-horsed"},{"ref":"53.11b","t":"Sun,"},{"ref":"53.12","t":"Mah."},{"ref":"53.12a","t":"We sacrifice unto the Moon that keeps in it the seed of the"},{"ref":"53.12b","t":"Bull. We sacrifice unto the Soul and Fravashi of the"},{"ref":"53.12c","t":"only-created Bull; we sacrifice unto the Soul and Fravashi of the"},{"ref":"53.12d","t":"Bull of many species."},{"ref":"53.13","t":"Tishtar."},{"ref":"53.13a","t":"We sacrifice unto Tistrya, the bright and glorious Star; we"},{"ref":"53.13b","t":"sacrifice unto the powerful Satavaesa, made by Mazda, who pushes"},{"ref":"53.13c","t":"waters forward; we sacrifice unto all the Stars that have in them"},{"ref":"53.13d","t":"the seed of the waters; we sacrifice unto all the Stars that have"},{"ref":"53.13e","t":"in them the seed of the earth; we sacrifice unto all the Stars"},{"ref":"53.13f","t":"that have in them the seeds of the plants; we sacrifice unto the"},{"ref":"53.13g","t":"Star Vanant, made by Mazda; we sacrifice unto those stars that"},{"ref":"53.13h","t":"are seven in number, the Haptoiringas, made by Mazda, glorious"},{"ref":"53.13i","t":"and healing; in order to oppose the Yatus and Pairikas."},{"ref":"53.14","t":"Goshorun."},{"ref":"53.14a","t":"We sacrifice unto the soul of the bounteous Cow; we"},{"ref":"53.14b","t":"sacrifice unto the powerful Drvaspa, made by Mazda and holy."},{"ref":"53.15","t":"Dai-pa-Mihr."},{"ref":"53.15a","t":"We sacrifice unto the Maker Ahura Mazda, the bright and"},{"ref":"53.15b","t":"glorious; we sacrifice unto the Amesha-Spentas, the all-ruling,"},{"ref":"53.15c","t":"the all-beneficent."},{"ref":"53.16","t":"Mihr."},{"ref":"53.16a","t":"We sacrifice unto Mithra, the lord of wide pastures, who has"},{"ref":"53.16b","t":"a thousand ears and ten thousand eyes, a God invoked by his own"},{"ref":"53.16c","t":"name; we sacrifice unto Rama Hvastra."},{"ref":"53.17","t":"Srosh."},{"ref":"53.17a","t":"We sacrifice unto the holy, tall-formed, fiend-smiting,"},{"ref":"53.17b","t":"world-increasing Sraosha, holy and master of holiness."},{"ref":"53.18","t":"Rashn."},{"ref":"53.18a","t":"We sacrifice unto Rashnu Razishta; we sacrifice unto Arstat,"},{"ref":"53.18b","t":"who makes the world grow, who makes the world increase; we"},{"ref":"53.18c","t":"sacrifice unto the true-spoken speech that makes the world grow."},{"ref":"53.19","t":"Frawardin."},{"ref":"53.19a","t":"We sacrifice unto the good, strong, beneficent Fravashis of"},{"ref":"53.19b","t":"the holy ones."},{"ref":"53.20","t":"Warharan."},{"ref":"53.20a","t":"We sacrifice unto the well-shapen, tall-formed Strength; we"},{"ref":"53.20b","t":"sacrifice unto Verethraghna, made by Ahura; we sacrifice unto the"},{"ref":"53.20c","t":"crushing Ascendant."},{"ref":"53.21","t":"Ram."},{"ref":"53.21a","t":"We sacrifice unto Rama Hvastra; we sacrifice unto the holy"},{"ref":"53.21b","t":"Vayu; we sacrifice unto Vayu, who works highly and is more"},{"ref":"53.21c","t":"powerful to destroy than all other creatures. Unto that part of"},{"ref":"53.21d","t":"thee do we sacrifice, O Vayu, that belongs to Spenta-Mainyu. We"},{"ref":"53.21e","t":"sacrifice unto the sovereign Sky; we sacrifice unto the Boundless"},{"ref":"53.21f","t":"Time; we sacrifice unto the sovereign Time of the long Period."},{"ref":"53.22","t":"Wad."},{"ref":"53.22a","t":"We sacrifice unto the beneficent, bounteous Wind; we"},{"ref":"53.22b","t":"sacrifice unto the wind that blows below; we sacrifice unto the"},{"ref":"53.22c","t":"wind that blows above; we sacrifice unto the wind that blows"},{"ref":"53.22d","t":"before; we sacrifice unto the wind that blows behind. We"},{"ref":"53.22e","t":"sacrifice unto the manly Courage."},{"ref":"53.23","t":"Dai-pa-Den."},{"ref":"53.23a","t":"We sacrifice unto the Maker Ahura Mazda, the bright and"},{"ref":"53.23b","t":"glorious; we sacrifice unto the Amesha-Spentas."},{"ref":"53.24","t":"Den."},{"ref":"53.24a","t":"We sacrifice unto the most right Chista, made by Mazda and"},{"ref":"53.24b","t":"holy; we sacrifice unto the good Law of the worshippers of Mazda."},{"ref":"53.25","t":"Ard."},{"ref":"53.25a","t":"We sacrifice unto Ashi Vanguhi, the bright high, strong,"},{"ref":"53.25b","t":"tall-formed, and merciful; we Sacrifice unto the Glory made by"},{"ref":"53.25c","t":"Mazda; we sacrifice unto the Weal made by Mazda. We sacrifice"},{"ref":"53.25d","t":"unto Parendi, of the light chariot; we sacrifice unto the Glory"},{"ref":"53.25e","t":"of the Aryas, made by Mazda; we sacrifice unto the awful kingly"},{"ref":"53.25f","t":"Glory, made by Mazda; we sacrifice unto that awful Glory, that"},{"ref":"53.25g","t":"cannot be forcibly seized, made by Mazda; we sacrifice unto the"},{"ref":"53.25h","t":"Glory of Zarathushtra, made by Mazda."},{"ref":"53.26","t":"Ashtad."},{"ref":"53.26a","t":"We sacrifice unto Arshtat, who makes the world grow; we"},{"ref":"53.26b","t":"sacrifice unto Mount Ushi-darena, made by Mazda, a God of holy"},{"ref":"53.26c","t":"happiness."},{"ref":"53.27","t":"Asman."},{"ref":"53.27a","t":"We sacrifice unto the shining Heavens; we sacrifice unto the"},{"ref":"53.27b","t":"bright, all-happy, blissful abode of the holy ones."},{"ref":"53.28","t":"Zam."},{"ref":"53.28a","t":"We sacrifice unto the Earth, a beneficent God; we sacrifice"},{"ref":"53.28b","t":"unto these places, unto these fields; we sacrifice unto Mount"},{"ref":"53.28c","t":"Ushi-darena, made by Mazda, a God of holy happiness; we sacrifice"},{"ref":"53.28d","t":"unto all the mountains, that are seats of holy happiness, of full"},{"ref":"53.28e","t":"happiness, made by Mazda, the holy and masters of holiness; we"},{"ref":"53.28f","t":"sacrifice unto the awful kingly Glory, made by Mazda; we"},{"ref":"53.28g","t":"sacrifice unto the awful Glory that cannot be forcibly seized,"},{"ref":"53.28h","t":"made by Mazda."},{"ref":"53.29","t":"Mahraspand."},{"ref":"53.29a","t":"We sacrifice unto the Mathra Spenta, of high glory; we"},{"ref":"53.29b","t":"sacrifice unto the Law opposed to the Daevas; we sacrifice unto"},{"ref":"53.29c","t":"the Law of Zarathushtra; we sacrifice unto the long-traditional"},{"ref":"53.29d","t":"teaching; we sacrifice unto the good Law of the worshippers of"},{"ref":"53.29e","t":"Mazda: we sacrifice unto the Devotion to the Mathra Spenta; we"},{"ref":"53.29f","t":"sacrifice unto the understanding that keeps the Law of the"},{"ref":"53.29g","t":"worshippers of Mazda; we sacrifice unto the knowledge of the"},{"ref":"53.29h","t":"Mathra Spenta; we sacrifice unto the heavenly Wisdom, made by"},{"ref":"53.29i","t":"Mazda; we sacrifice unto the Wisdom acquired through the ear and"},{"ref":"53.29j","t":"made by Mazda."},{"ref":"53.30","t":"Anagran."},{"ref":"53.30a","t":"We sacrifice unto the eternal and sovereign luminous space;"},{"ref":"53.30b","t":"we sacrifice unto the bright Garonmana; we sacrifice unto the"},{"ref":"53.30c","t":"sovereign place of eternal Weal; we sacrifice unto the"},{"ref":"53.30d","t":"Chinvat-bridge, made by Mazda; we sacrifice unto Apam Napat, the"},{"ref":"53.30e","t":"swift-horsed, the high and shining lord, who has many wives; and"},{"ref":"53.30f","t":"we sacrifice unto the water, made by Mazda and holy; we sacrifice"},{"ref":"53.30g","t":"unto the golden and tall Haoma; we sacrifice unto the enlivening"},{"ref":"53.30h","t":"Haoma, who makes the world grow; we sacrifice unto Haoma, who"},{"ref":"53.30i","t":"keeps death far away; we sacrifice unto the pious and good"},{"ref":"53.30j","t":"Blessing; we sacrifice unto the awful, powerful, cursing thought"},{"ref":"53.30k","t":"of the wise, a God; we sacrifice unto all the holy Gods of the"},{"ref":"53.30l","t":"heavenly world; we sacrifice unto all the holy Gods of the"},{"ref":"53.30m","t":"material world."},{"ref":"53.30n","t":"I praise, I invoke, I meditate upon, and we sacrifice unto"},{"ref":"53.30o","t":"the good, strong, beneficent Fravashis of the holy ones."},{"sp":"HDR","t":"Afrinagans (Prayers of Blessing)"},{"ref":"54.1","t":"<em>Translated by L. Mills, 1898<\/em>"},{"sp":"HDR","t":"Afrinagan-i Dahman"},{"ref":"55.1","t":"Yatha ahu Vairyo...."},{"ref":"55.1a","t":"Ashem Vohu...."},{"ref":"55.1b","t":"I profess myself a Mazda-worshipper, a follower of Zarathushtra,"},{"ref":"55.1c","t":"opposing the Daevas, accepting the Ahuric doctrine."},{"ref":"55.1d","t":"(Here recite the appropriate Gah dedication.)"},{"ref":"55.1e","t":"With propitiation of the Dahman Afrin of the good ones and the"},{"ref":"55.1f","t":"strong wise one with higher intellect, for worship, adoration,"},{"ref":"55.1g","t":"propitiation, and praise."},{"ref":"55.1h","t":"‘Yatha Ahu Vairyo’, the zaotar should say to me"},{"ref":"55.1i","t":"‘Yatha Ahu Vairyo’, he who is the zaotar should say to me"},{"ref":"55.1j","t":"‘Atha ratush ashatchit hacha’, the Asha-sanctified knowing one"},{"ref":"55.1k","t":"should say."},{"ref":"55.1l","t":"(Karda:)"},{"ref":"55.2","t":"May these blessings of the Asha-sanctified come into this"},{"ref":"55.2a","t":"house, namely, rewards, compensation, and hospitality; and may"},{"ref":"55.2b","t":"there now come to this community Asha, possessions, prosperity,"},{"ref":"55.2c","t":"good fortune, and easeful life, and the long enduring prominence"},{"ref":"55.2d","t":"of this Religion, which is Ahuric, Zarathushtrian."},{"ref":"55.3","t":"Now in this house may the cattle not be tainted, nor the Asha,"},{"ref":"55.3a","t":"nor the strength of Asha-sanctified men, nor the Ahuric doctrine."},{"ref":"55.4","t":"May the good, prosperity-giving, holy, Asha-sanctified, fravashis"},{"ref":"55.4a","t":"come here, accompanied by the healing virtues of Ashi, to the"},{"ref":"55.4b","t":"width of the Earth, the length of the rivers, and the height of"},{"ref":"55.4c","t":"the sun, to give the possession of good things, for the overthrow"},{"ref":"55.4d","t":"of misfortunes, and the advancement of riches and fortunes."},{"ref":"55.5","t":"May Hearkening (Sraosha) overcome disobedience within this"},{"ref":"55.5a","t":"house, and may peace overcome discord, generosity overcome greed,"},{"ref":"55.5b","t":"reverence overcome rebellion, and honesty overcome falsehood."},{"ref":"55.5c","t":"May Asha conquer the fiend,"},{"ref":"55.6","t":"so that, in it the Amesha Spentas may receive, through Sraosha,"},{"ref":"55.6a","t":"companion of Ashi, good acts of worship and prayers of praise;"},{"ref":"55.6b","t":"good in reverence and adoration, the abiding offering, the joyous"},{"ref":"55.6c","t":"offering, and the devotional offering, until the time of the final"},{"ref":"55.6d","t":"harvest."},{"ref":"55.7","t":"Let the comfort-giving good fortune never forsake this house,"},{"ref":"55.7a","t":"nor the comfort-giving riches, nor comfort-giving noble offspring,"},{"ref":"55.7b","t":"with long lasting company of what bestows paradise and good rewards."},{"ref":"55.7c","t":"Ashem Vohu...!"},{"ref":"55.7d","t":"(Asirvad:)"},{"ref":"55.8","t":"To Ahura Mazda, rich, possessing good things. Blessings on"},{"ref":"55.8a","t":"the rulers of the land, for greater strength, greater victory,"},{"ref":"55.8b","t":"greater rule, greater sovereignty, compassion, long rule, enduring"},{"ref":"55.8c","t":"physical vitality, and health."},{"ref":"55.9","t":"(Blessings) to Ama, well-built, fair of form, to Verethraghna,"},{"ref":"55.9a","t":"made by Ahura, and to the triumphing Uparatat, completely repelling"},{"ref":"55.9b","t":"malice, completely conquering the hostile malicious adversary"},{"ref":"55.9c","t":"with a blow."},{"ref":"55.10","t":"Blessings so that he may be winner of the battle, victorious"},{"ref":"55.10a","t":"over every malicious adversary, over every evil adversary, faulty"},{"ref":"55.10b","t":"in thoughts, words and deeds."},{"ref":"55.11","t":"(Blessings) that he may be victorious through timely thoughts,"},{"ref":"55.11a","t":"words, and deeds; to suppress all the evil-minded, and all Daeva-worshippers,"},{"ref":"55.11b","t":"so as to attain to good reward, and to good renown, and to long"},{"ref":"55.11c","t":"happiness of my soul."},{"ref":"55.12","t":"Blessings for long life, for the desired life, for the service"},{"ref":"55.12a","t":"of Asha-sanctified people, and for the disservice of ill done"},{"ref":"55.12b","t":"deeds - the best existence of the Asha-sanctified, the luminous,"},{"ref":"55.12c","t":"offering all blissful. Thus may it come as I wish."},{"ref":"55.12d","t":"We praise good thoughts, good words, and good deeds, performed"},{"ref":"55.12e","t":"here and elsewhere, now and in the past. Thus we glorify and invoke"},{"ref":"55.12f","t":"all that is good."},{"ref":"55.12g","t":"I yearn for good mind. May Peshotan son on Gushtasp come to my"},{"ref":"55.12h","t":"aid, may he accept my prayers, may he shine for me. Thus may the"},{"ref":"55.12i","t":"holy attain long life and may their desires be fulfilled."},{"ref":"55.12j","t":"May this Afrinagan and Khshnuman reach the Yazad Dahman."},{"ref":"55.12k","t":"May the knowledge, promulgation, and glory of the good Mazdayasnian"},{"ref":"55.12l","t":"religion spread throughout the seven regions of the world, through"},{"ref":"55.12m","t":"speech, righteous persuasion, the good kingly authority and justice."},{"ref":"55.12n","t":"So be it."},{"ref":"55.12o","t":"Yatha Ahu Vairyo...."},{"ref":"55.12p","t":"Ashem Vohu...!"},{"ref":"55.13","t":"Yatha Ahu Vairyo...."},{"ref":"55.13a","t":"I desire worship and adoration and strength and force for the"},{"ref":"55.13b","t":"Dahman Afrin of the good ones and the valiant wise one with higher"},{"ref":"55.13c","t":"intellect."},{"ref":"55.13d","t":"Ashem Vohu...."},{"ref":"55.13e","t":"May we all be one in Asha."},{"ref":"55.13f","t":"Thus may it come as I wish."},{"ref":"55.13g","t":"We praise good thoughts, good words, and good deeds, performed"},{"ref":"55.13h","t":"here and elsewhere, now and in the past. Thus we glorify and invoke"},{"ref":"55.13i","t":"all that is good."},{"sp":"HDR","t":"Afrinagan-i Gatha"},{"ref":"56.1","t":"As the Ahu is (revered and) to be chosen, so (is) the Ratu"},{"ref":"56.1a","t":"(one who rules) from the Righteous Order, a creator of mental"},{"ref":"56.1b","t":"goodness, and of life’s actions done for Ahura, and the Kingdom"},{"ref":"56.1c","t":"(is) to Mazda, which to the poor may offer a nurturer."},{"ref":"56.1d","t":"I confess myself a Mazda-worshipper - for the praise of Ahura"},{"ref":"56.1e","t":"Mazda, the resplendent, the glorious, and of the Bountiful Immortals,"},{"ref":"56.1f","t":"for the bountiful and holy Gathas which rule in the ritual order."},{"ref":"56.1g","t":"(Propitiation and praise be) to the Gatha Ahunavaiti, and to the"},{"ref":"56.1h","t":"Gatha Ushtavaiti, to the Gatha Spenta-mainyu, and to the Gatha"},{"ref":"56.1i","t":"Vohu-khshathra, and to the Gatha Vahishtoishti. 2. Propitiation"},{"ref":"56.1j","t":"to the Fravashis of the saints, the mighty, overwhelming, even"},{"ref":"56.1k","t":"to those of the saints of yore, who held the primeval faith (the"},{"ref":"56.1l","t":"Gathic faith), and to those of the next of kin."},{"ref":"56.3","t":"We sacrifice to Ahura Mazda, the resplendent, the glorious;"},{"ref":"56.3a","t":"and we sacrifice to the Amesha Spenta who rule aright, and who"},{"ref":"56.3b","t":"dispose (of all aright). And we sacrifice to the bounteous and"},{"ref":"56.3c","t":"holy Gathas, which rule (as the first) in the ritual order."},{"ref":"56.3d","t":"We sacrifice to the Gatha Ahunavaiti, the holy, as it rules in"},{"ref":"56.3e","t":"the ritual order; and we sacrifice to the Gatha Ushtavaiti, the"},{"ref":"56.3f","t":"holy, as it rules in the ritual order; and we sacrifice to the"},{"ref":"56.3g","t":"Gatha Spenta-mainyu, the holy, as it rules in the ritual order;"},{"ref":"56.3h","t":"and we sacrifice to the Gatha Vohu-khshathra, the holy, as it"},{"ref":"56.3i","t":"rules in the ritual order; and we sacrifice to the Gatha Vahishtoishti,"},{"ref":"56.3j","t":"the holy, as it rules in the ritual order."},{"ref":"56.4","t":"(=Yt13.49-52.)"},{"sp":"HDR","t":"Afrinagan-i Gahambar"},{"ref":"57.1","t":"[This prayer is part of the ceremony of blessing (Afrinagan) addressed to the community during the great seasonal festivals (Gahambars).]"},{"ref":"57.1a","t":"I confess myself a Mazda-worshipper, and of Zarathustra’s"},{"ref":"57.1aa","t":"order, a foe of the Daevas, devoted to the lore of the Lord, for"},{"ref":"57.1b","t":"the holy Havani, the regulator of the ritual order (and its lord"},{"ref":"57.1c","t":"in its turn), for its sacrifice, homage, propitiation, and praise;"},{"ref":"57.1d","t":"(and I confess myself) for Savanghi and for Visya, the holy lords"},{"ref":"57.1e","t":"of the ritual order for their sacrifice, homage, propitiation,"},{"ref":"57.1f","t":"and praise, and for that of the Asnya, the day-lords of the days"},{"ref":"57.1g","t":"during daylight, and of the days in their length, for the Mahya,"},{"ref":"57.1h","t":"month-lords, and the Yairya, year-lords, and for those of the"},{"ref":"57.1i","t":"especial seasons, and for the worship, homage, propitiation, and"},{"ref":"57.1j","t":"praise of that lofty lord who is the Ritual Righteousness (itself);"},{"ref":"57.1k","t":"yea, for the worship, homage, propitiation, and praise of the"},{"ref":"57.1l","t":"lords of the days, months, years, and seasons - for those lords"},{"ref":"57.1m","t":"of the ritual order who are of all the greatest, who are the regulators"},{"ref":"57.1n","t":"of the ritual at the time of Havani."},{"ref":"57.2","t":"To Maidhyo-zaremya, the lord [or to Maidhyo-shema, the lord,"},{"ref":"57.2a","t":"or to Paitishahya, the lord, or to Ayathrima, Maidhyairya, or"},{"ref":"57.2b","t":"Hamaspathmaedhaya], be propitiation, homage, and praise."},{"ref":"57.3","t":"O ye Mazdayasnians who are here present offer ye this ritual"},{"ref":"57.3a","t":"service, and present ye the Myazda which is that of the Maidhyo-zaremaya,"},{"ref":"57.3b","t":"taking a piece of sound flesh from a choice beast, with a full"},{"ref":"57.3c","t":"flow of milk."},{"ref":"57.4","t":"If ye are able to do this, (well); if ye are unable to do"},{"ref":"57.4a","t":"it, ye may take then (a portion) of some liquor of equal value,"},{"ref":"57.4b","t":"it matters not which it is, and have it consumed as it is proper;"},{"ref":"57.4c","t":"and so be ye discreet from your obedience, most correctly faithful"},{"ref":"57.4d","t":"in your speech, most saintly from your sanctity, best ordered"},{"ref":"57.4e","t":"in your exercise of power, least straitened by oppressions, heart-easy"},{"ref":"57.4f","t":"with rejoicings, most merciful of givers, most helpful to the"},{"ref":"57.4g","t":"poor, fulfilling most the ritual, the blest and longed-for Asha,"},{"ref":"57.4h","t":"(coy?) riches woman-minded (?) bringing (as reward). If ye can"},{"ref":"57.4i","t":"do this and with vigour, (well); if not, bring wood to the"},{"ref":"57.4j","t":"Ratu’s house. It matters not what kind, so it be well cut, and"},{"ref":"57.4k","t":"very dry, and in loads of fitting size. If that is possible, (well);"},{"ref":"57.4l","t":"if not, let a man bring wood to the Ratu’s dwelling, and heap"},{"ref":"57.4m","t":"it up as high as the ear, or to reach the fore-shoulder, or with"},{"ref":"57.4n","t":"the fore-arm measure, (or at least as high as the end of the hanging"},{"ref":"57.4o","t":"hand). If that is possible, (well); but if it has not been"},{"ref":"57.4p","t":"possible, then let the worshipper (with the mind’s offering) ascribe"},{"ref":"57.4q","t":"the power to him who rules the best, Ahura, (saying): Wherefore"},{"ref":"57.4r","t":"for this cause verily we offer and ascribe the Sovereign Power"},{"ref":"57.4s","t":"to Ahura Mazda, who rules the best, and to Righteousness (the"},{"ref":"57.4t","t":"ritual and moral Order), and we complete our sacrifice to them."},{"ref":"57.4u","t":"Thus is the Myazda offered with the well-timed prayer for blessings."},{"ref":"57.7","t":"In case that a man does not give of the first Myazda which"},{"ref":"57.7a","t":"is that of the Maidhyo-zaremaya, O Spitama Zarathushtra! the Ratu"},{"ref":"57.7b","t":"that has the right to that Myazda, and who has this person under"},{"ref":"57.7c","t":"his guidance, expels that (false) disciple who has not his Myazda"},{"ref":"57.7d","t":"with him, as a man that does not worship, from the midst of the"},{"ref":"57.7e","t":"Mazda-worshippers. 8. In the case that a man does not give of"},{"ref":"57.7f","t":"the second Myazda, O Spitama Zarathushtra! which is that of the"},{"ref":"57.7g","t":"Maidhyo-shema, then let the Ratu to whom the Myazda should come,"},{"ref":"57.7h","t":"and who has the person under his guidance, expel that disciple,"},{"ref":"57.7i","t":"since he comes without his Myazda, as he would a man who refuses"},{"ref":"57.7j","t":"to recite his vows, from among the number of the Mazda-worshippers."},{"ref":"57.9","t":"In the case that a man does not give of the third Myazda, O"},{"ref":"57.9a","t":"Spitama Zarathushtra! which is that of Paitishahya, then let the"},{"ref":"57.9b","t":"Ratu who ought to receive that Myazda, and who has had the person"},{"ref":"57.9c","t":"under his guidance, expel that disciple which brings no Myazda,"},{"ref":"57.9d","t":"as a detected reprobate, from among the number of the Mazdayasnians."},{"ref":"57.10","t":"In case that a man does not offer of the fourth Myazda, O"},{"ref":"57.10a","t":"Spitama Zarathushtra! which is that of the Ayathrima let the Ratu"},{"ref":"57.10b","t":"who ought to receive that Myazda, and who has the person under"},{"ref":"57.10c","t":"his guidance, expel that disciple, since he brings no Myazda,"},{"ref":"57.10d","t":"as a refuse beast from among the number of the Mazdayasnians."},{"ref":"57.11","t":"In the case that a man does not give of the fifth Myazda,"},{"ref":"57.11a","t":"which is that of the Maidhyairya, then let the Ratu to whom that"},{"ref":"57.11b","t":"Myazda belongs as a perquisite, and who has that person under"},{"ref":"57.11c","t":"his guidance, expel him, since he brings no Myazda, as an alien,"},{"ref":"57.11d","t":"from among the number of the Mazdayasnians. 12. In case that a"},{"ref":"57.11e","t":"man does not give of the sixth Myazda, which is that of the Hamaspathmaedhaya,"},{"ref":"57.11f","t":"O Spitama Zarathushtra! let the Ratu to whom that Myazda belongs"},{"ref":"57.11g","t":"as a perquisite, and who has this person under his discipline"},{"ref":"57.11h","t":"to learn him the lore of Ahura, expel him, (as ignorant) since"},{"ref":"57.11i","t":"he brings no Myazda, from among the number of the Mazdayasnians."},{"ref":"57.13","t":"And let him decry him afterwards without hesitation, and drive"},{"ref":"57.13a","t":"him out; and let that Ratu lay upon him afterwards the expiating"},{"ref":"57.13b","t":"deeds without reserve; and in accordance with these rules, let"},{"ref":"57.13c","t":"the disciple treat the Ratu. (Let him beware of failure to bring"},{"ref":"57.13d","t":"his Myazda, or if he fails let the disciple bear, as is befitting,"},{"ref":"57.13e","t":"what is due.) A blessing is Righteousness (called) the Best, it"},{"ref":"57.13f","t":"is weal, it is weal for this (man) when toward Righteousness Best"},{"ref":"57.13g","t":"there is right."},{"ref":"57.14","t":"I bless with my prayer the royal Province-chiefs (who are"},{"ref":"57.14a","t":"faithful worshippers) of Ahura Mazda, the resplendent, the glorious,"},{"ref":"57.14b","t":"(beseeching) for superior strength for them, and for more important"},{"ref":"57.14c","t":"victory, and more influential rule, and desiring for them further"},{"ref":"57.14d","t":"authoritative power, and helpful support, and long duration to"},{"ref":"57.14e","t":"their reign, and the prolonged vitality of their frames, and health."},{"ref":"57.15","t":"And I pray in my benediction for strength well-shaped and"},{"ref":"57.15a","t":"stately of growth, and which smites victoriously, Ahura-made,"},{"ref":"57.15b","t":"and crushing, and for an ascendency abundantly subduing all who"},{"ref":"57.15c","t":"are filled with furious hate, assaulting the evil-minded enemies,"},{"ref":"57.15d","t":"and destroying, as if at once, the deadly, godless foes."},{"ref":"57.16","t":"And I pray in my blessing that he (the province-governor)"},{"ref":"57.16a","t":"may conquer in victorious battles every malicious foe, and each"},{"ref":"57.16b","t":"malignant, profane in thoughts, and words, and actions, that"},{"ref":"57.16c","t":"he may indeed be constantly victorious in his own religious thoughts,"},{"ref":"57.16d","t":"and words, and deeds, and unvarying in the smiting of every foe,"},{"ref":"57.16e","t":"and of every Daeva-worshipper, and that he may, as he proceeds,"},{"ref":"57.16f","t":"be well rewarded, and of good repute, possessing a far-foreseeing"},{"ref":"57.16g","t":"preparation of the soul. 18. And I pray with blessings thus: Live"},{"ref":"57.16h","t":"thou long and blessed be thou, ‘hail’ to thee; live for the aid"},{"ref":"57.16i","t":"of holy men, and for the crushing of the evil; and I pray for"},{"ref":"57.16j","t":"Heaven (for thee) the best world of the saints, shining, all glorious."},{"ref":"57.16k","t":"And thus may it happen as I pray -. And I bless in my prayer the"},{"ref":"57.16l","t":"sacrifice, and homage, and the strength, and swiftness of the"},{"ref":"57.16m","t":"day-lords during daylight, and of the lords of the days in their"},{"ref":"57.16n","t":"length, of the month-lords, and the year-lords, and of the lords"},{"ref":"57.16o","t":"of the seasons (in their course), and for the worship, homage,"},{"ref":"57.16p","t":"propitiation, and praise of the lofty lord who is the Righteous"},{"ref":"57.16q","t":"Ritual itself, and of those lords of the ritual who are of all"},{"ref":"57.16r","t":"the greatest, and who are the lords of the ritual at the time"},{"ref":"57.16s","t":"of Havani, for Maidhyo-zaremaya the lord, [(or) for Maidhyo-shema"},{"ref":"57.16t","t":"the lord, (or) for Paitishahya the lord, or for Ayathrima, Maidhyairya,"},{"ref":"57.16u","t":"or Hamaspathmaedhaya]."},{"sp":"HDR","t":"Afrinagan-i Rapithwin"},{"ref":"58.1","t":"I confess myself a Mazda-worshipper, of Zarathushtra’s order,"},{"ref":"58.1a","t":"a foe to the Daevas, devoted to the lore of the Lord, for Rapithwina,"},{"ref":"58.1b","t":"the holy lord of the ritual order, for sacrifice, homage, propitiation,"},{"ref":"58.1c","t":"and praise, and for Fradat-fshu and Zantuma, the holy lord(s)"},{"ref":"58.1d","t":"of the ritual order. 2. And to Ahura Mazda, the resplendent, the"},{"ref":"58.1e","t":"glorious, and to the Bountiful Immortals, be propitiation, and"},{"ref":"58.1f","t":"to Asha Vahishta (who is Righteousness the Best), and to the Fire,"},{"ref":"58.1g","t":"Ahura Mazda’s son, and to all the holy Yazads, heavenly and earthly,"},{"ref":"58.1h","t":"and to the Fravashis of the saints, the mighty and overwhelming-."},{"ref":"58.3","t":"For thus did Ahura Mazda speak to Spitama Zarathushtra the"},{"ref":"58.3a","t":"word which was spoken for the ritual time of the Rapithwina, (saying):"},{"ref":"58.3b","t":"Ask us, O holy Zarathushtra, what are Thy questions to be asked"},{"ref":"58.3c","t":"of us, for Thy question is as that mighty one when Thy ruler speaks"},{"ref":"58.3d","t":"his mighty wish. 4. Then Zarathushtra asked Ahura Mazda: O Ahura"},{"ref":"58.3e","t":"Mazda, most bountiful creator of the material worlds and holy!"},{"ref":"58.3f","t":"what does that man acquire, what does he merit, what reward"},{"ref":"58.3g","t":"shall there be for that man who shall recite the Rapithwina"},{"ref":"58.3h","t":"office with the Rapithwina prayer for blessing, and who shall"},{"ref":"58.3i","t":"sacrifice with the Rapithwina office with hands (well) washed,"},{"ref":"58.3j","t":"and with (well) washed mortars, with the Baresman spread, and"},{"ref":"58.3k","t":"with Haoma high uplifted, and with fire brightly flaming, with","hvShift6":[[0,0],[57,58]]},{"ref":"58.3l","t":"Ahuna-vairya loud intoned, with Haoma-moistened tongue, and with"},{"ref":"58.3m","t":"a body Mathra-bound?"},{"ref":"58.6","t":"And Ahura Mazda answered him: As the wind from the southern"},{"ref":"58.6a","t":"quarter, O Spitama! causes the entire material world to advance"},{"ref":"58.6b","t":"and to increase, and as it will bless it, rejoice it, and cause"},{"ref":"58.6c","t":"it to progress, such a like reward does such a man receive,"},{"ref":"58.6d","t":"who recites the Rapithwina-ratu with the Rapithwina blessing,"},{"ref":"58.6e","t":"and sacrifices with it with (well) washed hands, and mortars,"},{"ref":"58.6f","t":"with Baresman spread, and Haoma lifted, with fire brightly flaming,"},{"ref":"58.6g","t":"and with Ahuna-vairya loud intoned, and with Haoma-moistened tongue,"},{"ref":"58.6h","t":"and a body Mathra-bound! 8. Thus hath Ahura Mazda declared to"},{"ref":"58.6i","t":"Spitama Zarathushtra the word which (should be) spoken at the"},{"ref":"58.6j","t":"Rapithwina time."},{"ref":"58.6k","t":"9-10. (See A1.14-19.)"}],[]);})();